(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#" :text "Routes a verified SsaModule's unboxed array and kernel builtin calls (f64, i64 and i8 ArrayLen, Get, Slice, Concat, Generate, Sum, CountEq, Fold, Scan; dot, axpy, gemm) to asl-target-llvm/arrays instead of libaslrt.a's arrays.c and kernels.c tables (plan unit ARRLOWER), the sysRoute and parRoute pattern. routeModule rewrites each such opBuiltin into an opCall of arrays' function for it, a call with another operand count than that function takes being ERR_LLVM_ARRROUTE_ARITY, and adds the arrays functions those calls reach (internal, so every module of a program keeps its own copy), its externs (a same-named extern of another signature is ERR_LLVM_ARRROUTE_EXTERN) and the strings it reads, reusing pool strings already there; a module function already named like an added one is ERR_LLVM_ARRROUTE_NAME. The functions need no libc facts, so every triple routes. finishText completes the emitted text of a module routeModule routed (routedNames? of its internal names; the text itself is never scanned to decide, since a program may hold any of these declarations in a string literal): the declarations of arrays' helpers become their definitions, and asl_alloc, llvm.fabs.f64 and llvm.fmuladd.f64 are declared when the text does not already declare them; a helper declaration it expects and does not find exactly once, or a module without rtError's rterr.raise, which aslArrRaise calls, is ERR_LLVM_ARRROUTE_TEXT.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#arity" :text "The operand count of the arrays function for builtin name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#arrayCalls" :text "Each distinct (builtin, operand count) of m's opBuiltin calls of the array and kernel builtins, in first-seen order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#routes?" :text "True when m calls an array or kernel builtin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#poolWith" :text "strings with each wanted string it lacks appended, and the index of every wanted string in the result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#mergeExterns" :text "own followed by each added extern it does not declare; an added extern own declares with another signature is ERR_LLVM_ARRROUTE_EXTERN.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#reachable" :text "names with every function of all one of them calls, transitively.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#routeModule" :text "m routed: unchanged, with no internal names, when it calls no array or kernel builtin; else verified first (its own diagnostics when it does not verify), its calls' operand counts checked, and rewritten as this module's :d describes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#routedNames?" :text "True when internal, the names a routing made internal, holds a function asl-target-llvm/arrays added: the module routeModule rewrote.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#extraDecls" :text "Declarations the helper definitions need, added when the text lacks them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrayRoute.asl#finishText" :text "res with arrays' helper declarations, whole lines the emitter wrote, replaced by their definitions when routed (routedNames? of the routing's internal names), else res unchanged whatever its text holds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#" :text "Native unboxed array builtins (plan unit ARRLOWER): SSA builders, the sys.asl and parallel.asl pattern, for asl/host/src/arrays.c's table (for P in f64, i64 and i8: PArrayLen, PArrayGet, PArraySlice, PArrayConcat, PArrayGenerate, PArraySum, PArrayCountEq, PArrayFold, PArrayScan) and kernels.c's dot, axpy and gemm, so a routed program (asl-target-llvm/arrayRoute) links neither arrays.o nor kernels.o. Each builtin is one function of Val operands returning a Val, named functionName of the builtin, a typed loop over the Arr object of value.h (Obj header, len at 8, elem at 16, data at 24) reading and writing f64, i64 and i8 elements in place. Generate, Fold and Scan call their closure through opCallClosure (rtObject objrt.call); an array held across that call stays a live Val the conservative stack scan reaches, and its data is reloaded from the object after each call. A result array is made as arrays.c mkArray makes one: past MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENTS (16777216) ERR_RANGE '<Type> of n elements exceeds the array allocation limit', gcWillAllocate, asl_alloc of an O_ARR Arr, a malloc of n*elem+1 bytes (ERR_OOM 'cannot allocate <Type> of n elements' when it fails) and gcAccount. Every argument check raises arrays.c's or kernels.c's code and text, formatted by snprintf into a malloc'd buffer and raised through (trap code msg), the path a source-level trap lowers to (rtError's rterr.trap); ERR_OOM, outside trap's vocabulary, goes to rtError's rterr.raise directly. Sums follow arrays.c: Neumaier-compensated for f64, ERR_INT_OVERFLOW '<who> leaves int64' for i64 and i8. The kernels' products accumulate through llvm.fmuladd, as clang compiles kernels.c's a*b+c under its default -ffp-contract=on. A Val's words, f64 element access, fabs, fmuladd, asl_alloc and the raw raise go through helpers arrayRoute defines in the emitted text (helperDefinitions), since asl-ir has no operation for them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#pn" :text "The module function name of an arrays function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#arrayBuiltinNames" :text "The 30 builtins this module implements: arrays.c's 27 rows, then kernels.c's 3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#functionName" :text "The function a routed call of builtin calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#maxElements" :text "value.h MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENTS.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#messageBytes" :text "The error message buffer, value.c aslErrorMsg's size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#tagNames" :text "value.c tagName, indexed by Tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#formats" :text "arrays.c's and kernels.c's error formats, %zu written %lld since every such operand is non-negative.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#arrStrings" :text "The pool strings the arrays functions read: error codes, formats, builtin names, type and tag names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#k" :text "d (i64): the literal n.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#ex" :text "d: a call of the extern or helper callee.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#hp" :text "d: a call of the arrays function named name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#ld" :text "d (i64): the 8 bytes at address addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#tagOf" :text "d (i64): the tag of v, the low half of its first word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#objOf" :text "d (i64): the payload word of v, an object's address (0 for the empty list).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#lenOf" :text "d (i64): the length of the array v.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#dataOf" :text "d (ptr): the element buffer of the array v, read from its object.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#offset" :text "d (ptr): base advanced by idx elements of elem bytes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#loadElem" :text "d: element idx of an array of kind, raw: f64 for f64, i64 for i64 and i8 (an I8 sign-extended).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#loadBoxed" :text "d (Val): element idx boxed, a Float or an Int.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#cs" :text "d (ptr): the pool string text, NUL-terminated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#raiseBlocks" :text "label runs pre, then raises code with the printf-style fmt over args (i64 or ptr), formatted into a malloc'd buffer: through (trap code msg) when trap accepts code, else through rterr.raise (aslArrRaise). A buffer malloc cannot give raises ERR_OOM 'cannot allocate an error message'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#tagNameOf" :text "d (ptr): value.c tagName of the i64 tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#tagNameFn" :text "tagName(tag) -> ptr: value.c tagName, '?' past the last tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#checkTag" :text "label goes on to okLabel when v's tag is want, else raises ERR_TYPE with fmt over args followed by the name of v's tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#checkArr" :text "arrays.c arr: v must be an array of kind, else ERR_TYPE '<who> expects <Type>, got <tag>'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#whoAnd" :text "The pointers checkArr's message reads, who and the type name, bound in the function's entry block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#checkInt" :text "arrays.c intArg: v must be an Int, else ERR_TYPE '<who> expects Int, got <tag>'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#newArrayFn" :text "new<kind>(n) -> Val: arrays.c mkArray for an n of zero or more: ERR_RANGE past MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENTS, gcWillAllocate, an Arr (asl_alloc O_ARR: len at 8, elem at 16, data at 24), a malloc'd buffer of n*elem+1 bytes (ERR_OOM when it fails) and gcAccount.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#st" :text "Stores the i64 v at address addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#mkv" :text "d (Val): the Val whose words are w0 and w1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#storeBlocks" :text "arrays.c setElem: label stores the Val v as element idx of the array arr and jumps to next with nextArgs; v must be a Float for f64 (ERR_TYPE '<who>: element must be Float, got <tag>'), an Int otherwise (... must be Int ...), and within -128..127 for i8 (ERR_RANGE '<who>: n outside I8').")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#concatFn" :text "arrays.c concat: the list's arrays, each checked, summed in a first pass, copied in a second after the allocation; the list stays live across it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#checkTagWord" :text "checkTag for the car of the Cons at address cell, read from memory (tag word at 8).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#foldScanFn" :text "arrays.c foldScan: acc = f(acc, x) left to right over xs; Scan keeps every acc in a new array (setElem's checks), Fold returns the last, which must be an Int for i64 and i8 (ERR_TYPE '<who>: accumulator must be Int, got <tag>').")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#sizeLimit" :text "SIZE_MAX / sizeof(double) on a 64-bit triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#productCheck" :text "kernels.c's overflow guard: when a and b are both positive and a exceeds (SIZE_MAX / 8) / b, ERR_RANGE message; else on to next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#gemmFn" :text "kernels.c bGemm: C (m x n) = A (m x k) times B (k x n), row-major, zeroed then accumulated over i, p, j.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#helperExterns" :text "The helpers arrayRoute defines in the emitted text in place of their declarations.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#arrExterns" :text "The externs the arrays functions call; those parallel.asl also declares carry its signatures (gcWillAllocate's void return read as an unused i64).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#helperDefinitions" :text "Each helper declaration the emitter writes for helperExterns, with the definition that replaces it: aslArrWord0 and aslArrWord1 extractvalue a %Val's words, aslArrMakeVal builds one, aslArrAlloc calls asl_alloc, aslArrLoadF64 and aslArrStoreF64 address a double element, aslArrFabs and aslArrMulAdd are llvm.fabs and llvm.fmuladd, aslArrRaise is rtError's rterr.raise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#arrFunctions" :text "Every arrays function, pool mapping each of arrStrings to its pool index: tagName, new<kind> for each kind, the 27 array builtins and the 3 kernels.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/arrays.asl#tagInt" :text "tag numbers follow the value.h Tag enum, object types its O_ constants")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#" :text "LLVM IR backend emitter consuming verified asl-ir and emitting typed SSA textual IR (.ll)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#llvmPreamble" :text "Emits target triple, runtime struct types, and string constants for LLVM IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmOperand" :text "Formats an operand identifier or literal for LLVM instruction arguments.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmExpr" :text "Emits LLVM instructions for evaluating an IR expression.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmStmt" :text "Emits LLVM instructions for an IR statement.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmBlock" :text "Emits LLVM instructions for a sequence of IR statements.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmFunction" :text "Emits an LLVM function definition from an IR function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/emit.asl#emitLlvmModule" :text "Verifies an IR module and emits full LLVM IR textual assembly.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#" :text "LLVM IR backend. emitLlvmModule and emitLlvmProgram lower a verified asl-ir SSA module (asl-target-llvm/ssa) with its unboxed array and kernel builtin calls routed through asl-target-llvm/arrayRoute to the ASL functions of asl-target-llvm/arrays (arrayRoute finishText completing the routed text), every other builtin call going through libaslrt.a's C tables, which build for any host; emitLlvmModuleFor and emitLlvmProgramFor first route its socket builtin calls (tcpListen, tcpConnect, sockAccept, sockLocalPort, unixListen, unixConnect) through asl-target-llvm/sysRoute to the ASL functions of asl-target-llvm/sysNet for a named triple's libc facts, the routed functions internal to the module, then its parMap and parFold calls through asl-target-llvm/parRoute to asl-target-llvm/parallel (parRoute finishText completing the routed text), then its array and kernel calls; emitLlvmModuleForTarget and emitLlvmProgramForTarget do so for explicit target facts, and for the libc-free wasm32 row (libc runtimeAbi) print lowers to the module's own formatter and write instead of a host import (lowerWasmPrint), while emitLlvmRuntimeForTarget (the collector) and emitLlvmSupportForTarget (asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime: allocator, C-ABI services, number formatting) give the other two objects a wasm32 program links with, none of them importing anything but runtimeAbi's host services; emitLlvmProgramNative! routes for the host it runs on when libc.asl verifies that host's triple (sysRoute routeHost!), as the asl1 build driver does, and routes the array and kernel calls on any host; emitLlvmSource lowers ASL source to LLVM IR via ssa; the remaining exports are the legacy IrModule statement emitter of asl-target-llvm/emit")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmModule" :text "Emits LLVM IR declarations and functions from an SSA module, its array and kernel builtin calls routed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmProgram" :text "Emits a complete LLVM IR program with an entry wrapper, its array and kernel builtin calls routed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmModuleFor" :text "emitLlvmModule with the socket, parMap and parFold builtin calls routed for the triple of facts, then the array and kernel calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmProgramFor" :text "emitLlvmProgram with the socket, parMap and parFold builtin calls routed for the triple of facts, then the array and kernel calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmModuleForTarget" :text "emitLlvmModuleFor with target calling conventions lowered; wasm trap facts rewrite rterr.raise to the asl.trap import. A wasm32 target, whose collector cannot scan the native stack, gets ssa's precise shadow-root frames (ssa/emitLlvmModuleWasm32).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmProgramForTarget" :text "emitLlvmProgramFor with target calling conventions lowered; wasm trap facts rewrite rterr.raise to the asl.trap import. A wasm32 target gets ssa's precise shadow-root frames (ssa/emitLlvmProgramWasm32).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmRuntimeForTarget" :text "The collector module a program for targetFacts links (asl-target-llvm/gcRoute collectorTextForTarget), for wasm32 its separate object beside the program and emitLlvmSupportForTarget's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmSupportForTarget" :text "asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime's support module for a wasm32 target whose libc row has a runtimeAbi: the linear-memory allocator, the C-ABI services the program and collector call and number formatting, importing only runtimeAbi's host services; ERR_LLVM_WASM_RUNTIME for any other target or row.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#routeForTarget" :text "routeFor, then on a libc-free row (libc runtimeAbi) lowerWasmPrint over the routed module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#lowerWasmPrint" :text "sysRoute's wasm32 routing turns each print operand into a call of a print extern taking a Val; with no libc a Val is not something a host can take, so each such call goes back to the one-operand print builtin, which the module's own formatter (asl-target-llvm/rtFormat) renders and writes through write, and the print extern goes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmProgramNative!" :text "emitLlvmProgram with the socket, parMap and parFold builtin calls routed for this host's triple when libc.asl verifies it, else unrouted, then the array and kernel calls on any host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#routeFor" :text "m routed by sysRoute, then by parRoute, for the triple of facts, then by arrayRoute.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#thenPar" :text "The routing par over the module routed holds, the internal names of both routings kept.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitRouted" :text "emit over the routed module, its routed text completed by parRoute and arrayRoute finishText, the functions routing added made internal in its text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#runtimeDecls" :text "Returns standard external runtime function declarations for LLVM.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmType" :text "Delegates to types module to emit LLVM type name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmClosure" :text "Delegates to types module to emit closure environment struct.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmPanic" :text "Delegates to types module to emit panic sequence.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmTargetTriple" :text "Delegates to types module to emit target triple directive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmBlock" :text "Delegates to emit module to emit a block of LLVM statements.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmStmt" :text "Delegates to emit module to emit an LLVM statement.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmExpr" :text "Delegates to emit module to emit an LLVM expression.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmFunction" :text "Delegates to emit module to emit an LLVM function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmSource" :text "Lowers ASL source code to SSA and emits an LLVM program. Writes src to a scratch file under asl/host/out/.emitLlvmSource (removed again before returning) and links it via asl-ir/link linkEntryBare! (LOWERPQ), so a prelude function (optionOr, pairFirst, pairSecond, listReverse, the Pair enum's pair, and any other prelude.asl declaration) and a real file-based import now resolve instead of being rejected as outside the lowered subset, while the entry module's own declarations and diagnostic loci stay unqualified, as emitLlvmSource's callers and goldens have always assumed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#emitLlvmSourceWith" :text "emitLlvmSource over asl-ir/link lowerSourceWith: the prelude functions the module reaches, transitively, are lowered from preludeSrc into the program.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/main.asl#llvmPreamble" :text "Delegates to emit module to emit LLVM target and layout preamble.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#" :text "Routes a verified SsaModule's parMap and parFold builtin calls to asl-target-llvm/parallel instead of libaslrt.a's parallel.c table (plan unit PARASL), the sysRoute pattern. routeModule rewrites each opBuiltin parMap or parFold with n operands into an opCall of parallel's wrapper for (name, n) and adds parallel's functions (internal, so every module of a program keeps its own copy), its externs (a same-named extern of another signature is ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_EXTERN), its keyTable global and the strings it reads, reusing pool strings already there; a module function already named like an added one is ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_NAME, a libc fact the triple lacks ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_FACTS. finishText completes the emitted text of a module routeModule routed (routedNames? of its internal names; the text itself is never scanned to decide, since a program may hold any of these declarations in a string literal): the declarations of parallel's five helpers become their definitions (aslParWord0 and aslParWord1 extractvalue a %Val's words, aslParMakeVal builds one with insertvalue, aslParAlloc calls asl_alloc, aslParErrorMsg returns value.c's aslErrorMsg buffer) and setjmp is declared returns_twice; a declaration it expects and does not find exactly once is ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_TEXT.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#parCalls" :text "Each distinct (builtin, operand count) of m's opBuiltin calls of parMap and parFold, in first-seen order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#routes?" :text "True when m calls parMap or parFold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#poolWith" :text "strings with each wanted string it lacks appended, and the index of every wanted string in the result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#mergeExterns" :text "own followed by each added extern it does not declare; an added extern own declares with another signature is ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_EXTERN.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#routeModule" :text "m routed for the triple of facts: unchanged, with no internal names, when it calls neither parMap nor parFold; else verified first (its own diagnostics when it does not verify) and rewritten as this module's :d describes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#routeHost!" :text "m routed for the host this runs on, as sysRoute routeHost! decides it: routeModule at sysRoute routeFactsFor of uname -s -m's triple, m unchanged when that triple has no verified libc.asl row; a failing uname is ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_HOST. uname runs only when m calls parMap or parFold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#helperDefinitions" :text "Each helper declaration the emitter writes for asl-target-llvm/parallel's helperExterns, with the text that replaces it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#routedNames?" :text "True when internal, the names a routing made internal, holds a function asl-target-llvm/parallel added: the module routeModule rewrote.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parRoute.asl#finishText" :text "res with parallel's helper declarations, whole lines the emitter wrote, replaced by their definitions when routed (routedNames? of the routing's internal names), else res unchanged whatever its text holds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#" :text "Native parMap and parFold (plan unit PARASL): SSA builders, the sys.asl and sysProc.asl pattern, for asl/host/src/parallel.c's bParMap and bParFold, so a routed program (asl-target-llvm/parRoute) links no parallel.o. Behaviour follows parallel.c: the worker count is the slots argument (hostCpuCount, sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN) or 4, when absent) capped by the element count and 256; one worker or none takes the sequential path (parMap's wraps an element's error as ERR_WORKER_TRAP 'parMap element i: <error>', parFold's lets it through); chunk k covers elements k*M/K up to (k+1)*M/K; before each fork stdio is flushed, and a failing pipe or fork, or ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK=1, reaps the workers already started and falls back to the sequential path. A worker closes the read ends it inherited, restores SIGPIPE, SIGINT and SIGTERM to SIG_DFL, catches an error through aslErrorHandlerSet and setjmp, and writes one frame to its pipe: status 0 then (parMap) the u64 element count and each result serialised, (parFold) its serialised accumulator; or status 1, a u32 length and the error text (parMap prefixed 'parMap element i: ', both cut as parallel.c cuts them). The parent polls every pipe, appending reads to a buffer bounded at 64 MiB (ERR_SERIALIZE_SIZE 'worker k response exceeds serialization size limit'), sends SIGTERM to the other workers once one reports an error or overflows, closes and reaps every worker, and raises ERR_WORKER_TRAP with the reported text, 'worker k killed by signal s' or 'worker k exited with code c'. The codec (serVal and deserVal) is parallel.c's byte for byte: tags unit 1, bool 2, int 3, float 4 (the bit pattern, so -0.0 and NaN payloads survive), keyword 5, string 6, bytes 7, list 8, ctor 9, record 10 (schema and keys by name, in the record's key order) and the F64, I64 and I8 arrays 11 to 13, little-endian lengths, a depth limit of 10000; in the parent keywords, constructor, schema and key names are re-interned (intern), a record's key-id array is shared through a per-module key table (internKeys), and arrays are rebuilt by newArray, parallel.c's mkArray (asl_alloc of an Arr, a malloc'd buffer, gcWillAllocate and gcAccount), so arrays.o is not referenced. Values are read and built through five helpers parRoute defines in the emitted text (aslParWord0, aslParWord1, aslParMakeVal: a %Val's two words; aslParAlloc: asl_alloc; aslParErrorMsg: value.c's aslErrorMsg), since asl-ir has no operation on a Val's words. Errors are raised by value.c aslError with parallel.c's codes and texts. value.h's tags and object layouts (Str, Cons, Ctor, Rec, Arr) and the wait-status encoding darwin and glibc share are written here; libc facts come from libc.asl.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#pn" :text "The module function name of a parallel helper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#wrapperName" :text "The function a routed call of builtin (parMap or parFold) with argc operands calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#serMax" :text "parallel.c SER_MAX_BYTES: a worker frame is at most 64 MiB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#depthMax" :text "parallel.c's codec depth limit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#maxFields" :text "SER_MAX_BYTES / sizeof(Val): the most fields a decoded Ctor or Rec may claim.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#jmpBufBytes" :text "Bytes reserved for a jmp_buf: above sizeof(jmp_buf) on every triple libc.asl covers (192 darwin-arm64, 200 linux-x86_64, 312 linux-aarch64); libc.asl has no jmp_buf row.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#bufBytes" :text "A SerBuf: data at 0, len at 8, cap at 16, err at 24, an 8-byte scratch word at 32 for serNum.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#k" :text "d (i64): the literal n.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ex" :text "d: a call of the extern or module function callee.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#hp" :text "d: a call of the parallel helper named helper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ld" :text "d (i64): the 8 bytes at address addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ldS32" :text "d (i64): the C int at addr plus off, sign-extended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ldU32" :text "d (i64): the uint32_t at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ldU8" :text "d (i64): the byte at addr plus off, zero-extended (rawLoadI8 zero-extends to i32).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#st" :text "Stores the i64 v at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#st32" :text "Stores v, an i64 in C int range, as the C int at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#words" :text "d.w0 and d.w1 (i64): the two words of the Val v, {tag, aux} and the payload.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#tagOf" :text "d (i64): the tag of v, the low half of its first word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#payload" :text "d (i64): the payload word of v (an Int's value, an object's address).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#mkv" :text "d (Val): the Val whose words are w0 and w1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ldVal" :text "d (Val): the Val stored at addr (a Cons car, a Ctor or Rec field).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#stVal" :text "Stores the Val v at addr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#cs" :text "d (ptr): a malloc'd C copy of the pool string text (value.c valToCStr).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#kf" :text "A fact parFacts resolved.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#chain" :text "Blocks prefix0, prefix1, ...: block i jumps to case i's label when var equals its number, else on to block i+1, the last to dflt.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#raiseB" :text "label runs pre, then raises code with the printf-style fmt over args (i64 or ptr) through value.c aslError, which never returns.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parFactNames" :text "The libc facts the parallel functions read, constants by name and struct facts as struct.field (struct.size for its size).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parFacts" :text "parFactNames resolved for the triple, or a build-time err naming the first one libc.asl lacks; also an err when pollfd's revents does not follow events by 2 bytes (collect reads both with one 32-bit load) or the triple names no errno accessor.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parStrings" :text "The pool strings the parallel functions read: error codes, aslError formats, the fallback variable and its value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#helperExterns" :text "The helpers asl-target-llvm/parRoute defines in the emitted text in place of their declarations: a Val's words, a Val from two words, asl_alloc, and value.c's aslErrorMsg buffer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parExterns" :text "The externs the parallel functions call; those sys.asl and sysProc.asl also declare carry the same signatures (void functions return i64, unused). setjmp is declared returns_twice by parRoute.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parGlobals" :text "keyTable: the address, as an Int, of an 8-byte cell holding the head of the module's interned key-array list (parallel.c's keyEntryHead), set once by keyTableInit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#errnoFn" :text "errno() -> i64: the calling thread's errno through the triple's accessor.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#cpuCountFn" :text "cpuCount() -> i64: parallel.c hostCpuCount, sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN) when at least 1, else 4.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#forcedFn" :text "forced() -> i1: ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK is set to exactly 1, parallel.c's test hook that takes the fork-failure fallback.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#countFn" :text "count(xs) -> i64: the length of the List xs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#reverseFn" :text "reverse(xs) -> Val: the List xs reversed (parallel.c reverseList).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#dropFn" :text "drop(xs, n) -> Val: xs without its first n elements.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#writeAllFn" :text "writeAll(fd, p, n) -> i64: parallel.c writeAll, write until n bytes went out, retrying on EINTR: 0, or -1 on another error.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#reapFn" :text "reap(pid, stAt) -> i64: waitpid(pid, stAt, 0), retried on EINTR; stAt 0 passes NULL. Returns waitpid's result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#killAllFn" :text "killAll(pids, rfds, n) -> i64: for the first n workers, SIGKILL, close the read end and reap, as parallel.c does before a fallback or an OOM error.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#killOthersFn" :text "killOthers(pids, n, keep) -> i64: SIGTERM to every worker but keep, once one has failed or overflowed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#serWriteFn" :text "serWrite(sb, src, n) -> i64: parallel.c serWrite, appending n bytes at src to the SerBuf sb (data, len, cap, err): err 3 past 64 MiB, err 1 when realloc fails, nothing once err is set; the capacity starts at 256 and doubles, capped at 64 MiB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#serNumFn" :text "serNum(sb, v, width) -> i64: the low width bytes of v, little-endian as parallel.c's memcpy of a native integer writes them on every covered triple, through sb's scratch word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#serNameBlocks" :text "label writes the NUL-terminated name (an address) as u32 length then bytes, err 3 when longer than UINT32_MAX, then jumps to next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#serValFn" :text "serVal(sb, v, depth) -> i64: parallel.c serVal, v appended to sb in the worker frame codec; err 2 past depth 10000, err 1 for a value of no codec tag (a closure, builtin or handle).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#deserHasFn" :text "deserHas(d, n) -> i1: parallel.c deserHas over the DeserCtx d (data, pos, len, err): n bytes remain and n is at most 64 MiB, else err 1. n is a u64 from the stream, so a negative i64 is out of range too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#deserNumFn" :text "deserNum(d, width) -> i64: parallel.c deserU8, deserU32 or deserU64 by width (1, 4, 8): the little-endian unsigned integer at pos, or 0 with err 1 when fewer than width bytes remain or err is set.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#internKeysFn" :text "internKeys(kbuf, n) -> i64: parallel.c internKeys, the address of a permanent int array equal to the n key ids at kbuf, shared by every record of that key order through the module's keyTable list (entries: next at 0, n at 8, the ids from 16); 0 when the table or a new entry cannot be allocated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#keyTableInitFn" :text "keyTableInit() -> Val: the keyTable cell's address as an Int, a zeroed 8-byte calloc; ERR_OOM when it fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#newArrayFn" :text "newArray(tag, n) -> Val: parallel.c's mkArray (arrays.c) for tag 12, 13 or 14 (F64Array, I64Array, I8Array): ERR_RANGE past MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENTS (16777216), gcWillAllocate, an Arr (asl_alloc O_ARR: len at 8, elem at 16, data at 24), a malloc'd buffer of n*elem+1 bytes (ERR_OOM when it fails) and gcAccount.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#deserStrBlocks" :text "label reads a u64 length and makes maker (mkStr or mkBytes) of that many bytes at pos, advancing pos; err or too few bytes go to fail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#deserNameBlocks" :text "label reads a u32 length and interns that many bytes at pos (value.c intern), advancing pos, and jumps to next with the id (i64); err or too few bytes go to fail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#deserValFn" :text "deserVal(d, depth) -> Val: parallel.c deserVal, the next value of the worker frame at d; on any error err is set and unit returned, the caller checking err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#childStateBytes" :text "A worker's calloc'd state: the jmp_buf, failIdx (8 bytes), its SerBuf and a 1024-byte packet (status, u32 length, at most 1019 bytes of text).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#childFn" :text "childMap(fn, init, xs, start, end, wfd) or childFold(...): a worker's whole life, never returning. It catches errors through aslErrorHandlerSet and setjmp (failIdx kept in memory, since the catch reads it after longjmp); parMap calls fn on each element of its chunk and serialises each result (ERR_SERIALIZE_SIZE or ERR_NOT_SERIALIZABLE raised as parallel.c does), parFold folds the chunk from init through fn and serialises the accumulator; it writes the frame, closes wfd, flushes stdio and _exits 0. Caught, it writes status 1, the u32 length and the text (parMap: 'parMap element i: ' and aslErrorMsg through snprintf into 1019 bytes, at most 1018 kept; parFold: aslErrorMsg, at most 1019 bytes) and _exits 1. A failing calloc of its state flushes stdio and _exits 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#seqMapFn" :text "seqMap(fn, xs) -> Val: parallel.c parMapSequential, map in order under an error handler that turns an element's error into ERR_WORKER_TRAP 'parMap element i: <error>' after restoring the previous handler; ERR_OOM when its state cannot be allocated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#seqFoldFn" :text "seqFold(fn, init, xs) -> Val: parFold's sequential path, a left fold with no error handler of its own.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#freeBufsFn" :text "freeBufs(bufs, n) -> i64: frees the data of the n SerBufs at bufs, then bufs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#freeCtlFn" :text "freeCtl(ctl) -> i64: frees the worker table workers built (K at 0, pids at 8, read ends at 16) and its arrays.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#workersFn" :text "workers(mode, fn, init, xs, M, K) -> i64: forks K workers (mode 0 parMap, 1 parFold) over chunks k*M/K .. (k+1)*M/K, each with its own pipe, flushing stdio before each fork; returns the worker table (K, pid array, read-end array), or 0 after killing and reaping the workers started when a pipe or fork fails or ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK=1, so the caller falls back to the sequential path. ERR_OOM ('parMap process tables') when the tables cannot be allocated. The child closes its read end and every earlier worker's, restores SIGPIPE, SIGINT and SIGTERM to SIG_DFL and becomes childMap or childFold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#collectFn" :text "collect(ctl, mode) -> i64: parallel.c's parent loop over the worker table ctl. It polls every read end (one pollfd per worker, from libc.asl's pollfd row), appends each read of up to 8192 bytes to that worker's SerBuf, notes the first worker whose buffer overflows 64 MiB or starts with status 1 and sends SIGTERM to the others, closes a pipe on EOF or a read error other than EINTR and EAGAIN; then finds a failed worker by buffer if none was noted, closes the remaining pipes and reaps every worker (EINTR retried), noting the first one killed by a signal or exiting nonzero when none failed. It raises ERR_SERIALIZE_SIZE for an overflow, ERR_WORKER_TRAP with the reported text (at most 1023 bytes; 'worker k reported error' when the length is 0 or past the buffer, 'worker trapped' when the text is empty), the signal or the exit code, freeing the buffers and tables first; else returns the K+1 SerBufs (the last one the caller's DeserCtx). ERR_OOM ('parMap poll buffers') after killing the workers when its buffers cannot be allocated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#kSlotsBlocks" :text "Blocks capping the worker count: workersK computes min(slots, m) then min with 256 and jumps to next with K.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#listGuardBlocks" :text "listCheck: ERR_TYPE '<who> expects List, got <tag>' (parallel.c want) unless xs is a List, then next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#ctxBlock" :text "label points the DeserCtx (the SerBuf slot after the K workers') at worker kk's buffer and jumps to next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#mapRunFn" :text "mapRun(fn, xs, slots) -> Val: bParMap after argument parsing: ERR_ARG for slots below 1, ERR_TYPE unless xs is a List, the empty list for no elements, seqMap for one worker or when workers falls back, else the workers' frames decoded in chunk order: ERR_WORKER_TRAP 'worker k sent corrupted data' for a bad status or count, 'deserialization error on worker k item i' for an undecodable result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#foldRunFn" :text "foldRun(step, combine, init, xs, slots) -> Val: bParFold after argument parsing: ERR_ARG for slots below 1, ERR_TYPE unless xs is a List, init for no elements, seqFold for one worker or when workers falls back, else each worker's accumulator decoded in chunk order ('worker k sent corrupted fold data', 'deserialization error on worker k fold accumulator') and combined left to right.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#arityFn" :text "builtin/argc for an argument count builtin does not take: parallel.c's ERR_ARITY text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#wrapperFn" :text "The function a routed call of builtin with argc operands calls: parMap/2 and parFold/4 take the host's CPU count (cpuCount) as slots; parMap/3 takes slots first when its first operand is an Int, else last when its third is, else ERR_TYPE; parFold/5 needs an Int fifth operand (ERR_TYPE 'parFold slots expects Int, got <tag>'); any other count is arityFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#parFunctions" :text "The parallel functions for the triple of facts, pool mapping each of parStrings to its pool index, with one wrapper per (builtin, argc) of calls; or parFacts' build-time err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#tagInt" :text "tag numbers follow the value.h Tag enum")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/parallel.asl#objRec" :text "object types follow the value.h O_ constants")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#" :text "LLVM text helpers for native error paths (ABIVAL-2): one raise writing asl-host's error line to fd 2 and exiting 1, the integer, type and match traps, main's Result to an exit code, the trap builtin and assert/refute with their counts and ASL_ASSERT_REPORT report. Emitted into each native module with internal linkage, except the two counters, weak so separately emitted modules share one pair. Every message keeps value.c aslError's layout, CODE: message truncated to 4095 bytes, and its abi.c/prelude.c text. Native code may run under an error handler (a routed parMap worker installs one through aslErrorHandlerSet): the raise then writes its line into asl-target-llvm/rtValue's message buffer and longjmps to the handler, as value.c aslError did, so no raise calls into the runtime (ABIVAL-5). rtErrorDefinitions closes over rtValue's pieces too, the intern table and value.c's entry points among them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorDecls" :text "External functions the helpers call; the caller adds each one its module does not already declare. longjmp delivers a raise to an installed handler.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#wasmTrapImport" :text "The wasm32 host trap import: message lengths use the target's i32 size_t.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#wasmRaiseFunction" :text "The wasm raise endpoint forwards the error code and message bytes to the host trap, which does not return.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#cText" :text "A private NUL-terminated constant of text, which holds only printable ASCII without a quote or backslash.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorTrapCodes" :text "The codes (trap code msg) accepts: prelude.c knownErrCodes less trapBlockedCode's ERR_PROBE, ERR_OOM and ERR_INTERNAL.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#tagNames" :text "value.c tagName, indexed by Tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#coreMessages" :text "Fixed message and format texts of the core raises, by constant suffix.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#valueMessages" :text "Fixed message and format texts of the value helpers, by constant suffix.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#reportText" :text "abi.c assertReport's line before its newline.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#raiseFixed" :text "Raises code with the fixed message key, then unreachable.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#coreCodes" :text "The codes the core raises use; the value helpers add the rest of the trap vocabulary.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorCoreLlvm" :text "The raise and the traps compiled code branches to, needing libc only; the raise first reads rtValue's handler cell and, under a handler, formats its line into rtValue's message buffer and longjmps there.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorValueLlvm" :text "Helpers over Vals: a non-exhaustive match naming its scrutinee as the VM does, main's Result to an exit code, the trap builtin, assert and refute with their counters, and the ASL_ASSERT_REPORT report. They render with rtFormat's asl_rt_format_val (valToCStrShort's depth limit 8) and intern ok through value.c intern, so the caller adds rtFormat's helpers and rtErrorCoreLlvm with them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#PieceScan.done" :text "Pieces closed so far, name and text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#PieceScan.name" :text "Name of the function being read, empty between definitions")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#PieceScan.body" :text "Lines of that function so far")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#pieceName" :text "The symbol a definition line introduces: @x of '@x = ...' or of 'define ... @x(...'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#piecesOf" :text "Splits helper lines into one piece per global or function, by the symbol it defines; blank lines between them are dropped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refersTo?" :text "text names name followed by a delimiter; one scan for name alone first, as most pieces are absent.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#tailOf" :text "text's last 256 bytes, so a name the scanned text ends with still meets the delimiter the next round's join adds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#closeOver" :text "The pieces text reaches, directly or through each other; each round scans only the text the previous round added, behind the tail of the text before it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorDefinitions" :text "The helpers text reaches, directly or through other helpers, rtValue's among them, in their declaration order, each a blank-line-led definition: a program carries only the raises, value runtime pieces and constants it can use.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#" :text "LLVM text helpers for native scalar formatting. These are private implementation functions emitted into each native module; names are kept behind one symbol-name builder so the runtime intern table can be retargeted independently.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatNameCall" :text "One indirection for runtime interned symbol/keyword names: asl-target-llvm/rtValue's native table (ABIVAL-5).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatDecls" :text "External functions the formatter helpers call. The caller adds each one its module does not already declare, since a module's own externs (libc, sys) may declare the same C symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatLlvm" :text "Generic native helpers for integer and float formatting/parsing. The caller appends these once per emitted module, with rtFormatDecls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatValueLlvm" :text "A recursive native renderer over the public Val layout. Object fields are read with byte offsets matching value.h; no value.c printer is called.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatValLlvm" :text "Exports the one private recursive value-rendering entry point used for str and output builtins.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatManyLlvm" :text "Formats the argument vector used by str/print/println/eprintln. Mode 0 is str, 1 is print, 2 println and 3 eprintln; stdout/stderr routing remains the caller's responsibility.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#rtFormatTerminalLlvm" :text "Val-facing parse and output adapters for the generic raw helpers. Construction of Option uses the existing runtime constructor allocator; output uses a complete low-level write loop.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#" :text "LLVM text helpers for records, variants, closures, strings, keywords and symbols over boxed Vals (ABIVAL-4), with abi.c's former semantics and texts (asl_rt_field, asl_rt_variant_field, asl_rt_closure_capture, asl_rt_call_closure, asl_rt_str, asl_rt_keyword, asl_rt_symbol), so native code reaches no abi.c entry for them. Objects keep asl/host/src/value.h's layout (Str len at 8 and bytes at 16; Rec n at 12, keys at 16, values at 24; Ctor id at 8, n at 12, fields at 16; Closure Proto at 8, n at 16, captures at 24; Proto name at 0, nparams at 16, native at 56). A name's interned id comes from value.c intern once per module and cell (objrt.nameId; value.c keeps the single table while a VM can share the process, ABIVAL-5 replaces it). A string constant is built once by asl_alloc into its module cell and rooted there with asl_rt_global_root (objrt.str). A call of a closure whose code is native checks its arity and calls the code directly; a partial application splices its operands (at most 64, vm.c vmCall's limit) and calls its head; a closure without native code fails ERR_INTERNAL, no evaluator being linked (NX4); any other value, a builtin value included, fails with vm.c's ERR_TYPE text. aslCall, the call libaslhost.a's C builtins make, is objrt.call in IR. Every failure raises through rtError with abi.c's code and text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#objText" :text "A private NUL-terminated constant of text, which holds only printable ASCII without a quote or backslash.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#objConstants" :text "The message texts by symbol, the partial keyword's name and its module id cell.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#formatted" :text "Lines raising code with the message snprintf builds from format and args (each ', <type> <value>') into a 4096-byte buffer, as aslError formats and truncates, then unreachable; p prefixes the names they bind.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#tagOf" :text "Binds %tag, the Tag of the Val v, and %obj, its payload as a pointer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#nameIdFunction" :text "The interned id of the name of len bytes, read from its module cell (-1 until resolved) or obtained once from asl-target-llvm/rtValue's intern table and kept there.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#strFunction" :text "The String Val of a constant's len bytes, built once into its module cell (tag 0 until built): a Str from asl_alloc(O_STR 0, 16+len+1) holding len, the bytes and a NUL, stored in the cell and rooted there through asl_rt_global_root; a length past INT32_MAX fails with abi.c's ERR_LIMIT text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#fieldFunction" :text "Record v's field of the name of len bytes (id cell cell), searched by interned key as abi.c asl_rt_field did: a non-record fails with ERR_TYPE '.-<field> expects a record, got <tag>', a record without the key with ERR_FIELD 'record has no field <field>'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#variantFieldFunction" :text "Field i of variant v as abi.c asl_rt_variant_field read it: a non-variant fails with ERR_TYPE 'variant field <i> of a <tag>', an index outside the Ctor's fields with ERR_RANGE 'variant <name> has <n> field(s), no field <i>', the name from value.c symName.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#patternArityFunction" :text "A switch arm naming variant name, declared with want fields, met a same-named Ctor of n fields: vm.c OP_TESTCTOR's ERR_ARITY 'pattern (<name>) binds <want> field(s), value has <n>'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#captureFunction" :text "Capture i of closure environment env as abi.c asl_rt_closure_capture read it: a non-function fails with ERR_TYPE 'closure environment is a <tag>', an index outside the captures with ERR_RANGE 'capture <i> outside the <n> captured value(s)'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#callFunction" :text "Calls function value fn with argc arguments at argv. A closure (Fn) whose Proto has native code: argc must equal its nparams, else ERR_ARITY '<name> expects <n> argument(s), got <argc>', then its code is called with the closure as environment. A partial application (a Ctor whose id is the interned 'partial', head first): its bound operands then the arguments, at most 64 or ERR_LIMIT as vm.c vmCall, go to its head. A closure without native code: ERR_INTERNAL '<name> is bytecode, which a native binary cannot run', since no evaluator is linked. Anything else, a builtin value included: ERR_TYPE 'cannot call a <tag>'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#aslCallFunction" :text "aslCall, the call of a function value the C builtins of libaslhost.a (parallel.c, arrays.c) make where a native program links them: objrt.call over argc arguments at argv. External, so the program's entry module carries one definition (asl-target-llvm/ssa valueExports) and it replaces vm.c's weak one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#symbolFunction" :text "A symbol constant: the host value model has none, so it fails with abi.c asl_rt_symbol's ERR_UNSUPPORTED text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#rtObjectPieces" :text "Constants then helpers, each by the symbol it defines, for the caller's reference closure (asl-target-llvm/ssa mathDefinitions).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl#rtObjectDecls" :text "The LLVM function the helpers call beyond rtError's and runtimeDecls' (asl_alloc, asl_rt_global_root): llvm.memcpy; the caller keeps one declaration per symbol. Names intern through asl-target-llvm/rtValue's table, which rtError's closure carries.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#" :text "LLVM text helpers for the generic operators over boxed Vals (ABIVAL-3): + - * / mod, < <= > >=, = and !=, not and unary minus, with vm.c's semantics and texts (asl/host/src/ops.h binop, cmpVals, typeErr2 and overflow; vm.c OP_NEG and OP_NOT; value.c valEq), so native code reaches no abi.c entry for them. Int with Int is exact or ERR_INT_OVERFLOW, / and mod floor toward negative infinity, a zero divisor is ERR_DIV_ZERO and INT64_MIN / -1 overflows while mod -1 is 0; Float with Float is IEEE, mod taking the divisor's sign (fmod moved, a zero result signed as the divisor); Int and Float never mix: any other pair of an arithmetic operator is ERR_TYPE '<op> expects two Int or two Float, got <a> and <b>'. An ordering compares two Ints, two Floats (NaN unordered), two Strings bytewise then by length, or two Keywords by name (value.c symName, strcmp), else the same ERR_TYPE text. = and != compare two Ints or two Floats directly (NaN differs from itself, -0.0 equals 0.0), else structurally as valEq does: unequal tags are ERR_TYPE '= compares <a> with <b>', Unit always equal, Bool, Int, closures, builtins, arrays and handles by payload, Keywords by id, Strings and Bytes by length and bytes, lists cell by cell in order, variants by constructor id, field count and fields in order, records by schema, field count and every field of the left one found by key in the right one; every nested comparison is one level deeper and a comparison entered at depth 10000 (value.c MAX_DATA_DEPTH) is ERR_DEPTH '= on values nested deeper than 10000'. Every helper has internal linkage and is emitted once per module, only when referenced (asl-target-llvm/ssa mathDefinitions); raises go through asl-target-llvm/rtError (rterr.int, rterr.raise, rterr.raiseText, rterr.tagName).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsSymbols" :text "Each operator with the suffix of its helper and constant names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsEntry?" :text "Builtin entries (asl-ir/types builtinEntries) whose opEntry is one call of an @opsrt helper: the eleven binary operators and not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsEntrySym" :text "The helper an opsEntry? operator calls, @opsrt.<suffix>; empty for any other name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsBuiltin?" :text "An opBuiltin of an operator or not, any operand count, which runs natively (opsBuiltinCall) where abi.c's asl_rt_builtin K_OP and K_NOT arms ran it: the lowering leaves only unary minus to a by-name call (asl-ir/lower folds + and * over more operands into binary entries and rejects other counts), while SSA built by hand may name any operator.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsBuiltinCall" :text "The IR of an opsBuiltin? call binding lhs ('  %d = '), with p ('%d') prefixing its temporaries and args the formatted operand Vals, as asl_rt_builtin's K_OP and K_NOT arms ran it: unary minus is @opsrt.neg; not of one operand is @opsrt.not; + and * fold any count from two left to right; any other operator of two operands calls its helper, a Bool result boxed as T_BOOL; every other count raises their ERR_ARITY text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsText" :text "A private NUL-terminated constant of text, which holds only printable ASCII without a quote or backslash.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsConstants" :text "The operator names typeErr2 prints and the message texts, by symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#operands" :text "Binds the tag (%a.tag, %b.tag), whole tag word (%a.tagw, %b.tagw) and payload (%a.bits, %b.bits) of the Vals %a and %b, and whether both are Ints (%ints) or both Floats (%floats).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#trapInt" :text "rterr.int with abi.c's integer trap kind: 0 '+', 1 '-', 2 '*', 3 '/' leaving int64, 5 division and 6 mod by zero.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#typeErr2" :text "The other block of an arithmetic helper or an ordering's cmp: typeErr2's ERR_TYPE for the operator.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#overflowArith" :text "+, - and * over two Vals: the Int result of the overflow intrinsic or rterr.int kind, the Float result of floatOp, else typeErr2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#divFunction" :text "/ over two Vals: Int floor division (ERR_DIV_ZERO for 0, INT64_MIN / -1 overflows as '/'), Float fdiv, else typeErr2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#modFunction" :text "mod over two Vals: Int floor mod, the sign of the divisor (ERR_DIV_ZERO for 0, exactly 0 for -1), Float fmod moved to the divisor's sign with a zero result signed as the divisor, else typeErr2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#ordering" :text "An ordering over two Vals: icmp intCmp on two Ints, fcmp floatCmp on two Floats (false when either is NaN), else the sign of @opsrt.cmp against zero.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#cmpFunction" :text "cmpVals past its Int and Float cases: two Strings by memcmp over the shorter length, then the shorter first; two Keywords by strcmp of their names (symName of the id in the Val's aux half); any other pair is typeErr2 naming who.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#equality" :text "= (negate false) or != (negate true) over two Vals: icmp intCmp on two Ints, fcmp floatCmp on two Floats, else @opsrt.valEq from depth 0, negated for !=.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#objOf" :text "Binds %<v>.obj to the object pointer of the Val %<v> from its payload %<v>.bits.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#fieldAt" :text "Loads the ty at byte offset off of %<v>.obj into %<into>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#valEqFunction" :text "value.c valEq at depth: ERR_DEPTH when depth has reached 10000, ERR_TYPE for unequal tags, else valEqInner by tag; nested comparisons run at depth + 1, in valEqInner's order, so the first difference or error is the host's. No allocation happens, so the operands need no rooting.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#formatTwoTags" :text "A noreturn helper raising ERR_TYPE with format over value.c tagName of two tags, after the operator name who when withWho.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#unaryFunction" :text "A one-operand helper: body runs when the Val %v's tag is wantTag (binding %v.tag, %v.bits), anything else raises ERR_TYPE with message and the tag's name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#opsFunctions" :text "The helpers by symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#rtOpsPieces" :text "Constants then helpers, each by the symbol it defines, for the caller's reference closure (asl-target-llvm/ssa mathDefinitions).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtOps.asl#rtOpsDecls" :text "The libc, runtime and LLVM functions the helpers call beyond rtError's: memcmp for Strings and Bytes, strcmp over asl-target-llvm/rtValue symName for Keyword order, llvm.copysign.f64 for Float mod and the overflow intrinsics; the caller keeps one declaration per symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#" :text "LLVM text for the value runtime native code used to reach in value.c (ABIVAL-5), so libaslrt.a carries neither value.o nor float.o. (1) The intern table: an open-addressing table of i32 slots (id + 1, 0 empty) over a name array of {ptr text, i64 length} records, FNV-1a hashed, grown at half load, in weak module globals every separately emitted module shares. valrt.intern and valrt.symName are what native code calls; they go through the weak aslInternShared and aslSymNameShared, which value.c defines strongly, so a program that links libaslhost.a has one table, value.c's, for native code and the C builtins alike. (2) valrt.str builds a String from bytes and valrt.args main's argument list (argv[1..] as List String), replacing abi.c asl_rt_args. (3) The raise handler cell and message buffer, reached through the weak aslHandlerSlot and aslErrorText (valrt.handler and valrt.errorMsg, or value.c's own where libaslhost.a is linked): rtError's raise copies its line into the buffer and longjmps to the handler a parMap worker installed, routed or in parallel.c, else reports and exits. (4) Internal definitions under value.c's names (intern, symName, mkStr, valToCStr, valToCStrN, aslError, aslErrorHandlerGet, aslErrorHandlerSet) for the routed sys, process, socket and parallel code that declares those C externs; aslError is variadic and hands its va_list to vsnprintf as the target passes one, a pointer value where va_start writes only that pointer (darwin arm64, wasm32) and the va_list's address where it fills a larger record (SysV x86_64, AAPCS64 Linux), told apart by a marker word va_start leaves untouched only in the first case. (5) Weak C definitions of KW_SOME..KW_PARTIAL (set by abi.c asl_rt_init from aslInternShared), tagName, mkCtor and aslInternShared for the C floor left in libaslrt.a (strFloor.c's string primitives, abi.c's asl_rt_init); a program that also links libaslhost.a takes value.c's strong ones where value.c has them. Object layouts and tags follow asl/host/src/value.h (Str len at 8, bytes at 16; Cons car at 8, cdr at 24; Ctor id at 8, count at 12, fields at 16; asl_alloc types O_STR 0, O_CONS 1, O_CTOR 3).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#valText" :text "A private NUL-terminated constant of text, which holds only printable ASCII without a quote or backslash.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#tagNames" :text "value.c tagName, indexed by Tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#vaMarker" :text "The word stored after a va_list's first pointer before va_start: no stack address, so still there afterwards only where va_start writes the pointer alone.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#storage" :text "The table and the raise state, weak so every module of a program shares one copy.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#hashFunction" :text "value.c hashStr: 64-bit FNV-1a over n bytes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#placeFunction" :text "Stores id + 1 in the first free slot of slots (mask + 1 of them, a power of two) from the hash of names[id]; the caller grows slots first, so a free one exists.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#growFunction" :text "Replaces the slots with capacity zeroed ones holding every interned id again; a failed calloc exits 70, as value.c intern does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#addFunction" :text "Interns a name not yet present: copies its bytes NUL-terminated, appends the record (the name array doubling from 1024), marks slotp and returns the new id; an id past INT32_MAX - 1 or a failed allocation exits 70, as value.c intern does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#findFunction" :text "The id of the name of length bytes at text, added when absent; the slots double (from 1024) first once the table is half full.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#internFunction" :text "value.c intern: the id of a name, the same for the same bytes within a process. aslInternShared is weak over the native table; value.c's strong one, in a program that links libaslhost.a, puts native code on value.c's table, the one the C builtins there intern into.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#symNameFunction" :text "value.c symName: the NUL-terminated name of id, '?' for an id never interned; weak as aslInternShared is, so it reads the table that interned the id.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#raiseStateFunctions" :text "The raise handler cell and message buffer, weak over valrt.handler and valrt.errorMsg; value.c's strong ones, in a program that links libaslhost.a, return its own, so a native raise and value.c's aslError longjmp to whichever handler a parMap worker installed and leave their line where it reads it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#failBody" :text "value.c aslError over its varargs: the formatted message raised under code through rtError's raise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#strFunction" :text "value.c mkStr: a String of length bytes copied from text and NUL-terminated, from asl_alloc(O_STR, 16 + length + 1).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#argsFunction" :text "abi.c asl_rt_args: argv[1..argc-1] as a List of Strings, built from the last argument back; argc of 1 or less is the empty list. The collector scans the native stack conservatively, so the list so far stays live across each allocation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#shimHeaders" :text "Each value.c name the routed sys, process, socket and parallel code calls with the first line of its internal definition here, the C signature those externs declare (void returns as i64).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#valueShimNames" :text "The value.c function names this module defines in IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#shimFunctions" :text "The value.c entry points over the native pieces; valToCStrN renders as value.c's valToCStrN does (rtFormat's renderer, no depth limit) into a malloc'd NUL-terminated text the caller frees, its length stored at lengthp.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#kwGlobals" :text "value.h's KW_* for the C floor, which abi.c asl_rt_init sets from aslInternShared before any other intern; value.c's strong definitions replace them in a program that links libaslhost.a, set there the same way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#rtValueLlvm" :text "Every global and function above as definition lines, for rtError's piece closure: a module carries only those its text reaches.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#rtValueExportRoots" :text "Text naming the C definitions the C floor in libaslrt.a calls (strFloor.c bStringSlice and the string primitives' messages, abi.c asl_rt_init): an entry module that links the runtime closes over it so the link finds them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#rtValueDecls" :text "The libc and LLVM functions the pieces call beyond rtError's and rtFormat's; asl_alloc comes from ssa runtimeDecls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtValue.asl#rtValueDefines?" :text "True when text holds this module's definition of the value.c function name, so the module declares no extern of that name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#int64Const" :text "A raw i64 literal instruction.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#int32Const" :text "A raw i32 literal instruction, for a native extern's int-sized argument.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#callInstr" :text "A direct call instruction (module function or extern, by checkCall's lookup) at the given result type.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#entryInstr" :text "A direct runtime-entry call (bytesGet, stringToBytes, stringLength, ...), typed by builtinEntry.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#primInstr" :text "A raw primitive instruction (addInt, mulInt, ltInt, neInt, ...), typed by primSignature.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#boxInstr" :text "Boxes a raw i64 value into Val (opBox is restricted to i64, f64 and i1, which is all this module ever boxes).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#listInstr" :text "A Val list literal from Val operands (used by sysClockGettimeFn to pair tv_sec and tv_nsec with no extra schema).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#constructResult" :text "An (ok field) or (err field) value of the Result type resultTypeDecl declares.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#block" :text "An SsaBlock with no block-local parameters, used throughout this module's hand-built errnoResultFn-style control flow.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#edgeTo" :text "An SsaEdge to label with no carried arguments, used by errnoResultFn's err/ok branch terminators.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#resultTypeDecl" :text "The ok/err ADT exactly as asl-ir/lower declares it for ASL source using Result, so a caller's module can both run these functions and pattern-match their results as ordinary ASL Result values.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#optionTypeDecl" :text "The some/none ADT exactly as asl-ir/lower declares it for ASL source using Option, so a caller's module can both run sysGetenv and pattern-match its result as an ordinary ASL Option value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#freeExtern" :text "free is void; declared returning i64 since SsaTy has no void and the result is always discarded (never read, never branched on), which is safe regardless of what a void return leaves in the result register.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#valToCStrExtern" :text "asl/host/src/value.c valToCStr(Val, int repr): repr 0 is the raw print form, which for a T_STR Val copies its exact bytes with no quoting (render's T_STR/!repr arm) -- the Val->ptr half of this module's String marshalling, mirroring mkBytes' ptr->Val half.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#mkBytesExtern" :text "asl/host/src/prelude.c mkBytes(const uint8_t*, size_t) -> Val Bytes: copies the given native buffer into a fresh, GC-managed Bytes value (the M5 Arr layout is the C function's business, not this module's; no pointer is ever extracted out of a boxed Bytes value here), used to read back an out-pointer (errno's int, clock_gettime's timespec, readlink's resolved path) a byte at a time with bytesGet, or as a function's own documented Bytes result (sysReadlinkFn). Declared under its own name, distinct from asl_rt_str (ptr+len -> Val String, T_STR, a different tag -- see mkStrExtern): asl_rt_str is reachable only through emitLlvmProgram's own opConst(constStr) path, never a legal opCall target (asl-ir/verify's checkCall requires every opCall callee to be a module function or a declared extern, and declaring it here would double its `declare` line against ssa.asl's own unconditional runtimeDecls emission, which clang rejects as a redefinition).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#mkStrExtern" :text "asl/host/src/value.c mkStr(const char*, size_t) -> Val String (T_STR), the real ptr+len -> String constructor cstrFieldBlocks needs (stringConcat and friends reject a Bytes value, T_BYTES, with ERR_TYPE): not asl_rt_str, which does the identical job by tag but is reachable only through opConst(constStr) and is never a legal opCall target, for the same reason mkBytesExtern's own :d gives for mkBytes vs asl_rt_str.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#errnoAccessorExtern" :text "The triple's errno accessor (__error on darwin, __errno_location on linux), taking no arguments and returning a pointer to the thread's errno int.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysCommonExterns" :text "The externs every sys* function in this module, directly or through sysErrnoValue, may call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#decodeLittleEndianBytes" :text "Instructions decoding the n bytes of the Bytes value bytesVal at [offset, offset+n) into one raw i64, least-significant byte first; returns them with the final accumulator's name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysErrnoValueFn" :text "The current thread's errno as a raw i64, read through the triple's accessor and decoded from its 4 raw bytes (a C int).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#errnoResultFn" :text "A function named `name`, taking `params`, that runs preInstrs, then calls `callee`(callArgs) at its real C return type (nativeRetTy): tyI64 for a genuinely i64/ssize_t-returning syscall, called straight into call.n, or tyI32 for the 0-success/-1-error int trick, called into call.raw and widened (rawWidenI32, sign-extending, round 2's fix for the declared-i64-for-an-int-return gap) into call.n so int's full negative range still compares right; call.n is checked with checkPrim (\"ltInt\" for i64/ssize_t, \"neInt\" for the i32 trick) against zero, and on a true result (the error branch) reads errno (sysErrnoValue) before errPre runs, since errPre is the caller's cleanup (typically free on a scratch buffer or a marshalled string) and free itself is a libc call free to clobber errno if it ran first; on false (the ok branch) runs okPre then returns (ok okValue). allocCheck, when some(ptrName), is a tyPtr value preInstrs already bound (a malloc result): the call only happens once rawPtrIsNull(ptrName) is false, with a null taking the same err branch (free(NULL) in errPre is a no-op, and a failed malloc leaves errno set by the allocator, so sysErrnoValue there is the right thing to read too) -- round 2's fix for the other declared-i64 gap, now that rawPtrIsNull exists.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#stringToPtrInstrs" :text "valToCStr(v, 0): a fresh, caller-owned copy of v's raw bytes; the caller must free dest exactly once.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#atLeastOneBlocks" :text "Three blocks computing max(sizeParam,1) into joinLabel's own first block parameter (plan S3b): pre runs once in the first block (sysReadlink's valToCStr, for instance), ahead of the zero check. A legitimate zero-length request still allocates 1 byte, so malloc's implementation-defined NULL-on-malloc(0) return is never mistaken for a real allocation failure (which would otherwise read and report a stale or zero errno as a bogus error) by the NULL check joinLabel's own block runs next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysGetpidFn" :text "sysGetpid() -> Int32: the raw getpid() result, with no errno path since getpid cannot fail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysReadFn" :text "sysRead(fd, max) -> Result Bytes Int64: reads at most max bytes into a scratch buffer malloc'd at max(max,1) -- never malloc(0), see atLeastOneBlocks's :d -- NULL-checked (rawPtrIsNull), wraps a successful read in a fresh Bytes value (mkBytes) and frees the scratch buffer either way. read itself still runs with the caller's real (possibly zero) max, only the allocation is bumped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysWriteFn" :text "sysWrite(fd, data) -> Result Int64 Int64: writes data (a String) through a valToCStr copy, freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#closeExtern" :text "close is int, declared at its real i32 return (round 2's fix for the declared-i64 gap, now that rawWidenI32 exists): errnoResultFn calls it at tyI32 and widens for the 0/-1 check.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysCloseFn" :text "sysClose(fd) -> Result Int64 Int64: close via the 0/-1 convention, no cleanup on either path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysPreadFn" :text "Like sysRead, at a given offset, and never malloc(0) for the same reason (atLeastOneBlocks).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysPwriteFn" :text "sysPwrite(fd, data, offset) -> Result Int64 Int64: like sysWrite but at a given offset, via a valToCStr copy of data freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysKillFn" :text "sysKill(pid, sig) -> Result Int64 Int64: kill via the 0/-1 convention, no cleanup on either path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysFsyncFn" :text "sysFsync(fd) -> Result Int64 Int64: fsync via the 0/-1 convention, no cleanup on either path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysFlockFn" :text "sysFlock(fd, op) -> Result Int64 Int64: flock via the 0/-1 convention, no cleanup on either path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysRenameFn" :text "sysRename(oldPath, newPath) -> Result Int64 Int64: rename via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling both path Strings through valToCStr copies freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysChmodFn" :text "sysChmod(path, mode) -> Result Int64 Int64: chmod via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling path through a valToCStr copy freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysMkdirFn" :text "sysMkdir(path, mode) -> Result Int64 Int64: mkdir via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling path through a valToCStr copy freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysUnlinkFn" :text "sysUnlink(path) -> Result Int64 Int64: unlink via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling path through a valToCStr copy freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysRmdirFn" :text "sysRmdir(path) -> Result Int64 Int64: rmdir via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling path through a valToCStr copy freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysSymlinkFn" :text "sysSymlink(target, linkPath) -> Result Int64 Int64: symlink via the 0/-1 convention, marshalling both Strings through valToCStr copies freed either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysReadlinkFn" :text "sysReadlink(path, max) -> Result Bytes Int64: the resolved target, as Bytes (mkBytes), not String (see mkBytesExtern's :d for why this reuses mkBytes rather than redeclaring asl_rt_str); its scratch buffer is malloc'd at max(max,1) (atLeastOneBlocks, same reasoning as sysRead) and NULL-checked. valToCStr(path) runs once in the shared size-check block, ahead of the zero branch, since p dominates both the entry join and the err/ok blocks either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#realpathExtern" :text "C's char *realpath(const char *path, char *resolved_path): called here with resolved_path NULL (POSIX.1-2008's dynamic-allocation overload, built via rawIntToPtr 0, plan S6 round 3's new prim -- not a second malloc'd buffer standing in for NULL, as sysNanosleepFn's rem argument no longer needs either). On success returns a malloc'd buffer the caller owns and must free; on failure returns NULL with errno set (ENOENT on a missing path component, ELOOP, EACCES, ENAMETOOLONG, ...). This overload needs no PATH_MAX-sized buffer of its own -- libc.asl's PATH_MAX fact (round LIBC-pathMaxIntToPtr) documents the size libc itself still allocates internally and is probe-verified so a future fixed-buffer caller never guesses it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysRealpathFn" :text "sysRealpath(path) -> Result (Val String) Int64: calls realpath(path, NULL) (the dynamic-allocation overload; see realpathExtern's :d), which returns a malloc'd resolved-path buffer on success or NULL with errno set on failure. On success, copies the buffer into a fresh Val String (strlen then mkStr) and frees the buffer; frees the path's own valToCStr copy either way. The err arm is the raw errno as an Int64, this module's Result convention throughout (sysErrnoValue), unlike the asl-host VM's own realPath builtin, which returns a Result String String (ioErr's formatted message) on failure -- a caller comparing the two (sysDirectTest's testRealpath, on the ok path only) must not expect the same shape on err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#nsGetExecutablePathExtern" :text "dyld's int _NSGetExecutablePath(char *buf, uint32_t *bufsize) (mach-o/dyld.h), darwin only: 0 with buf holding the exe path, -1 with *bufsize set to the size needed when buf is too small; it sets no errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#exePathExterns" :text "The externs sysExePathFn adds beyond sysCommonExterns, realpath and strlen: _NSGetExecutablePath where the triple names the exe through dyld, none elsewhere.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#cStringStoreInstrs" :text "rawStoreI8 of each byte of text, then a NUL, into ptrName at offsets 0..len: a literal C string built inside a malloc'd buffer, since a builder here cannot add to its caller's string pool.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#errnoReturnBlock" :text "Reads errno first (sysErrnoValue), then runs pre (cleanup frees, which may clobber errno), then returns (err errno).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#exePathFillBlocks" :text "The fill block (and its error exits) that leaves the running exe's path as a C string in buf and jumps to resolve: dyld's _NSGetExecutablePath into buf with a malloc'd uint32 size of PATH_MAX (rc -1 means the path is longer than PATH_MAX, reported as ERANGE since dyld sets no errno), or the literal /proc/self/exe, which realpath then follows.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysExePathFn" :text "sysExePath() -> Result (Val String) Int64, the native twin of asl-host's procExePath builtin (asl/host/src/sys.c bProcExePath over loader.c hostGetExecutablePath, then realpath): a PATH_MAX buffer receives the running exe's path by the triple's libc/exePathSource (darwin _NSGetExecutablePath, linux the /proc/self/exe link), then realpath(buf, NULL) resolves it and the result is copied into a Val String (strlen, mkStr) with every buffer freed. Errs at build time when libc.asl lacks PATH_MAX or ERANGE for the triple or names no exe source for it; at run time the err arm is the raw errno (ERANGE for a path longer than PATH_MAX on darwin), this module's Result convention, unlike the VM builtin's String.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysSysconfFn" :text "sysSysconf(name) -> Result Int64 Int64: sysconf, whose genuinely i64 return can be negative on success, so checked with ltInt against zero rather than the 0/-1 neInt trick.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysClockGettimeFn" :text "sysClockGettime(clockId) -> Result (List Int64 Int64) Int64: fills a malloc'd struct timespec, sized and offset by libc.asl's own timespec row for this triple (structByteSize/structOffset, never a hardcoded 16/0/8), NULL-checked like sysRead's; reads it back through mkBytes (as sysErrnoValueFn reads errno; see mkBytesExtern's :d for why this reuses mkBytes rather than redeclaring asl_rt_str) and decodes tv_sec and tv_nsec at their real offsets; the ok payload is (list secondsVal nanosVal), a plain Val list needing no extra schema.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysUsleepFn" :text "sysUsleep(micros) -> Result Int64 Int64: usleep via the 0/-1 convention; replaces nanosleep since this module cannot build the latter's timespec input struct (module :d).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#strlenExtern" :text "C strlen(ptr) -> i64: used only to size a copy of getenv's result. Not in libc.asl because its signature never varies by triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysGetenvFn" :text "sysGetenv(name) -> Option Bytes: (none) when the variable is unset, getenv's own NULL convention -- not an error, no errno path. On a hit, copies the environment's string (strlen then mkBytes) into a fresh, GC-managed Bytes value before returning, since the pointer getenv hands back is owned by the process environment and must never be freed or held past this call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fcntlExtern" :text "C's variadic int fcntl(int fd, int cmd, ...): the fixed (fd, cmd) pair plus a variadic int slot, enough for F_GETFL (sysFcntlGet calls it with 2 arguments, the slot unused -- a variadic callee reads only what its own cmd handling needs) and F_SETFL (sysFcntlSet calls it with the slot carrying the new flags). F_GETFL, F_SETFL and O_NONBLOCK are already in libc/libcConst; this module never bakes them in, callers supply them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysFcntlGetFn" :text "sysFcntlGet(fd, cmd) -> Result Int64 Int64: fcntl(fd, cmd) with no further argument (F_GETFL's shape). Checked with ltInt rather than the 0/-1 convention: F_GETFL's success return is the flags word itself, a legitimate 0 (O_RDONLY with no other bit set), so only a strictly negative result is -1-style failure.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysFcntlSetFn" :text "sysFcntlSet(fd, cmd, arg) -> Result Int64 Int64: fcntl(fd, cmd, arg) through fcntl's variadic slot (F_SETFL's shape, cmd and arg both caller-supplied, so this same function also serves any other single-int-argument fcntl command). Checked with ltInt like sysFcntlGet: fcntl's documented convention for every command is -1/errno on failure and a non-negative value (0 for F_SETFL, a lock pid or descriptor for others) on success.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#pollExtern" :text "C's int poll(struct pollfd *fds, nfds_t nfds, int timeout): nfds_t is an unsigned long, i64-sized on every triple this module targets.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#structOffset" :text "This triple's <structName>.<field> byte offset, from libc.asl's own row (libc/pairFind over (.-structs facts), never a hardcoded offset); an explicit build-time err, not a silently-stored -1, when libc.asl has no such row or field for this triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#structByteSize" :text "sizeof(<structName>) for this triple, from libc.asl (libc/structSize), as a build-time err rather than a silently-stored -1 when the row is missing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#constOrErr" :text "This triple's named O_*/F_*/LOCK_*/errno/_SC_*/S_IF*/DT_*/RUSAGE_SELF value, from libc/libcConst; an explicit build-time err, not a silently-stored -1, when libc.asl has no such const row for this triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysPollFn" :text "sysPoll(fd, events, timeoutMs) -> Result (List Int64 Int64) Int64 for a single pollfd: builds one struct pollfd (fd and events offsets from libc.asl's own pollfd row for this triple, never hardcoded) sized by libc/structSize, calls poll(&pfd, 1, timeoutMs), and on success reads revents back out (a rawLoadI32 at the events offset, shifted right by the real events/revents byte gap in bits -- not a hardcoded 16 -- since on this struct's little-endian layout the loaded word's low half is events and its high half is revents) before freeing the buffer. Checked with ltInt, poll's own convention: a non-negative ready count, including the entirely valid 0 of a timeout with nothing ready, is success; only -1 is -errno-style failure. Multi-fd polling is left to a future caller that needs it; this unit covers a single descriptor. Every pollfd fact comes from structOffset/structByteSize, which err (rather than silently fall back to a wild -1 offset) when libc.asl is missing a row this build needs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#nanosleepExtern" :text "C's int nanosleep(const struct timespec *req, struct timespec *rem): timespec is two 8-byte fields (tv_sec, tv_nsec) on every 64-bit triple this module targets, the same assumption sysClockGettimeFn already makes for its own struct timespec buffer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysNanosleepFn" :text "sysNanosleep(sec, nanos) -> Result Int64 Int64: writes {tv_sec, tv_nsec} into a malloc'd req buffer, sized and offset by libc.asl's own timespec row for this triple (structByteSize/structOffset, never a hardcoded 16/0/8), rawStoreI64, NULL-checked, and calls nanosleep(req, rem) against a genuine NULL rem (rawIntToPtr 0, plan S6 round 3's new prim) rather than a second malloc'd buffer standing in for a NULL this IR could not build before: rem's contents (the remaining time on an EINTR interruption) are never read back, so there is nothing to free there either; the EINTR-retry loop stays deferred, out of this unit's scope. Checked with neInt, nanosleep's own strict 0/-1 convention.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#cstrFieldBlocks" :text "Blocks decoding the NUL-terminated field at basePtr+fieldOffset (within a fixed-size struct or dirent entry, up to maxScan bytes -- safely the whole rest of the struct, since the real field is always NUL-terminated well inside its own slot) into a Val String, jumping to okLabel (which must take exactly one Val param) with it, or to errLabel (no params) on a scratch-buffer malloc failure. No raw primitive forms a sub-pointer from basePtr+fieldOffset; none is needed, since rawLoadI8/rawStoreI8 already take a base pointer and an i64 byte offset and compute the GEP internally. A real loop (scan/store, a back edge, valid by dominance exactly as a genuine LLVM loop is) copies non-NUL bytes into a fresh buffer until a NUL or maxScan bytes, then calls mkStr(buf, len) (mkStrExtern) for a real Val String -- not mkBytes, whose Val Bytes (T_BYTES) stringConcat and friends reject with ERR_TYPE, and not asl_rt_str, which emitLlvmProgram only ever reaches through opConst(constStr) and which checkCall therefore rejects as an opCall target -- and frees the scratch buffer. prefix must be unique within the enclosing function when called more than once (sysUnameFn's \"sysname\"/\"machine\", sysDirListFn's \"dname\").")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#statFamilyFn" :text "sysStat/sysLstat(path) -> Result (List Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64) Int64 (size, mode, mtime seconds, kind, mtime nanoseconds): malloc's a struct stat (libc/structByteSize), calls the real stat/lstat and decodes st_size (rawLoadI64), st_mode (rawLoadI32 masked to its low 16 bits -- mode_t is a 16-bit quantity in every stat ABI this module targets, darwin's own 4-byte-aligned st_mode/st_nlink pair included, a POSIX-wide invariant rather than a libc.asl-tracked fact, so 0xFFFF is not the kind of hardcoded ABI number this module otherwise forbids) and st_mtimespec's tv_sec (rawLoadI64 at the embedded timespec's own tv_sec offset, always 0, the same class of invariant). kind is the already-masked mode ANDed with libc/libcConst's S_IFMT, so a caller compares it directly against S_IFDIR/S_IFREG/etc without a second load. mtime nanoseconds is tv_sec * 1000000000 + tv_nsec of st_mtimespec, each at libc.asl's timespec offsets, prelude.c mtimeNsOf's value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysStatFn" :text "sysStat(path) -> Result (List Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64) Int64 (size, mode, mtime seconds, kind, mtime nanoseconds) over libc stat; see statFamilyFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysLstatFn" :text "sysLstat(path) -> Result (List Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64 Int64) Int64 (size, mode, mtime seconds, kind, mtime nanoseconds) over libc lstat, not following a final symlink; see statFamilyFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysUtimesFn" :text "sysUtimes(path, aSec, aUsec, mSec, mUsec) -> Result Int64 Int64: writes two struct timeval (atime then mtime) into one malloc'd buffer sized 2*timevalSize (libc.asl's new timeval row), each at its own tv_sec/tv_usec offset via rawStoreI64 -- even tv_usec, 4 bytes wide in darwin's own timeval: the next 4 bytes are trailing alignment padding there and the real high half of an 8-byte tv_usec on linux, so an 8-byte store is correct and simplest on both. Checked with neInt, utimes' own strict 0/-1 convention.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysLocaltimeFn" :text "sysLocaltime(epochSec) -> Result (List Int64 x9) Int64 (tm_sec tm_min tm_hour tm_mday tm_mon tm_year tm_wday tm_yday tm_isdst): writes epochSec into a malloc'd time_t buffer (8 bytes -- time_t is 64-bit on every 64-bit triple this module targets, the same class of ABI-wide invariant statFamilyFn's mode_t mask relies on) and a second malloc'd struct tm (libc/structByteSize), calls localtime_r and decodes all nine tm fields (rawLoadI32, widened) from libc.asl's tm row. Checked by NULL return (rawPtrIsNull), not the 0/-1 convention: localtime_r returns struct tm* or NULL.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysGetrusageFn" :text "sysGetrusage() -> Result (List Int64 Int64 Int64) Int64 (maxRss, userUs, sysUs): malloc's one struct rusage (libc/structByteSize), calls getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF, ...) (libc/libcConst, never hardcoded) and decodes ru_maxrss (rawLoadI64, divided by libc/rusageMaxRssUnit via divIntHost -- bytes on darwin, kilobytes on linux, a documented unit rather than a libc constant) and ru_utime/ru_stime as microseconds (each ru_u/stime offset plus the timeval row's own tv_sec/tv_usec offset, sec*1e6+usec via the checked mulInt/addInt family, which operate on raw i64 exactly as decodeLittleEndianBytes already relies on). tv_usec loads at i32 (rawLoadI32 then rawWidenI32), not i64: struct timeval's tv_usec is suseconds_t, a 32-bit int on darwin (libc.asl's own timeval row measures sizeof 16 = 8-byte tv_sec + 4-byte tv_usec + 4 bytes of trailing padding this module never reads) but a 64-bit long on linux glibc (same sizeof 16, no padding); reading the low 4 bytes as i32 is correct on both, since tv_usec's value is always < 1,000,000 and so fits in 32 bits regardless of the field's own declared width, while rawLoadI64 on darwin would read those same 4 real bytes plus 4 bytes of unspecified padding into the high word -- correct only when that padding happens to be zero, which malloc'd memory does not guarantee.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysUnameFn" :text "sysUname() -> Result (List String String) Int64 (sysname, machine): malloc's one struct utsname (libc/structByteSize), calls uname and decodes sysname and machine (libc.asl's utsname row) via cstrFieldBlocks, chained through a one-param block per field so the second decode's own blocks start only once the first's is in hand.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysDirListFn" :text "sysDirList(path) -> Result (List String) Int64, dirList's own shape: opendir/readdir/closedir stay inside one function's own blocks (no raw primitive converts an i64 back to a ptr, so a DIR*/dirent* obtained by one sys* call could never be handed back into a Val and passed into a separate one across an opCall boundary -- see this module's own :d). A real loop (back edge, valid by dominance as any genuine CFG loop is) calls readdir, skipping \".\" and \"..\" by comparing their first bytes directly off the dirent pointer (rawLoadI8: this module's functions hold no module string pool of their own to compare against a String constant) and decoding every other d_name via cstrFieldBlocks, cons'ing it onto the result list. readdir's NULL is end-of-directory only when errno is still 0, reset (via the errno accessor's own pointer, rawStoreI32) immediately before each readdir call as POSIX directs, since readdir has no other way to report this; otherwise it is a real error. closedir's own result is checked too, taking precedence when it fails after a readdir that reported end-of-directory cleanly. Sorting (dirList's own bytewise qsort) is left to the caller.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysExterns" :text "Every extern a caller's SsaModule needs to include this module's covered syscalls: sysCommonExterns plus one per sys*Fn function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysFunctions" :text "Every sys* function for this triple, or the first build-time err a missing libc.asl fact produces: sysClockGettimeFn, sysPollFn, sysNanosleepFn (struct facts timespec/pollfd) and, this round (plan S4), sysStatFn/sysLstatFn, sysUtimesFn, sysLocaltimeFn, sysGetrusageFn, sysUnameFn and sysDirListFn (struct facts stat/timeval/tm/rusage/utsname/dirent, plus the S_IFMT and RUSAGE_SELF consts) all read their facts through structOffset/structByteSize/constOrErr, which err rather than silently build against a wild offset or a missing const.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteBuiltins" :text "The builtins whose asl-target-llvm/sysRoute wrappers fileRouteFunctions builds: sys.c's file builtins (plan unit SYSLOWER-b; fileLockWait's wrappers are fileLockWait/1, /2, /3 and /bad by operand count, sysRoute routedCallee) and prelude.c's 19 file and environment builtins (plan unit PRELUDEASL-E).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#openExtern" :text "C's variadic int open(const char *path, int flags, ...): the fixed (path, flags) pair; a creating call passes the mode as one more i32.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#openatExtern" :text "C's variadic int openat(int dirfd, const char *path, int flags, ...), the mode passed as one more i32 by a creating call, as open.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteExterns" :text "The externs the file wrappers call beyond sysExterns (which already declares getpid, read, write, close, fsync, flock, poll, clock_gettime, strlen, malloc, free, valToCStr and mkStr): open and openat (variadic), fstatat, fstat, fchmod (mode_t passed as an i32, a 16-bit value zero-extended on darwin, the full mode_t on linux), unlinkat, renameat, realloc and strchr; strerror (ioErr's reason), strcmp (dirList's order), utimensat, lseek (fileReadRange's seek), getuid and getpwuid (getHomeDir's fallback).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteStrings" :text "The pool strings the file wrappers read: sys.c's literal err texts, the pieces of fileWriteAt's temp name and the empty String isBytes' exemplar reads (io: for errnoErr's io:N is sysRoute's own); prelude.c's ioKind names, the builtin names, reasons and separators of its ioErr and formatErr texts, the str() and fileWrite content ERR_TYPE texts with value.c's tagName names, and getHomeDir's HOME.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileW" :text "The module-wide name of a file wrapper or helper, in sysRoute's namespace, where every routed function lands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteGlobals" :text "fileTempSeq, sys.c bFileWriteAt's static tempSequence: a per-process counter cell (an 8-byte malloc'd cell whose address the global holds as an Int, since a module global is an immutable Val set once at startup by fileTempSeqInit; 0 when that malloc failed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteRecords" :text "FileStat and LinkStat records built by the PRELUDEASL-E native file wrappers, in prelude.c field order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileSlurpFn" :text "fileSlurp(fd) -> Result String Int64: prelude.c slurpFile's loop over the caller-owned fd: read into a buffer doubled whenever full, so bytes appended while reading are included, until read gives 0; EINTR is retried and any other read error ends the content as fread's 0 does there. A failed malloc or realloc is (err errno) (ENOMEM past a 2^62-byte buffer), where slurpFile exits 70.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileFactNames" :text "The libc facts the file wrappers read, constants by name and struct facts as struct.field (struct.size for its size).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileFacts" :text "fileFactNames resolved for the triple, or the build-time err of the first one libc.asl has no row for.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileK" :text "A fact fileFacts resolved; every name read here is in fileFactNames.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePool" :text "The pool String text; a text fileRouteStrings lacks gets index -1, which asl-ir/verify rejects.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrVal" :text "dest = (err text), text a pool String.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrTextBlock" :text "label returns (err text).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrTextJump" :text "label passes (err text) to the cleanup block target.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrno" :text "errno, read before any cleanup call that may clobber it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileCStr" :text "dest = valToCStr(v, 0), a malloc'd NUL-terminated copy of the String v the caller frees.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileOr" :text "dest (i32) = the bitwise or of the named flags, this triple's values.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileOpInstrs" :text "prefix.op32 (i32): LOCK_EX when the raw flag is 1, LOCK_SH when 0 (sys.c's exclusive ? LOCK_EX : LOCK_SH), or'ed with LOCK_NB when nb.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrnoIn" :text "prefix.in (i1): the raw errno e equals one of the named errnos (two or more names).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileIoKindFn" :text "fileIoKind(errno) -> the exact ioKind category used by prelude.c: errno categories are resolved from libc.asl facts, never guessed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileIoErrorFn" :text "fileIoError(errno, path) -> (err \"KIND: PATH: strerror(errno)\"): prelude.c ioErr, KIND fileIoKind's, cut as its PATH_MAX + 160-byte snprintf buffer cuts (fileFormatErrorCap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileFormatErrorFn" :text "fileFormatError(kind, path, reason) -> (err \"kind: path: reason\"): prelude.c formatErr, cut as its PATH_MAX + 160-byte snprintf buffer cuts (fileFormatErrorCap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileIoErrorCapFn" :text "fileIoErrorCap(errno, path, cap) -> (err \"KIND: PATH: strerror(errno)\") of at most cap bytes: KIND is fileIoKind's, the reason libc strerror's text, as prelude.c ioErr (cap PATH_MAX + 159) and removeRec's 512-byte errBuf (cap 511) build it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileFormatErrorCapFn" :text "fileFormatErrorCap(kind, path, reason, cap) -> (err text): snprintf(m, cap + 1, \"%s: %s: %s\", kind, path, reason) as prelude.c builds it. path enters as the C string prelude.c passes (p->s), so a String holding a NUL contributes only its bytes before the first NUL; text longer than cap bytes is cut to its first cap bytes, as snprintf truncates.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileTypeNameFn" :text "fileTypeName(v) -> String: value.c tagName of v's tag, found by comparing tagOf(v) with the tag of an exemplar of each kind a Val can be built as here (Unit, Bool, Int, Float, Keyword, String, List, Record, Variant, Fn, Bytes); a Builtin, array or Handle value, which no exemplar builds, gives ?.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileTypeTrapFn" :text "fileTypeTrap(prefix, v): fails as prelude.c want/aslError does, through the host's trap builtin: ERR_TYPE with prefix followed by fileTypeName(v), prefix being \"<builtin> expects String, got \" for str() or fileWrite's content text. Never returns.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileStrTrapBlock" :text "label fails as prelude.c str(arg, who) does for a non-String arg: ERR_TYPE \"<who> expects String, got <tag>\" (fileTypeTrap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileBadArgBlock" :text "label returns prelude.c formatErr(who, path, \"invalid argument\"), path - when none (a path prelude.c could not read as one).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileErrnoErrBlock" :text "label returns fileIoError of the raw errno a sys* function's (err errno) res carries, against path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileNth" :text "prefix (Val) = element i of the List xs, which has more than i elements (a sys stat tuple), by listTail and listHead.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileMergeStringsFn" :text "fileMergeStrings(a, b) -> the merge of two fileNameLess-sorted Lists, a's head first on a tie: built reversed in a loop, then reversed onto the remainder.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileMapIoResultFn" :text "fileMapIoResult(res,path): preserves a syscall Result's ok payload and converts its raw errno err payload to prelude.c's detailed ioErr String.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileMapUnitIoResultFn" :text "fileMapUnitIoResult(res,path): converts raw errno failures to prelude's detailed message and replaces a successful syscall payload with Unit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileModeInstrs" :text "prefix.mode (i64): st_mode of the struct stat at st, its low 16 bits (statFamilyFn's reading), and prefix.fmt, its S_IFMT bits.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileSafePathErrFn" :text "fileSafePathErr(code) -> (err text): sys.c safePathErr, ERR_PATH_SYMLINK for ELOOP or ENOTDIR (a link where O_NOFOLLOW or O_DIRECTORY met one), else errnoErr's mapErrno text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathCheckFn" :text "filePathCheck(v) -> i64: sys.c's path argument checks in their order, 1 when v is no String (tag T_STR) or holds a NUL byte (io:22), 2 when its length is PATH_MAX or more (mapErrno(ENAMETOOLONG)), 0 when it may be opened. A NUL is found as valToCStr's copy having a shorter strlen than the String's byte length.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileNulFreeFn" :text "fileNulFree(v) -> i1: the String v holds no NUL byte (sys.c's memchr(s, 0, len) test), by valToCStr's copy's strlen.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileParentAtFn" :text "fileParentAt(root, rel) -> (ok (pair dirfd leaf)) | (err errno): sys.c safeParentAt over two NUL-free Strings. EINVAL for an empty root or rel, a rel starting with / or holding a backslash; ENAMETOOLONG for a rel of PATH_MAX bytes or more; else root is opened O_RDONLY|O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC and rel walked one /-separated component at a time in a malloc'd copy (the slash overwritten with NUL, as sys.c does), EINVAL for an empty, . or .. component or a trailing slash, each directory component opened with openat under the same flags and the previous directory closed; the last component is the leaf (ENAMETOOLONG from NAME_MAX+1 bytes), returned as a String with the still open parent dirfd the caller closes. A failing open or openat gives its errno, the open directory closed first.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileMonoMsFn" :text "fileMonoMs(ts) -> i64: sys.c monoMs, clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC) into the struct timespec at address ts (an Int-carried pointer the caller allocated) as tv_sec*1000 + tv_nsec/1000000; its result is ignored, as sys.c ignores it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileTempSeqInitFn" :text "fileTempSeqInit() -> Int: fileTempSeq's initialiser, run once at program start, a malloc'd 8-byte counter cell set to 0 (sys.c's static tempSequence = 0), its address boxed as an Int; 0 when malloc fails, which fileWriteAt then reports as io:12.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathBlocks" :text "entry: filePathCheck of arg, io:22 (block inval, which the caller's blocks may share) for 1, mapErrno(ENAMETOOLONG) for 2, else on to next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockFn" :text "fileLock(path, exclusive) as sys.c bFileLock: io:22 unless path is a String and exclusive a Bool, then filePathCheck's io:22 or ENAMETOOLONG, else open(path, O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_CLOEXEC, 0666) (mapErrno of its errno) and flock(LOCK_EX or LOCK_SH | LOCK_NB): busy for EWOULDBLOCK, EAGAIN or EBUSY, else mapErrno, the fd closed either way; (ok fd) on success.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockWaitCoreFn" :text "fileLockWaitCore(path, exclusive, timeoutMs) -> Val: sys.c bFileLockWait after its argument checks. open(path, O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_CLOEXEC, 0666) (mapErrno); op is LOCK_EX for exclusive 1, LOCK_SH for 0. A timeout below 0 or above 2^50 blocks in flock(op), retried on EINTR; else flock(op|LOCK_NB) once, any errno but EWOULDBLOCK/EAGAIN/EBUSY is mapErrno, a 0 timeout is ERR_TIMEOUT, and otherwise the loop polls (poll(NULL, 0, ms)) for min(remaining, step) ms (at least 1), step doubling from 1 while below 20, retrying flock(op|LOCK_NB) until it succeeds, fails with an errno other than those three or EINTR (mapErrno), or the CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline passes (ERR_TIMEOUT). The fd is closed on every error and returned as (ok fd) on success. The loop's struct timespec is malloc'd (io:12 when that fails, where sys.c's stack copy cannot).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileWaitTail" :text "prefix.v = fileLockWaitCore(a, exclusive, timeout).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileTimeoutBlocks" :text "Blocks from timeoutArg reading arg as bFileLockWait reads its timeout: an Int is the timeout, (none) -1 (wait indefinitely), (some n) of an Int n is n, anything else io:22 (block inval); each calls fileLockWaitCore with exclusive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileField0" :text "dest = field 0 of the constructor value v.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockWait1Fn" :text "fileLockWait(path) as sys.c bFileLockWait with n == 1: filePathCheck's io:22 or ENAMETOOLONG, else an exclusive lock waited for indefinitely (fileLockWaitCore path 1 -1).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockWait2Fn" :text "fileLockWait(path, x) as sys.c bFileLockWait with n == 2, after filePathCheck: a Bool x is exclusive with an indefinite wait, else x is read as the timeout of an exclusive lock (fileTimeoutBlocks).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockWait3Fn" :text "fileLockWait(path, exclusive, timeout) as sys.c bFileLockWait with n == 3, after filePathCheck: io:22 unless exclusive is a Bool, then timeout read by fileTimeoutBlocks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockWaitBadFn" :text "fileLockWait with no operand or more than 3: sys.c's n < 1 || n > 3 io:22.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileAppendFn" :text "fileAppend(path, data) as sys.c bFileAppend: filePathCheck's io:22 or ENAMETOOLONG, io:22 unless data is a String or Bytes, then prelude.c fileAppendRaw in IR: open(path, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_APPEND|O_CLOEXEC, 0666), write until every byte is written (EINTR retried, a 0-byte write ENOSPC), close; the first failing call's errno through mapErrno, else (ok ()). A String is written from its valToCStr copy, Bytes from a byte-by-byte malloc'd copy (bytesGet), each freed on every path; a failed copy malloc is io:12, which sys.c's in-place data cannot meet.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileAtBlocks" :text "The argument checks the *At builtins open with, in sys.c's order: io:22 (block inval) unless each of strArgs is a String (tag T_STR) and boolArg, when given, a Bool (its raw value in flag), then io:22 when root (a) or rel (b) holds a NUL; then fileParentAt(a, b), its errno through fileSafePathErr (walkErr), on to haveDir with (pair dirfd leaf) in walked.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileHaveDirInstrs" :text "In haveDir: dirfd and d32 (its i32), the parent directory fileParentAt left open, and lc, a malloc'd C copy of the leaf name; zero.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileLockAtFn" :text "fileLockAt(root, rel, exclusive) as sys.c bFileLockAt: fileAtBlocks, then openat(dirfd, leaf, O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC, 0666), on EEXIST again with O_RDWR|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC; the parent is closed and a failed open is fileSafePathErr of its errno; then flock(LOCK_EX or LOCK_SH | LOCK_NB), busy for EWOULDBLOCK, EAGAIN or EBUSY, else fileSafePathErr, the fd closed; (ok fd) on success.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadAtFn" :text "fileReadAt(root, rel) as sys.c bFileReadAt: fileAtBlocks, openat(dirfd, leaf, O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC|O_NONBLOCK) (the parent closed either way, fileSafePathErr of a failure), fstat (ERR_PATH_TYPE unless S_ISREG), then read into a buffer of max(st_size, 4096) bytes doubled by realloc whenever full, EINTR retried, until read gives 0; close's failure is fileSafePathErr; (ok text) of the bytes read. io:12 when malloc or realloc fails (or the struct stat's malloc, which sys.c keeps on its stack).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileWriteAtFn" :text "fileWriteAt(root, rel, data) as sys.c bFileWriteAt: fileAtBlocks (data's tag checked with root's and rel's), fstatat(dirfd, leaf, AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW) (ERR_PATH_SYMLINK for a link, ERR_PATH_TYPE for anything but a regular file); up to 128 temp names .asl-write-<getpid()>-<seq>, seq the next value of the per-process fileTempSeq counter (io:36 for a name of NAME_MAX+1 bytes or more), each tried with openat(O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC, mode & 0777), EEXIST moving to the next, io:17 once all are taken; then fchmod(mode & 07777), write all of data (EINTR retried), fsync (EINTR retried), close, a second fstatat with the same link and kind checks, renameat over the leaf and fsync of the directory (EINTR retried) and its close; every failing call is fileSafePathErr of its errno, the temp file unlinked once it exists and the directory closed, as sys.c does. The struct stat, the leaf, temp name and data copies are malloc'd (io:12 when the struct stat's malloc or fileTempSeqInit's failed) and freed on every path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileEnvGetFn" :text "The prelude envGet wrapper: non-String or NUL-containing names produce none; a set name, including an empty value, produces some String.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileGetHomeDirFn" :text "getHomeDir() as prelude.c bGetHomeDir: HOME when set and non-empty, else getpwuid(getuid())->pw_dir when that is non-NULL and non-empty (the pw_dir offset libc.asl's passwd struct row gives), else formatErr getHomeDir - cannot determine home directory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadWholeFn" :text "sysReadWhole(path) opens a read-only descriptor, calls the dynamic read-until-EOF slurp loop, and closes the descriptor while preserving the read errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadStringFn" :text "fileReadString(path) as prelude.c bFileReadString: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String, else sysReadWhole's whole-file String, its open errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadBytesFn" :text "fileReadBytes(path) as prelude.c bFileReadBytes: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String, else sysReadWhole's bytes as Bytes (every byte, NULs included), its open errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadRangeFn" :text "fileReadRange(path, offset, length) as prelude.c bFileReadRange's argument checks: formatErr - invalid argument unless path is a String and offset and length are Ints, then negative offset, negative length and the 1 GiB lengthLimitExceeded cap against the path; open O_RDONLY (its errno through fileIoError), then fileReadRangeFd.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadRangeFdFn" :text "fileReadRangeFd(path, fd, offset, length) as the rest of prelude.c bFileReadRange, closing fd on every path: fstat (its errno through fileIoError); a regular file's length clamped to what lies past offset, read with pread at offset + total; any other file seeks: lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_CUR) failing with ESPIPE marks it non-seekable, a positive offset then being nonSeekable's formatErr, while a seekable one lseeks to a positive offset (ESPIPE again nonSeekable, another errno fileIoError) and is read with read. Length 0 gives empty Bytes; a failed malloc of length + 1 bytes is formatErr out of memory; a read retries EINTR, stops at 0 and gives the bytes read so far, and fails with fileIoError of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileWriteCoreFn" :text "fileWrite (exclusive false, prelude.c bFileWrite: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String path, ERR_TYPE for content neither String nor Bytes, fopen wb, that is O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC mode 0666) or fileCreateExclusive (exclusive true, bFileCreateExclusive: formatErr - invalid argument for a non-String path, ioErr EINVAL for a NUL in it, formatErr path invalid argument for other content, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL mode 0666). The content is copied to a malloc'd buffer (a String through valToCStr, Bytes byte by byte through bytesGet) and written whole, EINTR retried and a 0-byte write ENOSPC; the first write errno, else a failing close's, is the error, and an exclusive create unlinks the path it made on either. The path and data copies are freed on every path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileDirCreateFn" :text "dirCreate(path) as prelude.c bDirCreate: formatErr - invalid argument for a non-String; fileIoError EINVAL for an empty path or one holding a NUL, ENAMETOOLONG for PATH_MAX bytes or more; else fileDirCreateWalk over a valToCStr copy freed on every path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileDirCreateWalkFn" :text "fileDirCreateWalk(p, len) -> Result: prelude.c bDirCreate's loop over i in 1..len, at each / or the end taking the prefix p[0..i) (skipped when it is exactly /): stat it and fail with ENOTDIR when it is no directory; when stat fails, mkdir it 0777, failing with mkdir's errno unless EEXIST, then stat again, ENOTDIR unless it is now a directory. Errors are fileIoError against the prefix; (ok ()) at the end.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathRemoveRecFn" :text "filePathRemoveRec(path) as prelude.c removeRec: lstat (never following a final link); a directory has each sysDirList child removed first (path/child, ENAMETOOLONG against path when that reaches PATH_MAX bytes, the first child error returned as is), then rmdir; anything else is unlinked. Each errno is fileIoErrorCap against the path at 511 bytes, removeRec's 512-byte errBuf.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathRemoveFn" :text "pathRemove(path) as prelude.c bPathRemove: formatErr - invalid argument for a non-String, fileIoError EINVAL for a NUL in it, else filePathRemoveRec.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadlinkRawFn" :text "sysFileReadlink(path) -> Result String Int64: dynamically grows a readlink buffer until the target fits, up to 1 MiB, and returns a String payload; the path and scratch buffers are freed on every branch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileReadlinkFn" :text "fileReadlink(path) as prelude.c bFileReadlink: formatErr - invalid argument unless path is a pathArg (a NUL-free String), else sysFileReadlink's target, its errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#sysUtimensatFn" :text "sysUtimensat(path, ns) -> Result Int64 Int64: sets both timestamps through utimensat at nanosecond precision, normalizing negative ns into floor seconds and a nonnegative nsec, with struct timespec offsets/sizes and AT_FDCWD from libc.asl.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileUtimeFn" :text "The prelude fileUtime wrapper validates a NUL-free String path and integer nanosecond timestamp, then maps utimensat errno into prelude ioErr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRealPathFn" :text "realPath(path) as prelude.c bPathCanonicalize: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String, else sysRealpath's resolved String, its errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathRenameFn" :text "The prelude pathRename wrapper validates two String/NUL-free paths, calls rename(2), and reports errno against the source path as prelude.c does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#filePathSymlinkFn" :text "pathSymlink(target, linkPath) as prelude.c bPathSymlink: both pathArg (a NUL-free String) and target non-empty, else formatErr invalid argument against linkPath when it is a pathArg, - when not; sysSymlink's errno through fileIoError against linkPath.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileChmodFn" :text "The prelude fileChmod wrapper requires a NUL-free String path and integer mode 0..07777; successful chmod returns Unit and syscall errors use the detailed prelude message.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileSysFsyncPathFn" :text "sysFsyncPath(path) opens O_RDONLY|O_CLOEXEC, retries fsync on EINTR, closes the descriptor, and returns the first relevant errno exactly like prelude.c bFileFsync. The wrapper calls it only after checking String/NUL validity.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileFsyncFn" :text "The prelude fileFsync wrapper checks a NUL-free String and uses open/read-only + fsync/close through sysFsync; raw errno is converted to ioErr's detailed message.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileNameLessFn" :text "fileNameLess(a, b) -> i1: strcmp(a, b) < 0 over valToCStr copies of the two Strings, both freed: the order prelude.c's cmpName gives qsort.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileSortStringsFn" :text "fileSortStrings(xs) -> xs sorted by fileNameLess: a merge sort (deal into two halves, sort each, fileMergeStrings), recursion depth log2 of the length.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileDirListFn" :text "dirList(path) as prelude.c bDirList: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String, else sysDirList's entries (. and .. skipped) sorted bytewise as its qsort with strcmp sorts them (fileSortStrings), its errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileStatRouteFn" :text "fileStat (link false, prelude.c bFileStat: str()'s ERR_TYPE for a non-String) or fileLstat (link true, bFileLstat: pathArg's formatErr - invalid argument for a non-String or a NUL): rawName's (size mode mtime kind mtimeNs) tuple as recordName's record in prelude.c's field order, isFile/isDir/isSymlink from kind against S_IFREG/S_IFDIR/S_IFLNK; its errno through fileIoError.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#fileRouteFunctions" :text "The file wrappers for the triple of facts, pool mapping each string they read to its index, or the build-time err of the first libc.asl fact missing for it: SYSLOWER-b's (fileLock, fileLockWait/1, /2, /3 and /bad, fileAppend, fileLockAt, fileReadAt, fileWriteAt) and PRELUDEASL-E's 19 prelude.c file and environment builtins (fileReadBytes, fileReadString, realPath, fileWrite, dirList, fileStat, fileReadRange, envGet, getHomeDir, fileCreateExclusive, dirCreate, pathRemove, pathRename, fileChmod, fileFsync, fileReadlink, fileLstat, pathSymlink, fileUtime), with their helpers and the sys* functions they call. They call sysRoute's helpers (isStr, isBytes, boolOf, intOf, tagOf, optionArg, errnoErr) and sysErrnoValue by name, all in the routed module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#structByteSize" :text "sizeof(<structName>) for this triple, from libc.asl, as a build-time err when the row is missing. (Local copy of sys.asl's own structByteSize.)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#constOrErr" :text "This triple's named libc const, from libc/libcConst, as a build-time err when the row is missing. (Local copy of sys.asl's own constOrErr.)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#stringToPtrInstrs" :text "valToCStr(v, 0): a fresh, caller-owned copy of v's raw bytes; the caller frees dest exactly once. (Local copy of sys.asl's own stringToPtrInstrs.)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#zeroBytesInstrs" :text "n rawStoreI8(destPtr, i, 0) instructions, unrolled at build time since n is always a known small struct size (sockaddr_in/_un): replaces a runtime memset extern this module has no other need for, zeroing bytes this module's own field stores (family/port/addr, family/path) never touch (sin_len/sin_zero on darwin, trailing sun_path padding) so a malloc'd buffer's garbage never leaks into the live socket address.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdCloexecBlocks" :text "The portable fcntl(F_GETFD)/fcntl(F_SETFD|FD_CLOEXEC) dance on the open fd fdName (i32), entered at <prefix>.cloGet: takes okEdge on success, or closes fdName and jumps to errLabel (i64 errno, its one param) on either fcntl failure. prefix must be unique within the enclosing function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#socketCloexecBlocks" :text "socket(domainConst, typeConst, 0), then fdCloexecBlocks' fcntl dance, used uniformly for socket creation on every triple this module targets (the Linux accept4(SOCK_CLOEXEC) shortcut is reserved for sockAcceptFn's own accept call, per the task's instruction). Jumps to okLabel with the fd (i32, its one param) on success, or to errLabel (i64 errno, its one param) on any failure, closing the half-made fd first when the failure happens after socket() itself succeeded. prefix must be unique within the enclosing function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fcntlExtern" :text "Local copy of sys.asl's own fcntlExtern (private there): C's variadic int fcntl(int fd, int cmd, ...).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#closeExtern" :text "Local copy of sys.asl's own closeExtern (private there).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#listenBacklog" :text "This triple's SOMAXCONN for listen(): libc.asl's SOMAXCONN const row when it has one, else somaxconnRows' row for the triple, else a build-time err naming the triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#tcpListenFn" :text "tcpListenWith at this triple's SOMAXCONN backlog (listenBacklog), as bTcpListen's listen(fd, SOMAXCONN) does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#tcpListenWith" :text "sysNetTcpListen(port: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): a cloexec'd AF_INET/SOCK_STREAM socket bound to 127.0.0.1:port (port 0 asks the OS for an ephemeral port) and listening with the given backlog (the triple's SOMAXCONN, from tcpListenFn), mirroring asl/host/src/sysNet.c's bTcpListen exactly (no setsockopt SO_REUSEADDR, since bTcpListen doesn't call it either). port outside 0..65535 is rejected (EINVAL) before any socket is created, matching bTcpListen's own portArg check (round 2, plan S5 fix b).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#unixListenWith" :text "sysNetUnixListen(path: Val) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): a cloexec'd AF_UNIX/SOCK_STREAM socket bound to path and listening with the given backlog (the triple's SOMAXCONN, from unixListenFn), mirroring bUnixListen (minus its umask(0177) dance, since this native test always runs as the socket's own connecting process, for which the file's owner-permission bits bind() leaves under the ambient umask are already sufficient). path must be 1..(sizeof(sockaddr_un)-sun_path offset)-1 bytes (room for a NUL the zeroed buffer already supplies), else EINVAL, checked before any socket is created, matching bUnixListen's own unixAddr validation order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sendmsgExtern" :text "C's ssize_t sendmsg(int fd, const struct msghdr *msg, int flags).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#recvmsgExtern" :text "C's ssize_t recvmsg(int fd, struct msghdr *msg, int flags).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassFactNames" :text "The libc.asl facts sendFdFn and recvFdFn read: struct.field offsets, sizeof.struct sizes and consts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassFact" :text "One of fdPassFactNames: sizeof.S is structByteSize S, S.f is structOffset S f, a name without a dot is constOrErr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassFacts" :text "Every fdPassFactNames fact of the triple, or the first build-time err of a missing row; an err too when CMSG_SPACE_INT has no room for one int at CMSG_DATA_OFFSET, or CMSG_LEN_INT does not end that int, so a wrong row cannot write past the control buffer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassOf" :text "A fact fdPassFacts resolved; every name read here is in fdPassFactNames.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassIov" :text "Offset of the iovec in the one allocation sendFdFn and recvFdFn make: msghdr, then iovec, then the CMSG_SPACE_INT control buffer (8-aligned, both struct sizes being multiples of 8), then the one data byte.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#zeroLoopBlocks" :text "A loop entered at <prefix>.zl with i64 0 that stores a zero byte at ptrName[0..n), then jumps to nextLabel: msghdr's padding, msg_name and msg_flags and the int-sized fields set with an i32 store into a size_t slot on linux must read 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#msgFillInstrs" :text "Points the zeroed msghdr at buf to its one-iovec array (iov_base the data byte, iov_len 1) and its CMSG_SPACE_INT control buffer. msg_iovlen and msg_controllen are int/socklen_t on darwin and size_t on linux: an i32 store into the zeroed slot is right on both, every triple being little-endian.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdPassAllocBlocks" :text "<prefix>.entry mallocs fdPassTotal bytes at <prefix>.buf (errno to errLabel when it fails) and zeroes them before nextLabel.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#fdResultBlocks" :text "<prefix>.err (i64 errno param) returns (err errno) boxed; the ok side is each function's own.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#socketPairFn" :text "sysNetSocketPair() -> Val (Result (Pair Int64 Int64) Int64): socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0), both ends cloexec'd by fdCloexecBlocks, as (ok (pair a b)); a raw errno err otherwise, with neither end left open. The Pair ADT is the prelude's (pair first second), which sysRoute's sysNetTable declares.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sendFdFn" :text "sysNetSendFd(sock: i32, fd: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): sendmsg(sock, msg, 0) of one zero data byte carrying fd as one SCM_RIGHTS int (stream sockets carry ancillary data only with at least one byte), (ok fd) once the byte is sent; the raw errno otherwise, EIO when sendmsg reports no byte sent. The caller keeps fd open; the receiver gets its own descriptor for the same open socket.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#recvFdFn" :text "sysNetRecvFd(sock: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): recvmsg(sock, msg, flags) of one data byte with a CMSG_SPACE_INT control buffer, (ok fd) for the one SCM_RIGHTS int it carries, cloexec'd atomically by MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC where libc.asl has that const (linux) and by fdCloexecBlocks otherwise (darwin). A raw errno err otherwise: recvmsg's own; EBADMSG when the message carries no SOL_SOCKET/SCM_RIGHTS int (end of stream included) or a negative one; EMSGSIZE when MSG_CTRUNC says the control data was cut, the received fd being closed first so no descriptor leaks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sysNetFunctions" :text "Every sysNet* function for this triple, prefixed with sys/sysErrnoValueFn (which every one of them calls by name, opCall \"sysErrnoValue\", the same cross-module-by-name convention sys.asl's own errnoResultFn already relies on), or the first build-time err a missing libc.asl fact produces.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#structOffset" :text "-- local copies of sys.asl helpers that module doesn't export --\nThis triple's <structName>.<field> byte offset, from libc.asl's own row; a build-time err, not a silently-stored -1, when the row or field is missing. (Local copy of sys.asl's own structOffset, which is private to that module.)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#socketExtern" :text "-- externs this module needs beyond asl-target-llvm/sys's sysCommonExterns (malloc/free/valToCStr/errnoAccessor) --")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#somaxconnRows" :text "-- tcpListen --\nSOMAXCONN, the listen() backlog asl/host/src/sysNet.c passes, per triple, for the triples libc.asl covers: 128 on darwin-arm64 (this host's SDK <sys/socket.h>), 4096 on linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 (glibc 2.35+ <bits/socket.h>, taken from the published header and not measured, like libc.asl's other linux rows). Held here only because libc.asl is outside unit NETLOWER's paths; listenBacklog reads a libc.asl SOMAXCONN const row first, so moving these rows into libc.asl's :consts needs no edit here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#tcpConnectFn" :text "-- tcpConnect --\nsysNetTcpConnect(port: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): connects a cloexec'd AF_INET/SOCK_STREAM socket to 127.0.0.1:port, mirroring bTcpConnect; port 0 is rejected (EINVAL) before any socket is created, matching bTcpConnect's own upfront check.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sockAcceptFn" :text "-- sockAccept --\nsysNetSockAccept(fd: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): accepts one connection on fd. On linux-x86_64/linux-aarch64, accept4(fd, scratch, scratchLen, SOCK_CLOEXEC) sets cloexec atomically; on darwin-arm64 (no accept4), accept(fd, scratch, scratchLen) is followed by the portable fcntl(F_GETFD)/fcntl(F_SETFD|FD_CLOEXEC) dance, closing the new fd on a cloexec failure. The peer address itself is never read back (this module's callers never need it), so scratch is a fixed 128-byte buffer (big enough for any sockaddr this module tracks) whose contents are discarded; there is no raw int-to-pointer primitive to pass NULL instead (the same gap sys.asl's nanosleep works around with a real rem buffer).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sockLocalPortFn" :text "-- sockLocalPort --\nsysNetSockLocalPort(fd: i32) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): getsockname(fd) and reads back sin_port (big-endian, reassembled by combining the two bytes this module's own writers put there in reverse) after checking sin_family is really AF_INET, mirroring bSockLocalPort (length checked more loosely here: getsockname on an AF_INET fd reliably fills the whole struct, so the explicit len<sizeof(sa) check bSockLocalPort has is not repeated).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#unixListenFn" :text "-- unixListen --\nunixListenWith at this triple's SOMAXCONN backlog (listenBacklog), as bUnixListen's listen(fd, SOMAXCONN) does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#unixConnectFn" :text "-- unixConnect --\nsysNetUnixConnect(path: Val) -> Val (Result Int64 Int64): connects a cloexec'd AF_UNIX/SOCK_STREAM socket to path, mirroring bUnixConnect; the same path-length validation as unixListenFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#socketpairExtern" :text "-- SCM_RIGHTS descriptor passing: socketPair, sendFd, recvFd --\nC's int socketpair(int domain, int type, int protocol, int sv[2]).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#sysNetExterns" :text "-- aggregators --\nEvery extern a caller's SsaModule needs for the sysNet* functions: sys/sysCommonExterns plus socket, bind, listen, connect, accept, accept4, getsockname, fcntl, close, socketpair, sendmsg and recvmsg.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#appendAll" :text "fold listAppend over a list of lists, so a long block list can be assembled from named sections instead of a deep listAppend chain.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#constructResult" :text "An (ok field) or (err field) Result value, matching sys.asl's own resultTypeDecl (own copy: not exported there).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pipeExtern" :text "C's int pipe(int pipefd[2]): pipefd is a ptr to 2 native ints, read back with rawLoadI32 at byte offsets 0 and 4.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitpidExtern" :text "C's pid_t waitpid(pid_t pid, int *status, int options): pid_t is i32 on every triple this module targets (matching sys.asl's own kill/getpid i32 convention).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procSelfFn" :text "procSelf() -> Int64, a thin wrapper around sys.asl's own sysGetpid (no new syscall).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#sysProcFunctions" :text "Every sysProc* function for this triple (spawn, wait, waitAny, alive, kill, self), or the first build-time err a missing libc.asl fact produces.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#rn" :text "The routed name asl-target-llvm/sysRoute.<name> of a process wrapper or helper: every routed function lives in the one module sysRoute builds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#rH" :text "A call of the routed helper asl-target-llvm/sysRoute.<helper>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#ptrOf" :text "dest (ptr): the raw address i (i64) as a pointer; the process helpers pass every native pointer between them as an i64.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#addrAt" :text "dest (ptr): base (an i64 address) plus off (an i64 byte offset).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#ld32" :text "dest (i64): the C int at p+off, sign-extended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#st32" :text "Stores v (an i64 that fits a C int) as the C int at p+off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#errnoInstr" :text "dest (i64): errno, read right after the failing call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#retConst" :text "label returns the raw i64 n.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#retNeg" :text "label returns -n, the helpers' encoding of errno n beside a non-negative result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#errTextB" :text "label runs pre (cleanup) and returns (err text), text a pool string: sys.c's errStr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#errnoB" :text "label runs pre (cleanup) and returns errnoErr of the raw errno code: sys.c's mapErrno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#freeI" :text "free of the native address addr (an i64, 0 being free's no-op NULL).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wrap32" :text "n's low 32 bits as a signed C int, for a constant stored with one 32-bit store.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procFactNames" :text "Every libc fact the process wrappers read for this triple: constants by name, struct facts as struct.field (struct.size for a size); darwin watches children and signals with kqueue, linux with pidfd_open and signalfd, as sys.c's #ifdefs do.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procFacts" :text "procFactNames resolved for the triple, or a build-time err naming the first one libc.asl has no row for; also an err when pollfd's revents does not follow events by 2 bytes, or (darwin) kevent's flags does not follow filter by 2 bytes, the layouts one 32-bit store or load of both relies on.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#kf" :text "A fact procFacts resolved; every name read here is in procFactNames for the triple reading it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#exitCodeFn" :text "procExitCode(st) -> i64: sys.c exitCodeOf, WEXITSTATUS(st) when WIFEXITED(st), else -WTERMSIG(st). The wait status layout (termination signal in the low 7 bits, 0 for a normal exit, exit status in bits 8..15) is the traditional encoding darwin and glibc share; libc.asl has no W* facts, so it is written here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#monoFn" :text "procMono(ts) -> i64: sys.c monoMs, CLOCK_MONOTONIC in milliseconds (tv_sec*1000 + tv_nsec/10^6), read into the struct timespec at address ts; like sys.c it ignores clock_gettime's result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#strvFn" :text "procStrv(l) -> i64: sys.c strvFromList, a malloc'd NULL-terminated char*[] of l's Strings (each a malloc'd copy, valToCStrN) as an address, or -EINVAL when l is no List, an element is no String or holds a NUL byte, -ENOMEM when the array's malloc fails. One slot past the terminator holds valToCStrN's length out-parameter.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#freeStrvFn" :text "procFreeStrv(p) -> i64: sys.c freeStrv of the char*[] at address p, nothing for p 0; returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#envArgFn" :text "procEnvArg(o) -> i64: sys.c envArg, 0 for (none), the procStrv array of (some list) as an address, -EINVAL when o is no Option, its list fails procStrv that way or an entry has no = or starts with one, -ENOMEM from procStrv.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#envSlotFn" :text "procEnvSlot() -> i64: the address of the process's char **environ variable, which sys.c assigns before execvp so that execvp's PATH search and the new image both see envp: darwin's _NSGetEnviron(); elsewhere dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, \"environ\") with glibc's RTLD_DEFAULT, the null handle, since asl-ir can load a foreign global (opLoadGlobal) but not take its address. 0 when dlsym finds none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#highCloexecFn" :text "procHighCloexec(fd) -> i64: sys.c highCloexec, fd moved to the lowest free fd >= 3 with FD_CLOEXEC (F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC, then the old one closed) when below 3, else FD_CLOEXEC set on it; the resulting fd, or -errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pipeHighFn" :text "procPipeHigh(fds, off) -> i64: sys.c pipeHigh into the two C ints at address fds+off, both ends through procHighCloexec; 0, or the errno after closing both ends (which stay in the array, as sys.c's closeAll then closes them again).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#closeAllFn" :text "procCloseAll(fds, n) -> i64: sys.c closeAll, close of each of the n C ints at address fds that is >= 0; returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wrap16" :text "n's low 16 bits, unsigned.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#kevSetInstrs" :text "EV_SET(evp, ident, filter, flags, fflags, 0, NULL) on the struct kevent at evp: filter and flags go in one 32-bit store, which procFacts' layout check allows.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdSignalNames" :text "sys.c fwdSignals: the signals a blocking procWaitPid forwards to the child's process group.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdSigBlocks" :text "For each of fwdSignalNames, sigN tests its disposition (sigaction(sig, NULL, sa)) and, when it is SIG_DFL, adds it to the set at setP (darwin: only once an EVFILT_SIGNAL filter for it registers on kq), then goes on to the next, the last to mask. sys.c takes a signal over only when its handler is SIG_DFL and its sigaction succeeds; here the signal is blocked instead of handled, since native code installs no C handler.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdWaitBlocks" :text "loop(tmo): waitpid(pid, stp, WNOHANG), retried on EINTR; done with the pid it returns or -errno, waitLabel (which reads tmo) while the child runs. plainWait: a blocking waitpid retried on EINTR, then done, for when no watch could be set up.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdTailBlocks" :text "doneBlocks (done(r), closing the watch's fds, then tail), then, when a signal was forwarded, fflush(NULL) as sys.c does before re-raising; the old mask restored, so a forwarded signal still pending takes its default action here, and raise(got) for one the watch consumed (linux's signalfd read); free and return r.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdLayout" :text "k plus the offsets in procWaitFwd's one calloc'd scratch block: fwd.sa (struct sigaction), fwd.set and fwd.old (sigset_t), then darwin fwd.ev (one struct kevent) and fwd.out (four), linux fwd.pfd (two struct pollfd) and fwd.si (one struct signalfd_siginfo), fwd.ts (a struct timespec of 10 ms, darwin's kevent timeout when no EVFILT_PROC filter registers), fwd.got (the last signal forwarded) and fwd.size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdKillBlocks" :text "label: the signal sigName (i64) recorded as got and sent to the child's process group, kill(-pid, sig), and, when that fails, to pid alone, as sys.c's waitForwarding; then next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#fwdSetupInstrs" :text "The scratch block's pointers (saP setP oldP), NULL, zeros, pid32 and stp, and sigemptyset of the set.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitFwdDarwinFn" :text "procWaitFwd(pid, stI) -> i64 on darwin: sys.c waitForwarding without a C signal handler. Each of SIGINT SIGTERM SIGHUP whose disposition is SIG_DFL gets an EVFILT_SIGNAL filter on a kqueue and is blocked (sigprocmask), and the child an EVFILT_PROC NOTE_EXIT filter; until waitpid(pid, WNOHANG) reports it, kevent waits, and each signal event is forwarded to the child's process group (kill(-pid), else kill(pid)). The blocked signal stays pending, so restoring the mask after the child is reaped (fflush(NULL) first) delivers it with its default action, as sys.c's raise does. With no kqueue the wait is a plain blocking waitpid; with no EVFILT_PROC filter kevent wakes every 10 ms. Returns waitpid's pid, or -errno; the status goes to the C int at stI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pollfdStoreInstrs" :text "Struct pollfd number idx (an i64) at pfdP gets fd (an i64) and events, revents cleared: events and revents go in one 32-bit store, which procFacts' layout check allows.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#reventsInstrs" :text "pre (i64): revents of struct pollfd number idx at pfdP, the high half of the 32-bit word at events.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitFwdLinuxFn" :text "procWaitFwd(pid, stI) -> i64 on linux: sys.c waitForwarding without a C signal handler. Each of SIGINT SIGTERM SIGHUP whose disposition is SIG_DFL is blocked and read from a signalfd; the child is watched by pidfd_open; until waitpid(pid, WNOHANG) reports it, poll waits on both, and each signal read is forwarded to the child's process group (kill(-pid), else kill(pid)) and raised again once the child is reaped and the mask restored (fflush(NULL) first). With no pidfd poll wakes every 10 ms. Returns waitpid's pid, or -errno; the status goes to the C int at stI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pidsCountFn" :text "procPidsCount(l) -> i64: the first pass of sys.c pidsArg, l's length when l is a List of Ints in 1..INT_MAX, else -1 (EINVAL).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pidsFillFn" :text "procPidsFill(l, p) -> i64: the second pass of sys.c pidsArg, l's Ints (procPidsCount checked them) as pid_t C ints at address p; returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wsLayout" :text "k plus the offsets in a wait set's calloc'd state block (sys.c's WaitSet and ChildWatch, with the scratch structs sys.c keeps on its stack): i64 slots ws.nReady ws.nExited ws.wfds ws.wn ws.regErr ws.pfd ws.masks ws.donePid ws.doneCode ws.nUser, ws.zero (a zero struct timespec, watchDrain's kevent timeout), ws.ts (monoMs's struct timespec), ws.status (a C int), ws.si (a siginfo_t), darwin ws.ev (one struct kevent) and ws.out (sixteen), and ws.size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wsAllocFn" :text "procWsAlloc(nUser, np) -> i64: sys.c waitSetAlloc, a wait set state block (wsLayout) holding calloc'd pfd (nUser + max(np,1) struct pollfd), masks (max(nUser,1) i64), donePid and doneCode (max(np,1) C ints each) and nUser; its address, or 0 (ENOMEM) after freeing whatever was allocated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wsFreeFn" :text "procWsFree(st) -> i64: sys.c waitSetFree of the wait set state block at address st, the block included; returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wsSlot" :text "pre (i64): the wait set state block's slot ws.<slot>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#watchRegFailBlocks" :text "regFail: a child watch that failed to register with ESRCH marks known[i] (the child is gone, so waitid may block on it); any other errno becomes regErr when none is recorded yet, as sys.c's watchOpen; then next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#watchOpenFn" :text "procWatchOpen(st, pids, np, known) -> i64: sys.c watchOpen into the wait set at st (ws.wfds, ws.wn, ws.regErr): nothing for np 0; darwin one kqueue (FD_CLOEXEC) with an EVFILT_PROC NOTE_EXIT EV_ONESHOT filter per pid, linux one pidfd_open per pid. 0, or the errno that left no watch (ENOMEM, kqueue's, fcntl's).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#watchCloseFn" :text "procWatchClose(st) -> i64: sys.c watchClose, close of each watch fd >= 0, free of the fd array, ws.wfds and ws.wn cleared; returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#watchDrainFn" :text "procWatchDrain(st, pids, np, known) -> i64: sys.c watchDrain, known[i] set for each child the watch reports gone: darwin reads the kqueue without blocking, sixteen events at a time, keeping EVFILT_PROC NOTE_EXIT events without EV_ERROR; linux takes the pidfds poll reported POLLIN or POLLHUP on. Returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#exitScanFn" :text "procExitScan(st, pids, np, known, exited) -> i64: sys.c exitScan, waitid(P_PID, pid, WEXITED|WNOWAIT, plus WNOHANG unless known[i]) on each pid (retried on EINTR) into the wait set's siginfo_t, exited[i] = si_pid != 0; the count of exited children, or -errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#reapFn" :text "procReap(pid, codeAt, stI) -> i64: sys.c reapPid, waitpid(pid, WNOHANG) retried on EINTR, the status at the C int stI and exitCodeOf it stored as the C int at codeAt; 0, ECHILD when the child is not ready, or errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitSetFn" :text "procWaitSet(st, pids, np, tms, reapAll) -> i64: sys.c waitSet over the wait set at st (its nUser user pollfds already filled): watchOpen, a deadline of tms ms (none when tms < 0 or > 2^50), then until something is ready: exitScan, regErr when no child exited, poll of the user fds and the watch fds (timeout 0 once a child exited, else what is left of the deadline), each ready user fd recorded in masks as (index << 3) | readable 1 | writable 2 | hangup/error 4, watchDrain and a second exitScan when the watch woke poll, and each exited child reaped (procReap) into donePid/doneCode, all of them when reapAll, else the first, a pid listed twice reaped once; stops on a ready fd, a reaped child or poll's timeout. 0, or the errno that stopped it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#wrapperP" :text "The routed wrapper asl-target-llvm/sysRoute.<name> over Val params, returning a Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pipeBlocks" :text "pipe0..pipe3: procPipeHigh of the stdin, stdout, stderr and report pipes into fds[0..7], the first failure going to pipeFail with its errno, else on to forkB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#spawnFn" :text "procSpawnv(argv, cwd, env) as sys.c bProcSpawnv: argv through procStrv (mapErrno of its errno), io:22 for an empty argv, for a cwd that is no Option, (some x) of a non-String, an empty String or one holding NUL (io:12 when its length scratch's malloc fails), env through procEnvArg (mapErrno), aslLogSpawn(argv[0]); four pipes through procPipeHigh (stdin, stdout, stderr and an exec report pipe, every end >= 3 and FD_CLOEXEC), fork; the child calls setpgid(0, 0), restores SIGPIPE to SIG_DFL, dup2s its ends onto 0, 1 and 2, chdirs, assigns environ (procEnvSlot, ENOSYS without one) and execvps, writing the errno of the first failing step to the report pipe before _exit(127); the parent calls setpgid(pid, pid), closes the child's ends, frees, reads the report (EINTR retried) and, given one, reaps the child, closes its own ends and returns mapErrno of it, else (ok {:pid :stdin :stdout :stderr}), a SpawnedProc record. The int[8] of pipe ends and the report and status ints live in one malloc'd block, which sys.c keeps on its stack (ENOMEM when it fails).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitPidFn" :text "procWaitPid(pid, nohang) as sys.c bProcWaitPid: io:22 unless pid is an Int and nohang a Bool, and for pid outside 1..INT_MAX; nohang: waitpid(pid, WNOHANG) retried on EINTR, else procWaitFwd (the blocking wait that forwards SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP); mapErrno of an errno, (ok (none)) while the child runs, else (ok (some exitCodeOf(status))). The status int lives in a malloc'd cell (ENOMEM when it fails).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#timeoutBlocks" :text "label and its successor: sys.c timeoutArg, io:22 (inval) unless msV is an Int >= -1, which goes on to next as tms.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#waitAnyFn" :text "procWaitAny(pids, timeoutMs) as sys.c bProcWaitAny: timeoutArg first (io:22), then pidsArg (mapErrno EINVAL for no List or a pid outside 1..INT_MAX, ENOMEM), io:22 for no pids; procWaitSet reaping the first child that exits within the timeout: (ok (some (pair pid exitCode))), (ok (none)) on timeout, or mapErrno of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pollFn" :text "procPoll(fds, pids, timeoutMs) as sys.c bProcPoll: io:22 unless fds is a List and timeoutArg holds; pidsArg (mapErrno); io:12 when the wait set's allocation fails; each fds item through pollItem (badFd for an fd outside 0..INT_MAX, io:22 for any other shape) with a mask in 1..3 (io:22), readable POLLIN and writable POLLOUT; procWaitSet reaping every exited child: (ok (pair ready exited)), ready the (pair fd mask) of each ready fd in fds order (mask readable 1, writable 2, hangup/error 4), exited the (pair pid exitCode) of each child reaped; or mapErrno of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#rusageDecode" :text "The three Rusage fields of the struct rusage at up+base, boxed as <tag>.rss, <tag>.user and <tag>.sys: ru_maxrss over unit (sys.c maxRssKb) and ru_utime, ru_stime as tv_sec*1000000 + tv_usec (sys.c cpuUs), tv_usec read as its low 32 bits, which hold it on darwin (an int) and on little-endian linux (a long below 1000000).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#rusageFn" :text "procRusage() as sys.c bProcRusage: getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF) and getrusage(RUSAGE_CHILDREN) into one malloc'd pair of struct rusage (sys.c's stack; ENOMEM when it fails), mapErrno of the first failure's errno, else (ok {:selfMaxRssKb :selfUserUs :selfSysUs :childrenMaxRssKb :childrenUserUs :childrenSysUs}), a Rusage record; ru_maxrss is divided by libc/rusageMaxRssUnit (sys.c RSS_UNIT).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#execvFn" :text "procExecv(argv, env) as sys.c bProcExecv: argv through procStrv (mapErrno of its errno), io:22 for an empty argv, aslLogSpawn(argv[0]), env through procEnvArg (mapErrno), fflush(NULL); given env, environ (procEnvSlot, ENOSYS without one) is pointed at it; SIGPIPE back to SIG_DFL, execvp, and only when it returns: SIGPIPE to SIG_IGN again, environ restored, both arrays freed and mapErrno of execvp's errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procRouteBuiltins" :text "The process builtins whose asl-target-llvm/sysRoute wrappers are built natively in this module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procPreludeGlobals" :text "Module-owned process handle state used by native processSpawn/processWait, preserving one monotonically increasing id and the active linked-list head across builtin calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processHandleStateInitFn" :text "One-time state initializer: a 16-byte cell stores next id at byte 0 and the active handle-list head at byte 8. A failed allocation initializes to boxed zero, which callers report as ENOMEM.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procRouteExterns" :text "The externs the process wrappers call beyond sys/sysExterns: fork, exec, pipe and wait calls, signal masks and dispositions, aslLogSpawn (libaslrt.a's spawn log), valToCStrN; darwin adds kqueue, kevent and _NSGetEnviron, linux signalfd, syscall (pidfd_open) and dlsym. void C functions are declared returning i64, as free is, and their result is unused.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procRouteStrings" :text "The pool strings the process wrappers read.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procRouteRecords" :text "The record schemas the process wrappers build: sys.c bProcSpawnv's SpawnedProc and bProcRusage's Rusage, keys in sys.c's order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processRunFn" :text "Native processRun: /bin/sh -c command with the inherited stdin, no new process group, and two independently polled output pipes. Each stream is read until EOF (including pipe writers inherited by backgrounded descendants), then the direct child's shell-compatible exit code and both byte strings form ProcessOutput. A poll failure other than EINTR ends reading and reaps the child with what was collected, as prelude.c bProcessRun does; a short capture write is out of memory. open_memstream owns unbounded, NUL-safe stream buffers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processFormatErrFn" :text "The prelude formatErr(kind,path,reason) byte shape: `kind: path: reason`, wrapped as Result.err String.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processSpawnFn" :text "Native prelude processSpawn: validate the command and embedded NUL, create and unlink two CLOEXEC temp files, fork `/bin/sh -c`, make the child a new process group with /dev/null stdin, and insert the parent fds under a monotonically increasing global handle. The record layout is 40 bytes: handle, pid, output fd, error fd, next pointer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processIoErrFn" :text "The prelude ioErr(path, errno) rendering: IoError-kind, path, and strerror text joined with `: `, then Result.err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processIsIntFn" :text "Check the runtime integer tag by comparing tagOf's ABI tag for the input with the tag of an integer boxed here, without baking in the Tag enum value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#processWaitFn" :text "Native processWait consumes the native processHandleState list entry, waits for its child, slurps both unlinked output files, and returns ProcessOutput.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procRouteFunctions" :text "The process wrappers and their helpers for the triple of facts, pool mapping each string they read to its index, or procFacts' build-time err naming a fact libc.asl lacks for the triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#" :text "Routes a verified SsaModule's host-builtin calls to the ASL syscall functions of this package instead of libaslrt.a's C builtin tables (plan rows NETLOWER and NATIVE-netBuiltinLowering). routeModule rewrites every opBuiltin whose name a routing table lists into an opCall of that table's wrapper, asl-target-llvm/sysRoute.<builtin>, and adds the table's functions (its asl-target-llvm/sys* functions plus one wrapper per builtin), its externs (deduplicated by name against the module's own; a same-named extern with another signature is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_EXTERN), the types and record schemas its wrappers use when the module lacks them and the strings they read (tableStrings) to the module's string pool, reusing a string already there, only for tables the module calls; a module function already named like an added one is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_NAME. A wrapper checks its argument as the VM's C builtin does and maps the raw errno Result of the sys* function to the VM's shape, (ok v) or (err \"io:N\") with N the errno, (err \"io:<EINVAL>\") for an invalid argument. internalize gives the added functions internal linkage in the emitted text, so every module of a separately compiled program carries its own private copy and no symbol is defined twice at link. The tables are sysNetTable (tcpListen, tcpConnect, sockAccept, sockLocalPort, unixListen, unixConnect, and unixSocketPair, sockSendFd and sockRecvFd for SCM_RIGHTS descriptor passing, which asl/host/src/sysNet.c has no builtin for yet, over asl-target-llvm/sysNet) and sysTable (plan unit SYSLOWER-a: fdRead, fdWrite, fdClose, fdPoll, fdNonBlocking, cpuCount, platformInfo, localDate, envList, procSelf, procAlive?, procKill, procExePath over asl-target-llvm/sys and libc externs), whose wrappers return exactly sys.c's VM shapes: its tag checks (intOf, isString, boolOf, isList, read from a value's printed form since asl-ir has no tag test), argument ranges, literal err texts (badFd, io:22, io:12, io:38) and mapErrno (errnoErr), plus the Pair type and the PlatformInfo record schema they build; a module's own PlatformInfo schema with other fields is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_RECORD. clockTable (PRELUDEASL-A) routes nowNs and monotonicNs over clock_gettime and sleepMs over nanosleep, resumed on EINTR, with prelude.c's ERR_TYPE, ERR_RANGE and ERR_IO texts instead of sys.c's shapes; it stays apart from sysTable so a program that only reads a clock does not carry sysTable's functions. A further table is a RouteTable variant with its rows in tableBuiltins, tableExterns, tableStrings, tableTypes, tableRecords and tableFunctions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routeTables" :text "Every routing table, in the order routeModule adds their functions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableBuiltins" :text "The builtin names a table routes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableStrings" :text "The strings a table's wrappers read from the module's string pool.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableTypes" :text "The ADTs a table's functions construct or switch on, added when the module lacks them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableRecords" :text "The record schemas a table's functions build, added when the module lacks them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableGlobals" :text "The module globals a table's functions read, each initialised by one of its functions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tableFunctions" :text "A table's syscall functions for the triple followed by its wrappers, or the first build-time err a missing libc.asl fact produces; pool maps each of tableStrings to its index in the module's string pool.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#wrapperName" :text "The function a routed call of builtin calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#int32Max" :text "C INT_MAX, the largest fd bSockAccept and bSockLocalPort accept, and the largest i32 the sysNet functions take.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#netWrappers" :text "The sysNet wrappers with sysNet.c's argument ranges: a port 0..65535 (tcpConnect 1..65535, as bTcpConnect rejects port 0), an fd 0..INT_MAX, a unix path a String; sockSendFd's socket and fd and sockRecvFd's socket are fds in the same range, and unixSocketPair takes nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#showInstr" :text "(str v): the display text the host's str builtin gives, through asl_rt_builtin's core table.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sameReprInstrs" :text "prefix.same (i1): whether (str (list a)) equals (str (list b)). Inside a list str prints each element as data, a String quoted and a Float with its point or exponent, so the two texts are equal exactly when a and b are the same value of the same type; = itself would trap on two types, as valEq does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#resultBlocks" :text "The blocks after a wrapper's call: res, the sysNet function's Val (Result Int64 Int64), is returned as is when ok; its raw errno, or einval from the bad block, becomes (err \"io:N\") as sysNet.c's netErrno and netBad build it, from the pool's \"io:\" at ioIndex.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#intWrapper" :text "wrapperName builtin (arg: Val) -> Val: callee(i32) when arg is an Int in lo..hi, else (err io:EINVAL), as sysNet.c's intArg/portArg range check does. There is no tag test on a Val in asl-ir, so the Int test is built from host builtins: arg's display text parses (stringToFloat64) to a number f in lo..hi, n = floatToInt f, and (list arg) prints as (list n) does (sameReprInstrs), which holds exactly when arg is the Int n; an Int too large for a float to hold exactly is far outside lo..hi, so it is rejected either way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#pathWrapper" :text "wrapperName builtin (arg: Val) -> Val: callee(arg) when arg is a String, else (err io:EINVAL), as sysNet.c's stringArg does; the String is a String exactly when (list arg) prints as (list (str arg)) does, str of a String being the String itself. The callee checks the path's length and NUL bytes as unixAddr does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#intCheckBlocks" :text "The Int test of arg in lo..hi that intWrapper and intPairWrapper run, as blocks <prefix>.entry, <prefix>.number and <prefix>.whole, jumping to goodLabel with <prefix>.n (i64) defined, else to bad.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#intPairWrapper" :text "wrapperName builtin (arg: Val, arg2: Val) -> Val: callee(i32, i32) when both are Ints in lo..hi (intCheckBlocks, intWrapper's test), else (err io:EINVAL).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#unitWrapper" :text "wrapperName builtin () -> Val: callee(), its raw errno err mapped to io:N as the other wrappers map it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#builtinNames" :text "The set of builtin names m's opBuiltin instructions call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tablesUsed" :text "The routing tables m calls a builtin of.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routes?" :text "True when m calls a builtin some routing table routes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routedCallee" :text "The wrapper a routed call of builtin with argc operands calls: wrapperName, except for fileLockWait, which sys.c's table lists with arity -1 and bFileLockWait reads as 1, 2 or 3 operands: its wrapper is fileLockWait/1, /2 or /3 by argc, and fileLockWait/bad (no parameters, sys.c's n < 1 || n > 3 io:22) for any other count.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routedArgs" :text "The operands a routed call passes: all of them, except to fileLockWait/bad, which takes none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#rewriteFunction" :text "f with each opBuiltin of a routed name turned into an opCall of its wrapper, same dest, type and arguments (the wrapper takes and returns Val, as the builtin call did).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#dedupeExterns" :text "One extern per name, the last of each, in first-seen order: sys/sysCommonExterns and a table's own copies of shared externs (fcntl, close) repeat a name with the same signature.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#mergeExterns" :text "own followed by each added extern own has no extern of that name for; an added extern whose name own declares with another signature is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_EXTERN.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#dedupeFunctions" :text "One function per name, the first: two tables may each carry sys/sysErrnoValueFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#withTypes" :text "own plus each added ADT (Result and Option as asl-ir/lower declares them, Pair as the prelude does) whose name own lacks: the wrappers construct and switch on them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#mergeRecords" :text "own plus each added record schema own lacks; an own schema of an added name with other fields is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_RECORD, since the wrapper builds the record with the added fields.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#poolAt" :text "The pool index of s, -1 (which asl-ir/verify rejects as ERR_IR_STRING_INDEX) for a string no table listed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#poolWith" :text "strings with each wanted string it lacks appended, and the index of every wanted string in the result: a string already in the pool is reused.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routeModule" :text "m routed for the triple of facts: unchanged, with no internal names, when it calls no routed builtin on native targets; else verified (its own diagnostics when it does not verify) and rewritten as this module's :d describes. wasm32 targets verify even modules without imports, rewrite print with unique spaced calls, and reject calls to native routing-table builtins without wasm implementations with ERR_CAPABILITY_ABSENT; other builtin names are not classified by this router and remain for later lowering.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tripleOf" :text "The libc/libcTriples triple of a host whose uname sysname and machine (uname -s and uname -m) are os and machine, empty for a host libc.asl covers no triple of.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routeFactsFor" :text "The facts a native build on a host of triple routes for: the triple's libc.asl row when libc.asl marks it verified (measured on such a host: darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64, plan unit SYSLINUX), none for an unmeasured row or a triple libc.asl lacks, whose programs keep the C builtin tables of libaslhost.a and cannot lower a builtin with no native definition (envGet and the other prelude builtins only routing defines).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#unamePair" :text "The sysname and machine uname -s -m printed as text, none unless text is exactly two words.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#hostFactsOf" :text "The facts routeFactsFor gives the host whose uname -s -m printed text: (ok (none)) for a host without a verified libc.asl row, whose native programs keep the C builtin tables of libaslhost.a, and an err when text is not two words.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routeHost!" :text "m routed for the host this runs on: routeModule at routeFactsFor of the host's triple (tripleOf over uname -s -m, through processRun, which asl-ir/lower lowers, unlike platformInfo), or m unchanged when that triple has no verified row; a failing uname or output that is not two words is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_HOST. uname runs only when m calls a routed builtin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#internalize" :text "res with each function of names, defined by asl-target-llvm/ssa as define tailcc <ty> @<llvmName>(, given internal linkage, so the routed functions stay private to the module that carries them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#signalNames" :text "The signal names procKill accepts, in sys.c's sysSignals order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#errKinds" :text "sys.c sysErrKind's named errnos and their err texts, in its switch order; EWOULDBLOCK equals EAGAIN on every triple libc.asl covers, so the EAGAIN row stands for both. Any other errno is io:N.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sysStrings" :text "The sys table's pool strings: io: for io:N, the literal err texts sys.c returns (badFd, io:22, io:12, io:38), sysErrKind's names, the empty String fdRead 0 gives, ((pair  for fdPoll's item test, - and 0 for localDate, and the signal names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#routeConst" :text "The triple's value of name, libc.asl's row (EROFS, EOVERFLOW, POLLPRI, POLLERR, POLLHUP and the signal numbers included, each probed by libcTableTest on darwin-arm64).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#structFact" :text "libc.asl's offset of structName.field, or the struct's size when field is size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sysFactNames" :text "Every libc fact the sys wrappers read: constants by name, struct facts as struct.field.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sysFacts" :text "sysFactNames resolved for the triple, or a build-time err naming the first one libc.asl has no row for; also an err when pollfd's revents does not follow events by 2 bytes, the layout fdPoll's one 32-bit store and load of both rely on.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fact" :text "A fact sysFacts resolved; every name read here is in sysFactNames.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#pairTypeDecl" :text "The prelude's Pair enum, (pair first second), whose ctor fdPoll's ready list holds, as sys.c's mkPairVal builds it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#platformInfoDecl" :text "sys.c bPlatformInfo's record: schema PlatformInfo, keys os, release and machine in that order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#nsGetEnvironExtern" :text "darwin's char ***_NSGetEnviron(void), as asl-target-llvm/sysProc reads the inherited environment.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#errTextBlock" :text "label returns (err text), text a pool string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#okBlock" :text "label runs pre and returns (ok value).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#mapErrnoBlock" :text "label returns errnoErr of the raw errno code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#errnoBlock" :text "label reads errno before cleanup (frees may clobber it), runs cleanup and returns errnoErr of it, as sys.c's mapErrno(errno).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#resultErrBlock" :text "label maps the err arm of a sys* function's Result, its raw errno, through errnoErr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#outsideInstrs" :text "prefix.out (i1): v < lo or v > hi.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#intOfFn" :text "intOf(v) -> (Option Int): (some v) exactly when v is an Int, as sys.c's tag test a.tag == T_INT. asl-ir has no tag test on a Val, so v's display text is parsed as a decimal int64 (an optional - and digits, overflow checked by accumulating downward from 0, which also covers INT64_MIN) and the parsed n is accepted only when (list v) prints as (list n) does (sameReprInstrs): a String of digits prints quoted inside a list, a Float with its point, so only the Int n passes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#isStringFn" :text "isString(v) -> i1: v is a String (T_STR) exactly when (list v) prints as (list (str v)) does, str of a String being the String itself, as pathWrapper tests it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#boolOfFn" :text "boolOf(v) -> i64: 1 when v is true, 0 when false, -1 when v is no Bool (T_BOOL), by comparing (list v)'s text with (list true)'s and (list false)'s.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#letterInstrs" :text "prefix.letter (i1): the byte b is an ASCII letter, the first byte of a constructor's name in a printed value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#reprBytesInstrs" :text "repr: the text of (list v); bytes: its bytes; b1 and b2: its second and third byte. The text is at least 3 bytes, ( and ) around v's own non-empty print form.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#absExtern" :text "libc's int abs(int), declared to take a %Val by value: tagOf's read of a value's tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tagOfFn" :text "tagOf(v) -> i64: v's runtime tag, asl/host/src/value.h's Tag, the field sys.c's a.tag == T_* tests read. asl-ir has no tag operation, so v is passed by value to libc's abs(int): on arm64 and x86_64 alike the %Val {i64, i64} travels in two integer registers, the first holding {u32 tag, u32 aux}, and an int parameter is that register's low 32 bits, so abs reads the tag; a tag is small and never negative, so abs returns it unchanged. The tag tests (tagTestFn) compare it with the tag of a value of the wanted type built in place, so no Tag number is written down here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tagGuardText" :text "tagCheck's stderr line when abs did not return a tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tagCheckFn" :text "tagCheck(t) -> i64: t when it lies in 0..255, which every value.h Tag does; otherwise tagOf's ABI assumption broke (a %Val passed indirectly, so abs read a pointer or garbage), and tagCheck prints tagGuardText to stderr through eprintln and traps (an unreachable terminator, rterr.match by the function name, exit 1) rather than let a tag test answer wrongly.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#tagTestFn" :text "name(v) -> i1: v's tag (tagOf) equals the tag of ex, the value the exemplar instructions build.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#isListFn" :text "isList(v) -> i1: v is a List (T_LIST), as fdPoll's first argument must be: v's tag equals (list)'s, sys.c's a[0].tag != T_LIST test. Unit, whose text is the empty List's, is no List here, so fdPoll of unit is io:22 as in sys.c rather than an empty poll.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#isStrFn" :text "isStr(v) -> i1: v is a String (T_STR), sys.c's a.tag == T_STR, by tag rather than by printed form.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#isBytesFn" :text "isBytes(v) -> i1: v is Bytes (T_BYTES), the other data bFileAppend writes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#optionArgFn" :text "optionArg(v) -> i64: sys.c's optionArg, 0 for (none), 1 for (some x), -1 for anything else. v must be a constructor (the tag of (none), T_CTOR); it is none when (list v) prints as (list (none)) does, and some when that text starts ((some  and v prints as (some f0) of its own first field does, which also rejects a constructor named some of another arity, as c->n == 1 does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#errnoErrFn" :text "errnoErr(code) -> (err text): sys.c's mapErrno, errKinds' text for its named errnos (the triple's values), io:N for any other N.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#pollItemFn" :text "pollItem(item) -> (Result (pair fd mask) Int): sys.c's fdPairArg. item is (pair fd mask) or a List of at least two elements whose first two are fd and mask; (ok (pair fd mask)) when both are Ints and fd is in 0..INT_MAX, (err 2) for an fd out of range (badFd), (err 1) for any other shape (io:22). The shape is read from (list item)'s text as isList reads it: a constructor prints its name after ((, and only pair's ((pair  prefix is a pair; a List whose first element is a symbol named pair is the one value this reads as a pair.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#intArgBlocks" :text "label tests arg with intOf into label.opt, going on to next when it is an Int and to fail when not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdRangeBlock" :text "label unboxes intOf's (some fd) in opt to fd and fd32, and goes to badFd unless fd is in 0..INT_MAX, as sys.c's fd range check.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdReadFn" :text "fdRead(fd, max) as sys.c bFdRead: badFd unless both are Ints and fd in 0..INT_MAX, io:22 for max outside 0..2^24, (ok \"\") for max 0, else read(2) into a malloc'd buffer (io:12 when malloc fails) returned as a String of the bytes read, or errnoErr of read's errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdWriteFn" :text "fdWrite(fd, s) as sys.c bFdWrite: badFd unless fd is an Int, io:22 unless s is a String, badFd for fd outside 0..INT_MAX, else sys/sysWrite's (ok written) or errnoErr of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdCloseFn" :text "fdClose(fd) as sys.c bFdClose: badFd unless fd is an Int in 0..INT_MAX, else sys/sysClose, (ok ()) or errnoErr of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdNonBlockingFn" :text "fdNonBlocking(fd, on) as sys.c bFdNonBlocking: badFd unless fd is an Int, io:22 unless on is a Bool, badFd for fd outside 0..INT_MAX, else F_GETFL, O_NONBLOCK set or cleared, F_SETFL (sys/sysFcntlGet and sysFcntlSet), (ok ()) or errnoErr of the failing call's errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#fdPollFn" :text "fdPoll(items, ms) as sys.c bFdPoll: io:22 unless items is a List (isList) and ms an Int of at least -1, ms above INT_MAX polls INT_MAX; no items is poll(NULL, 0, ms) and (ok ()); else one struct pollfd per item (pollItem: io:22 or badFd for a bad item, events POLLIN for mask bit 1 and POLLOUT for bit 2) in a malloc'd array (io:12 when malloc fails), poll, and (ok ready) with ready the (pair fd m) of each item whose revents is set, in item order, m 1 for POLLIN or POLLPRI, 2 for POLLOUT, 4 for POLLHUP, POLLERR or POLLNVAL; errnoErr of poll's errno when it fails. events and revents are one 32-bit word (sysFacts checks the layout): its store clears revents, its load's high half is revents.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#cpuCountFn" :text "cpuCount() as sys.c bCpuCount: errno cleared, then sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN); (ok c) for c at least 1, else errnoErr of errno, or io:38 when sysconf left errno 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#platformInfoFn" :text "platformInfo() as sys.c bPlatformInfo: uname(2) into a malloc'd struct utsname, then (ok {:os sysname :release release :machine machine}), a PlatformInfo record; errnoErr of errno when malloc, uname or a field copy fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#padBlocks" :text "prefix.check and two blocks giving the decimal text of n with a leading 0 below 10, as strftime's %m and %d, to join's one Val parameter.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#localDateFn" :text "localDate() as sys.c bLocalDate: the wall clock's seconds (the nowNs wrapper's Int over 10^9, time(NULL)'s truncation) through sys/sysLocaltime, then (ok \"YYYY-MM-DD\") as strftime %Y-%m-%d; errnoErr of localtime_r's errno, EOVERFLOW when it left errno 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#environInstrs" :text "envp: the process's char **environ, through darwin's _NSGetEnviron (one more load) or the environ global elsewhere, as asl-target-llvm/sysProc realEnvironBlocks reads it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#envListFn" :text "envList() as sys.c bEnvList: every NAME=value string of environ, in environ's order, as a List (no Result).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#procSelfFn" :text "procSelf() as sys.c bProcSelf: getpid() as an Int (no Result).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#procAliveFn" :text "procAlive?(pid) as sys.c bProcAlive: io:22 unless pid is an Int in 1..INT_MAX, else kill(pid, 0): (ok true) on success or EPERM, (ok false) on ESRCH, errnoErr of any other errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#procKillFn" :text "procKill(pid, signal) as sys.c bProcKill: io:22 unless pid is an Int and signal a String, pid within -INT_MAX..INT_MAX and outside -1..1, and signal one of signalNames; else kill(pid, the triple's number for signal), (ok ()) or errnoErr of its errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#procExePathFn" :text "procExePath() as sys.c bProcExePath: sys/sysExePath's (ok path), or errnoErr of its errno (ERANGE for a path longer than PATH_MAX).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#ioTrapInstrs" :text "Fails as prelude.c aslError(\"ERR_IO\", \"<prefix>%s\", strerror(errno)) does, errno the raw i64 code: through the host's trap builtin, the path a source-level trap lowers to (rtError's rterr.trap). The block holding these ends unreachable.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#clockFn" :text "nowNs() (clockId CLOCK_REALTIME) or monotonicNs() (CLOCK_MONOTONIC) as prelude.c bClockRealtimeNs and bClockMonotonicNs (PRELUDEASL-A): sys/sysClockGettime's tv_sec * 1000000000 + tv_nsec as an Int; a clock_gettime error is ERR_IO '<builtin>: strerror(errno)' (ioTrapInstrs).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sleepMsFn" :text "sleepMs(ms) as prelude.c bSleepMs (PRELUDEASL-A): want(ms, T_INT)'s ERR_TYPE 'sleepMs expects Int, got <tag>' (tagOf, clockTagName), ERR_RANGE 'sleepMs: <ms> is negative' for ms < 0, else nanosleep of ms/1000 seconds and (ms mod 1000) * 10^6 nanoseconds into malloc'd req and rem timespecs laid out by libc.asl's timespec row, resumed from rem's remaining time while it fails with EINTR, and unit; any other nanosleep errno, or a failed malloc of either timespec (whose errno ENOMEM stands where prelude.c's stack copies cannot fail), is ERR_IO 'sleepMs: nanosleep: strerror(errno)' (ioTrapInstrs) after both buffers it holds are freed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#clockTagNames" :text "value.c tagName, indexed by value.h Tag, as rtError's own tag table lists it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#clockStrings" :text "The clock table's pool strings: prelude.c's texts for its three builtins, tagCheck's guard line and clockTagName's names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#clockTagNameFn" :text "clockTagName(tag) -> String: value.c tagName of a tagOf tag, ? past the table, as prelude.c want's message names the type it got.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#clockTableFunctions" :text "The clock table's functions: sys.asl's sysErrnoValue and sysClockGettime, the tag helpers tagOf, tagCheck and clockTagName, and the nowNs, monotonicNs and sleepMs wrappers; or the first build-time err a missing fact produces.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sysTableFunctions" :text "The sys table's functions: the sys.asl builders the wrappers call (sysErrnoValue, sysWrite, sysClose, sysFcntlGet, sysFcntlSet, sysLocaltime, sysExePath, sysClockGettime), the helpers intOf, isString, boolOf, isList, errnoErr and pollItem, the 13 wrappers and the clock table's nowNs, which localDate reads; or the first build-time err a missing fact produces.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysRoute.asl#sysTableAll" :text "sysTableFunctions followed by the file wrappers of asl-target-llvm/sys (fileRouteFunctions) and the process wrappers of asl-target-llvm/sysProc (procRouteFunctions), or the first build-time err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#" :text "Target-independent emission facts shared by the LLVM backend and the collector.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#nativeTargetFacts" :text "Native target properties retained byte-for-byte by legacy emission.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#wasm32TargetFacts" :text "wasm32 target properties for object emission; traps and host imports are subsequent units.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#isWasm32" :text "True for wasm32 facts: triple wasm32-unknown-unknown with 32-bit pointers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#growsLinearMemory" :text "Collector pages come from memory.grow on linear memory 0 rather than mmap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#llvmDefineSignature" :text "Extracts return type and parameter types from an LLVM define statement.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#llvmCallSignature" :text "Extracts return type and argument types from an LLVM call statement.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#lowerLlvmLines" :text "Lower LLVM lines while carrying the enclosing definition's signature to validate wasm musttail calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/target.asl#lowerLlvmText" :text "Emitted LLVM text for facts: memory.grow uses its intrinsic name; wasm32 uses C calling convention because LLVM does not implement tailcc, retains musttail only for matching caller and callee signatures, and marks definitions for the tail-call feature; global lines (string constants) are left unchanged, and native mmap text is returned unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/types.asl#" :text "LLVM IR backend type mapping, closure environment synthesis, and panic generation")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/types.asl#emitLlvmType" :text "Maps an IR type to its LLVM IR type representation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/types.asl#emitLlvmClosure" :text "Emits an LLVM struct type declaration for a closure environment.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/types.asl#emitLlvmPanic" :text "Emits LLVM instructions to call panic with an error code and trap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/types.asl#emitLlvmTargetTriple" :text "Maps a target architecture string to an LLVM target triple directive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmAlloc.asl#" :text "The wasm32 linear-memory allocator as LLVM IR text, the malloc, free, realloc and calloc the program, collector and runtime modules call on a libc-free target (asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime supportText links it). A block is an 8-byte header (capacity, free-list next) then its bytes rounded up to 8; malloc takes the first freed block that fits, else carves from the allocator's own run of pages, a new run of at least 16 wasm pages (1 MiB) taken by memory.grow when the run is short, and returns null when memory cannot grow. The run is the allocator's own: memory grown by another party (the collector's memory.grow page source) between two runs is never handed out, since a run continues only when memory.grow returns the run's own end. free pushes the block on the free list; realloc keeps a block whose capacity holds the new size, else copies into a new one; calloc zeroes count times width bytes, null on overflow. asl_wasm_free is free returning an unused i64, the shape the collector's SSA externs declare (asl-target-llvm/gcAsl freeName). Single-threaded, as wasm32 without shared memory is.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmAlloc.asl#allocatorImports" :text "The LLVM intrinsics wasmAllocatorText calls: memory.grow, which lowers to the memory.grow instruction, and memcpy and memset, which lower to memory.copy and memory.fill under the bulk-memory feature; none is a host import.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmAlloc.asl#wasmAllocatorText" :text "The allocator's definitions, as this module's :d describes, one LLVM line per element.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmFormat.asl#" :text "Number formatting and parsing for wasm32 as LLVM IR text, the C-ABI snprintf, dprintf, strtod and atoi the shared emitted IR (asl-target-llvm/rtFormat, rtError, the collector) calls, which asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime supportText links into a libc-free program. asl_wasm_vformat is the printf core: flags - 0 + space #, a width or precision as digits or *, the length modifiers hh h l ll z j t L and the conversions d i u x X o c s p e E f F %%, an integer read at the LP64 width the emitted IR passes (l ll z j t: i64; none h hh: i32), %p and %s a pointer ((null) for a null %s, 0x0 for a null %p), any other conversion a gcFloorFail ERR_INTERNAL naming the format. %e and %f are exact: asl_wasm_dec_digits writes a double's complete decimal expansion from a base-1e9 big integer (the mantissa times 2^e or 5^-e) and asl_wasm_dec_round rounds it to the precision, ties to even, as Darwin and glibc printf do; inf and nan print as inf, -inf and nan (upper case under E and F). strtod reads leading white space, a sign, then inf, infinity or nan in any case, or decimal digits with an optional point and exponent (at most 800 significant digits kept, a nonzero tail beyond them kept as a sticky digit), and rounds to the nearest double, ties to even: a double estimate from the first 19 digits is corrected one ulp at a time by comparing the exact decimal value with the halfway points beside it in big integers (asl_wasm_cmp_decimal); hexadecimal floats are not read, the number ending before the x, and errno is not set, wasm32 having none. atoi reads white space, a sign and decimal digits, wrapping in i32.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmFormat.asl#formatImports" :text "The LLVM intrinsics and C-ABI functions formatText calls beyond its own: va_start, va_copy and va_end, fabs and trap (a big-integer capacity overrun, which the sizes here rule out), malloc and free (asl-target-llvm/wasmAlloc), and asl_wasm_write_all and gcFloorFail (asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmFormat.asl#formatText" :text "The formatting definitions, as this module's :d describes, one LLVM line per element.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmLink.asl#" :text "Links wasm32 objects with wasm-ld and reads a linked module's import section. linkWasm32 never passes --allow-undefined, so a symbol no object defines fails the link, and passes --fatal-warnings, so a function signature mismatch between objects (which wasm-ld otherwise bridges with a trapping stub) fails it too; the entry is _start (asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime), linear memory is exported, the stack is 1 MiB and each name in exports is exported as well. wasmImports lists the module.name of every import in the section, read by Node's WebAssembly.Module.imports from the bytes themselves; importsOutside is the part of such a list not in an allowed list.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmLink.asl#linkWasm32" :text "wasm-ld over objects into output, as this module's :d describes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmLink.asl#wasmImports" :text "The module.name of each import of the module in the file wasm, in section order; an err with Node's stderr when the bytes do not compile as a module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmLink.asl#importsOutside" :text "The imports not in allowed, in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#" :text "The support module a libc-free wasm32 program links beside its own object and its collector's (asl-target-llvm emitLlvmSupportForTarget): asl-target-llvm/wasmAlloc's allocator, asl-target-llvm/wasmFormat's number formatting and parsing, and the C-ABI services the shared emitted IR calls, all LLVM IR, importing only the host services the target's libc runtimeAbi row names. _start runs main and exits with its result; exit runs the atexit functions (up to 32), last first, then calls the host exit; write and asl_wasm_write_all go to the host write, fflush has no buffer to flush getenv finds no variable and unsetenv has none to remove, wasm32 having no environment; asl_rt_init and asl_rt_global_root are abi.c's (the collector initialised, then some, none, ok, err and partial interned first, and a growing table of module global slots), gcMutatorRoots marks those slots as abi.c's abiGcRoots does, gcFloorFail is strFloor.c's (CODE: message on fd 2, exit 1), asl_wasm_exit and asl_wasm_now_ns are the i64-shaped exit and the host clock the collector's SSA externs call (asl-target-llvm/gcAsl exitName and clockName), and memcmp, strcmp, strchr, strlen, memset, memcpy and qsort (an insertion sort) are C's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#importAttrs" :text "The wasm import attributes of a runtimeAbi service module.name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#hostImportDecls" :text "The host imports runtimeText calls, each named by the runtimeAbi row: asl_wasm_host_write (fd, bytes, length -> bytes written) from its output service, asl_wasm_host_exit from its exit service and asl_wasm_host_now_ns (monotonic nanoseconds) from its clock service.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#runtimeDecls" :text "The functions runtimeText calls in the program and collector objects: main, the collector's gcInit and the program's intern table entry aslInternShared (asl-target-llvm/rtValue).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#runtimeText" :text "The C-ABI service definitions, as this module's :d describes, one LLVM line per element.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/wasmRuntime.asl#supportText" :text "The whole support module for a runtimeAbi row: the wasm32 triple, the host imports, the intrinsics and cross-object declarations, then the allocator, the runtime services and the formatter.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#" :text "SSA programs for the runtime ABI gate (plan SH unit A1, asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest). alloc builds a list of n Ints with cons in a loop, sums it by the module loop foldVals calling a compiled closure, maps a capturing compiled closure over rangeVals with mapVals (fold, map and range left the runtime in plan RT-PRELUDE P3b, so these loops are SSA in the module), walks the mapped list with listHead, listTail and a tag switch, concatenates a string m times, stores two results in a record, reads element 7 through the fused listGetOr entry and the field of a compiled some, no prelude function by name, prints the figures and exits 0 only when every figure equals its closed form; allocSmall is the same program small enough to run with a collection on every allocation. The fail programs each end in one runtime error, except negate and negateFloat, which check unary minus, and switchPick, which switches on the third and second variant of a three-variant type and exits 3; switchInt switches on an Int and switchForeign on a variant of another type; asserts passes two asserts and a refute, then fails an assert. joined, failed and tooBig are entries taking the argument list and returning a Result, as asl-host run mains do. deepTail recurses a million calls deep through three self tail calls, one returned through a join block, one returned directly and one returned through a chain of two joins, and exits 42. nestedTail is source whose self tail calls sit in if and mt arms three deep, run a million deep, and exits 42. main prints the named program's .ll")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#listWalk" :text "A loop over the list in the first state slot: entry jumps to loop with start; loop reads listHead, none returns done, some binds x and rest and runs step, then jumps back with next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#foldValsFn" :text "fold by hand: the compiled closure f is called from compiled code once per element (plan RT-PRELUDE P3b moved fold out of the runtime).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#fusedVariantFn" :text "A some/none switch whose some arm reads field 0 by opVariantField then opUnbox to t, the only use, so it fuses (RT-INLINE-2); test computes \"ok\" (i1) from \"xi\" (the unboxed value, typed t) and 42 is wired through unused valInt yes/no to a pass/fail branch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#fusedVariantRangeFn" :text "opVariantField past the end of a 1-field variant, unboxed to Int: bounds-checked on the fast path, falls to objrt.variantField, which gives ERR_RANGE as the unfused path always did.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#fusedVariantWrongTagFn" :text "opVariantField field 0 holds a String, unboxed to Int: the fast path's own Val-tag check misses, falls to asl_rt_unbox_int, which gives ERR_TYPE as the unfused path always did.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#fusedRecordIntFn" :text "Two record fields read by opField then opUnbox to Int, each the only use, so both fuse; the sum must equal the closed form.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#fusedRecordMissingKeyFn" :text "opField names a key absent from Pair2's declared fields, unboxed to Int: the fast path's scan exhausts the record's keys without a match, falls to objrt.field, which gives ERR_FIELD as the unfused path always did.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#staticFieldRecordFn" :text "RT-MEMORY M4: two record fields read by opField and used directly as Val, not fused to an opUnbox: base is defined by opRecord in the same function, so each read knows its static slot index at compile time and tries it first, with no call to objrt.field since both match; the values returned must equal what was stored.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#staticFieldMissingFn" :text "A plain opField names a key absent from Pair2's declared fields, used directly as Val, not fused: the field isn't among the compile-time-known fields at all, so RT-MEMORY M4 leaves the unfused call path untouched, giving ERR_FIELD as it always did.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 gate: direct opEntry calls (not opBuiltin, so the fast path this plan unit adds is the one that runs) to cons, listHead, listTail, listEmpty?, bytesAlloc, bytesSet, bytesLength and bytesGet; the Option field this walk reads is unboxed (opUnbox) back to raw before the raw opPrim addInt chain, since a generic opBuiltin never runs over it (RT-PRELUDE P4 inlines straight to a gep load/store, no asl_rt_b_<name> call, for every one of these but bytesAlloc, bytesGet and bytesSet's own bounds check, which nativeRunTest's IR-text assertions on this function cover one by one). listFail returns -1 if listEmpty? disagrees with a 3-element list's own shape, a defect in this fixture rather than the lowering being graded; the closed form is (1 + listLength [2 3]) + (4 + (65 + 200)) = 3 + 269 = 272.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineConsBadFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: cons's second operand (a raw Int here, not a List) fails the fast path's tag check, raising from its cold block (natively since PRELUDEASL-B), so the native program reports the host's own ERR_TYPE text (cons expects List, got Int) rather than a generic match-trap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineListHeadBadFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: listHead's operand (a raw Int, not a List) fails the fast path's tag check, raising the host's own ERR_TYPE text from its cold block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineListTailBadFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: listTail's operand (a raw Int, not a List) fails the fast path's tag check, raising the host's own ERR_TYPE text from its cold block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineListEmptyBadFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: listEmpty?'s operand (a raw Int, not a List) fails the fast path's tag check, raising the host's own ERR_TYPE text from its cold block; raw i1 result, so this needs its own ssaFunction rather than valFn's fixed Val return.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#preludeInlineBytesLengthBadFn" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: bytesLength's operand (a raw Int, not Bytes) fails the fast path's tag check, raising the host's own ERR_TYPE text from its cold block; raw i64 result, so this needs its own ssaFunction rather than valFn's fixed Val return.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/abiPrograms.asl#unknownModule" :text "A builtin no native code defines, alone in its module: emission rejects the module at build time (ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED), so it cannot share failModule.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayNativeTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit ARRLOWER: a program calling every f64, i64 and i8 array builtin (Len Get Slice Concat Generate Sum CountEq Fold Scan, f64ArrayFold with a Float64 and an Int64 accumulator) builds with asl1, routes each call to its asl-target-llvm/arrays function (arrayRoute) with no asl_rt_builtin_array call left, links against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a and uses nm -P to confirm the binary has neither the C array nor kernel builtin entry, then prints natively what asl-host run prints, which equals the values worked by hand from the prelude.asn Arrays section.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayNativeTest.asl#arraySource" :text "f = [0 1.5 3 4.5 6], n = [-4 -3 0 5 12 21], b = [90 60 30 0 -30 -60 -90]; each line prints lengths, elements, sums, counts, folds and scans of them and of their slice concatenations.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayNativeTest.asl#arrayExpected" :text "fc = f ++ [1.5 3]: 7 elements, fc[6] 3, sum 19.5, two 3.0s, fold 2a-x from 1 gives -7, four elements above 2, scan from 0.5 ends at 15.5; nc = [0 5 12] ++ n: 9, 0, sum 48, two 5s, fold x-a from 7 gives 22, scan 2a+x from 1 ends at -47; bc = b ++ [90 60]: 9, -90, sum 150, two 90s, sum of squares 25200, scan x-a from 3 ends at -3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit ARRLOWER-2 (asl-target-llvm/arrays and arrayRoute), with the asl1 build and clang link nativeRunTest's source programs use: (1) arrMod, calling all 30 array and kernel builtins directly and inside closures passed as values, builds and its IR calls each one's routed asl-target-llvm/arrays function, with no by-name builtin call of any of them and no asl_rt_builtin_array or asl_rt_builtin_kernel; (2) nm -P on each linked binary shows no arrayBuiltins, mkArray, kernelBuiltins, bDot or bGemm; (3) arrMod's native stdout equals asl-host run's byte for byte, floats printed by repr and by exact exponent and significand (compensated sums with cancellation, a dot whose fused multiply-add rounding shows, folds and scans over capturing closures, slices at 0 and at the length, concat of 0, 1 and 3 arrays, i8 values below 0), and errMod, one failing call per argument (index and slice ranges, negative and 16777217-element lengths, i8 values outside -128..127, an int64 sum overflow, dot, axpy and gemm shape and range errors), exits 1 as asl-host does with asl-host's error line; (4) gcMod, an array allocation loop whose arrays only compiled frames hold across closure calls that allocate, prints asl-host's output plain and under ASL_GC_STRESS=1, and under stress ASL_GC_STATS shows collections and frees all but a few objects. Every expected value is read from asl-host, never pasted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#arrayNames" :text "arrays.c's 27 builtins, then kernels.c's 3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#arraySource" :text "arrMod: every builtin directly and in a closure passed as a value; bits prints a float's repr with its exact sign, exponent and significand.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#errorSource" :text "errMod: main runs the failing call its first argument names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#gcSource" :text "gcMod: 120 rounds of Generate, Scan, Slice, Concat, axpy, Fold and Sum whose closures allocate, the folded array held only by the compiled fold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#routedSymbol" :text "The emitted symbol of the asl-target-llvm/arrays function for builtin name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#symbolNames" :text "The first field of each nm -P line, a leading underscore dropped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#build" :text "Writes src, builds it with asl1, checks its IR (gate 1) and links it against libaslrt.a, checking the binary's symbols (gate 2); the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#statOf" :text "The integer after :key in an ASL_GC_STATS line, -1 when absent.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#accountSource" :text "accountMod: main makes one array of the kind and length its arguments name, through Generate with a closure that allocates nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/arrayRouteTest.asl#testAccount" :text "arrays.c mkArray counts an array's data buffer, n * elem bytes, toward GC pacing (gcAccount): under ASL_GC_STATS the native binary's bytesAllocated for a 200000-element array exceeds its bytesAllocated for a 100000-element one by exactly what asl-host run's does, for each kind (two lengths of equal digit count, so the argument and printed strings allocate alike), so a native newArray that skips gcAccount fails here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#" :text "Gate for PRELUDEASL-Z: prelude.c's core builtin table left libaslrt.a with asl_rt_builtin. (1) For every name of prelude.c's coreBuiltins initializer (read from the file, so a new row fails here until it has a case), a fixture calls it directly and as a function value: runtimeDecls declares no asl_rt_builtin, the emitted IR calls neither asl_rt_builtin nor an asl_rt_b_ ENTRY wrapper and passes opt -passes=verify, and the native binary's stdout, stderr and exit code equal asl-host run's for one call each, trap failing alike; a variadic builtin used as a value fails at build time naming it. (2) nm -A -P on asl/host/out/libaslrt.a lists no prelude.o or zstd.o member, defines no coreBuiltins, asl_rt_builtin, bFileStat or zstdDecompress, defines bStringConcat, bStringLength and bStringSlice in strFloor.o, and no member refers to a symbol libaslhost.a's prelude.o or zstd.o defines (hostVerbLink.o, the hostVerb bridge that did, left in NX4). (3) A program naming a builtin no native code defines (fileReadString without the host routes, a name no table holds) fails at build time with ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED naming it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#tableRows" :text "The (name arity) rows of prelude.c's const Builtin coreBuiltins[] initializer, in table order; empty when text holds none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#cases" :text "One case per core builtin as (name operands view): the fixture prints view with %% replaced by the call, directly and through the builtin bound as a value; a view hides what differs between two runs in different work directories (paths, times, handles). Effects run in this order, the value call after the direct one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#caseFns" :text "dk calls the builtin directly; vk, for a fixed-arity builtin, through a let-bound value of it. trap's pair raises, so main reaches it only for its own ops.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#fixtureSrc" :text "The fixture: op all prints every case but trap as name, direct result, value result; trap and trapValue raise through trap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#compiled" :text "path straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testTable" :text "The case table covers prelude.c's coreBuiltins exactly, each name once (its order follows the effects, pathSymlink before fileReadlink).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testRunParity" :text "op all in two fresh work directories: native stdout, stderr and exit code equal asl-host run's, line by line first so a failure names its builtin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testTrapParity" :text "asl-host run reports the trap as FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts); the native binary writes CODE: message as its one stderr line, both exiting 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testVariadicValues" :text "A variadic core builtin used as a value has no fixed arity to lift; its program fails at build time with a diagnostic naming it, never reaching asl_rt_builtin or a link.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#memberOf" :text "The archive member of an nm -A -P line, between [ and ].")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#symbolOf" :text "The symbol of an nm -A -P line, after the member's colon, without the Mach-O leading underscore.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testArchive" :text "Gate (2) over nm -A -P: libaslrt.a's members, what they define, and what they refer to of prelude.o and zstd.o, whose definitions libaslhost.a's members give.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/coreTableGoneTest.asl#testUnsupported" :text "Gate (3): emitted without the host routes, a program calling fileReadString, and a program naming a builtin no table holds, fail at build time with ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED naming the builtin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitScaleTest.asl#" :text "Measures LLVM emission CPU time for large list literals and straight-line function bodies and bounds its 4000->8000 growth; lowering and verification scaling is measured by lowerScaleTest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/entryResultTest.asl#" :text "Tests parity between asl1 LLVM build and asl-host run for Result entry exit codes and main entry name (plan SH unit RP1)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/exitCodeTest.asl#" :text "Tests parity between asl1 native build and asl-host run for entry exit codes and names (plan SH unit LV1)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for ptr and i32 SsaTy and native (ccc) extern declarations (plan RT unit S2): a raw program declaring getpid() -> i32 and write(i32, ptr, i64) -> i64 links against no runtime (libc only) and its write call prints known bytes to stdout; a raw program declaring the variadic open(ptr, i32, ...) -> i32 creates a file at a path chosen by this test and its mode, read back by a tiny stat probe under umask 0, is exactly the mode passed to open. A second (unused) pool string sits right after the path (@str.1, the decoy); the emitted .ll is asserted to declare @str.0 at exactly path-length+1 bytes ending \\00 right before @str.1, which is the actual, deterministic check that @str.N is NUL-terminated (a missing terminator is layout-dependent at runtime on this toolchain and does not reliably corrupt the open() call, so the running program's own behaviour is not relied on for that). O_WRONLY|O_CREAT and the host's real mode mask come from tiny C probes compiled with the platform's own headers, not hardcoded darwin flag numbers, so this runs on Linux too. A third program (plan IR-rawPrims) declares malloc(i64) -> ptr, stores and loads i64/i32/i8 at explicit byte offsets into the mallocd buffer, widens and narrows between i32 and i64, checks the buffer pointer is not null and its ptrToInt is nonzero, masks a shift count past the operand width (65 against i64's 63, 33 against i32's 31) and wraps i32 arithmetic past INT32_MAX with no trap, folding every check into one i1 so the program's own exit code (0 or 1, the zext i1 to i32 @main wrapper already gives raw i1 entries) is the gate; opt -passes=verify runs over this emitted .ll too, skipped only when no opt binary is found. Runs clang and the programs through processRun in a fresh temporary directory, as asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#compileAndRun" :text "Compiles a tiny C probe against the platform's own headers and runs it, so a flag or mode value comes from the real host, not a hardcoded darwin number.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's own opt, not shipped beside /usr/bin/clang on this host: checks a few known homebrew locations, then PATH, so verifyLl can run opt -passes=verify over emitted IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#verifyLl" :text "opt -passes=verify over an emitted .ll: skipped, with a logged reason, only when optBin finds no opt binary at all; otherwise asserts a clean verify.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#getpidWriteModule" :text "getpid() -> i32 (called and ignored) and write(1, \"ok\\n\", 3): the pointer and the fd are raw ptr/i32, not boxed Val; the exit code is write's own return value, the byte count.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#openModule" :text "open(path, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT, mode), a variadic native extern (declared arity 2, called with 3): mode is the vararg, typed by its own definition (i32) since it is past the declared params. A second, unused pool string (the decoy) sits right after path in the string pool, giving testVariadicOpen's text assertion something concrete to check @str.0's declared size and terminator against.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#rawPrimsModule" :text "malloc(64), then every raw<Op><Width> primitive (plan IR-rawPrims) over its buffer and over plain i32/i64 values, each check folded by andBool into one final i1 (allOk, the function's own return and so the native program's exit code): the buffer is not null (rawPtrIsNull/notBool) and its rawPtrToInt is nonzero (neInt); an i64, an i32 and an i8 stored at distinct byte offsets (rawStoreI64/rawStoreI32/rawStoreI8, getelementptr inbounds i8 by offset) read back equal (rawLoadI64/rawLoadI32, eqInt/rawEqI32; rawLoadI8 zero-extends); the i32 read back round-trips through rawWidenI32 (sext) and rawNarrowI32 (trunc, in range so no trap) to the same i32; rawShlI64 and rawAshrI64 by a count of 65 against -8 match a plain shift by 1 (mask to 63: -16 and -4), rawLshrI64 by 1 against -8 is the large positive logical shift (9223372036854775804); rawAndI64/rawOrI64/rawXorI64 on i64 and rawShlI32 by 33 against 8 (mask to 32's 1, giving 16) check bitwise and masked-shift i32; rawAddI32 of INT32_MAX and 1 wraps to INT32_MIN with no trap, unlike the checked addInt; rawIntToPtr (plan RT unit S6 round 3) round-trips buf's own rawPtrToInt back to a non-null ptr whose own rawPtrToInt matches the original int, and rawIntToPtr of 0 is a ptr rawPtrIsNull sees as null -- the null-pointer constant this module's rawPtrToInt/rawPtrIsNull pair could not build before.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest.asl#loadGlobalModule" :text "opLoadGlobal \"environ\" (plan RT unit S6 round 4: generalizes the one hardcoded extern global, @asl_rt_spill, to any foreign C global by name): reads the real process environ pointer with no C accessor at all, checks it is not null, then dereferences its first element (environ[0], a char*) and checks that is not null either -- proving the loaded ptr is the genuine, populated environ array, not a stray symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#" :text "GCASL-1 and GCASL-2 gate: the native collector written in ASL (asl-target-llvm/gcAsl, emitted by gcRoute) is libaslrt.a's member gcAsl.o, and gc.c reaches a native link no more. Part 1: ar t lists gcAsl.o and no gc.o in libaslrt.a, gc.o only in asl-host's libaslhost.a; gcAsl.o defines every gc.c entry point (gcRoute entryNames) that any libaslrt.a member leaves undefined (nm -u), and some member does; a program bin/asl builds defines the collector entries and gcAsl.state and none of gc.o's statics (sizeClasses, pageSet, pageSetCap, largeIndex, markStk). Part 2: gcStressTest's programs, nativeRunTest's alloc and an asl1-built heap program, each linked once against libaslrt.a alone (the ASL collector) and once with gc.o taken from libaslhost.a ahead of it (the frozen gc.c as asl-host links it, its statics checked by nm), give the same stdout, stderr and exit plainly, under ASL_GC_STRESS=1 and under ASL_GC_VERIFY=1, and the heap program's output is asl-host run's. Part 3: ASL_GC_STATS (:gcStats ...) lines carry the same keys in the same order with equal objectsAllocated and bytesAllocated, and equal collections under ASL_GC_STRESS=1, where every allocation collects; a churn program whose live set is rooted precisely gives equal stats but totalGCNs by default, under ASL_GC_GROWTH and ASL_GC_MIN_MIB settings and under a cap; bad ASL_GC_GROWTH, ASL_GC_MIN_MIB and ASL_GC_MAX_MIB values fail alike; the ASL collector adds a (:gcPhases ...) line whose munmap calls never exceed the pages it unmaps. Elsewhere collections, objectsFreed, bytesLive and pages follow what the conservative stack scan retains, and each collector scans its own frames: alloc, whose list heads a stale word can keep, collects 15 or 19 times on either link as only the environment size changes, so those are not compared. Part 4: an ASL_GC_MAX_MIB=8 heap exhausted by live conses exits with asl-host run's ERR_OOM line on both links, and a short list fits. Part 5: hand-written IR runs a raising finalizer and a raising external-roots hook under a setjmp guard, then collects again; a two-cell cycle and a two-million-cell list under ASL_GC_VERIFY=1 fail with ERR_HEAP_CYCLE and ERR_LIMIT; both links print and exit alike. Part 6, only under ASL_GC_PERF=1: asl1 lowered by asl-host, linked both ways, compiles asl1.asl itself under ASL_GC_STATS=1 and /usr/bin/time, both runs side by side; the two .ll outputs are byte-identical and the ASL collector's sys time is at most 3 s, its GC time at most 1.10x, its wall time at most 1.05x and its peak RSS at most 1.15x gc.c's, the numbers printed as one (:gcPerf ...) line. Binaries of one program share a basename in sibling directories (gcc and asl), so argv[0], PWD and with them the stack layout the conservative scan reads are alike on both links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#programs" :text "gcStressTest's abiPrograms entries and the exit each must give.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#linkBoth" :text "Links ll with libaslhost.a's gc.o ahead of libaslrt.a as work/gcc/name, so gcAsl.o is never pulled, and against libaslrt.a alone as work/asl/name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#floorIr" :text "Writes ssa cRuntimeModule, the C floor's IR definitions (KW_*, tagName, mkCtor, aslInternShared and the raise state) a hand-written IR fixture calling asl_rt_init needs since ABIVAL-5, as work/floor.ll; returns that path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#sameRun" :text "Runs work/gcc/name and work/asl/name under env; both exit alike with the same stdout and stderr. Returns the gc.c run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#nmNames" :text "The symbol names nm lists for a binary, local ones included, without the leading underscore Mach-O adds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#collectorNames" :text "Symbols the ASL collector module defines for the runtime.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#gcStatics" :text "Static storage of gc.c that only a gc.o link carries.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#floorSource" :text "floorRtTest's program: a list of count live conses.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#hostErrorLine" :text "The ERR_<CODE>: <message> part of an asl-host run failure, as floorRtTest reads it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#buildLl" :text "Writes source as work/name.asl and lowers it with asl1 to work/name.ll; returns the source path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#statsPairs" :text "The :key value pairs of a (:gcStats ...) line, in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#stressKeys" :text "Under ASL_GC_STRESS=1 every allocation collects, so collections count allocations whatever the stack retains.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#policyKeys" :text "Every key but totalGCNs, for programs whose live set is rooted precisely.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#sameStats" :text "ASL_GC_STATS=1 runs of both links: same output, one stats line each with the same keys in the same order, and equal values for keys.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#phasesPairs" :text "The :key value pairs of the (:gcPhases ...) line of out's stderr, empty without one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#members" :text "The member names ar t lists for archive, its symbol table entries left out.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#symbolNames" :text "The last word of each line cmd (an nm listing) prints, without the leading underscore Mach-O adds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testArchive" :text "Part 1: the archives' members, the collector symbols every libaslrt.a member imports, and the symbols of a native program bin/asl builds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testReference" :text "The gc.c side really is gc.c: allocSmall linked with gc.o ahead of libaslrt.a carries gc.o's statics and no gcAsl.state, the libaslrt.a link the reverse.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testPrograms" :text "Part 2 and part 3 over abiPrograms: each program plainly, stressed and verified, then its stats.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testHeavy" :text "Parts 2 and 3 over nativeRunTest's alloc (100k-element list, closures, 20k concatenations) and the asl1-built stressMod, and refused settings.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testCap" :text "Part 4: floorRtTest's programs under ASL_GC_MAX_MIB=8 on both links and asl-host run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#guardIr" :text "Under a setjmp gcFloorGuard: 64 finalized handles whose finalizer raises, then an external-roots hook that marks one cons and raises, then a recollection; prints what was caught, the finalizer call count and the mark byte of the cons before and after the recollection. guardIr prints the mark byte after the aborted collection, which must be clear on both sides; after a normal collection gcAsl keeps the epoch there (9b7aa36bd) where gc.c clears it, a representation the guard does not compare")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#shapeIr" :text "Without arguments a rooted two-cell cons cycle; with one, a rooted list of two million cells; then a collection.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#churnIr" :text "Three million conses, every tenth linked into a list rooted through asl_gc_root_push: the live set is the rooted list, so a stale stack word keeps at most one unlinked cell and the collection schedule follows the growth policy alone.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testChurn" :text "Part 3 for the growth policy: churn's full stats but totalGCNs are equal on both links by default, under ASL_GC_GROWTH and ASL_GC_MIN_MIB, and under an ASL_GC_MAX_MIB cap it fits.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testIr" :text "Part 5: the finalizer, raise and heap-shape programs on both links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#timeWord" :text "The value after key on the line /usr/bin/time -p prints as key value, empty when absent.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#rssBytes" :text "Peak resident bytes from the line /usr/bin/time -l (darwin, bytes) or -v (linux, KiB) prints, -1 when absent.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#perfRound" :text "One round of the asl1 self-compile on both links side by side under ASL_GC_STATS=1 and /usr/bin/time: both exit 0 and write byte-identical IR; returns the gc.c and ASL stderr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#testPerf" :text "Part 6 (ASL_GC_PERF=1): asl1 lowered by asl-host and linked both ways, then perfRounds rounds of perfRound; the medians over the rounds against the GCASL-2 targets: ASL sys at most 3 s, GC time at most 1.10x, wall at most 1.05x, peak RSS at most 1.15x gc.c's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#perfRounds" :text "Rounds of the self-compile pair: the machine is shared, so each target is judged on the median.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#parityEnv" :text "parityEnv gives both collectors the same explicit ASL_GC_MIN_MIB, so a comparison holds whatever each one's default is")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcStressTest.asl#" :text "Bounded GC stress gate for the by-value native ABI (RT-MEMORY M1): native programs that allocate lists, records, variants, closures and strings, read fused fields, dispatch switches, tail call and pass spilled arguments run once normally, once with ASL_GC_STRESS=1 and once linked against the ASan runtime with detect_stack_use_after_return under stress, which collects on every allocation so the conservative native stack scan is the only thing keeping compiled code's values alive; both runs must exit alike with the same output. The full nativeRunTest under stress runs past two hours; this set finishes in minutes. listStressMod (PRELUDEASL-B) holds list literals, conses, fused listGet/listHead/listTail/stringSlice results, partial Ctors and Bytes only in compiled frames while @listrt and @bytesrt helpers allocate, and must print what asl-host run prints; it compiles through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker, which has no partial. objStressMod (ABIVAL-4) does the same for records, variants, closures, keywords and string constants built and read by the @objrt helpers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcStressTest.asl#programs" :text "abiPrograms entries and the exit each must give, stressed or not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcStressTest.asl#asanStress" :text "ASan with detect_stack_use_after_return moves the runtime's C locals into heap fake frames, which the native stack scan must also reach.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcStressTest.asl#testObjectStress" :text "objStressMod (ABIVAL-4) holds records, variants of 0, 3 and 8 fields, closures over captured run-time Strings, keywords and string constants only in compiled frames while objrt helpers allocate and read them; under stress and ASan fake stacks it prints what asl-host run prints.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#" :text "Gate for the LLVM IR emitter on the SSA contract (plan SH unit L1). Hand-built SsaModule fixtures: fib over Val with a branch and recursion, a raw i64 loop whose back edge swaps two block parameters and calls a raw function whose branch sends both edges to one parameterised join, an ADT switch with and without default, one module using every Val operation, raw fib over i64 with prim compare, sub and add, a prim self-check program exercising every primitive natively with a counter carried through phis after trapping primitives, and trap programs for each trapping primitive with a non-trapping control. The emitted text is compared with golden .ll; main prints a fixture's .ll so asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest can compile it with clang and run it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#floatSame" :text "True when a and b are indistinguishable by eqFloat alone, or both NaN (eqFloat is false for a NaN against itself), or agree in the sign of zero (1.0/0.0 and 1.0/-0.0 differ only in sign, so their eqFloat tells +0.0 from -0.0 where a plain eqFloat a b cannot).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#mathIs1" :text "Checks opEntry builtin called with one f64 operand against want, which a caller gets from calling the same builtin directly (the host interpreter runs this test source, so (sqrt 2.0) here is the host's own answer): the native lowering (an @llvm.*.f64 intrinsic for floor/ceil/round/sqrt, a direct libm declare for the rest) must equal it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#mathIs2" :text "mathIs1's two-operand counterpart, for pow and atan2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#mathChecks" :text "P5: floor, ceil, round, sqrt (@llvm.*.f64 intrinsics) and pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sin, cos, tan, atan2 (direct libm declares) via opEntry, no asl_rt_b_ wrapper. Covers NaN, +-inf, -0.0 (including atan2's 4 zero-sign quadrants), round's halfway cases (2.5, -2.5), domain edges (sqrt/log/log2/log10 of a negative or zero, pow of 0 and of a negative base to a fractional exponent) and large values (pow 2 62, exp 700 still finite and exp 710 overflowing to inf, a large tan argument).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#narrowEntry" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: rawNarrowI32 of an i64, widened back so the function still returns i64 like every other trap entry (unreachable on the trap path; the control variant stays in range, so it does round-trip).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#trapEntries" :text "Still die by a raw signal (addInt/subInt/mulInt/quotInt/remInt, IR-internal with no ASL source path, NATIVE-trapMessage left them as is).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#hostMsgEntries" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: floatToInt and rawNarrowI32 out of range now fail through rterr.int (asl-target-llvm/rtError) with a one-line ERR_INT_OVERFLOW message and exit 1, not a bare signal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/irE2eTest.asl#testAbiLimits" :text "RT-MEMORY M1: no runtime C declaration needs stack arguments, and a typed extern whose arguments overflow asl_rt_spill is refused like a module function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/libcTableTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for asl-target-llvm/libc (plan RT unit S1): clang builds the test-only probe tests/fixtures/libcProbe.c, which prints offsetof/sizeof and O_*/F_*/LOCK_*/errno/_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN constants for the current triple; this host is darwin-arm64, so the probe's output is compared row by row against lc/darwinArm64Facts. Fails before the table exists (import error); fails if any const, struct size or field offset in the table disagrees with the real headers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/libcTableTest.asl#assertVariadicProbe" :text "Native oracle for the :variadic table, instead of restating it: a call with one extra argument compiles against a variadic prototype (open takes (path, flags, ...)) and fails to compile against a fixed-arity one (flock takes exactly (fd, operation)), so clang itself proves the flags.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for RT unit LIBC-linuxLayoutGate: the linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 rows of asl-target-llvm/libc are read from published headers (:verified false) and never exercised against a real linux libc on this darwin host by any other gate -- libcTableTest only probes darwin-arm64. This gate compiles tests/fixtures/libcProbe.c (made portable for glibc: __errno_location not __error, st_atim/st_mtim/st_ctim not st_atimespec/st_mtimespec/st_ctimespec, <dirent.h> not <sys/dirent.h>, under __APPLE__) and runs it, then diffs every measured O_/F_/LOCK_/errno/_SC_ const and struct size/field offset against lc/linuxAarch64Facts and lc/linuxX8664Facts respectively -- the same assertOneConst/assertStructsMatch comparison libcTableTest.asl already uses for darwin-arm64, duplicated here rather than imported since libcTableTest exports only runTests. tripleStrategy (LIBC-linuxGateNative) picks, per triple and from plain uname -s/-m plus docker's own availability: 'native' (the host's own cc, no docker/QEMU) when the host IS that Linux triple, 'docker' (`docker run --platform linux/arm64|linux/amd64 gcc:14`) otherwise, or 'missingDocker', which fails only that triple's assertions loudly, naming the missing dependency, instead of skipping silently and reporting a false green. On darwin this always selects docker/missingDocker, which is the gate's original unconditional-docker behaviour.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#tripleStrategy" :text "Pure selection for one target platform ('linux/amd64' or 'linux/arm64') given the host's uname -s/-m and docker availability. 'native' when the host IS that Linux triple (built directly with the host's own cc, no docker/QEMU); otherwise 'docker', or 'missingDocker' when docker is unreachable. A non-Linux host (darwin) never matches a Linux triple, so it always falls to docker/missingDocker, which is the prior unconditional-docker behaviour.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#probeSrcAbs" :text "docker -v needs an absolute host path; probeSrc is relative to the repo root asl-host runs tests from.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#probeNative" :text "Builds and runs libcProbe.c with the host's own cc; used only when the host IS the target triple, so no docker/QEMU is needed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#probeInDocker" :text "Mounts probeSrc read-only, copies it into the container's own /tmp (so gcc's output artifacts never touch the host-mounted, read-only source directory), builds with gcc:14 and runs it. --platform (linux/arm64 or linux/amd64) selects the triple regardless of the docker host's own architecture, via QEMU emulation when it differs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl#runOneTriple" :text "Builds and runs libcProbe.c for platform per strategy ('native' with the host's own cc, 'docker' under docker, or 'missingDocker' to fail loudly without attempting a build), diffs its output against facts (lc/linuxAarch64Facts or lc/linuxX8664Facts), and returns the wall-clock run time in whole seconds (monotonicNs-measured) for the caller to report.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxTripleSelectTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for RT unit LIBC-linuxGateNative: linuxLayoutGateTest always built both linux triples under docker, even on a Linux host where the host's own triple could be compiled directly with cc. This asserts the pure triple-selection function (duplicated from linuxLayoutGateTest.asl's tripleStrategy rather than imported, since tests export only runTests) over all four host/docker combinations: darwin with docker up, darwin with docker down, a Linux host matching one of the two platforms (native, no docker needed), and a Linux host that does not match (docker, or missingDocker if docker is down).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxTripleSelectTest.asl#L21" :text "darwin, docker up: both triples are foreign, docker is reachable -> docker")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxTripleSelectTest.asl#L24" :text "darwin, docker down: both triples are foreign and unreachable -> missingDocker")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxTripleSelectTest.asl#L27" :text "linux host IS one of the two triples: native for its own triple regardless of docker, docker (or missingDocker) for the other")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/linuxTripleSelectTest.asl#L32" :text "the other arch name spellings uname -m can report, and the aarch64 host symmetric case")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/llvmRuntimeHelpersTest.asl#" :text "D81 acceptance gate fixture for Task 58601: LLVM IR SSA Generator and Native Runtime Expansion")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/llvmTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for asl-target-llvm LLVM IR backend emitter and types")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#" :text "Measures source lowering and SSA verification for large list literals and straight-line function bodies; compiles/runs an all-ones list literal, checks its sum, and checks that runtime fixtures are removed on every path. Emission scaling is measured by emitScaleTest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#PhaseTimes.lowerCpuUs" :text "Self user and system CPU microseconds spent in source lowering")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#PhaseTimes.verifyCpuUs" :text "Self user and system CPU microseconds spent in SSA verification")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#FixtureRun.failure" :text "Empty when the fixture compiled, linked and ran; otherwise the first failing step")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#FixtureRun.exitCode" :text "Exit code of the fixture binary, -1 when it did not run")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#FixtureRun.stdout" :text "Standard output of the fixture binary")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#FixtureRun.removed" :text "The fixture directory was removed afterwards")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/multiModuleTest.asl#" :text "Gate for multi-module native compilation (plan SH unit M1): the linkTest 3-module fixture (app imports util and geom, util imports geom) goes through compilePackageToLlvm! to one .ll equal to its golden (native formatting helpers, no generic str dispatch), whose @main calls linkfx/app.main; clang links it against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a and the program exits 42; compiling again gives the same text; an entry calling an unexported function is a compile diagnostic (the checker reports it before the link does). Runs clang and the program through processRun in a fresh temporary directory")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/musttailClangTest.asl#" :text "Apple clang musttail compatibility gate for sysRoute calls and compatible tailcc recursion")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/mutualTailChildTest.asl#" :text "Focused native gate: ten million mutually recursive tail calls must fit a 512 KiB child stack via procSpawnv")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/mutualTailChildTest.asl#SpawnedProc.pid" :text "child pid")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/mutualTailChildTest.asl#SpawnedProc.stdin" :text "child stdin")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/mutualTailChildTest.asl#SpawnedProc.stdout" :text "child stdout")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/mutualTailChildTest.asl#SpawnedProc.stderr" :text "child stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeBuiltinGapsTest.asl#" :text "Native execution parity for SHA-256 and IEEE float constants.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeFormatTest.asl#" :text "Native formatting gate: generated LLVM must not route formatting through value.c/float.c wrappers and its bytes must equal asl-host run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeFormatTest.asl#decimalZeros" :text "A decimal literal of exactly length bytes, \"0.\" then zeros; asl-host floatParse accepts at most 511 bytes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeFormatTest.asl#formatFloatLoop" :text "The retry loop of asl_rt_format_float, from its try: label to its done: label; empty when either is missing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeFormatTest.asl#testDepth" :text "A value nested exactly 10000 deep formats; one level deeper fails as asl-host does, ERR_DEPTH and exit 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeGapsTest.asl#" :text "Native regressions for native-only lowering gaps.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#" :text "Gate for PRELUDEASL-B: native code reaches neither prelude.c nor abi.c for list, listTail, listHead, listEmpty?, cons, bytesLength, bytesAlloc, bytesGet, bytesSet, bytesGetFloat64, bytesSetFloat64 and partial, nor for the fused entries @listHeadOr @listTailOr @listGetOr @stringSliceOr @listFirst @listRest and list literals. (1) runtimeDecls declares none of the fourteen deleted asl_rt_b_ wrappers nor asl_rt_list, and the IR of a program calling the twelve directly, the ten fixed-arity ones also as function values, and every fused entry neither declares nor calls them, nor asks asl_rt_builtin for any of the twelve by name; it calls the @listrt and @bytesrt helpers instead, builds its bigCount-element list literal with @listrt.cell and no argument array, and passes opt -passes=verify. list and partial as values have no native form: lowering rejects them (ERR_LOWER_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL), so they cannot reach asl_rt_builtin either. (2) Native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's for each value group (direct calls, values, fused entries on full and empty operands, partial with one, two and three bound arguments, the Float64 accessors on the first and last slot, and the bigCount-element literal summed by a tail-recursive walk), and a failing case's one native stderr line is the message asl-host run reports: bytesGet and bytesSet slots outside the buffer and negative, bytesSet values outside 0..255, bytesAlloc negative and past what malloc gives, bytesGetFloat64 and bytesSetFloat64 at slot len/8, len-8, len-7 and -1 and on mistyped operands, the type errors of listHead, listTail, listEmpty?, cons, bytesLength, bytesGet and the fused entries, and partial of nothing. Over-applying a partial fails with asl-host's own ERR_ARITY line, naming the function the partial applies (ABIVAL-4: a function value's lifted wrapper carries the function's Proto name). Compiles straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker step, since asl-checker has no partial; the fixture hides its mistyped operands from asl-host's checker behind function values and type-variable parameters")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#bigCount" :text "Elements of the fixture's list literal: lowering and emission grow quadratically with one function's size (a 10000-element literal took 6 min 23 s through link and emit on 2026-10-04), so the gate checks the literal's shape here and its stack use by construction (no argument array).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#fixtureLines" :text "The fixture module before its bigList function, line by line")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#deletedEntries" :text "The abi.c entries this unit deletes, by asl_rt_b_ symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#groupNames" :text "The twelve builtins with the @name. constant asl_rt_builtin would be asked for each by (ssa.asl llvmName).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#helperCalls" :text "Helper calls the fixture's IR must make: one per fused entry, bytesAlloc, the Float64 accessors, partial of nothing and the list literal cell.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#compiled" :text "path straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#sourceDirs" :text "The directories whose sources describe native list and bytes code, each with the file suffixes read there: this package's src and tests, and the host runtime the native binary links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#sourceFiles" :text "Every file directly under sourceDirs with one of its suffixes; an unlistable directory is a failed assert.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#testStaleNames" :text "No source under sourceDirs names a deleted asl_rt_b_ entry: the emitter, the host and the tests that pin them describe the @listrt and @bytesrt paths that replaced them, and this file builds the old names only from deletedEntries.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#testValuesRejected" :text "list and partial are variadic, which a native closure cannot be: lowering rejects either as a value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#testFailingParity" :text "asl-host run reports a failed run as FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts); the native binary writes CODE: message as its one stderr line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeListBytesTest.asl#testOverApplied" :text "Both fail with the same ERR_ARITY line, naming add3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#" :text "Gate for ABIVAL-4: native code builds and reads records, variants, closures, strings, keywords and symbols without abi.c. (1) runtimeDecls declares none of asl_rt_construct, asl_rt_record, asl_rt_field, asl_rt_variant_field, asl_rt_make_closure, asl_rt_closure_capture, asl_rt_call_closure, asl_rt_str, asl_rt_keyword, asl_rt_symbol and asl_rt_tag, libaslrt.a defines none of them nor aslCall, which a program's IR defines (NX4), and no IR this test emits (the two-module fixture, a C-linked library, a symbol constant, a separately emitted suite and its entry) declares or calls any of them, while the fixture calls the @objrt helpers. (2) The fixture, built natively, prints and exits as asl-host run does for records of 1 and 40 fields, a missing field and a non-record, constructors of 0 to 8 fields, a variant of one module matched by another module's same-named variant of other arity, closures capturing 0, 1, 7 and 256 values called with the right and wrong arity (300, past asl-host's load limit of 256, natively against the texts asl-host gives the others), lambdas of 256 and 257 parameters called with the right and wrong argument count, a partial application and a named function value over- and under-applied, a non-function called, keywords compared across the two modules, and one string constant read in a loop of 1,000,000 iterations, which allocates fewer than 100 objects more than 10 iterations do (ASL_GC_STATS=1 objectsAllocated); two field-less records built from hand-built SSA (the lowerer has no field-less schema) compare equal and lack a field as asl-host's do; a record built by C with its keys in another order than its schema's reads the right fields and fails on a missing one as asl-host does; a symbol constant fails with abi.c asl_rt_symbol's former ERR_UNSUPPORTED text; and an entry module holding no assert reports, under ASL_ASSERT_REPORT=1, the asserts and refutes a separately emitted module executed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#deletedEntries" :text "The abi.c functions this unit deletes and whose work native code now does itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#nestedSum" :text "(+ a (+ b ... z)) over names; one name alone is itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#capSource" :text "fn capN returning, as a T, a closure of one Int parameter over n captured values 1..n that adds them to its argument.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#wideSource" :text "fn wideN returning, as a T, a lambda of n parameters a0..a(n-1) that returns its last.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#callCases" :text "Each call case's name with the expression it evaluates.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#appSource" :text "The fixture's entry module: main prints the value of the case its first argument names, given its second argument as an Int.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#compiled" :text "path through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testArchive" :text "libaslrt.a, the runtime every native binary links, defines none of the deleted functions, nor aslCall, which a program's IR defines (NX4): nm -g lists each defined text symbol as T (W when weak on ELF), with or without the platform's leading underscore.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#verified" :text "code names no deleted function, is written to dir/name.ll and passes opt -passes=verify.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#hostErrorLine" :text "The ERR_<CODE>: <message> part of an asl-host run failure, reported as 'FAIL <file>: ERR_...: ... (after N asserts)'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testParity" :text "The native binary and asl-host run on the same arguments exit alike; at exit 0 they print the same stdout and native stderr is empty, at exit 1 native stderr is asl-host's error line alone and stdout agrees.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#objectsAllocated" :text "N from gc.c's '(:gcStats ... :objectsAllocated N ...)' exit line in text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testConstantLoop" :text "The loop reading one string constant 1,000,000 times allocates fewer than 100 objects more than 10 iterations do, the difference being the longer argument and printed number: objrt.str builds the constant once into its module cell, where a per-iteration build would add 1,000,000.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testCapture300" :text "A closure over 300 captured values, past compile.c's limit of 256 at which asl-host refuses to load the program (ERR_LIMIT), adds them all natively and fails a wrong arity with the text asl-host gives any lambda of one parameter (the fixture's cap1Many and cap1Few cases compare it).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#cFixture" :text "C main building an R record with its keys b, a in the reverse of the schema's order, as the VM or a host builtin may, and reading it through the compiled readA, readB and readZ (tailcc taking one %Val in two integer registers, as the C convention does).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testCRecord" :text "A record C builds with its keys in another order reads the right fields through objrt.field and fails on a missing one with asl-host's error line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testSymbol" :text "A symbol constant, which only hand-built SSA holds, fails natively with abi.c asl_rt_symbol's former ERR_UNSUPPORTED text: asl-host has no symbol value to compare with.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#emptyRecordCase" :text "An entry building two records of the field-less schema Empty (the lowerer has no field-less schema; asl-host does), passing the first through idOf so no read knows it was built here, then last.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testEmptyRecord" :text "A record of no fields, built natively, equals another and has no field zz, as asl-host's (Empty) does: emptyEq exits 1 where asl-host prints 1, emptyField fails with asl-host's error line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeObjectTest.asl#testReport" :text "An entry module holding no assert or refute, emitted apart from the module whose asserts run, installs the ASL_ASSERT_REPORT report in its @main: the binary reports the suite's 2 asserts and 1 refute under ASL_ASSERT_REPORT=1 and nothing without it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#" :text "Gate for ABIVAL-3: native code does generic arithmetic, comparison, equality, not and unary minus over boxed Vals without abi.c. (1) runtimeDecls declares no asl_rt_b_ entry, libaslrt.a defines none of the twelve operator entries asl_rt_b_<op> nor asl_rt_int, asl_rt_float, asl_rt_bool, asl_rt_unit and asl_rt_unbox_int/float/bool, no source of this package or the host runtime names an operator entry, and neither the IR of the parity fixture nor that of a program using every operator and not as a function value (map, fold, a list of operators) declares or calls any of them or calls asl_rt_builtin naming an operator, while both call the @opsrt helpers. (2) The parity fixture, built natively, prints and exits as asl-host run does for every operator over Int, Float, Int and Float either way round, String, List, Record, variant, Unit, Bool, Keyword, Bytes and String with Int pairs, results or ERR_TYPE texts; floor division and mod signs, zero divisors, overflow at the Int64 extremes, unary minus of Int64 min, n-ary + and * over Vals, = on nested records and lists (equal, written in another key order, another schema), NaN, -0.0, closures, and lists nested 9999, 10000 and 100000 deep (value.c's depth limit and its ERR_DEPTH) or 100000 long. asl-host has no operator values, so the value program's output is compared with asl-host running the same program with each operator written as a lambda. (3) Source construction stores fields in schema order, so records of one schema in two key orders come from a C caller building them with asl_alloc and intern: compiled = and != match keys by name as value.c valEq does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#fixtureLines" :text "The parity fixture: main applies the operator its first argument names to the values the others name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#opSymbols" :text "Each operator with the suffix of its deleted asl_rt_b_ entry and of its @opsrt helper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#deletedEntries" :text "The abi.c functions this unit deletes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#pairKinds" :text "One pair of value names per kind of operand pair the matrix applies every binary operator to.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#edgeCases" :text "Cases past the matrix: signs, zeros and extremes, NaN and -0.0, Strings, Keywords, structures, unary operators, n-ary folds, closures and depth.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#valuesTemplate" :text "A program using every operator and not as a function value, {op} standing where each appears.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#valuesSrc" :text "valuesTemplate with each operator as itself (asValues) or as the lambda asl-host can run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#compiled" :text "path straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testArchive" :text "libaslrt.a, the runtime every native binary links, defines none of the deleted functions: nm lists its defined symbols.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#sourceDirs" :text "The directories whose sources describe native operator code, each with the file suffixes read there: this package's src and tests, and the host runtime the native binary links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#sourceFiles" :text "Every file directly under sourceDirs with one of its suffixes; an unlistable directory is a failed assert.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testStaleNames" :text "No source under sourceDirs names an operator entry asl_rt_b_<op> or abi.c's OPENTRY macro that defined them: the emitter, the host and the tests describe the @opsrt helpers that replaced them, and this file builds the old names only from opSymbols.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testIr" :text "code names no deleted function and no asl_rt_builtin call of an operator, calls every helper in helpers, and passes opt -passes=verify.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testParity" :text "args, each word single-quoted for the shell: the native binary and asl-host run on the same arguments exit alike; at exit 0 they print the same stdout and native stderr is empty, at exit 1 the native binary writes CODE: message as its one stderr line, which asl-host run reports as FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts), and stdout agrees.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testValues" :text "The operator-value program builds natively with no operator entry or by-name operator call and prints what asl-host prints for its lambda twin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#ssaCase" :text "An entry named name over Val constants c0, c1, ... applying op by name (opBuiltin) to all of them: it returns the result, or with branches 1 when the result holds and 2 when not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#ssaCases" :text "SSA built by hand may call an operator by name with any operand count (asl-ir/verify allows it), as asl_rt_builtin's K_OP and K_NOT arms took it: each entry with the expression asl-host evaluates for it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testSsaBuiltins" :text "Each ssaCases entry, emitted as a program, calls no asl_rt_builtin and exits with the Int asl-host prints for its expression, or fails as asl-host does: a raise both report under the same code and message, an arity asl-host rejects at load with the same text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#keyOrderSource" :text "Compiled = and != over two P records, as Int64 so the C caller reads a plain return register.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#keyOrderCaller" :text "Host-built records through asl_alloc and value.c intern, as the VM or a host builtin may build them. xy is {x 1 y 2} in declared order; yx holds the same fields swapped; swap is {x 2 y 1} swapped, whose slots read by index equal xy's; other is schema Q with xy's keys and values.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeOpsTest.asl#testKeyOrder" :text "= and != on records of one schema in different key orders match each key by name, as value.c valEq does: a native = comparing slots by index would call xy and yx different and xy and swap equal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRtGapsTest.asl#" :text "Native runtime parity for the schema records replacing invalid keyword-headed web values.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for the LLVM path (plan SH units L1, I1b, D1, A1): every irE2eTest fixture emits its golden .ll and clang compiles it; raw programs link without the runtime and exit with their result, trapping programs die by a signal; Val programs (fib from SSA and from source, abiPrograms alloc) link against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a for the asl_rt_* ABI and exit with their result; alloc runs again against the ASan build, once at full size and once small with a collection on every allocation, with no sanitizer report; each abiPrograms failure program exits 1 with the host's error message, a match reaching no arm included; a switch reads its tag inline (getelementptr, with host-style type and foreign-variant traps on the miss path), switchPick dispatches the third and second variant and exits 3, and a switch on an Int or on another type's variant still fails with the host's error; assert and refute check, count and fail as the interpreter's special forms do; the one-operand - builtin negates an Int and a Float; an entry taking the argument list gets argv and exits by its Result as asl-host run does; a self tail call runs a million deep without growing the stack, also from source through nested arms. stringToFloat64 on bad text, float64ToInt64 on NaN, infinities and out-of-range values, and Float mod signs give natively what asl-host run gives. A program calling stringSplit, mapGet and listSort carries those prelude functions in its own module and runs with prelude.asl absent, and asl_rt_builtin refuses a prelude name with ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL (plan RT unit P2). Runs clang and the programs through processRun in a fresh temporary directory")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's own opt, not shipped beside /usr/bin/clang on this host: checks a few known homebrew locations, then PATH, so verifyLl can run opt -passes=verify over emitted IR and catch a malformed phi (mismatched predecessor labels, RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2) that clang -x ir's own codegen can silently mishandle instead of rejecting.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#verifyLl" :text "opt -passes=verify over an emitted .ll (RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2): skipped, with a logged reason, only when optBin finds no opt binary at all; otherwise asserts a clean verify, which is how the wrong-predecessor-label phi bug (emitListExtract naming <none|some>Lbl instead of <none|some>Lbl.alloc) was confirmed to fail ('PHI node entries do not match predecessors!') before the fix and pass after.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#trapRun" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: like trapExit but keeps stderr, for the entries that now fail through rterr.int with a one-line host-style message instead of dying by a bare signal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testTraps" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: addInt/subInt/mulInt/quotInt/remInt are IR-internal raw primitives with no ASL source path (lower.asl only ever emits their *Host counterparts for +, -, *, /, mod), so they were left dying by a bare signal rather than widened to match a VM that can never run them. floatToInt and rawNarrowI32 are the same kind of IR-internal, no-source-path primitive, but this unit routes their out-of-range case through rterr.int anyway (team-lead decision: a message beats a bare SIGTRAP), so there is still no VM leg to compare against here -- the parity checked below is only that the stderr text and exit code the native binary now gives match rterr.int's own wording exactly, not a second run of anything on asl-host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#nmNames" :text "The symbol names nm lists for a native binary, local and undefined included, without the leading underscore Mach-O adds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#quotedNames" :text "Every {\"name\", row opener in C table text: the name between the quotes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#cTableText" :text "The initializer of const Builtin <table>[] in asl/host/src/<file>, up to its closing };.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#arrayTableNames" :text "arrays.c builds its rows with ROWS(P): each #P \"Array<Op>\" name in the ROWS macro, for each P the table expands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testArrayTableSync" :text "asl-target-llvm/arrays arrayBuiltinNames, the names arrayRoute rewrites to native functions, equals arrays.c's ROWS names then kernels.c's kernelBuiltins names in order, so a builtin added to or dropped from either C table without its native builtin fails here instead of at runtime with ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testBuiltinTableSync" :text "ssa.asl builtinTables mirrors the C tables a native binary links on use: each table's names, read from its const Builtin initializer in asl/host/src, equal the emitter's list in order, so a builtin added to or dropped from either side fails here; and builtinTableSym routes each to its asl_rt_builtin_<table>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testRuntimeLink" :text "Plan RT unit S7: a native binary links libaslrt.a, the runtime floor, not the stage-0 host. alloc (closures over fold and map, linked by testAlloc) carries the runtime ABI and no evaluator (vmCall, vmRunProto), compiler (compileModule), loader, host verb (cmdHostVerb) or sys.c builtin (bFdRead); sysTableMod calls fileAppend, which asl1 routes to its sysRoute wrapper (SYSLOWER-b), so it links neither asl_rt_builtin_sys nor sys.c, and it appends as asl-host run does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testByValueAbi" :text "RT-MEMORY M1: compiled code passes Val by value as %Val = {i64, i64}, boxes Int, Float and Bool inline, and the runtime has no Box layer; runs after testIrFixtures and testAlloc, which emit ops.ll, alloc.ll and fib.ll. RT-MEMORY M2: opUnbox and a Val termBranch inline their own tag check against a cold rterr.type block, so no fixture's IR calls asl_rt_unbox_int, asl_rt_unbox_float or asl_rt_unbox_bool.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testInlineVariantAndCapture" :text "RT-MEMORY M3: a general (non-fused) opVariantField result and a closure trampoline's captures read Ctor.f[i]/Closure.up[i] inline (gep, load %Val) on the fast path, with no call to objrt.variantField/objrt.capture there; a miss (wrong tag, out of range) still falls to the runtime call on its own cold block, unreachable from the fast path, so headNone's ERR_RANGE stays the host's. alloc.ll (emitted by testAlloc) reads walk's h/t variant fields this way and addK's capture through the trampoline; runs after testAlloc.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testFusedFields" :text "RT-INLINE-2: an opVariantField/opField result whose only use is an opUnbox to Int/Float/Bool is read inline (tag check, bound check, raw Val load), no box allocated and no call to objrt.variantField/objrt.field on the fast path; a miss (range, wrong tag, missing key) still falls to the runtime call and gives the same error as the unfused path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#functionIr" :text "One function's own define block in a .ll that defines several (every abiPrograms fixture shares failModule): from '@name(' onward up to, but not including, the next '\\ndefine', or to the end of the file. Needed because a whole-file stringContains?/refute would see every sibling fixture's calls too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testStaticFields" :text "RT-MEMORY M4: a plain opField not fused to an opUnbox (RT-INLINE-2), whose base is defined in the same function by opRecord, knows the field's index in that opRecord's declared field order at compile time (asl-ir/verify checkRecord rejects any opRecord whose fields disagree with the schema's declared order, ERR_IR_UNKNOWN_FIELD, tried and confirmed rejected while writing this test) and reads a static %Val slot at that index, with no call to objrt.field at all. No fixture drives the defensive tag/bound mismatch branch (it traps by function name, as a non-exhaustive match does): since checkRecord proves a verified base's keys always match its schema's declared order, that branch cannot be reached without a verifier bug, so it is only checked for presence in the IR below, not exercised at runtime. staticFieldMissing's field is absent from Pair2's declared fields entirely, so it is not compile-time-known at all and keeps running the unfused field call (objrt.field since ABIVAL-4) and its exact ERR_FIELD text, unchanged by M4.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testVariantBoundary" :text "RTTAG: variantBoundarySource is run by asl-host and also lowered, emitted and linked natively, and the native binary of that same program fails with asl-host's own error line; the abiPrograms switchForeign SSA fixture gives that line too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#hostErrorLine" :text "The ERR_<CODE>: <message> part of an asl-host run failure, which reports it as 'FAIL <file>: ERR_...: ... (after N asserts)': from the first ERR_ up to the ' (after ' suffix or the end of that line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#defineIr" :text "One function's define block in ll, from its define header up to its closing brace; empty when ll does not define it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#beforeSlow" :text "A typed field read's fast path: its function text up to the first cold .slow block label, the only block that may call objrt.field.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#probeBranch" :text "The branch line a typed read's index-1 bound check must end with: the register name r is taken from frag's own '%r.sIn = icmp slt i32 1, %r.n' line, and the line sends a true bound to r.sprobe and a false one to r.<miss> (slow for a plain read, loop for a fused one). Without that compare line the result names no register and so matches nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testTypedFields" :text "M4b-2: an opField whose base is a parameter typed by a schema (tyRec) reads its static slot (declared index i) only after checking tag T_REC, i < Rec.n and keys[i] == @fieldId.<field>, else a cold .slow block calls objrt.field: getY (fused into an opUnbox) and nameOf (a plain Val read) return the right field for a record built natively (equal to asl-host run), for host-built records of the same schema in declared and in swapped key order (fixtures/typedFieldRec.c through asl_alloc), and a non-record or a record without the field fails with asl-host's own error line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#readlinkFixtureSource" :text "fileReadlink through the native builtin subset (lower.asl's builtinArity), printed the same way asl-host eval's Result does, so parity is a stdout compare against asl-host run of the same source")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testSpillArgs" :text "RT-MEMORY M1: a tailcc call never passes stack arguments; arguments past the registers go through asl_rt_spill, and values live across such a call survive it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#schemaDefaultsShadowSource" :text "A :default expression calls a module fn tagText; the caller shadows that same name with a local lambda at the constructor call site. A correct default resolves tagText in the schema's own module, not the caller's local.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#schemaDefaultsScopeModSource" :text "The importer defines its own private tagText, unrelated to the library's; constructing the library's schema must still resolve the default against the library's own tagText.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#schemaDefaultsCollideLibASource" :text "A library declaring a schema Widget whose default-thunk bare name (Widget$default$tag) is identical to another library's; only module qualification keeps the two thunks distinct when both are linked into one program.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#schemaDefaultsCollideLibBSource" :text "A second library, independently declaring its own Widget with the same field and default-thunk bare name as LibA but a different tagText body.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#schemaDefaultsCollideModSource" :text "Imports both same-named-schema libraries and constructs one of each; only if each thunk's target symbol is qualified by its own declaring module does each Widget get its own library's default, not the other's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#mathBuiltinsSource" :text "NB1's 4 intrinsic math builtins, plus (P5 r2) the 9 libm ones the checker and lower.asl's builtinArity learned from source: pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sin, cos, tan, atan2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#builtinCallIr" :text "A program that asks asl_rt_builtin for the prelude function stringSplit by name, as no lowered program does; asl_rt_builtin left libaslrt.a with prelude.c's core table (PRELUDEASL-Z), so it no longer links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testPreludeNative" :text "RT unit P2: asl1 links the prelude functions a program calls into its module, so the native program runs them without the bytecode VM, prelude.asl absent included, and prints what asl-host run prints; no by-name runtime entry is left to ask for a prelude name, so a program calling asl_rt_builtin fails to link, naming it, rather than reaching a VM.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#p3aMovedSource" :text "RT-PRELUDE P3a: resultOr and resultMap moved out of the C builtin table into prelude.asl; this program calls both, plus min, max, stringFromInt64, stringStartsWith? and stringContains? for output coverage. abs, min, max, stringFromInt64, stringStartsWith? and stringContains? stayed in C. abs: confirmed by direct reproduction (native build of a module calling (abs -5) alone, no Float call site in sight) that an N -> N prelude abs traps ERR_TYPE natively even on an Int-only call: the lowering's return-type unification for the if/if branch structure treats the whole function as returning Float regardless of which branch a given call site takes, so the Int branch's result is read back as a double and the tag check on it fails; a monomorphic Int64 -> Int64 abs has no such branch-unification path and lowers correctly, so the bug is specific to the N-generic dispatch, not to abs itself (out of this unit's :owns to fix). min/max: the VM lets (min \"a\" \"b\") through silently (returns \"a\") because > is polymorphic over Strings, where the host's bMin/bMax strictly trap ERR_TYPE on a non-Int/Float pair; ASL has no trap-with-code builtin (LANG-trapPrim) to reproduce that exact code from source, so min/max stay C entries. The remaining three are called directly (without going through asl-ir/link.asl's prelude closure) by consumers with no prelude-linking fallback of their own: stringFromInt64 and stringStartsWith? by the frozen asl-target-c corpus (sample.asl, strings.asl), stringContains? by asl-ir/tests/lowerParityTest.asl's single-module lowering fixture.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testP3aMoved" :text "RT-PRELUDE P3a gate: the emitted IR has no @asl_rt_b_resultMap/resultOr (fails before this unit); the module defines each as an ordinary prelude function, and the native binary prints what asl-host run prints. abs, min, max, stringFromInt64, stringStartsWith? and stringContains? stayed C entries (see p3aMovedSource :d), so they are not asserted here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#p3bMovedSource" :text "RT-PRELUDE P3b: map, filter, fold, listLength, listReverse and range moved out of the C builtin table into prelude.asl; a million-element range folded natively checks that the prelude loops are tail calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testP3bMoved" :text "RT-PRELUDE P3b gate: the emitted IR defines map, filter, fold, listLength, listReverse and range as prelude functions and calls no @asl_rt_b_ entry for them (fails before this unit: fold lowered to @asl_rt_b_fold); the native binary, a million-element fold included, prints what asl-host run prints.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#preludeInlineBadCases" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 round 2 item 2: fixture name to the host's own runtime ERR_TYPE text (prelude.c's want()) its cold path must report (raised natively since PRELUDEASL-B) when the fast path's tag check fails, in place of the generic ERR_MATCH_NONEXHAUSTIVE a plain non-exhaustive-match trap gave before this round.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testPreludeInline" :text "RT-PRELUDE P4 gate: cons, listHead, listTail, listEmpty? and bytesLength/bytesGet/bytesSet lower to gep loads/stores plus asl_alloc on their fast path, raising the host's own error text from a cold block on a tag (or, for bytesGet/bytesSet, range) mismatch (round 2 item 2; natively since PRELUDEASL-B, through asl_rt_b_<name> before); fails before round 1's change (a plain opEntry call reached the abi.c wrapper of each builtin unconditionally), passes after. Source does reach opEntry for these builtins too (lower.asl:573's generic builtin-call lowering emits it whenever ty/builtinEntry resolves a name, round 2 item 4 correcting round 1's 'source never reaches opEntry' claim), but asl-checker/src/types.asl's builtin signature table is missing bytesSet entirely (a pre-existing gap outside this unit's :owns, bytesGetFloat64/bytesSetFloat64 present beside it), so asl1 can't build a program calling it from source at all; abiPrograms.asl's preludeInline and its five …Bad fixtures build these through opEntry directly via raw SSA instead, bypassing that gap and letting a type mismatch through uncaught, as asl1's checker otherwise would. opt -passes=verify (round 2 item 3) runs over every emitted .ll here, skipped only when no opt binary is found; it is what actually caught round 1's bug, a phi naming the wrong predecessor block (<none|some>Lbl instead of <none|some>Lbl.alloc, since emitCtorAlloc's own .resolve/.alloc pair is what the branch instruction after it actually lands in), which clang -x ir's own codegen silently mishandled rather than rejecting.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#numericGenericLibSource" :text "NATIVE-genericNumUnify: abs-shaped N -> N functions that test the run-time kind through (str x), in an imported module: asl1 checks only the entry, as the prelude is never checked, so the Float literals beside N arms reach the lowering. gabs nests if under if, gabsCond is a cond with :else, gabsAny is gabs over the plain type variable T (round 2: a fix keyed to N alone left it trapping); each joins a raw Float arm with a Val arm that holds an Int on the Int path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#numericGenericCases" :text "Entry module name to the println body it runs: Int-only call sites, Float-only, and both kinds in one module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testNumericGeneric" :text "NATIVE-genericNumUnify gate: an N -> N function whose arms are a raw Float on its Float path and a Val on its Int path joined at Float, unboxing the Int path's Val as a double, so an Int-only caller trapped ERR_TYPE natively (fails before the fix); a join with any Val arm now stays Val, whatever the signature (gabsAny over T fails at 2ecfa1dc, whose fix keyed on N). Each entry's native stdout equals asl-host run's and the pinned text, and opt -passes=verify accepts the IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#preludeSingleSource" :text "P3b-preludeLinking: a single module calling prelude-only ASL functions with no C entry (stringSplit, stringJoin, resultOr, listContains?), stringSplit reaching further prelude helpers (preludeSplit, preludeSlice, preludeTrap) only through prelude.asl.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#testPreludeSingleModule" :text "P3b-preludeLinking gate: plain lowerSource rejects the module's prelude-only calls; asl-ir/link lowerSourceLinked! lowers it with the prelude closure as prelude.<name> functions, its own main unqualified; emitLlvmSourceWith and asl-target-c emitC11SourceWith over the same prelude build native binaries whose stdout equals asl-host run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeRunTest.asl#escapeBodies" :text "no NUL: native println stops at NUL")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#" :text "Gate for PRELUDEASL-C: native code reaches neither prelude.c nor abi.c for stringLength, stringConcat, stringSlice, stringFromInt64, stringStartsWith?, stringContains? and stringToBytes. (1) runtimeDecls declares none of their seven asl_rt_b_ wrappers, libaslrt.a defines none of them, no source under the package or the host runtime names one, and the IR of a program calling the seven directly and as function values neither declares nor calls them, nor asks asl_rt_builtin for any of the seven by name; it calls the @strrt helpers and @asl_rt_format_i64 instead and passes opt -passes=verify. (2) Native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's for each value group (empty strings, multi-byte UTF-8 sliced inside a code point, stringSlice bounds with start past end, negative and past the end, the concat of two 1 MiB strings, stringFromInt64 of 0, -1, Int64 min and max, empty, equal and longer needles, stringToBytes of non-ASCII, the seven as values), and each failing case's one native stderr line is the ERR_TYPE message asl-host run reports: every operand of the seven given a value of the wrong type, through function values and type-variable parameters (hiding them from asl-host's checker), and stringSlice with both its String and an Int operand wrong, which names the String as asl-host's operand order does, also when the String is bound in a block dominating the call's. Compiles straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker step.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#fixtureLines" :text "The fixture module, line by line; its non-ASCII text is written as \\x escapes the host reader turns into UTF-8 bytes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#deletedEntries" :text "The abi.c entries this unit deletes, by asl_rt_b_ symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#groupNames" :text "The seven builtins with the @name. constant asl_rt_builtin would be asked for each by (ssa.asl llvmName).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#helperCalls" :text "Calls the fixture's IR must make, one per builtin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#compiled" :text "path straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#testArchive" :text "libaslrt.a, the runtime every native binary links, defines none of the seven wrappers: nm lists its defined symbols.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#sourceDirs" :text "The directories whose sources describe native string code, each with the file suffixes read there: this package's src and tests, and the host runtime the native binary links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#sourceFiles" :text "Every file directly under sourceDirs with one of its suffixes; an unlistable directory is a failed assert.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#testStaleNames" :text "No source under sourceDirs names a deleted asl_rt_b_ entry or the abi.c ENTRY row that defined it: the emitter, the host and the tests that pin them describe the @strrt and formatter paths that replaced them, and this file builds the old names only from deletedEntries.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeStringTest.asl#testFailingParity" :text "asl-host run reports a failed run as FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts); the native binary writes CODE: message as its one stderr line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTestReportTest.asl#" :text "Native test binaries report their executed assertion counts exactly like asl-host and reject an exported runTests that executes no assertions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#" :text "Native error-path gate (ABIVAL-2): emitted IR neither declares nor calls any abi.c error entry ABIVAL-2 deleted (removedSymbols), no doc in the package names one (testDocs), and each failing program's native stderr, stdout and exit equal asl-host run on the same source, read from asl-host here: asl-host run reports 'FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts)' where a native binary prints 'CODE: message' alone, so a failing run is compared on that error line. Programs asl1 build rejects before they could fail (an Int condition, a non-exhaustive match) are lowered without the checker through emitLlvmSource; rawNarrowI32 and floatToInt have no ASL source path and no VM operation, so their irE2eTest fixtures are checked against the native wording alone.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#removedNames" :text "removedSymbols as bare names, the way prose writes them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#packageFiles" :text "Every .asl file directly under packageDirs; an unlistable directory adds none, which testDocs's file count catches.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#docsOf" :text "The module and fn docstrings of one top form, each keyed by path and name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#parsed" :text "path read through asl-parser as the compiler reads it, or why it could not be.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#fileDocs" :text "path's docstrings; none when it does not parse, which parseFailures reports.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#staleDocs" :text "The docs naming a removed abi.c entry, which no longer exists for them to describe.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#testDocs" :text "No module or fn doc in asl-target-llvm's src or tests names a removed abi.c entry: the emitter, the helpers and the tests that pin them describe rtError's rterr.* paths, and removedSymbols alone carries the old names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#removedIn" :text "The removed abi.c entries ir declares or calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#one" :text "An Int the compiler cannot fold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#cases" :text "Programs asl1 builds, each failing (or exiting) one way, by name; main returns (Result Int64 String) unless the source says otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#uncheckedCases" :text "Programs the checker rejects but asl-host runs: an Int where a condition wants a Bool (a type variable hides it from asl-host's checker) and a match missing an arm.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#failLine" :text "CODE: message of asl-host run's 'FAIL <src>: CODE: message (after N asserts)' line, empty when there is none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#failAsserts" :text "N of asl-host run's '(after N asserts)', empty when there is none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#expectedStderr" :text "What the native binary must print to stderr: asl-host's error line when it reported one, else its stderr as is (a run exiting (ok 3) fails nothing).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#buildChecked" :text "Writes text, builds it with asl1, checks the IR names no removed entry and links it; the binary path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#buildUnchecked" :text "Writes text and lowers it through emitLlvmSource with entry main, no checker; checks and links the IR as buildChecked does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#irConstants" :text "The text of every i8 array constant in ir (c\"...\"), with the \\0A, \\22, \\5C escapes decoded and \\00 dropped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#specRest" :text "p after its leading printf conversion: flags, width, precision and length letters, then the conversion character.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#formatPieces" :text "The literal pieces of printf format c between its conversions; a format with no conversion is one piece.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#fitsFormat" :text "Whether printf format c can print the 'CODE: message' line whole or its message alone (a site printing the code apart).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#fitsText" :text "Whether printf format c, trailing newline dropped, can print line: its first piece starts line, the others occur in order after it and the last ends it. A format whose literal pieces hold fewer than 6 bytes ('%s', '%s: %s') fits nothing, as it names no raise site.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#testMixed" :text "One binary, built by asl1 with the host routes, raising through sleepMs of -1 and through Int overflow: both print asl-host's line. No C is left to raise the sleepMs line since asl_rt_builtin and prelude.c left libaslrt.a (PRELUDEASL-Z): the emitted IR holds the routed sleepMs's text pieces and calls no asl_rt_builtin, so native code wrote it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#testOrdering" :text "Output before a raise reaches stdout ahead of the error on one stream, as asl-host flushes stdout before reporting.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#testReport" :text "ASL_ASSERT_REPORT=1 prints the counts asl-host test reports after a passing run, and after a failing one the counts asl-host run's (after N asserts) gives, behind the error line; unset, nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeTrapTest.asl#testRawTraps" :text "rawNarrowI32 and floatToInt out of range (irE2eTest fixtures, no ASL source path, no VM operation): exit 1 with the native one-line message, linked without libaslrt.a since their IR now needs libc alone.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit PARASL: a native program's parMap and parFold run asl-target-llvm/parallel's functions, routed by asl-target-llvm/parRoute, not asl/host/src/parallel.c. Programs are lowered as nativeRunTest lowers them (lowerSourceWith over the prelude), emitted by emitLlvmProgramFor for this host's libc.asl facts and linked by clang against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a: (1) the IR calls neither builtin through asl_rt_builtin_parallel and defines each wrapper it uses internal; (2) nm -P -A on libaslrt.a shows no parallel.o member and nm -P on the native programs shows no bParMap or serVal symbol (nor mkArray in the programs that use no array builtin; arrays.c stays in RT_SRCS, as no unit routes the array builtins yet); (3) native stdout, exit and error text equal asl-host run's for parMap over 0, 1, 7 and 10000 elements with 1, 2 and 64 workers and parFold over the same with a non-commutative combine (casesSource), results of every codec tag (codecSource), a closure raising ERR_DIV_ZERO in one element of parMap and of parFold, one raising a 2000-byte ERR_ARG message in each (parallel.c cuts the text a worker sends to 1018 and 1019 bytes), a worker that SIGKILLs itself, an unserialisable result, results at the 64 MiB limit on both sides of the child's and the parent's checks, non-positive slots, ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK=1 (failSource), and parMap with 2 and parFold with 4 arguments, the real builtins called directly (aritySource; unit ARITY gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity rows for these shorter arities); (4) after each casesSource case the process has as many children and inherited fds as before it (a ps and /dev/fd census), no worker pid a failSource run reports is alive after it exits, and once a worker fails the others are terminated rather than left to finish (stall); the IR declares setjmp returns_twice (checked in the text: the unoptimised build this gate links does not expose the undefined behaviour its absence allows); (5) routeModule leaves a module without parMap or parFold unchanged and finishText rejects routed text that lacks a helper declaration (ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_TEXT).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to a libc/libcTriples triple, independently of sysRoute tripleOf, empty for any other host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#hostFacts" :text "This host's libc.asl row; a host libc.asl has no row for fails the gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#casesSource" :text "parMap over 0, 1, 7 and 10000 elements with 1, 2 and 64 workers and parFold over the same with a non-commutative combine, each with a census of children and fds before and after; then whether a worker runs in the caller.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#codecSource" :text "parMap results of every codec tag next to map's: nested records, ctors, keywords, unicode strings, Bytes, the three array kinds, Int64 extremes, -0.0 and NaN payload bits, Bool, Unit and nested lists.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#failSource" :text "One failing or large parMap or parFold per mode (the last argument); each element writes its worker pid to stderr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#aritySource" :text "parMap with 2 and parFold with 4 arguments, the real builtins called directly: unit ARITY gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity a row for each shorter arity, so no stand-in is needed for either asl-host or the native lowering.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#lowered" :text "src lowered over the host's prelude (lowerSourceWith, as nativeRunTest's driver lowers it).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#build" :text "Writes work/name.asl (hostSrc, for asl-host run) and work/name.ll, the IR emitLlvmProgramFor emits at hostFacts for nativeSrc, and returns the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#wrapperDef" :text "The emitted definition line prefix of parallel's wrapper for name with argc operands, internal to its module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#checkIr" :text "Gate (1): the IR neither calls nor declares asl_rt_builtin_parallel and defines the wrapper of each (builtin, operand count) the program uses, internal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#nmNames" :text "The symbol names nm -P prints for a linked binary, local ones included, each without the leading underscore of the darwin C ABI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#checkSymbols" :text "Gate (2), program half: nm -P lists symbols for bin and none of forbidden, parallel.c's and arrays.c's C functions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#hostError" :text "The error asl-host run reports for path: the text between 'FAIL path: ' and ' (after', or empty when it reports none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#otherLines" :text "text without its empty lines, joined by newlines.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#pidsOf" :text "The pids of the 'pid N' lines in text, in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#checkParity" :text "Gate (3): under env, the native binary's stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source and arguments, and the native binary's stderr is asl-host's reported error; returns both outputs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#pidLines" :text "The pids failSource's elements appended to path, in order; none when no element ran.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#checkGone" :text "Gate (4), failing runs: no worker pid either run reported is alive once both runs have exited.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#cTableNames" :text "parallel.c's and arrays.c's C functions a routed program must not link (parallel.c's builtin entry, its parMap and serialiser, arrays.c's allocator).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testCases" :text "Gates (1)-(4) on casesSource, run as is and under ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK=1: every line agrees with map or the sequential fold and reports a clean census, and the workers run in children except under the fallback.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testCodec" :text "Gates (1)-(3) on codecSource: every codec tag survives the round trip and agrees with map.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#failModes" :text "failSource's modes, each with the error asl-host reports (empty when it succeeds): parallel.c's texts. longTrap and foldLong raise a 2000-byte message, so the text is parallel.c's cut: parMap's 'parMap element 5: <error>' to 1018 bytes, parFold's error to 1019.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testFail" :text "Gates (1)-(4) on failSource: each mode's native stdout, exit and error equal asl-host run's and failModes' text, no worker outlives a run, and trap and foldTrap under ASL_PAR_FORCE_FALLBACK=1 report the sequential path's errors.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testArity" :text "Gates (1) and (3) on aritySource: parMap with 2 and parFold with 4 arguments take the worker count from the processor count, as parallel.c does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testArchive" :text "Gate (2), archive half: nm -P -A on libaslrt.a lists no parallel.o member.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testRouteModule" :text "Gate (5): routeModule leaves a module that calls neither builtin unchanged, with no internal names, and finishText rejects routed text missing a helper declaration and passes other text through.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#litSource" :text "A program printing parallel's helper declarations and the text finishText used to look for as string literals; routed, it also calls parMap, whose results carry such a literal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testLiteral" :text "Gate (6): a program whose string literals hold parallel's helper declarations emits, links and prints what asl-host run prints, both when it calls neither builtin (finishText must leave it alone: before the routing result drove finishText, emission failed with ERR_LLVM_PARROUTE_TEXT and asl1, which holds these literals, could not lower itself) and when parMap routes it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#wireDumpFn" :text "f, the wireDump stand-in, with its body replaced: asl-target-llvm/parallel serVal of its argument into a calloc'd 48-byte SerBuf (data, len, cap, err, scratch), then [err i64][len i64] and the bytes written to fd 1, the buffers freed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#testWire" :text "Gate (7): the native codec writes parallel.c's bytes. wireSource's values, serialised by asl-target-llvm/parallel serVal in a routed native program, are frames parallel.c deserVal takes whole and parallel.c serVal re-encodes byte for byte (wireCheckSource), for every codec tag; a consistent renumbering of a tag on both native sides, which every native round trip survives, fails here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#wireSource" :text "Values of every codec tag passed to the wireDump stand-in, which testWire replaces with a frame writer over parallel serVal; the parMap call makes routeModule route the module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/parRouteTest.asl#wireCheckSource" :text "A C program over asl/host/src/parallel.c itself (included, as tests/host/parallelDeserTest.c does): for each [err i64][len i64][bytes] frame on stdin it requires err 0, parallel.c deserVal to take exactly the bytes, and parallel.c serVal of the result to give the same bytes; prints frames N equal, else the first failing frame and exits 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit PRELUDEASL-E: a native program's 19 prelude.c file and environment builtins (fileReadBytes, fileReadString, realPath, fileWrite, dirList, fileStat, fileReadRange, envGet, getHomeDir, fileCreateExclusive, dirCreate, pathRemove, pathRename, fileChmod, fileFsync, fileReadlink, fileLstat, pathSymlink, fileUtime) run asl-target-llvm/sysRoute's wrappers over asl-target-llvm/sys, not prelude.c's coreBuiltins through asl_rt_builtin. The program is lowered as nativeRunTest and sysRouteTest lower theirs (lowerSourceWith over the host prelude; unit ARITY gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity a row for every one of these 19 names, so each is called directly, with no stand-in) and emitted by emitLlvmProgramFor for this host's triple. Gate (1): its IR calls none of the 19 through asl_rt_builtin, and defines each one's wrapper internal; the builtins routedNames calls directly are called directly, and the same 19 names each pass as a function value too (viaBytes and kin). Gate (2): run in a fresh fixture tree (empty, 1-byte, 3 MiB and missing files, a directory, fifos with writers, dotfiles, a tree to remove, a long symlink), the native binary's stdout, stderr and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source, with HOME set, empty and unset (getpwuid's fallback), and the run reaches its last case.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to a libc/libcTriples triple, independently of sysRoute tripleOf, empty for any other host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#hostFacts" :text "This host's libc.asl row; a host libc.asl has no row for fails the gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#lowered" :text "src lowered over the host's prelude (lowerSourceWith, as nativeRunTest's driver lowers it): unit ARITY gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity a row for every one of routedNames, so each lowers to an opBuiltin directly, with no stand-in.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#build" :text "Writes work/fsRoute.asl and work/fsRoute.ll, the IR emitLlvmProgramFor emits at hostFacts for src, and returns the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#coreCall" :text "The emitted call of builtin name through prelude.c's core table, as asl-target-llvm/ssa emits an opBuiltin of a core name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#wrapperDef" :text "The emitted definition line prefix of a routed wrapper, internal to its module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#checkIr" :text "Gate (1): no routed name is called through asl_rt_builtin, and each has its wrapper defined internal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#setupScript" :text "Builds the fixture tree at $1 and starts one detached writer per fifo.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#releaseFifos" :text "Opens each fifo read-write, so a writer still blocked in open (a run that failed before reading it) finishes instead of lingering.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#runIn" :text "A fresh fixture tree at work/tree, then cmd on it under env, then the fifos released.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeFsRouteTest.asl#checkParity" :text "Gate (2): native stdout, stderr and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source and a fresh fixture tree, under env; the native run exits 0 and reaches the last case.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#" :text "PRELUDEASL-P: native processRun/processSpawn/processWait route through sysProc. IR must not call these through asl_rt_builtin; native output and spawn log must equal asl-host on the same source.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#lowered" :text "processSpawn/processWait carry a builtinArity row (PRELUDEASL-P), so lowering emits opBuiltin for all three coreNames directly; no stand-in definitions or post-hoc opCall rewrite are needed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#stdinCheckScript" :text "Exits 0 when fd 0 is the same file as /dev/null (device and inode match), 1 otherwise; a spawned child's stdin must be /dev/null regardless of what the test process's own stdin is.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#source" :text "Exercises processRun's command/output/status, signal death and EOF behavior, processSpawn/processWait success and timeout, reused and invented handles, a SIGTERM-ignoring child that outlives the timeout but not the grace and one that outlives both (their 300 ms timeout leaves the shell time to install the trap before SIGTERM), non-String or non-Int arguments, a command with an embedded NUL byte (\\x00, rejected before fork), several live handles waited out of order, and a spawned command that checks its own stdin is /dev/null (scriptPath, written by the caller) rather than the test process's inherited stdin. The timed processWait alone is measured against the 2 s SIGTERM grace. The host and native execute this identical source.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#runNative" :text "Redirects its own stdin from a real file, not /dev/null: the test's own stdin is sometimes /dev/null already (a sandboxed foreground run), which would make a spawned child's stdin look like /dev/null whether or not processSpawn redirects it. A real file as this process's stdin makes the fd distinguishable, so stdin-devnull in the exercised source only passes when processSpawn truly redirects.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#ioShimSource" :text "Interposes libc poll, read, fwrite and free; ASL_IO_SHIM picks the injected fault: poll fails with EINVAL (and the exit report says whether the two polled pipes were closed), the first 4096-byte pipe read fails with EINTR (and the exit report says whether that buffer was freed), or fwrite into a non-stdio stream writes nothing. Each injection writes a marker to stderr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testPollFailure" :text "prelude.c bProcessRun breaks out of the read loop on a non-EINTR poll failure, closes both pipes, reaps the child and returns what it collected; native must do the same.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#stderrOnly" :text "Writes to the child's stderr alone and holds stdout open and silent, so processRun's first pipe read and capture write are on the stderr stream.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testReadInterrupted" :text "An EINTR read retries without losing output and frees the buffer it read into.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testCaptureWriteFailure" :text "A short fwrite into the capture stream is an out-of-memory failure, not silently truncated output.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testExternsCalled" :text "Every extern procRouteExterns declares is called by a procRouteFunctions instruction: a declaration nothing calls only adds a C signature nothing checks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#factReads" :text "The names text passes to sysProc's fact lookup as (kf k \"NAME\"), excluding the struct.field layout names the layout maps add.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testFactsDeclared" :text "kf reads a fact procFacts resolved and yields 0 for a name procFactNames lacks, so every name sysProc.asl reads through kf must be in procFactNames of a supported triple (linux-only and darwin-only names are read only on their own triple): a missing SIGKILL made every kill(pid, SIGKILL) a kill(pid, 0).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#globalDestNamed" :text "The dest of an opGlobal instruction anywhere in f whose global name contains namePart.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#unboxDestOf" :text "The dest of an opUnbox instruction anywhere in f whose unboxed operand is v.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#eqIntDestOn" :text "The dest of an eqInt opPrim instruction anywhere in f with v among its operands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#branchBlockOn" :text "The block of f whose terminator is a two-way branch on cond.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#argIsOomConst" :text "True when a is the dest of an instruction in instrs whose op is the pool's 'out of memory' string constant.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#callIsFormatErrOom" :text "True when i calls the routed processFormatErr helper with some argument whose own instruction (in the same instrs) is the pool's 'out of memory' string constant.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#blockHasFormatErrOom" :text "True when instrs call the routed processFormatErr helper with an argument that is the pool's 'out of memory' string constant, both defined in instrs (the block its own call and operands live in, matching how sysProc builds a one-block error return).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#reachesFormatErrOom" :text "True when, following only plain jumps from label (bounded by fuel, so a cycle cannot loop forever), some block calls processFormatErr with the pool's 'out of memory' text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/preludeProcRouteTest.asl#testWaitStateGuard" :text "Structural gate for processWait's OOM-state guard: there is no malloc-failure shim to force the real codepath (processHandleStateInit's malloc(16) failing), so this checks the SsaFunction shape instead. processWait must read the processHandleState global, unbox it, compare it with eqInt, branch on that comparison, and one arm of the branch must resolve (through plain jumps) to a block calling the routed processFormatErr helper with the pool's 'out of memory' text -- exactly the structure the stateMissing/stateOom guard adds and reverting it removes, so this is red without the guard.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/recordTyRunTest.asl#" :text "Gate for record-typed SSA (tyRec) through the LLVM backend: a record Val passes as %Val, a tail call between a Val and a record return stays musttail, an entry returning a record gets the Val main wrapper, and a program over record parameters, returns, joins and typed lets compiles with clang and exits with the value it computes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/shadowRootTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-B collector root mode regression. The linear-memory target skips native-stack scanning and continues to mark explicit roots; native target emission keeps its conservative stack walk. On wasm32 the mark phase also walks the program's shadow-root frames from @asl_gc_shadow_top, which the wasm32 collector defines and the native one does not; wasmStackRootsTest covers the frames generated code keeps.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sourceE2eTest.asl#" :text "Gate for compiler driver to LLVM (plan SH unit D1): compiles paren-dialect fib source to .ll and verifies golden; checks that unsupported constructs return lowering diagnostics; verifies compilePackageToLlvm! no longer refuses a package with imports (multiModuleTest runs one)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sourceE2eTest.asl#main" :text "Prints the .ll of fib, or with argument negMain or negMin of the negation program entered there.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for asl-target-llvm/sys (plan RT unit S3, round 2 IR-rawPrims): for each of the 19 covered syscalls (read write close pread pwrite kill fsync flock rename chmod mkdir unlink rmdir symlink readlink sysconf clock_gettime usleep getpid) the emitted IR declares the real C function (close, kill, fsync, flock, rename, chmod, mkdir, unlink, rmdir, symlink, clock_gettime and usleep now at their real i32 return, widened by rawWidenI32/sext before the 0/-1 check) and never calls the matching fdRead/fdWrite/fdClose host builtin; sysRead's (and sysReadlink's, sysClockGettime's) malloc'd scratch buffer is NULL-checked (rawPtrIsNull/icmp eq ptr) before the real syscall runs; a native success-path run exits with a value checked against the operation's own effect (a byte count, a filesystem side effect probed by the shell, or a fixed sentinel once the call cannot fail by construction), and a native error-path run exits with the decoded errno, checked against libc/libcConst for this host's own triple (hostFacts, from uname, not a facts table pinned ahead of time) -- EBADF (read, write, pread, pwrite, close, fsync, flock), ENOENT (rename, unlink, rmdir, readlink), EEXIST (mkdir, symlink) and EINVAL (kill, clock_gettime) are each exercised at least once. getpid, sysconf and usleep have no portable failure input exercised here: getpid cannot fail, sysconf's only failure (an unsupported name) is not reliably reproducible across hosts, and usleep's documented EINVAL (a microsecond count of 1,000,000 or more) is not enforced on this host (confirmed with a standalone C probe), so only their success path runs. Builds clang and the programs through processRun in a fresh temporary directory, as asl-target-llvm/tests/externNativeRunTest does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#repoRootAbs" :text "Absolute path to the repo root, for building an absolute asl-host path after a `cd` into work (the relative `host` path only resolves from the repo root, which is where every other test here already runs from).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to one of libc/libcTriples, or to a recognized-but-unsupported triple name (darwin-x86_64: types.asl's emitLlvmTargetTriple accepts x86_64-apple-darwin for LLVM emission, but libc.asl carries no verified struct-offset row for it, since a C probe needs a real Intel-Mac host to run -- rather than guess, hostFacts below hard-errors on it instead of silently reusing darwin-arm64's offsets); empty for any other unrecognized host, which hostFacts also hard-errors on.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#hostFacts" :text "This host's own TripleFacts (libc/libcFacts (hostTriple)), so the gate exercises the triple it actually runs on rather than a facts table pinned ahead of time. Hard-errors (assert false) when hostTriple names a triple libc.asl has no verified row for, or recognizes no triple at all, instead of silently defaulting to darwin-arm64's offsets on an unverified host; the returned emptyTripleFacts is unreached in practice.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#dateFromEpoch" :text "`date` at epoch under TZ=UTC, portably: BSD/Darwin's date takes -r <epoch>, GNU/Linux's takes -d @<epoch> (neither accepts the other's flag).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#moduleOf" :text "A module over the given TripleFacts, resultTypeDecl and optionTypeDecl plus every extern sys.asl declares for that triple, and the given functions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#constOf" :text "The named O_*/F_*/LOCK_*/errno/_SC_* value for this host's own triple, from libc/libcConst, -1 (and asserted away by expectErrno) when the table has no such row.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#errCaseInstrs" :text "Unboxes the err field of resv (bound by runFn's switch) into errCode.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#unwrapFn" :text "Unwraps a sys/*Fn builder's Result (round 3, plan S3b: sysPollFn, sysClockGettimeFn and sysNanosleepFn now read struct facts through structOffset/structByteSize and can err at build time), failing the assertion with libc.asl's own missing-fact message instead of silently building against a bad function; the dummy sysGetpidFn fallback is never reached on a host whose libc.asl row is actually present.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#runFn" :text "A `run` function: entryPre, then callee(callArgs) as a Result (dest resv), switched to okCase (okInstrs, returns okReturn) or errCase (decodes resv's errno, returns it).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#caseModule" :text "One `run` program over the given facts and string pool, declaring sysErrnoValue plus whatever other sys* functions the case calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#errnoCaseModule" :text "A case whose only interesting path is the error branch: the ok branch returns a fixed, unreached sentinel so the function still type-checks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#getenvModule" :text "A `run` program calling sysGetenv(strings[0]), switched to someCase (someInstrs, returns someReturn) or noneCase (returns the fixed noneReturn sentinel, since getenv's miss is not an error).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#runCase" :text "Emits, links and runs one case's module under the given shell command (cmd names the built binary, e.g. work/name or a redirection wrapped around it).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#runWithFd3" :text "Opens fd 3 read-write on path (POSIX sh's own exec, no subshell) before exec'ing the binary, since this module has no open(2) wrapper of its own.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testReadZeroLength" :text "SYS-freeDeclAndMalloc0 gate: sysRead(fd, 0) is a legitimate zero-length read (POSIX read() returns 0, not an error, when the requested count is 0) and must come back ok with an empty Bytes, not the stale-errno err a malloc(0)-returns-NULL implementation could otherwise produce; sysReadFn already mallocs max(max,1) (plan IR-rawPrims round S3b, atLeastOneBlocks) rather than malloc(0) for exactly this reason, so this locks that fix in as a regression gate: reverting malloc(allocSize) to malloc(max) here makes this test the one that goes red.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testFreeDeclaredPtr" :text "SYS-freeDeclAndMalloc0 gate: free's extern declaration must take ptr, not i64 -- an i64 argument would force every call site through a ptrtoint round-trip (box the malloc'd ptr back to an integer just to call free) and would mismatch the real libc free(void*) at the LLVM IR level. Asserts the emitted declare line directly, on the same read-path module testRead already builds (sysReadFn is the simplest function that mallocs and frees). A param-type mutant (ptr -> i64) never reaches this assertion in the first place: asl-ir/verify's checkCall rejects every free call site first (ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH, 'buf' is ptr where i64 is required), confirmed by hand against this same module -- the verifier is the real gate, this assertion is the regression lock for the declaration itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#realpathWriteModule" :text "A `run` program chaining sysRealpath(path) into sysWrite(1, resolvedPath) on success, so the test can compare the exact resolved-path bytes written to stdout against asl-host's own realPath+print, not merely a length (a wrong path of the same length would otherwise pass); any err along the chain returns a fixed, unreached sentinel -1, since the gate only exercises the success chain (the missing-path case is exercised separately, one call at a time, by errnoCaseModule).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testRealpath" :text "LIBC-pathMaxIntToPtr gate: sysRealpath against a symlink (absolute path), the same symlink by a relative name (cd into work first), and a missing path. The two success cases print the full resolved path natively (sysRealpath chained into sysWrite(1, ...), realpathWriteModule) and compare the exact stdout bytes against asl-host's own realPath+print -- not a hand-copied expected string, since the exact resolved path (symlinks in /tmp itself included) is host-dependent, and not merely a length (stringLength, mod 256 as an exit code), since a wrong path of the same length would otherwise also pass. The missing case has no resolved path to print, so it stays checked by errno alone (ENOENT).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#exePathWriteModule" :text "A `run` program chaining sysExePath() into sysWrite(1, path), so the test compares the exact resolved exe path bytes, not a length; any err returns the sentinel -1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testExePath" :text "T2 gate for sysExePath, the native twin of asl-host's procExePath: the native program, run through a symlink from another cwd, prints the resolved path of its own binary, which must equal asl-host's realPath of that binary (the link resolved, so neither argv0 nor the cwd leaks in); and asl-host's own procExePath, run through a symlink to asl-host from cwd /, equals its realPath of the asl-host binary, the same semantics on the VM side (dyld reports the invoked link, so a procExePath without realpath fails here). On darwin the emitted IR declares dyld's _NSGetExecutablePath, on linux it does not (the /proc/self/exe link instead).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testUsleep" :text "No error path: POSIX documents EINVAL for a microsecond count of 1,000,000 or more, but this host's usleep(2000000) returns 0 (confirmed with a standalone C probe, errno left stale at ETIMEDOUT from an unrelated earlier call, not set by this one), so the old limit is not enforced here; success-only, like testGetpid and testSysconf.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testGetenv" :text "sysGetenv: PATH is set in every environment this gate runs under, so the hit case decodes a non-empty Bytes; a name this test invents is not, so the miss case takes the none branch (not an error -- no errno path at all here, hence no expectErrno).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#fcntlSetThenGetModule" :text "A `run` program chaining sysFcntlSet(fd=3, setCmd, arg) into sysFcntlGet(fd=3, getCmd) on success, masking the re-read flags against nonblock (rawAndI64, eqInt) and returning 1 when the bit is set, 0 when it is not; any err along the chain returns a fixed, unreached sentinel 2, since the gate only exercises the success chain (EBADF is exercised separately, one call at a time, by getErrMod/setErrMod).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testFcntl" :text "sysFcntlGet/sysFcntlSet against a real read-write fd (opened by runWithFd3's own shell redirection, O_RDWR and nothing else): F_GETFL's exit equals O_RDWR, F_SETFL(O_NONBLOCK) exits 0 and a later F_GETFL on the same fd (fcntlSetThenGetModule, round 3 item 3) reads O_NONBLOCK back set, and both F_GETFL and F_SETFL report EBADF on a closed fd.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testPoll" :text "sysPoll against a real fd (a FIFO, opened read-write by runWithFd3/runCase's own shell redirection, since this module has no open(2) or pipe(2) wrapper of its own): with nothing written, poll(POLLIN, 0ms) returns 0 ready; once a byte has been written into that same fd before exec'ing the probe (shell-side printf, since the fd is bidirectional), it returns 1 ready with revents==POLLIN; a never-opened fd (99) reports revents==POLLNVAL with poll() itself still succeeding (POSIX: an invalid fd is a per-descriptor condition, not a -1/errno failure), so unlike every other covered syscall this case has no errno path at all -- round 3 item 3's stronger gate for a non-degenerate single-fd poll.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testNanosleep" :text "sysNanosleep(0, 1000000) (1ms): succeeds with exit 0. sysNanosleep(-1, 0): POSIX requires EINVAL for a negative tv_sec on both darwin and linux.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#listFieldInstrs" :text "Unboxes the first n Int64 elements of a boxed Val list (listVar, built by one of sys.asl's own list-returning functions) into n raw i64 names, via @listHeadOr/@listTailOr (defaulting to a boxed 0, never reached for a well-formed n-element list); returns the instructions and the raw names in order. Build-time unrolling (fold/range, exactly as sys.asl's own decodeLittleEndianBytes does), not a runtime loop, since n is fixed and known here.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#joinIntsInstrsGo" :text "Build-time recursion (not a runtime loop: names is a fixed, already-known list) converting each raw i64 name to a String (stringFromInt64) and joining them with spaceName (a Val String constant the caller already bound, from its own module's string pool, since this test module -- unlike sys.asl's own functions -- has one).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testStatFamily" :text "sysStat/sysLstat(path) printed as \"size mode mtime kind\\n\" to stdout and compared against an oracle for size, mode and mtime, plus libc/libcConst's wantKind matched against the printed kind field, and against ENOENT on a missing path. The oracle is this host's own asl-host run of a fixture calling the matching host builtin -- fileStat (follows a symlink, as sysStat/stat(2) does) when followLink is true, fileLstat (does not follow, as sysLstat/lstat(2) does) when false -- never a shell `stat`, whose flags differ between BSD/Darwin and GNU/Linux; fileLstat's own LinkStat record exposes mtime exactly as fileStat's FileStat does, so sysLstat's size/mode/mtime can be checked against the link itself rather than, wrongly, its target.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#mustSizeIn" :text "size of a stat row that must exist on every triple reaching here (hostFacts already hard-errors otherwise), failing loudly rather than defaulting to 0 and reading garbage offsets if it somehow does not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#mustOffsetIn" :text "Byte offset of field within a stat row that must exist on every triple reaching here; see mustSizeIn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#readAtimeMtimeModule" :text "A `run` program calling stat(path) directly (not through sysStatFn, which decodes st_mtimespec but not st_atimespec) and printing \"atimeSec atimeNsec mtimeSec mtimeNsec\\n\" to stdout, so testUtimes can check sysUtimes set atime and mtime independently, sub-second precision included -- no asl-host builtin exposes atime, only mtime (fileStat/fileLstat's FileStat/LinkStat records). Builds its own malloc/valToCStr/free sequence directly (stringToPtrInstrs and freeInstr are sys.asl-internal, not exported) since the extern list a module needs (sysExterns) already declares malloc, free, valToCStr and stat for every triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testUtimes" :text "sysUtimes(path, aSec,aUsec, mSec,mUsec) with aSec != mSec and both usec fields nonzero and distinct (a mutant swapping the atime/mtime timeval pair, or truncating usec, must fail): reads st_atimespec.tv_sec and st_mtimespec.tv_sec straight back with a dedicated native stat decode (readAtimeMtimeModule; no asl-host builtin exposes atime) and checks both against the exact seconds set, not merely that mtime changed; ENOENT on a missing path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testLocaltime" :text "sysLocaltime(1700000000) under TZ=UTC (so both the native run and the date oracle agree), the nine tm fields printed and compared against date's own decomposition of that epoch under TZ=UTC (%S %M %H %d (%m - 1) (%Y - 1900) %w (%j - 1)), via dateFromEpoch (portable: BSD -r vs GNU -d @). 1700000000 (2023-11-14 22:13:20 UTC), not epoch 0, deliberately: at epoch 0 tm_sec/tm_min/tm_hour are all 0, so a mutant swapping their decode offsets would still pass (0 read from the wrong offset is still 0); 1700000000's sec=20, min=13, hour=22, mday=14, mon=11, year=2023 are pairwise distinct, so a swapped or misaligned offset -- or a moved struct tm field width -- changes at least one printed value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testGetrusage" :text "sysGetrusage() printed as \"maxRss userUs sysUs\\n\": a fresh process' own usage is not reproducible against a second, separate asl-host invocation, so this checks shape (all three non-negative, maxRss and the sum of userUs/sysUs strictly positive -- loading and running even a trivial native binary burns measurable rss and some cpu) rather than equality with a host run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testUname" :text "sysUname() printed as \"sysname machine\\n\" and compared against `uname -s`/`uname -m`.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#dirListPrintLoopModule" :text "sysDirList(path), then a real runtime loop (list length unknown at build time) writing each name plus a newline to fd 1 via sysWrite, in whatever order sysDirList returned them (the test sorts both sides before comparing).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#testDirList" :text "sysDirList(dir) printed one name per line (dirListPrintLoopModule), sorted and compared against asl-host's own dirList(dir) (also sorted, since bytewise-sorted is already dirList's own contract -- sorting again is idempotent) for a small directory of known names; ENOENT on a missing directory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest.asl#quoteSh" :text "Single-quotes s for a POSIX shell word, escaping an embedded single quote the standard '\\''  way.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit NETLOWER: a native program's tcpListen, tcpConnect, sockAccept, sockLocalPort, unixListen and unixConnect run asl-target-llvm/sysNet's ASL functions through asl-target-llvm/sysRoute, not asl/host/src/sysNet.c's C table. Programs are lowered as nativeRunTest lowers them (lowerSourceWith over the prelude) and emitted by emitLlvmProgramFor for this host's own libc.asl facts (uname mapped to a triple, as sysNetTest does), or built by asl1 for the two-module program, then linked by clang against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a: (1) the emitted IR of programs calling all six has no asl_rt_builtin_sysNet call and defines the routed wrappers internal; (2) nm -P on the linked binaries lists no bTcpListen, bSockAccept, bUnixListen or sysNetBuiltins; (3) native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on a TCP and a Unix loopback echo and on the error cases (ports and fds out of range or not Int, a bound port, a refused connect, empty, 200-byte and missing unix paths, a path that is not a String), whose errnos are the host triple's EINVAL, ECONNREFUSED and ENOENT; (4) a two-module program calling tcpListen in both modules links and runs, built as one linked module by asl1 and separately per module through emitLlvmModuleFor and emitLlvmProgramFor; (5) the pure emitLlvmProgram routes nothing, so its IR builds for any host, and asl1 build (emitLlvmProgramNative!) routes exactly when libc.asl verifies the host's triple (darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 since SYSLINUX; on any other host the program keeps libaslhost.a's C table). Also: emitLlvmProgramFor routes for the linux-x86_64 facts (accept4, __errno_location) and its IR verifies, and sysNet's listen backlog is the triple's SOMAXCONN (128 darwin-arm64, 4096 linux).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to a libc/libcTriples triple, independently of sysRoute tripleOf, empty for any other host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#hostFacts" :text "This host's libc.asl row; a host libc.asl has no row for fails the gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#hostConst" :text "The VM's err text for errno name on this host: io: and the host triple's value of name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#echoSource" :text "Loopback echo over tcpListen 0, sockLocalPort, tcpConnect and sockAccept, then over unixListen and unixConnect at <dir>/echo.sock, dir the first argument; prints each step and exits 0 when both echoes arrive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#errorsSource" :text "The error cases, each printed as its label and ok or the err message: ports and fds out of range, a port already bound, a refused connect, empty, 200-byte and missing unix paths, and a non-Int port and non-String path passed through untyped parameters.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#sixSource" :text "One call of each routed builtin, no prelude function, for the single-module lowering asl-ir/lower lowerSource does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#wrapperDef" :text "The emitted definition line prefix of a routed wrapper, internal to its module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#build" :text "Writes work/name.asl and work/name.ll, the IR emitLlvmProgramFor emits at hostFacts for src lowered over the host's prelude (lowerSourceWith, as nativeRunTest's testPreludeSingleModule driver lowers it), and returns the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#linkBinWith" :text "Links the IR files lls against the archives libs into work/name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#nmNames" :text "The first column of nm -P: every symbol of the binary, local ones included, without Mach-O's leading underscore.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#checkIr" :text "Gate (1): no call goes through asl_rt_builtin_sysNet and every routed wrapper is defined, internal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#checkSymbols" :text "Gate (2): the binary links none of sysNet.c's table.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#checkParity" :text "Gate (3): the native binary's stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source; returns the native stdout.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testTwoModules" :text "Gate (4): tcpListen in both modules of one program; the asl1 linked build defines each routed function once when libc.asl verifies this host's triple and otherwise calls asl_rt_builtin_sysNet with no routed function, and the separately compiled modules, emitted for hostFacts, each carry an internal copy and still link.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testLinuxRouting" :text "emitLlvmProgramFor routes for the linux-x86_64 facts: accept4 and __errno_location replace darwin's accept and __error, and opt -passes=verify accepts the IR (skipped with a printed reason when no opt is installed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#backlogIn" :text "The constant the instruction dest of a sysNet function defines, -1 when absent.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testBacklog" :text "listen()'s backlog is the triple's SOMAXCONN, as sysNet.c's listen(fd, SOMAXCONN).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#clashSource" :text "A program defining a function named like sysNet's tcpListen function, and calling tcpListen.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testRouteModule" :text "routeModule's module merging: a module function named like an added one is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_NAME, an own extern of an added name with another signature is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_EXTERN, an identical own extern is kept once, the string io: is appended to the pool only when absent, and a module calling no routed builtin comes back unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testNativeEntries" :text "Gate (5): the pure emitLlvmProgram emits netSix with its socket calls through asl_rt_builtin_sysNet and no routed function, so the IR builds on any host; it is the unrouted reference, whose C sysNet table left libaslrt.a with SYSLOWER-b, so it links libaslrt.a then libaslhost.a, which keeps sysNet.o as the oracle path; routeFactsFor gives facts for the measured darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 rows (SYSLINUX) and none for an unknown host; tripleOf over this host's platformInfo agrees with uname; and emitLlvmProgramNative! routes netSix exactly when routeFactsFor gives this host's triple facts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#bi" :text "An opBuiltin call, as asl-ir/lower emits for a host builtin, which routeModule rewrites.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#fdOf" :text "prefix.i32, the i32 fd of a boxed Int.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#handoffExterns" :text "The libc calls the handoff program makes itself; malloc and close are declared exactly as sysNet declares them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#handoffRun" :text "run() -> i64: unixSocketPair, then fork. The child closes end a, takes a listening socket from end b with sockRecvFd, sockAccepts one connection on it and writes A to it, returning 0. The parent closes end b, and only then unixListens at strings[0], so the child can hold the listener through SCM_RIGHTS alone and not through fork; it passes the listener over end a with sockSendFd (whose ok value is the fd sent), closes its own listener and end a, unixConnects, reads the child's byte and waits for the child, returning the byte, 65, when all of it holds. Each failing step returns its own 2xx code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#programTypes" :text "The Result and Pair ADTs as asl-ir/lower declares them from the prelude, which the program switches on and destructures before routing adds anything.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#fdErrorsRun" :text "run() -> i64 printing each result: sockRecvFd -1 and 2147483648, sockSendFd -1 0 and 0 \"x\" (io:EINVAL, the wrappers' range and Int checks), sockRecvFd on a socket pair end whose peer is closed (no descriptor: io:EBADMSG) and sockSendFd on that closed end (io:EBADF); exits 0, or 1 when unixSocketPair fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#withConst" :text "facts with the const name moved by delta (a later pair wins in libc/pairFind).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#emitRun" :text "work/name.ll from emitLlvmProgramFor facts m with entry run; returns the IR text, empty after a failed assertion.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#runGuarded" :text "bin run with a 20 s watchdog, so a handoff that never arrives fails with 137 instead of hanging the gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testFdHandoff" :text "Gate FDHANDOFF: the handoff program, routed for this host's facts, links with no asl_rt_builtin_sysNet call and its parent reads the A the child wrote on the connection it accepted on the listener received over the socket pair (exit 65); the error program prints the wrappers' io:EINVAL, io:EBADMSG for a message with no descriptor and io:EBADF; a mutant SCM_RIGHTS row turns the handoff red, and libc.asl rows whose CMSG_LEN_INT does not end CMSG_DATA_OFFSET's int are refused at build as ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_FACTS.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testFdHandoffLinux" :text "The handoff program routed for linux-x86_64 receives with MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC (1073741824) instead of the fcntl dance and its IR verifies (skipped with a printed reason when no opt is installed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#rowOf" :text "A struct field offset of facts, -1 when absent (the probe-verified rows sendRawInstrs reads all exist).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#sendRawInstrs" :text "A sendmsg built here rather than by sysNet's sendFdFn: one zero byte with one SOL_SOCKET/SCM_RIGHTS control message of cmsg_len cmsgLen carrying the i32 fds, in a controlLen control buffer; <p>.n is sendmsg's result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#fdEdgesRun" :text "run() -> i64 printing, over one channel pair: the FD_CLOEXEC bit (fcntl F_GETFD) of a descriptor sockRecvFd received (1); then a raw sendmsg (its 1) of two SCM_RIGHTS fds, which sockRecvFd's one-int control buffer cuts (MSG_CTRUNC: io:EMSGSIZE); then a raw sendmsg (its 1) of an SCM_RIGHTS message with no int, whose cmsg_len is CMSG_DATA_OFFSET (io:EBADMSG). Exits 0, or 1 when a channel or the first pass fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#testFdEdges" :text "sockRecvFd's edges natively: the received descriptor is close-on-exec, a cut control message is io:EMSGSIZE and an SCM_RIGHTS message carrying no int is io:EBADMSG.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetRouteTest.asl#ki" :text "-- FDHANDOFF: SCM_RIGHTS descriptor passing over unixSocketPair, sockSendFd and sockRecvFd --")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for asl-target-llvm/sysNet (plan RT unit S5): a hand-built native program (step chain over sysNetTcpListen/sysNetSockLocalPort/sysNetTcpConnect/sysNetSockAccept, then sys/sysWriteFn/sysReadFn for the actual echo) binds an ephemeral TCP port on loopback, connects to itself, accepts, writes one byte and reads it back, exiting with the echoed byte's code (65, 'A') on success or a distinct 2xx sentinel naming which step failed; a second program does the same over an AF_UNIX socket in a temp directory. Both are compared against asl-host run of an equivalent ASL-source program using the real tcpListen/tcpConnect/sockAccept/sockLocalPort/unixListen/unixConnect/fdWrite/fdRead builtins (asl/host/src/sysNet.c's own VM path), which must exit with the same 65. opt -passes=verify checks both emitted .ll files. A mutant TripleFacts with sockaddr_in's sin_port offset wrong by one byte is built and run the same way, demonstrating the gate is sensitive to a real byte-layout bug (it must NOT exit 65).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#opt" :text "opt is not on PATH by default on macOS (LLVM.org's opt, not Xcode's own toolchain, which carries none): Homebrew's llvm keg has it; fall back to bare \"opt\" (PATH) for a Linux CI host where llvm-opt is already on PATH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#verifies?" :text "opt -passes=verify on the emitted .ll, a structural check independent of the binary actually running correctly.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#okI64Instrs" :text "Unboxes a Result's ok field as a raw i64 (for the sysNet*/sys.asl functions whose ok value was boxed via boxInstr: fd, port, byte counts).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#okValInstrs" :text "The ok field as a Val directly, no unbox (sysRead's ok value is already a Val Bytes, mkBytes' own result, never boxed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "Local copy of sysDirectTest's own hostTriple (private there): uname -s/-m mapped to a libc/libcTriples triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#mutantSockaddrInFacts" :text "base with sockaddr_in's sin_port offset shifted by +1 byte, everything else identical: the mutation the task's :gate clause asks for.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#dedupExternsByName" :text "sys/sysExterns and sysNet/sysNetExterns both declare sysCommonExterns (malloc/free/valToCStr/errnoAccessor) and sysNet.asl separately redeclares fcntl/close (private in sys.asl, so it carries its own copies): the combined list has duplicate names by name, same signature, which this module's own emitter rejects outright (ERR_IR_DUPLICATE_DEFINITION) rather than silently folding, so the caller dedupes first, last occurrence per name wins.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#tcpSourceFixture" :text "An equivalent ASL-source program over the real tcpListen/tcpConnect/sockAccept/sockLocalPort/fdWrite/fdRead builtins (asl/host/src/sysNet.c's VM path), returning the same 65-on-success / 2xx-sentinel convention as tcpEchoRunFn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#emitAndVerifyOnly" :text "Structural check only (round 2, plan S5 fix c): emits sysNet IR for a triple this darwin host can never execute (linux-x86_64/linux-aarch64) and runs opt -passes=verify, so sockAcceptFn's accept4(SOCK_CLOEXEC) branch is actually checked by something other than reading the source.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#nulPathRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: calls sysNetUnixListen on a 4-byte path 'a','b',0,'c' built via a raw malloc'd buffer + mkStr (so the embedded NUL survives, unlike an ASL source string literal); returns 65 only if the call errs with EINVAL, as bUnixListen's own unixAddr (memchr) does (round 2, plan S5 fix a).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#portRangeRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: calls sysNetTcpListen(65536) and sysNetTcpConnect(70000), both outside 0..65535; returns 65 only if both err with EINVAL, as bTcpListen/bTcpConnect's own portArg does (round 2, plan S5 fix b).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#tcpEchoRunFn" :text "-- the native echo-over-tcp program --\nrun() -> Int64: tcpListen(0), sockLocalPort, tcpConnect, sockAccept, write 'A' on the connecting fd, read 1 byte back on the accepted fd, close all three, return the echoed byte's code (65 on success); a distinct 2xx sentinel per step on failure.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysNetTest.asl#unixEchoRunFn" :text "-- the native echo-over-unix-socket program --\nrun() -> Int64: unixListen(path), unixConnect(path), sockAccept, write 'A', read it back, same sentinel convention as tcpEchoRunFn. path is strings[1] of the enclosing module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's own opt, not shipped beside /usr/bin/clang on this host: checks a few known homebrew locations, then PATH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#verifyLl" :text "opt -passes=verify over an emitted .ll: skipped, with a logged reason, only when optBin finds no opt binary at all.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to one of libc/libcTriples; empty when this host matches none of them, in which case hostFacts falls back to darwinArm64Facts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#sysFns" :text "sys.asl's own functions for this triple, or an assertion failure plus an empty list on a missing libc.asl fact (sysPollFn/sysClockGettimeFn/sysNanosleepFn can err at build time; not expected on a host libc.asl covers).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#pidRangeRunFn" :text "Run native procKill with a pid one above INT32_MAX and require EINVAL before the narrowed pid reaches kill.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#testProcPidRange" :text "The generated procKill rejects a positive Int64 PID it cannot represent as pid_t before calling kill.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#probeEnv" :text "The environment prefix both runs share, setting the variable infoSource looks for in envList.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#routedNames" :text "The process builtins this file's programs must reach through asl-target-llvm/sysProc's wrappers (sysRouteTest's routedNames lists them with the rest of the sys table).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#cTableCall" :text "The emitted call of builtin name through sys.c's table, as asl-target-llvm/ssa emits an opBuiltin of a sys name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#wrapperDef" :text "The emitted definition line prefix of a routed wrapper, internal to its module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#lowered" :text "src lowered over the host's prelude (lowerSourceWith, as nativeRunTest's driver lowers it): unit STANDINS gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity a row for every one of routedNames, so each lowers to an opBuiltin directly, with no stand-in.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#build" :text "Writes work/name.asl and work/name.ll, the IR emitLlvmProgramFor emits at hostFacts for src, and returns the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#checkIr" :text "Gate (1): no routed name is called through asl_rt_builtin_sys, and each name the program uses has its wrapper defined internal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#checkParity" :text "Gate (2): the native binary's stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source, both under probeEnv; returns both outputs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#procSource" :text "Every procSpawnv, procWaitPid, procWaitAny, procPoll, procRusage and procExecv case in one program: spawn of echo, sh exit 7, a missing binary, PATH and environment taken from the env argument, cwd, the SpawnedProc record and its three pipes; a child killed by SIGTERM; a 50 ms timeout while a child runs (procWaitPid nohang, procWaitAny, procPoll); procWaitAny over three children; procPoll before and after a child exits and reaping two at once; procRusage's shape; every argument error; procExecv failing in this process and, in children running this program again under PROC_MODE (the binary itself, or asl-host run of work/sysProc.asl), replacing the child's image with echo or sh. PROC_MODE=fwd spawns a child that records a SIGTERM in PROC_DIR and waits on it. Pids and fds print by name, since the two runs number them apart.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#procWant" :text "sys.c's results for procSource's main mode: exitCodeOf (an exit status, or minus the signal), mapErrno's texts (ENOENT notFound, ECHILD noChild, any other errno io:N), errStr io:22 for every argument sys.c rejects and badFd for an fd outside 0..INT_MAX, a SpawnedProc record of pid stdin stdout stderr and a Rusage record of six fields in sys.c's order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#testProc" :text "procSource built natively: the six process builtins route to their wrappers, and native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's and sys.c's computed results.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#fwdRun" :text "cmd run in PROC_MODE=fwd with PROC_DIR work/tag in the background; once its child has written ready (and 300 ms more, for the parent to block in procWaitPid), a shell sends the parent SIGTERM; returns the parent's exit status, its stdout and what the child wrote to term, one per line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#testProcFwd" :text "sys.c's waitForwarding: a SIGTERM sent to a parent blocked in procWaitPid reaches the child's process group (the child's trap writes term and exits) and then kills the parent by the same signal after its output is flushed; the native binary's status and output equal asl-host run's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#testProcLinux" :text "The linux build of the six wrappers, which this darwin host cannot run: procSource emitted for facts' triple routes every process builtin to its wrapper, watches children with pidfd_open (syscall) and signals with signalfd, finds environ through dlsym and has no darwin kqueue or _NSGetEnviron, and its IR passes opt -passes=verify (verifyLl).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit SYSLINUX (plan rows SYSLOWER-linux and LINUX-unroutedPreludeBuiltins): a native build on a linux-x86_64 or linux-aarch64 host routes. (1) routeFactsFor gives each linux triple its libc.asl row, marked verified, hostFactsOf maps the uname -s -m text of either linux host to it as routeHost! and parRoute routeHost! do, and darwin-arm64 keeps its row; an unknown host stays unrouted. (2) One fixture calls every builtin asl-ir/lower builtinArity lists (its rows read from lower.asl, so a new row is covered at once), linked as asl1 build links it (lk/linkEntry! over the host prelude and the native overlay); for each linux triple it is emitted as emitLlvmProgramNative! emits it on that host (routed for hostFactsOf's facts, else the unrouted emitLlvmProgram): every builtin lowers or is in documentedGaps with its reason, and a documented gap must still fail. The IR calls no asl_rt_builtin_* table, so the program links libaslrt.a without libaslhost.a, defines internal the wrapper of every builtin the sys, sysNet, clock and parallel routes list (envGet and the PRELUDEASL-E/P fs and proc builtins included), reads errno through __errno_location, names no darwin symbol, and clang -target compiles it to an ELF object of the triple. (3) factTable: each row names a libc fact, its value on linux-x86_64, linux-aarch64 and darwin-arm64 and the linux header defining it; each triple's libc.asl row holds that value and the triple's emitted IR materialises it as the named constant of the named routed function, so darwin-arm64's column also shows its row and IR unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#unameText" :text "What uname -s -m prints on a host of triple; a host libc.asl has no triple for otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#arityRows" :text "The (name arity) rows of asl-ir/lower's builtinArity, read from its source text in source order; empty when text holds no such function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#documentedGaps" :text "Builtins builtinArity lists that a linked linux build cannot lower, each with its reason. None: through lk/linkEntry! the native overlay and the prelude define floatNan, floatInf, floatNegInf, zstdDecompress and bytesSha256 (which lowerSourceWith alone leaves without a native definition), and every sys, socket, clock and parallel builtin routes on both linux triples.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#operands" :text "n placeholder operands, one for a variadic builtin (n below 0).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#fixtureSrc" :text "One function bK per row calling its builtin directly over placeholder operands, and main calling each; the gate lowers and emits it, never runs it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#gapFunctions" :text "The fixture function of each documented gap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#diagFunction" :text "The function a diagnostic locates, its locus up to any @.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#nativeOnHost" :text "m emitted as emitLlvmProgramNative! emits it on a host of triple: routed for the facts hostFactsOf gives that host's uname text, else unrouted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#routedWrappers" :text "The emitted definition prefix of the wrapper of every builtin the sysRoute tables and parRoute route; fileLockWait's wrapper is per operand count (sysRoute routedCallee), fileLockWait/1 for the fixture's one operand, as parallel's is (parMap/3 and parFold/5 for the fixture's full-arity calls).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#hostTripleOf" :text "The triple of the facts hostFactsOf gives for uname text, the err text itself when it fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#testRouteFacts" :text "Gate (1).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#checkLinuxIr" :text "Gate (2)'s IR checks for a linux triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#objectFor" :text "clang -target compiles work/triple.ll to an object of the triple: the emitted text is valid IR that lowers to the triple's machine code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#testBuiltins" :text "Gate (2); returns the linux triples whose IR it wrote to work/triple.ll.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#factTable" :text "Facts the routed functions read, each with the linux header defining it (kernel UAPI path or installed glibc header); darwin's column is its measured libc.asl row, -1 where darwin's row lacks the fact because its routed code takes another path (no pidfd or signalfd, recvmsg without MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC), so only the row's absence is checked. Every linux value was measured by tests/fixtures/libcProbe.c under glibc 2.36 on both triples (linuxLayoutGateTest).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#factValue" :text "A libc.asl fact: a constant by name, a struct field offset as struct.field, a struct's size as struct.size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#constScan" :text "awk program printing function|local value for each named integer constant (%local = bitcast iN value to) in emitted IR, function being the enclosing define's symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#irConsts" :text "Every named constant of work/triple.ll by function|local key (IR symbol names), each key's values in IR order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteLinuxTest.asl#testFacts" :text "Gate (3) for triple: its libc.asl row holds every factTable value, and, when its IR was emitted to work/triple.ll, the IR materialises each as the row's named constant.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#" :text "Gate for unit SYSLOWER-a: a native program's fdRead, fdWrite, fdClose, fdPoll, fdNonBlocking, cpuCount, platformInfo, localDate, envList, procSelf, procAlive?, procKill and procExePath run asl-target-llvm/sysRoute's wrappers over asl-target-llvm/sys, not asl/host/src/sys.c's table. Programs are lowered as nativeRunTest lowers them (lowerSourceWith over the prelude), emitted by emitLlvmProgramFor for this host's libc.asl facts and linked by clang against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a: (1) the emitted IR calls none of the 13 through asl_rt_builtin_sys and defines each wrapper it uses internal; (2) native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on a pipe round trip through cat (0-byte, 1-byte and 64 KiB transfers, end of file, use after close), fdPoll on idle, ready and closed fds with 0, 50 ms and over-INT_MAX timeouts, fdNonBlocking then fdRead on an empty pipe, fds -1, 999999 and 2^31 and every argument-type and range error, and on cpuCount, platformInfo, localDate, envList, procSelf, procAlive? and procKill each compared inside the program with a command reporting the same fact (getconf, uname, date, env, sh's $PPID), procAlive? on itself, a reaped child and pid 1, procKill with valid, unknown and out-of-range arguments; procExePath prints the binary's own realpath; (3) the constants routeConst reads from libc.asl (signal numbers, sysErrKind's errnos, EROFS, EOVERFLOW, POLLPRI, POLLERR, POLLHUP) equal this host's C headers, by a compiled probe; (4) unit SYSLOWER-b: a program calling procSpawnv, procWaitPid, procWaitAny, procPoll, procRusage, procExecv, fileLock, fileLockWait, fileAppend, fileLockAt, fileReadAt and fileWriteAt has no call through asl_rt_builtin_sys in its IR (testTwelve), the file wrappers' native runs equal asl-host run's (testFile), nm -P on libaslrt.a shows no sys.o or sysNet.o member (both left RT_SRCS; libaslhost.a keeps them) and nm -P on a native program using fdRead, procSpawnv and fileLockAt shows no bFd, bProc or bFile symbol (testArchive, testTwelve); (5) the pure emitLlvmProgram routes no sys builtin, and emitLlvmProgramFor routes them for the linux-x86_64 facts through __errno_location and the environ global with IR that verifies; (6) routeModule adds the sys strings once and rejects a module's own PlatformInfo schema with other fields (ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_RECORD).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#probeEnv" :text "The environment prefix both runs share, setting the variable infoSource looks for in envList.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#hostTriple" :text "uname -s/-m mapped to a libc/libcTriples triple, independently of sysRoute tripleOf, empty for any other host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#hostFacts" :text "This host's libc.asl row; a host libc.asl has no row for fails the gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#fdSource" :text "A pipe round trip through cat (procSpawnv, from the C table) and the fd error cases; fds print as r and w, since the two processes number them apart.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#infoSource" :text "cpuCount, platformInfo, localDate, envList, procSelf, procAlive? and procKill, each compared with a command reporting the same fact, and procExePath on stderr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#fileSource" :text "fileLock, fileLockWait, fileAppend, fileLockAt, fileReadAt and fileWriteAt in a directory testFile prepares; a second process is this program run again through processRun, args[0] being the command that runs it (the binary, or asl-host run of the source), so lock contention and appends cross a process boundary in both runs; lock fds print as ok since the runs number them apart.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#cTableCall" :text "The emitted call of builtin name through sys.c's table, as asl-target-llvm/ssa emits an opBuiltin of a sys name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#wrapperDef" :text "The emitted definition line prefix of a routed wrapper, internal to its module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#lowered" :text "src lowered over the host's prelude (lowerSourceWith, as nativeRunTest's driver lowers it): unit STANDINS gave asl-ir/lower's builtinArity a row for every one of routedNames, so each lowers to an opBuiltin directly, with no stand-in.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#build" :text "Writes work/name.asl and work/name.ll, the IR emitLlvmProgramFor emits at hostFacts for src, and returns the IR text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#checkIr" :text "Gate (1): no routed name is called through asl_rt_builtin_sys, and each name the program uses has its wrapper defined internal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#checkParity" :text "Gate (2): the native binary's stdout and exit equal asl-host run's on the same source, both under probeEnv; returns both outputs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#fileDirSetup" :text "dir with sub/f.txt (old, mode 640), the empty sub/big.txt and sub/empty.txt, real/r.txt, the directory link link -> real, the file link sub/lnk -> f.txt and the fifo sub/fifo.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#fileNames" :text "The file wrappers sysFile's IR must define: fileLockWait's by operand count (sysRoute routedCallee).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#errnoText" :text "sys.c mapErrno's io:N text for an errno sysErrKind does not name, at this host's value of name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#times" :text "n copies of s, space separated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#fileWant" :text "sysFile's lines as sys.c gives them: io:22 for bad arguments, refused paths and fileLockWait's arity, busy and ERR_TIMEOUT against a held lock, EISDIR and ENAMETOOLONG as io:N, ERR_PATH_SYMLINK for a link on the walk, at the leaf or as the root, ERR_PATH_TYPE for a fifo or directory leaf, io:17 once 128 temp names are taken.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testFile" :text "Gates (1) and (2) for the file wrappers: sysFile's IR calls none of them through asl_rt_builtin_sys and defines each wrapper; the native binary and asl-host run, each in its own prepared directory and each running itself as the second process, print the same lines, sys.c's (fileWant), and exit alike; fileWriteAt kept f.txt's mode 640 in both directories.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#lowerNames" :text "The 12 builtins plan unit SYSLOWER-b routes, the last of sys.c's table.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#twelveSource" :text "A program calling each of lowerNames once with arguments sys.c rejects or answers without side effects (procRusage reduced to whether it succeeded), so both runs print the same line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#twelveWant" :text "sys.c's answers to twelveSource's calls: fdRead of 0 bytes is (ok \"\"), an empty argv, pid 0, an empty pid list, a timeout below -1, an empty root, an empty rel and a .. component are io:22, and opening the empty path is notFound.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#nmSymbols" :text "The symbol names nm -P prints for a linked binary, local ones included, each without the leading underscore of the darwin C ABI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#sysCNames" :text "The bFd, bProc and bFile symbols libaslhost.a's sys.o defines, local ones included, without the leading underscore of the darwin C ABI: sys.c's own builtins, which prelude.c's bFile and bProcess functions are not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testTwelve" :text "Gate (1): the IR of a program calling the 12 SYSLOWER-b builtins and fdRead neither calls nor declares asl_rt_builtin_sys (runtimeDecls keeps its line; usedDecls emits it only when used) and defines each wrapper internal, fileLockWait's by its argument count; the binary prints sys.c's answers, as asl-host run does. Gate (3), program half: nm -P on that binary, which uses fdRead, procSpawnv and fileLockAt, shows no bFd, bProc or bFile symbol of sys.c, local ones included.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#probeSource" :text "A C program printing NAME value for each of names from <errno.h>, <poll.h> and <signal.h>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testConsts" :text "Gate (3): routeConst, libc.asl's rows, gives this host's C header value of every errno, poll bit and signal the sys wrappers read (sysErrKind's errnos, the poll bits fdPoll maps and the signals procKill names).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#nmLines" :text "nm -P -A over archive: member, symbol, type for each line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testArchive" :text "Gate (3), archive half: nm -P -A on libaslrt.a shows no sys.o or sysNet.o member and no member defines a global sys.o or sysNet.o defines in libaslhost.a (which keeps both for asl-host and unrouted programs), and no member refers to one (hostVerbLink.o, which did through its builtinTables, left in NX4).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testPortable" :text "Gate (5): the pure emitLlvmProgram keeps every sys call on asl_rt_builtin_sys with no wrapper, and emitLlvmProgramFor routes them for linux-x86_64 through __errno_location and the environ global, its IR verifying under opt -passes=verify (skipped with a printed reason when no opt is installed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testRouteModule" :text "Gate (6): routeModule appends each sys pool string once and reuses one already in the pool; a module's own PlatformInfo schema with the same fields is kept once and with other fields is ERR_LLVM_SYSROUTE_RECORD.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#tagProbe" :text "name() -> i64: sysRoute's tagCheck of the raw n, the check tagOf applies to what abs returns.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysRouteTest.asl#testTagGuard" :text "tagOf's ABI guard: a program routed for this host (it calls fdClose, so the sys table and its tagOf and tagCheck are added) gets two entries calling tagCheck: with 6, a Tag, it exits 6; with 300, which no Tag is, it prints tagGuardText on stderr and exits non-zero instead of returning.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmAllocTest.asl#" :text "Executes the emitted wasm32 allocator in Node: small allocations share a run, freed blocks are reused, realloc preserves bytes, a block taken after a foreign memory.grow (the collector's pages) lies outside the foreign page, and failed growth returns null. The module is 2 initial pages under a 36-page maximum: the first run takes 16, the foreign grow 1, the 1100000-byte block a fresh 17-page run, so the 4000000-byte request cannot grow.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmE2eTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-E2 compares wasm stdout bytes and status with native for every runnable fixture; arithmetic/list/map/trap deliberately have nonzero expected status.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmE2eTest.asl#missingCollectorRejected" :text "A program's collector ABI reference fails linking when the collector object omits it; it never becomes a wasm host import.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmE2eTest.asl#absentCapabilityRejected" :text "The real wasm target lowering reports tcpListen as an absent capability.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-A gate. Part 1: the wasm32 collector emits memory.grow and no mmap or munmap, and it and a wasm32 hello compile with llc (from a candidate list or PATH) to wasm32 objects. Part 2: the memory.grow page source runs natively: the collector is emitted for the host triple with the memory.grow page source, its llvm.wasm.memory.grow.i32 call renamed to wasmGrowEmulated, which wasmGrowDriver.c defines over a PROT_NONE reservation whose grown part it makes readable and writable 64 KiB at a time, so a page outside grown memory faults; the driver builds rooted cons lists and checks every cell's address and value. One 1 MiB grow serves 64 collector pages, a refused grow is ERR_OOM, and pages a collection frees past the cache limit are reused rather than grown again. Work files live in a mktemp -d directory removed at the end.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#llcBin" :text "LLVM's llc from a known homebrew or Debian location, else PATH; empty when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#driverSource" :text "wasmGrowEmulated stands in for memory.grow on memory 0: it returns the reservation's page index before growing, -1 past limitPages; the reservation is 64 KiB aligned so page index * 65536 is the grown address. Modes: run builds one list of n cells and prints grow calls, grown 64 KiB pages and bad cells; reuse builds n cells, collects, drops them, collects and builds n again, printing grown pages after each build and bad cells.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#nativeGrowFacts" :text "The host's native target with the wasm page source: what Part 2 runs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#buildDriver" :text "The driver binary linked with the host-triple memory.grow collector; a failing step is asserted and the runs that follow fail on the missing binary.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#bounded" :text "A driver run killed by SIGALRM (exit 142) after 120 s: a corrupt heap can loop, which must fail the gate rather than hang it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#testGrow" :text "30000 cons cells fill 76 collector pages: two grows of 16 wasm pages (1 MiB, 64 collector pages each), every cell inside grown memory and intact.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#testOom" :text "With memory capped at one run (16 wasm pages), the 65th collector page's grow is refused: ERR_OOM through gcFloorFail, exit 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmGcPageSourceTest.asl#testReuse" :text "500000 live cells (about 1263 pages) collected, dropped and collected leave the pages past the 8 MiB cache limit free; rebuilding them grows no memory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmImportTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-D: wasm32 syscall routing imports supported Val builtins, verifies wasm modules, rejects listed unsupported sys builtins and leaves unrelated builtin classification to later lowering.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-E1b gate: hello, an allocation loop that forces collections and a program printing Int64 and Float64 values are emitted with the wasm32 facts row (libc/wasm32Facts, libc/runtimeAbi), compiled by llc, linked by wasm-ld without --allow-undefined, and their import sections read from the bytes by Node must lie inside the allowlist asl.write asl.exit asl.nowNs asl.trap, with no env.* import and no libc name; each is then instantiated in Node with one stub per allowed import and its stdout bytes and exit code must equal the native build of the same source for the host this runs on, linked against libaslrt.a. A control module importing asl.snprintf and env.malloc must be flagged by the same check.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#runnerJs" :text "Instantiates argv[2] with one stub per allowed import, refusing any other, calls _start and leaves its exit code; with argv[3] stats it writes freed N to stderr from the exported gcFreedObjects.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#allocationSource" :text "300 rounds of 1000 allocations, each a string and two lists; bounded depth since a self call on wasm32 is not a loop.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#stringSource" :text "A 2000-step string build, Int64 extremes, shortest round-trip Float64 text from subnormal to the largest finite, stringToFloat64 over accepted and rejected text; exits 3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#nativeRun" :text "The program built for the host triple with its libc facts and linked against libaslrt.a, run with its stdout captured.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmNoLibcTest.asl#controlLl" :text "A module that takes snprintf from module asl and malloc from env, as a renamed libc would.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#" :text "WASMROOTS2 gate: wasm32 programs keep heap values live in locals across calls that allocate past the collector's 8 MiB threshold (gcFreedObjects grows), then read those values back. Scenarios: a caller's list of fresh strings held across one allocating call; a non-tail recursion whose every frame holds a fresh string across an allocating call and the recursive call, and a tail-call chain whose accumulator is held across an allocating call; a closure whose only reference to its captured string is the closure value a caller holds; a variant (some) wrapping a list held across an allocating call. Each source is emitted with the wasm32 facts row, compiled by llc, linked by wasm-ld with the collector and support objects, run in Node, and built natively for this host and linked against libaslrt.a; the native stdout must equal the expected text, the wasm stdout must equal it byte for byte, the exit codes must agree and the wasm run must report freed objects.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#runnerJs" :text "Instantiates argv[2] with one stub per allowed host import, calls _start, leaves its exit code and writes freed N to stderr from the exported gcFreedObjects.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#churnLines" :text "churn rounds acc: rounds of 1000 allocations of a string and three cons cells each, garbage at once; bounded depth since a self call on wasm32 is not a loop. 30 rounds pass 6 MiB, so a few calls cross the 8 MiB threshold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#callerLocalSource" :text "kept, a list of 60 fresh strings, lives only in main's local while churn allocates about 30 MiB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#recursionSource" :text "descend: each of 25 non-tail frames holds mine and acc across churn and across the recursive call; tailChain: 25 tail calls whose accumulator is held across churn before each tail call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#closureSource" :text "greeter's captured prefix is reachable only through the closure main holds across churn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#variantSource" :text "held, a some wrapping a list of fresh strings, lives only in main's local while churn allocates.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#phiSource" :text "joined is the heap Val selected by a block-parameter phi in main; it stays live across churn before it is read.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#listLiteralSource" :text "A real opList with enough heap-valued cells to collect during its construction under a lowered GC threshold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#nativeRun" :text "The program built for the host triple with its libc facts and linked against libaslrt.a, run with its stdout captured.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmStackRootsTest.asl#sharedObjects" :text "The collector and support objects every scenario links, compiled once into workRoot.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmSysValTest.asl#" :text "Gate for WASMSYSVAL: wasm32 programs calling fileReadString or absent sys externs fail at compile with ERR_CAPABILITY_ABSENT naming the extern, and programs using only print contain only allowlisted imports.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmTailCallTest.asl#" :text "A million-deep self tail call and a million-deep mutual tail-call pair execute in wasm32 with stdout equal to native output.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmTailCallTest.asl#findExecutable" :text "Find an executable from known system locations, falling back to PATH via command -v.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmTrapTest.asl#" :text "WASMRT-C: the node harness runs division-by-zero and explicit raises from real compiler-emitted wasm, compares both recorded codes to the same source's native emitted binary, and verifies assert and integer-overflow source lowering.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmTrapTest.asl#wasmTrapCode" :text "Compiles an additional real ASL failure source and verifies its native rtError path retains the specific error code and is rewritten to the wasm callback, without invoking unrelated runtime imports in this isolated callback test.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmTrapTest.asl#wasmTrapCase" :text "Compiles a real trapping ASL source through lowerSource and emitLlvmProgramForTarget, checks wasm import symbols, links the resulting wasm32 object and compares its host callback code and message to the native emitted binary's error line for that exact source.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#" :text "Per-target-triple libc ABI facts for darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 (plan RT unit S1), with a libc-free wasm32-unknown-unknown row whose runtime services runtimeAbi names as host imports: O_* F_* LOCK_* flags, errno numbers, _SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN, the errno accessor symbol, a variadic flag per libc function, and struct sizes/field offsets for stat, flock, sockaddr_in, sockaddr_un, utsname, tm, rusage, dirent, pollfd, timespec, timeval, msghdr, cmsghdr and iovec, with CMSG_LEN, CMSG_SPACE and CMSG_DATA's offset for one int (SCM_RIGHTS fd passing) as consts. The darwin-arm64 row is measured on this host by tests/libcTableTest.asl against tests/fixtures/libcProbe.c (:verified true). The linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 rows are taken from the Linux kernel UAPI and glibc headers, one definition per header with the header named in its (:m) comment, and are measured by tests/linuxLayoutGateTest.asl, which runs the same probe under glibc 2.36 on both triples (natively on a Linux host, in docker otherwise) and compares every row (:verified true, plan unit SYSLINUX).\n  S_IF*/DT_*/RUSAGE_SELF (plan RT unit S4) are POSIX/BSD-and-Linux-common values (sys/stat.h, dirent.h, sys/resource.h), identical on all three triples, so they sit in each triple's own :consts rather than a fourth shared-consts function; S4's own libcProbe.c additions confirm them against this host's headers. RUSAGE_MAXRSS_UNIT is not a libc constant at all but the man-page-documented unit of struct rusage's ru_maxrss (bytes on Darwin/BSD, kilobytes on Linux -- see RSS_UNIT in asl/host/src/sys.c, which this table's value must keep matching), included here so sys/sysGetrusage never hardcodes it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sys.asl#" :text "Native-only syscall IR builders (plan RT unit S3): for each covered syscall, an SsaExtern against the real C ABI and an SsaFunction (named sysRead, sysWrite, ...) that calls it, checks its return and boxes a Result. A caller (sysDirectTest, or a future native-compilation pass) includes the needed externs, resultTypeDecl and functions in its own SsaModule and calls these by name through opCall; no part of the asl-ir/asl-target-llvm emitter or verifier is touched.\n  Result is the plan ASL-level ADT: (ssaTypeDecl \"Result\" ((ok 1) (err 1))), exactly as asl-ir/lower declares it when source uses ok/err. A syscall's error path always calls sysErrnoValue (errno read via the S1 TripleFacts accessor, e.g. __error or __errno_location) and boxes it as (err code); its success path boxes the raw result, a Bytes value (mkBytes) or a 2-element List (clock_gettime) as (ok value).\n  Round 2 (plan IR-rawPrims) closes the two structural gaps S3 reported rather than hacked around: close, kill, fsync, flock, rename, chmod, mkdir, unlink, rmdir, symlink, clock_gettime and usleep are now declared at their real i32 return (closeExtern et al.), called at tyI32 and widened to i64 by errnoResultFn's rawWidenI32 (sign-extending, sound for the full int range, not just the 0/-1 convention) before the existing ltInt/neInt check against zero; and mallocExtern's return (called by sysRead, sysPread, sysReadlink and sysClockGettime) is NULL-checked by errnoResultFn's allocCheck (rawPtrIsNull), taking the error branch (which reads errno, set by the allocator on failure, exactly as a genuine syscall error would) instead of running read/pread/readlink/clock_gettime against a null buffer.\n  Two gaps remained after round 2; round 3 (plan S3b) closes four of the five deferred items:\n    - poll (sysPoll, single-fd only) builds its own struct pollfd from libc.asl's own pollfd row for the host triple (libc/structFieldOffset, libc/structSize -- never a hardcoded offset) and is checked with ltInt, not the 0/-1 convention: a non-negative ready count, including the entirely valid 0 of a timeout with nothing ready, is success.\n    - fcntl (sysFcntlGet/sysFcntlSet) is declared once, through ssaExternVariadic, as the real C ABI's variadic int fcntl(int, int, ...); sysFcntlGet calls it with 2 arguments (F_GETFL's shape) and sysFcntlSet with 3 (F_SETFL's shape, or any other single-int-argument cmd), both checked with ltInt since F_GETFL's success return is the flags word itself, a legitimate 0. F_GETFL, F_SETFL and O_NONBLOCK are already in libc.asl (libcConst); callers read them from there, never hardcoded.\n    - getenv (sysGetenv) returns Option Bytes, (none) on an unset variable (getenv's own convention, not an error -- no errno path), copying the environment's string out with strlen (a new, triple-independent extern; libc.asl has no entry for it because its signature never varies) then mkBytes before returning, since the pointer getenv hands back is owned by the process environment and must never be freed or held past the call.\n    - nanosleep (sysNanosleep) writes {tv_sec, tv_nsec} into a malloc'd req buffer (rawStoreI64, NULL-checked) and calls nanosleep(req, rem) against a second malloc'd rem buffer rather than NULL: this IR has no raw int-to-pointer conversion to build a null ptr constant (checkConst only allows a raw i64/i32 constant to type as i64, i32 or val, never ptr), so passing NULL to the rem argument is not buildable without a new op. rem's contents are never read back; the EINTR-retry loop round 2's :d deferred stays deferred, out of this unit's scope too. Checked with neInt, nanosleep's own strict 0/-1 convention.\n    - sysRead, sysPread and sysReadlink now malloc(max(n,1)) rather than malloc(n): a two-block diamond (size.z/size.nz) joins into the `entry` block's own parameter (allocSize) carrying either the real max or a literal 1, so a legitimate zero-length read never risks malloc(0)'s implementation-defined NULL (which would otherwise fall into the NULL-check's error branch and report a stale or zero errno as a bogus failure), while the actual read/pread/readlink call still passes the caller's real (possibly zero) length.\n    - realpath stays deferred, now for two concrete, reported reasons rather than scope alone: PATH_MAX is not in libc.asl and genuinely differs by triple (1024 on darwin, 4096 on linux), so it cannot be guessed; and the POSIX.1-2008 realpath(path, NULL) overload that would avoid needing it is blocked by the same missing int-to-pointer op nanosleep's rem buffer works around above by allocating a second real buffer instead.\n    - usleep is a thin wrapper some platforms still ship as calling nanosleep internally; it stays in place (not replaced by a direct nanosleep call), since that replacement would still need the same EINTR-retry handling nanosleep's own :d above defers.\n  Round 4 (plan S4) covers the struct-layout syscalls round 3 left out, all read through libc.asl's structOffset/structByteSize (never a hardcoded offset):\n    - stat and lstat (sysStatFn/statFamilyFn) malloc a struct stat, call the real syscall and decode st_size (rawLoadI64), st_mode (rawLoadI32, masked to its low 16 bits -- mode_t is a 16-bit quantity in every stat ABI this module targets, darwin's own 4-byte-aligned st_mode/st_nlink pair included, a POSIX-wide invariant rather than a libc.asl-tracked fact) and st_mtimespec's tv_sec (rawLoadI64 at the embedded timespec's own offset, which is always 0, same invariant), then masks the decoded mode against libc/libcConst's S_IFMT to report the file's kind without a second load.\n    - utimes (sysUtimesFn) writes two struct timeval (atime, mtime) into one malloc'd buffer sized 2*timevalSize, each at its own tv_sec/tv_usec offset (libc.asl's timeval row, new this round) via rawStoreI64 (even tv_usec, 4 bytes wide on darwin's timeval: the next 4 bytes are trailing alignment padding on darwin and the real high half of an 8-byte tv_usec on linux, so an 8-byte store is correct on both and simplest).\n    - localtime_r (sysLocaltimeFn) writes a caller-supplied epoch seconds into a malloc'd time_t buffer (8 bytes -- time_t is 64-bit on every 64-bit triple this module targets, the same class of invariant as mode_t's width above) and a second malloc'd struct tm, calls localtime_r and decodes all nine tm fields (rawLoadI32, widened) from libc.asl's tm row; checked by NULL return (rawPtrIsNull), not the 0/-1 convention, since localtime_r returns struct tm* or NULL.\n    - getrusage (sysGetrusageFn) malloc's one struct rusage, calls getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF, ...) (libc/libcConst) and decodes ru_maxrss (rawLoadI64, divided by libc/rusageMaxRssUnit -- bytes on darwin, kilobytes on linux, a documented unit rather than a libc constant) and ru_utime/ru_stime as microseconds (each ru_u/stime offset plus the timeval row's own tv_sec/tv_usec offset, sec*1e6+usec via the checked mulInt/addInt family, which operate on raw i64 exactly as decodeLittleEndianBytes already relies on).\n    - uname (sysUnameFn) malloc's one struct utsname, calls uname and decodes sysname and machine (libc.asl's utsname row) as NUL-terminated strings via cstrFieldBlocks.\n    - opendir/readdir/closedir (sysDirListFn) are one function, dirList's own shape (a Result (List String) Int64), never three separate ones: no raw primitive converts an i64 back to a ptr (nanosleep's :d above), so a DIR* or dirent* obtained by one sys* call could never be handed back into a Val and passed into a second one across an opCall boundary; keeping all three native calls inside one function's own blocks needs no such conversion, since the ptr values stay native the whole time. Loops with a real back edge (dominance, not block order, decides SSA validity here, exactly as a real CFG loop does in LLVM) scanning entries via readdir, skipping \".\" and \"..\" by comparing their first bytes directly (rawLoadI8 on the dirent pointer, not a decoded String: this module's own functions cannot hold a String constant, having no module string pool of their own), decoding every other d_name via cstrFieldBlocks and cons'ing it onto the result list; readdir's own NULL is end-of-directory only when errno is 0 (set to 0, via the errno accessor's own pointer, immediately before each readdir call, as POSIX directs, since readdir has no other way to report this host's accessor can write, not just read, errno) and a real error otherwise. Sorting (dirList's own bytewise qsort) is left to the caller: a test wanting dirList-equal output sorts both sides itself.\n    - cstrFieldBlocks decodes a NUL-terminated field embedded in a fixed-size struct without ever forming a sub-pointer (no raw primitive does: rawLoadI8/rawStoreI8 take a base ptr and an i64 byte offset, computing the GEP internally, so the base pointer this module already holds -- a struct buffer or a dirent entry -- is enough): a loop scans forward from the field's own offset copying non-NUL bytes into a fresh buffer until a NUL or maxScan bytes (safely the whole remaining struct, since the real field is always NUL-terminated well before the struct ends), then calls mkStr(buf, len) -- a real Val String (T_STR), not mkBytes' Val Bytes (T_BYTES), since the decoded field feeds stringConcat (sysUnameFn's sysname/machine, this test's printed line) which rejects Bytes with ERR_TYPE; not asl_rt_str either, which emitLlvmProgram only ever reaches through opConst(constStr) and which checkCall therefore rejects as an opCall target -- and frees the scratch buffer.\n  Round 4 (plan LIBC-pathMaxIntToPtr, over sh/S6's new rawIntToPtr prim) closes realpath: sysRealpath calls realpath(path, NULL) via rawIntToPtr(0), copying the malloc'd resolved-path buffer into a Val String (strlen then the new mkStrExtern) and freeing it; PATH_MAX is now in libc.asl (darwin 1024, linux 4096), probe-verified, even though the NULL overload never needs it directly, so a future fixed-buffer caller never guesses it. sysNanosleep's rem argument, malloc'd above only because rawIntToPtr did not exist yet, is now also a genuine NULL (rawIntToPtr 0): no second buffer, nothing to free on that path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysNet.asl#" :text "Native-only syscall IR builders for sockets (plan RT unit S5), the direct-libc-extern twin of asl/host/src/sysNet.c's VM builtins: tcpListen, tcpConnect, sockAccept, sockLocalPort, unixListen, unixConnect, plus SCM_RIGHTS descriptor passing (unit FDHANDOFF: socketpair, sendmsg and recvmsg with libc.asl's msghdr, cmsghdr, iovec and CMSG_* facts), which asl/host/src/sysNet.c has no builtin for yet. Each is an SsaFunction (named sysNetTcpListen, sysNetTcpConnect, sysNetSockAccept, sysNetSockLocalPort, sysNetUnixListen, sysNetUnixConnect, sysNetSocketPair, sysNetSendFd, sysNetRecvFd) that calls socket/bind/listen/connect/accept/accept4/getsockname as direct externs, built against the real C ABI (no new C). A caller includes sysNetExterns and sysNetFunctions (which already carries sys/sysErrnoValueFn, so no separate import of asl-target-llvm/sys's own functions is required) in its own SsaModule.\n  Error shape: every function here returns Val (Result Int64 Int64) -- a raw boxed errno, matching asl-target-llvm/sys's own convention (its functions' Result shapes already don't match the high-level ASL builtins they underlie either), not the VM's Result _ String \"io:N\" formatting, since this module has no string pool of its own to build a literal \"io:\" prefix with (the same limitation sys.asl's own :d notes for sysDirListFn).\n  Byte order: there is no htons primitive, so a runtime port value is written network-order (big-endian) via two rawStoreI8 byte stores (the high byte at the field's own offset, the low byte at offset+1) and read back the same way. 127.0.0.1 (INADDR_LOOPBACK) is a fixed value, not a runtime one, so it is written whole via one rawStoreI32 of the build-time constant 16777343 (0x0100007F) -- the byte-reversal of 0x7F000001 that a plain little-endian store needs to land network-order bytes [127,0,0,1] in memory, sound on every triple this module targets (arm64 and x86_64 are both little-endian).\n  There is no pointer-arithmetic primitive (no base+offset->ptr op, the same gap sys.asl's cstrFieldBlocks works around) and no memset/memcpy extern is declared, so a sockaddr's non-field bytes are zeroed by zeroBytesInstrs (n individual rawStoreI8(ptr,i,0) instructions, unrolled at build time since n is always a small compile-time struct size) and a String's bytes are copied into sun_path by a real loop (rawLoadI8 from the source ptr, rawStoreI8 into sa at sunPathOff+idx, a back edge valid by dominance exactly as cstrFieldBlocks' own scan loop is).\n  Platform branch: sockAcceptFn is the only function whose IR differs by triple, per the task's own instruction -- accept4(..., SOCK_CLOEXEC) on linux-x86_64/linux-aarch64, accept(...) followed by the portable fcntl(F_GETFD)/fcntl(F_SETFD|FD_CLOEXEC) dance on darwin-arm64. Every other function's socket() call uses that same fcntl dance uniformly on all three triples (socketCloexecBlocks), since the task's accept4-vs-accept+fcntl instruction is specifically about accepting a connection, not about creating one.\n  setsockopt(SOL_SOCKET, SO_REUSEADDR) is deliberately never called: asl/host/src/sysNet.c's bTcpListen doesn't call it either, and matching that exactly keeps this module's native output byte-for-byte behaviorally identical to the VM's for the echo gate. SOL_SOCKET and SO_REUSEADDR still go into libc.asl per the task's own instruction, for a future caller that wants them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#" :text "Native-only process spawn/wait IR builders (plan RT unit S6, round 3: no C floor shim -- every op below is\n  built from sys.asl's own externs/functions, this module's own new pipe/waitpid/posix_spawn* externs, and raw IR\n  prims, including rawIntToPtr (this round's own new prim: asl-ir/types.asl's primSignature and\n  asl-target-llvm/ssa.asl's emitPrim, one inttoptr mirroring rawPtrToInt's ptrtoint). Round 2's spawnShim.c is\n  gone: every control-flow gap it existed to cover (building argv/envp arrays, a NULL attrp, a timed wait) is\n  buildable directly in IR once a real pointer can be synthesized from a raw int.\n  argv/envp: procSpawn takes them as ordinary ASL (List String) values, not a NUL-separated blob. ptrArrayBlocks\n  walks one with a block-param loop (idx, remaining-list), mallocs 8*(n+1) bytes once up front, stores each\n  entry's own valToCStr(s,0) pointer (rawPtrToInt into an i64 slot, since there is no raw op to store a ptr\n  directly) at idx*8, and a trailing 0 terminator at n*8; freePtrArrayBlocks walks the same range back out\n  (rawLoadI64 then rawIntToPtr to recover each element's pointer) before free. inheritEnv's real environment is\n  now genuinely NULL (rawIntToPtr 0), not a never-read blob standing in for a NULL this IR could not build\n  before.\n  spawn: two pipes (pipeExtern, a malloc(8) scratch buffer rawLoadI32'd at offsets 0/4 for the two fds, matching\n  how a C caller reads int pipefd[2], freed immediately after both fds are read out), FD_CLOEXEC set on both read\n  ends via sys.asl's own sysFcntlSet, a posix_spawn_file_actions_t buffer (malloc'd at libc.asl's own struct size\n  for this triple, never hardcoded) dup2/close-configured and posix_spawn'd. posix_spawn_file_actions_init\n  /adddup2/addclose/destroy and posix_spawn itself all return the error number directly on failure (0 on\n  success), the pthread_*-style convention, never -1/errno; only the true syscalls here (pipe, waitpid) use the\n  -1/errno convention sys.asl's own sysErrnoValue reads. Every error path converges on freeCommon, which frees\n  path/argv/envp once and returns (err codeBox); every success path converges on the symmetric finishOk after the\n  same argv/envp frees.\n  wait: procWait and procWaitAny poll waitpid(pid, &status, WNOHANG) in a loop against a CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline\n  (sysClockGettime; libc.asl's own WNOHANG/CLOCK_MONOTONIC facts, never hardcoded), sleeping sysNanosleep(0, 10ms)\n  between polls; a negative timeoutMs is an effectively-infinite deadline (INT64_MAX nanoseconds), never a\n  separate code path. procWaitAny sweeps its own two pids with WNOHANG each iteration and never calls\n  waitpid(-1, ...), which could reap a pid outside its own pair that the caller still owns.\n  procKill/procSelf/procAlive are thin wrappers around sys.asl's own sysKill/sysGetpid (no syscall of their own);\n  procAlive is sysKill(pid, 0) with ESRCH (libc.asl's own fact, never hardcoded) mapped to false, any other error\n  propagated, and success mapped to true.\n  Plan unit SYSLOWER-b: procRouteFunctions builds the asl-target-llvm/sysRoute wrappers of sys.c's procSpawnv,\n  procWaitPid, procWaitAny, procPoll, procRusage and procExecv (fork + execvp as sys.c, its argument checks, err texts,\n  exitCodeOf and record shapes), with helpers named procStrv, procEnvArg, procWaitFwd, procWaitSet and the like; the\n  blocking waits forward SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP to the child's process group (kqueue on darwin, signalfd and\n  pidfd_open on linux) and re-raise the signal once the child is reaped. Every libc fact they read comes from\n  procFacts, a missing one being a build-time err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#stringToPtrInstrs" :text "valToCStr(v, 0): a fresh, caller-owned copy of v's raw bytes (own copy of sys.asl's helper of the same name:\n  sys.asl exports only its smaller IR-instruction primitives -- int64Const, callInstr, ... -- reused below via the\n  sys/ import, not this larger helper, which it keeps private).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#errnoErrBlock" :text "A block reading the real errno (a true -1/errno syscall or a NULL malloc just failed) FIRST, before\n  preFrees runs its own stage-specific cleanup -- free() and kin are themselves libc calls free to clobber errno,\n  exactly as errnoResultFn's own :d in sys.asl explains, so the read must happen before any of them run, never\n  after -- then boxes the captured value and jumps to nextLabel (typically freeCommon) with that box as its one\n  argument.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#errnoFinBlock" :text "A terminal block taking one boxed errno (positionally, from whichever errnoErrBlock jumped here) and\n  returning it as (err box) directly -- used where the errno never needs this module's own argv/envp cleanup\n  (envp's own array malloc failing before anything else exists to free; a mid-poll waitpid error with its own\n  stage-specific cleanup already run by the caller).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#ptrArrayBlocks" :text "Blocks binding prefix.ptr (tyPtr, a malloc'd NUL-terminated array of listVar's own String elements' own\n  valToCStr(s,0) pointers, each stored as a rawPtrToInt'd i64 slot since there is no raw op to store a ptr\n  directly) and prefix.n (tyI64, listVar's own length, counted by the prefix.count loop since listLength is a prelude\n  function with no runtime entry) for every block downstream (prefix.alloc, which binds both, dominates them all); okLabel's own jump carries no arguments, since both names are already in\n  scope there by dominance, the same cross-block convention sys.asl's own straight-line functions (sysReadFn's\n  own buf, used unchanged across its call/err/ok blocks) rely on throughout. The only failure point is the array\n  malloc itself (errLabel, also with no arguments); valToCStr's own per-element copy is never NULL-checked,\n  matching every other stringToPtrInstrs call site in sys.asl, which checks none of them either.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#freePtrArrayBlocks" :text "Blocks freeing each of ptrName's own nName element pointers (rawLoadI64 then rawIntToPtr to recover each\n  one) and then ptrName itself, before an unconditional jump to nextLabel with no arguments. prefix names this\n  chain's own labels and temporaries only; ptrName/nName are passed in explicitly (rather than derived from\n  prefix, as ptrArrayBlocks' own prefix.ptr/.n are) so the same underlying array can be freed from more than one\n  differently-labelled call site (procSpawnFn's own error-path and success-path frees of the same argv/envp\n  arrays, under distinct label prefixes to avoid colliding on the same block names).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#close4FdsInstrs" :text "sysClose on all four pipe fds, fire-and-forget (its own Result is never checked, matching how every other\n  cleanup call in this module -- free, posix_spawn_file_actions_destroy -- is also unchecked: there is no\n  meaningful error to propagate from a close during an unrelated failure's own cleanup).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#posixSpawnExtern" :text "C's int posix_spawn(pid_t *pid, const char *path, const posix_spawn_file_actions_t *file_actions, const\n  posix_spawnattr_t *attrp, char *const argv[], char *const envp[]): file_actions and attrp are both real\n  pointers, attrp always NULL (rawIntToPtr 0 -- default spawn attributes, never built as a real\n  posix_spawnattr_t); its own return is the error number directly, never -1/errno (see this module's own :d).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#pidGuardBlocks" :text "First block of the function (plan RT unit S6 round 4: pid guard), placed at position 0 so it becomes the\n  function's own entry (an edge may never target the entry block, the IR's own ERR_IR_ENTRY_TARGET rule, which is\n  why goodLabel -- the function's previous first block, now moved to position 1 -- is an ordinary jump target):\n  computes condInstrs, branches on condName to goodLabel when every pid checked is within 1..INT32_MAX, otherwise\n  to badPid, which returns (err EINVAL) immediately with no syscall made at all. pid 0 and -1 are meaningful,\n  dangerous values to waitpid/kill (0 is the caller's own process group, -1 is every process the caller may\n  signal), while values above INT32_MAX cannot be represented as pid_t and would trap during narrowing; reject\n  both classes before the real syscall interprets them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#nsGetEnvironExtern" :text "C's char*** _NSGetEnviron(void) (darwin only, <crt_externs.h>): the supported way to read the process's\n  real, inherited environ from a dynamically loaded darwin binary, since plain `environ` is not guaranteed\n  exported the way glibc's own environ symbol is on linux (opLoadGlobal \"environ\", used there instead; plan RT\n  unit S6 round 4). Its own return is a pointer to where the real char** environ lives, dereferenced once more\n  (rawLoadI64 then rawIntToPtr) to recover that char** itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#realEnvironBlocks" :text "The 'envSelect.inherit' block (plan RT unit S6 round 4): binds envSelect.inherit.real (tyPtr, the process's\n  own, genuinely inherited environ) and jumps to envSelect.join with it. darwin: _NSGetEnviron() returns a\n  char***, one more rawLoadI64+rawIntToPtr indirection than linux's own opLoadGlobal \"environ\", which reads the\n  char** directly. No C accessor either way -- team-lead's own round-4 :mustFix line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procSpawnEntryBlocks" :text "env.ptr/env.n (plan RT unit S6 round 4) are now ALWAYS built from the caller's own envp list, regardless of\n  inheritEnv -- always a malloc'd array, safe to free unconditionally on every path, exactly as procSpawnOkTailBlocks\n  and freeCommon already do. spawnEnvp, bound after envReady by a runtime branch on inheritFlag (envSelect.own vs\n  envSelect.inherit/realEnvironBlocks), is the SEPARATE value posix_spawn actually receives: the caller's own\n  envp.ptr when not inheriting, or the real process environ when inheriting. Decoupling what gets freed from what\n  gets spawned-with is the whole fix: inheriting the real environ must never free it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procSpawnFn" :text "procSpawn(path, argv, envp, inheritEnv) -> Result (List pid outFd errFd) Int64: path is a String, argv and\n  envp ordinary ASL (List String) values; inheritEnv is a raw i32, nonzero to spawn with the real environment (a\n  genuine NULL envp -- envp is then never read). Two CLOEXEC pipes feed the child's stdout/stderr through a\n  posix_spawn_file_actions_t buffer; the ok payload is a ProcSpawnResult record (pid, outFd, errFd, the open\n  read-end fds the caller owns and eventually sysClose's).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procWaitDeadlineBlocks" :text "Blocks binding deadline (tyI64, a CLOCK_MONOTONIC nanosecond count), then jumping to nextLabel(deadline): a\n  negative timeoutMs (forever) joins on INT64_MAX; otherwise sysClockGettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC) now plus\n  timeoutMs*1e6 nanoseconds. clockConst must already be bound by the caller (procWaitFn/procWaitAnyFn's own\n  entry). deadline.unpack clamps timeoutMs against deadline.maxTimeoutMs -- (INT64_MAX - now) / 1e6, the largest\n  ms value the mulInt/addInt chain below can take without the checked-overflow trap this round fixed -- treating\n  anything above it the same as deadline.inf's own already-infinite path, rather than letting a caller-controlled\n  timeoutMs crash the whole process. preFrees (plan RT unit S6 round 4) runs in deadline.clockErr before\n  returning, so the caller's own statusBuf is freed on this rare error path too, not just on every other one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#nowNanosBlocks" :text "Blocks binding label.nowNanos (tyI64, a fresh CLOCK_MONOTONIC reading) and jumping to okLabel with no\n  arguments (dominance, as ptrArrayBlocks' own :d explains); on sysClockGettime's own rare error, runs preFrees\n  (plan RT unit S6 round 4: the caller's own statusBuf free) then returns its already-boxed err payload directly\n  instead.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procWaitFn" :text "procWait(pid, timeoutMs) -> Result (List status timedOut) Int64: polls waitpid(pid, &status, WNOHANG) in a\n  loop against a CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline (procWaitDeadlineBlocks/nowNanosBlocks), sleeping sysNanosleep(0, 10ms)\n  between polls; a negative timeoutMs never times out (INT64_MAX deadline). On a real exit, status is the raw\n  waitpid status and timedOut 0; on a timeout, status is 0 (meaningless, the caller must check timedOut first)\n  and timedOut 1; the child is left running and unreaped on a timeout.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procWaitAnyFn" :text "procWaitAny(pid1, pid2, timeoutMs) -> Result (List index pid status timedOut) Int64: each loop iteration\n  sweeps pid1 (index 0) then, only if pid1 was not ready and waitpid did not error, pid2 (index 1) with its own\n  WNOHANG poll -- never waitpid(-1, ...), which could reap a pid outside this pair that the caller still owns\n  (round 2's own ECHILD-stealing bug, carried forward here as the reason this module never takes that shortcut).\n  On a timeout every field but timedOut is 0, not meaningful; the child is left running and unreaped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procKillFn" :text "procKill(pid, sig) -> Result Int64 Int64, a thin wrapper around sys.asl's own sysKill (no new syscall),\n  rejecting pid 0 or -1 with EINVAL before it (plan RT unit S6 round 4).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#procAliveFn" :text "procAlive(pid) -> Result Bool Int64: sysKill(pid, 0) (a signal-0 probe, no signal actually sent); ok maps to\n  true, an err whose boxed errno equals libc.asl's own ESRCH (never hardcoded) maps to false, any other error is\n  propagated as-is. Rejects pid 0 or -1 with EINVAL before the probe (plan RT unit S6 round 4).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#sysProcExterns" :text "_NSGetEnviron (plan RT unit S6 round 4) is declared only for darwin triples -- it does not exist to link\n  against on linux, which reads environ directly via opLoadGlobal instead (no extern of its own needed; the LLVM\n  emitter declares its `@environ = external global ptr` itself, from loadGlobalNames).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/sysProc.asl#sysProcRecords" :text "The record schemas procSpawn/procWait/procWaitAny construct and a caller's opField reads back; see this\n  module's top :d for each one's fields.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#" :text "Native gate for asl-target-llvm/sysProc (plan RT unit S6, round 3: procSpawn/procWait/procKill built from\n  pipe/waitpid/posix_spawn* externs and raw IR prims, no C floor shim): a native program using\n  procSpawn/procWait/procKill spawns /bin/echo and reads its real stdout back through the pipe fd procSpawn\n  returns (sys.asl's own sysRead), checking the exact bytes and a clean exit status after reaping with procWait;\n  a second program spawns /bin/sleep, confirms a 50ms procWait times out while it is still running, then\n  procKill(SIGKILL)s and procWait(-1)s it, checking the reaped status carries SIGKILL; a third spawns a slow\n  sleep and a fast echo and procWaitAny(-1)s them, checking the echo (index 1) is the one that actually finished,\n  then kills and reaps the slow one. argv/envp are now real ASL (List String) values built in IR with opList over\n  individually pooled string constants (round 2's single NUL-separated blob string is gone along with the shim\n  it existed for). Each program reports its own pass/fail as its exit code (0 pass, a distinct code per failing\n  check); asl-host run of a tiny fixture using the interpreted processSpawn/processWait builtins runs alongside\n  as the comparable reference (both spawn echo and see exit 0, stdout \"hi\\n\"). Builds clang and the programs\n  through processRun in a fresh temporary directory, as asl-target-llvm/tests/sysDirectTest does.\n  Unit SYSLOWER-b (testProc, testProcFwd, over sysRouteTest's harness copied under the same names): a native\n  program's procSpawnv, procWaitPid, procWaitAny, procPoll, procRusage and procExecv run asl-target-llvm/sysProc's\n  routed wrappers (no asl_rt_builtin_sys call, each wrapper defined internal), and its stdout and exit equal\n  asl-host run's and sys.c's computed results on every case procSource lists; a SIGTERM sent to the native parent\n  blocked in procWaitPid reaches the child's process group and then kills the parent with asl-host run's status.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#procFns" :text "sysProc.asl's own functions for this triple, or an assertion failure plus an empty list on a missing\n  libc.asl fact (FD_CLOEXEC/F_SETFD/WNOHANG/CLOCK_MONOTONIC/ESRCH/posix_spawn_file_actions_t; not expected on a\n  host libc.asl covers).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#moduleOf" :text "A module over this triple's resultTypeDecl/optionTypeDecl, sysProc's own record decls, every extern sys.asl\n  and sysProc.asl declare for it (sys.asl's own malloc/free/valToCStr, never duplicated by sysProc's copies), and\n  sys.asl's plus sysProc's own functions plus extraFns (the test's own run function).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#strListConstInstrs" :text "An ASL (List String) built with opList over indices.length freshly pooled string constants (each named\n  prefix.N), for procSpawn's own argv/envp parameters: round 3 takes them as real ASL lists, not round 2's single\n  NUL-separated blob string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#spawnEchoRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns /bin/echo hi, reads its stdout pipe (sysRead), checks the exact 3 bytes, reaps it\n  (procWait forever) and checks a clean exit (raw status 0). 0 on every check passing; 1 spawn err, 2 read err,\n  7 wait err, 9 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#spawnTimeoutKillRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns /bin/sleep 2, procWait(50ms) while it is still running (expect timedOut 1), then\n  procKill(SIGKILL) and procWait(-1) to reap, checking the raw status carries SIGKILL (9) with no timeout. 0 pass;\n  1 spawn err, 7/8/9 wait/kill/second-wait err, 10 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#waitAnyRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns a slow /bin/sleep 2 (pid1) and a fast /bin/echo hi (pid2), procWaitAny(-1)s both,\n  checking the echo (index 1, pid2, status 0, no timeout) is the one that actually finished first, then kills and\n  reaps the slow one. 0 pass; 1/2 spawn err, 3 waitAny err, 11 a value mismatch (the slow sleep isn't reaped by\n  design -- its own exit is irrelevant once killed -- so no sentinel covers the cleanup kill/wait, whose Results\n  this function discards unread, same as spawnEcho/spawnTimeoutKill discard sysClose's).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#procSelfRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: procSelf() widened and stringified, compared byte-for-byte against the real $PPID a spawned\n  /bin/sh -c 'echo $PPID' child prints to stdout -- its parent is this very process, so this is an external,\n  independently-computed check of procSelf's own return value, not a hardcoded constant. 0 pass; 1 spawn err,\n  2 read err, 7 wait err, 9 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#procAliveRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns /bin/sleep 2, confirms procAlive(pid) is true while it is still running, then\n  procKill(SIGKILL)s and procWait(-1)s to reap it, confirms procAlive(pid) is false (ESRCH) once reaped -- a real\n  before/after lifecycle check, not a hardcoded boolean. 0 pass; 1 spawn err, 2/5 alive err, 3 kill err, 4 wait\n  err, 13 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#spawnEnoentRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: procSpawn of a path that cannot exist fails, and this checks its boxed err payload is\n  exactly ENOENT (2), the real errno posix_spawn reports for a missing executable, not a guess about which\n  branch runs. 0 pass; 2 spawn unexpectedly ok; 9 wrong errno.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#inheritEnvRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns /bin/sh -c 'echo $FOO' with inheritEnv 0 and an explicit envpBlob of just FOO=bar,\n  checking the child's real stdout is exactly 'bar\\n' -- proof envpBlob, not this process's own environment,\n  reached the child. 0 pass; 1 spawn err, 2 read err, 7 wait err, 9 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#inheritEnvRealRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: spawns /bin/sh -c 'echo $FOO' with inheritEnv 1 and an EMPTY envp list, checking the\n  child's real stdout is exactly 'bar\\n' -- proof that when this very native binary is itself run under FOO=bar\n  (testInheritEnvReal wraps the binary's own invocation in `env FOO=bar`, not procSpawn's own envp), the real,\n  inherited environ (opLoadGlobal \"environ\" on linux, _NSGetEnviron() on darwin; plan RT unit S6 round 4), not\n  envp's own caller-built empty array, is what reaches the child via posix_spawn's spawnEnvp. 0 pass; 1 spawn\n  err, 2 read err, 7 wait err, 9 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#waitAnyNoStealRunFn" :text "run() -> Int64: the S6 round-2 grader repro. Spawns a fast /bin/echo (A) and two slow /bin/sleep 2's (B, C),\n  procWaitAny(B, C, 50ms)s -- expecting a timeout, since B and C are still sleeping -- then procWait(A, forever).\n  Before this round's fix, aslWaitAnyProc's timeout and post-poll paths called waitpid(-1, ...), which could reap\n  A (already exited, outside the {B, C} batch) out from under this very procWait(A, ...) call, turning it into an\n  ECHILD error; this checks that no longer happens, then kills and reaps B and C. 0 pass; 1/2/3 spawn err, 4\n  waitAny err, 5 waitA err, 12 a value mismatch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/sysProcTest.asl#testHostComparison" :text "The comparable asl-host reference (plan S6 gate): the interpreted processSpawn/processWait builtins run the\n  same /bin/echo hi this unit's native spawnEcho program runs. Compared against a real, independently-run\n  reference (this test's own sh helper spawning the same command at test time), not a hardcoded exit/stdout\n  constant guessed at ahead of time -- a change to what /bin/echo hi actually prints or exits with would move\n  both sides together and still pass, which a literal \"hi\\n\"/0 could not catch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#" :text "The collector of native programs written in ASL (plan unit GCASL-1): SSA builders, the arrays.asl and parallel.asl pattern, for asl/host/src/gc.c's precise mark-sweep collector, so a native program linking asl-target-llvm/gcRoute's collector module links no gc.o. Object layouts are value.h's (Obj header: size u32 at 0, type at 4, mark at 5, perm at 6, classIdx at 7; Cons car at 8 and cdr at 24; Rec n at 12 and values at 24; Ctor n at 12 and fields at 16; Closure n at 16 and captures at 24; Arr data and Handle fin at 24, Handle p at 16; Proto consts at 40 and nconsts at 48; a Val is 16 bytes, tag in the low half of its first word, payload in its second), and the collector is gc.c's: 63 size classes of (c+2)*8 bytes up to 512, 16 KiB pages with a 512-byte header (here: next 0, nextFree 8, classIdx 16, slotSize 24, slotCount 32, allocCount 40, markedCount 48, bumpOffset 56, freeList 64, the inUse bitmap at 72), bump allocation then per-page free lists rebuilt by the sweep from every slot below bumpOffset, empty pages cached up to the pages of the next threshold (plan unit GCASL-2: gc.c caches 32 and frees the rest to malloc), live pages in an open-addressed set hashed by (base>>14)*0x9E3779B97F4A7C15>>20, objects over 512 bytes and every Arr and Handle as LargeObj (next 0, bytes 8, span 16, the object at 24) in a list and an address index sorted on demand for gcFindObj, permanent objects calloc'd with perm set; marking through an explicit stack from gcMutatorRoots, gcExternalRoots, the gcStackBase..*gcStackTop Vals, the pushed roots (at most 4096) and every registered Proto's constants; growth threshold max(gcMinBytes, live*gcGrowth) capped at 2^46 and by ASL_GC_MAX_MIB; ASL_GC_STRESS, ASL_GC_STATS (the same atexit line), ASL_GC_GROWTH, ASL_GC_MIN_MIB, ASL_GC_MAX_MIB and ASL_GC_VERIFY (gc.c's cycle check, its (:gcCycle ...) line and ERR_HEAP_CYCLE and ERR_LIMIT) read once by gcInit with gc.c's ERR_ENV texts and exit 2; every fatal error leaves through strFloor.c's gcFloorFail with gc.c's code and text, a failing realloc of the mark, verify or proto stack through exit 70 as there. Page memory comes from mmap in runs of 64 pages, 16 KiB aligned (an unaligned run is remapped with one page of slack and trimmed); the pages past the cache are munmapped after the sweep, sorted, one call per run of adjacent pages. ASL_GC_STATS adds a (:gcPhases ...) line of mark, sweep and release times and page counts. All state lives in one static block (stateBlockText) whose words the functions address by slot. A Val's words, f64 bits, function-pointer calls (finalizers, root hooks, the guard of asl-host's gcFloorGuard), setjmp, qsort and llvm.cttz go through helpers asl-target-llvm/gcRoute defines in the emitted text (helperDefinitions), since asl-ir has no operation for them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#pn" :text "The module function name of a collector function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#functionName" :text "The SSA function name of the collector function name (alloc, allocCons, markRoot, markPhase, sweepPhase, ...), which gcRoute's C entry points call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#wasmDefaultMinMib" :text "wasm32 has no environment (ASL_GC_MIN_MIB can never be read), so its floor stays the pre-GC-POLICY 8 MiB measured for wasm's small linear memory rather than the native-only 32 MiB adopted in perfBaseline.asn.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#runPages" :text "Pages one mmap reserves for page checkout.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#frameBytes" :text "A verify DFS frame: the object at 0, the next child index at 8, the child count at 16.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sTimespec" :text "Four words of scratch for clock_gettime's struct timespec.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sEndPtr" :text "strtod's and strtoull's end pointer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sReleaseBuf" :text "releaseCache's scratch array of the page addresses it unmaps.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sMarkNs" :text "The phase times and page counts of the (:gcPhases ...) line, sMarkNs to sUnmapCalls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#stateWords" :text "Words in the state block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#stateBlockText" :text "The LLVM definition of the state block for a target: threshold and gcMinBytes set to defaultMinMibFor that target (native 32 MiB, wasm32 8 MiB since wasm32 can never override via ASL_GC_MIN_MIB), gcGrowth 2.0 as its bit pattern, the large index sorted, heapLo UINTPTR_MAX, every other word zero.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcFactNames" :text "The libc facts the collector reads.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcFacts" :text "gcFactNames resolved for the triple, or an err naming the first one libc.asl lacks; also an err when struct timespec does not fit the four scratch words or the triple names no errno accessor.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcFactsFor" :text "gcFactNames resolved for the triple, or an err naming the first one libc.asl lacks; also an err when struct timespec does not fit the four scratch words or the triple names no errno accessor. A wasm32 target needs no libc fact: its collector reads no environment and takes its clock, exit and free from asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime and wasmAlloc, so it resolves to an empty fact map.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#freeName" :text "The collector's free: libc free (read as an unused i64), or on wasm32 wasmAlloc's asl_wasm_free, whose i64 result keeps the C-ABI void free the program module declares a distinct wasm signature.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#exitName" :text "The collector's exit: libc exit (read as an unused i64), or on wasm32 wasmRuntime's asl_wasm_exit, an i64-returning exit beside the program's void exit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#clockName" :text "wasmRuntime's monotonic nanosecond clock over the runtimeAbi clock import, which the wasm32 collector calls in place of clock_gettime.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcStrings" :text "The module's string pool, NUL-terminated C strings the collector passes as ptr: error codes and gc.c's texts, the environment variable names and the object type names of the cycle report.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#k" :text "d (i64): the literal n.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#cs" :text "d (ptr): the pool string text as a C string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ex" :text "d: a call of the extern callee.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#cl" :text "d (i64): a call of the collector function name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#quot" :text "d: a / b for a non-negative a and a positive b.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#shr" :text "d: a shifted right logically by b.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#byteAtK" :text "d: the byte of the header word h at bit shift.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#flip" :text "d: a with its sign bit flipped, so a signed compare of flipped words orders them unsigned.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ult" :text "d: a < b as unsigned words, gc.c's size_t and uintptr_t compares.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ld" :text "d (i64): the 8 bytes at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ldS32" :text "d (i64): the C int at addr plus off, sign-extended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ldU32" :text "d (i64): the uint32_t at addr plus off (a Val's tag, an Obj's size).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#ld8" :text "d (i64): the byte at addr plus off, zero-extended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#st" :text "Stores the i64 v at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#st8K" :text "Stores the byte n at addr plus off.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#state" :text "s (i64): the state block's address.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sld" :text "d: the state word slot.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sinc" :text "Adds by to the state word slot.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#classAddr" :text "d: the address of size class sc's three words (pages, freePages, activePage).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#elem" :text "d: base plus i * size.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#hasObj" :text "d: gc.c hasObj, the tag one of String, List, Record, Variant, Fn, Bytes, the three arrays or Handle and the object non-null.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#blkp" :text "A block binding i64 parameters.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#retZero" :text "label runs parts, then returns 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#fun" :text "A collector function of i64 parameters returning i64.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#failB" :text "label fails through gcFloorFail with code and a message: fmt itself when argNames is empty, else fmt over argNames (which args define) formatted by snprintf into the 1024-byte gcAsl.failBuf first, since rtFloor gcFloorFail prints its message verbatim; gcFloorFail does not return.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#exitB" :text "label exits the process with code, as gc.c does when a realloc of one of its stacks fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#helperExterns" :text "The helpers gcRoute defines in the emitted text in place of their declarations (helperDefinitions).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#helperExternsFor" :text "helperExterns, less gcAslAtexitStats on wasm32, whose collector registers no exit-time statistics, and with gcAslShadowTop there, the head of the program's shadow-root frames.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcExterns" :text "The externs the collector functions call: its helpers, libc (void functions read as an unused i64) and strFloor.c's gcFloorFail. On wasm32 the same C-ABI services come from IR (asl-target-llvm/wasmAlloc, wasmRuntime and wasmFormat): calloc, realloc, asl_wasm_free, memset, memcpy, strlen, dprintf, asl_wasm_exit, the asl_wasm_now_ns clock and gcFloorFail, with linear memory grown by its intrinsic; there is no getenv, strtod, strtoull, errno or clock_gettime.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#helperDefinitions" :text "Each helper declaration the emitter writes for helperExterns, with the definition that replaces it: gcAslState is the state block's address; gcAslCollect calls asl_gc_collect; gcAslMutatorRoots and gcAslExternalRoots call gcMutatorRoots and gcExternalRoots (when set) with gcAslMarkRootC; gcAslStackBase and gcAslStackTop read gcStackBase and gcStackTop; gcAslCallFin calls a Handle's finalizer, gcAslFinGuarded calls it under the guard's handler (1 when it raised, its message left in the guard's buffer) and gcAslRethrow calls the guard's rethrow; gcAslSortLarge qsorts the large index by address; gcAslCtz is llvm.cttz; gcAslAtexitStats registers gcAslPrintStatsC; gcAslF64Bits and gcAslBitsF64 bitcast, gcAslF64ToU64 is fptoui, C's (size_t) of a double.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#helperDefinitionsFor" :text "helperDefinitions for target. On wasm32 gcAslState has external linkage so the end-to-end probe can export it and verify actual collections; gcAslShadowTop reads @asl_gc_shadow_top (gcRoute), the head of the program's shadow-root frames; gcAslAtexitStats goes (no exit-time statistics) and gcAslFinGuarded calls the finalizer without setjmp: asl_gc_collect passes no guard there (gcRoute), so the guarded call is never taken and wasm32 has no setjmp to arm it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#registerProtoFn" :text "gcRegisterProto(p): the proto array doubles from 64 by realloc, exit 70 when it fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#growMarkFn" :text "The full mark stack of cap entries doubles from 1024 by realloc (exit 70 when it fails); returns the new stack.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#markValFn" :text "gc.c markVal: markObj of a Val's object when hasObj holds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#typeChain" :text "Blocks prefix0, prefix1, ...: block i jumps to case i's label when ty equals its number, else on to block i+1, the last to dflt.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#objCases" :text "The value.h object types with children, O_CONS 1, O_REC 2, O_CTOR 3 and O_CLOSURE 4.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#drainFn" :text "gc.c drain: pops the mark stack until empty, marking a cons cell's car and cdr, a record's values, a variant's fields and a closure's captures as markVal does; the stack pointer, stack and capacity stay in block parameters (the state block is written back on growth and at the end), since every store through an object address may alias the state block. drain: an empty mark stack (most stack words) returns after one load; the loop carries the stack, its capacity and the marked byte count in registers and stores them back on exit or growth; a child whose type has no fields is marked but never pushed, and a page's mark count is taken from its bitmap at sweep, so a marked object costs its header, its epoch byte and one bitmap word")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#markRootFn" :text "gc.c markRoot over a Val's two words: markVal, then drain.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#markValAt" :text "markVal of the Val at address a, then drain.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#shadowFrameBlocks" :text "Marks every Val slot of the program's shadow-root frames (asl-target-llvm/ssa emitLlvmProgramWasm32), then goes on to next: from the head gcAslShadowTop gives, each frame's word 0 is the caller's frame (0 ends the chain), word 1 its slot count n, and its n Vals follow from offset 16.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#markPhaseFn" :text "The mark phase of asl_gc_collect: collecting set, then gcMutatorRoots, gcExternalRoots, native stack Vals when the target's page source is not linear memory, on wasm32 every slot of every shadow-root frame (shadowFrameBlocks), each pushed root and each registered Proto's constants, every root drained at once, and collecting cleared.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#poolScanFn" :text "gc.c forEachPooled over every in-use pooled object, class by class, page by page, slot by ascending index: mode 1 zeroes each page's markedCount and clears each object's mark (clearMarks), mode 0 runs the verify DFS from it (gcVerifyHeap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#clearMarksFn" :text "gc.c clearMarks: every large object's mark, then every pooled one's and every page's markedCount, back to zero.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#abortMarkFn" :text "What asl_gc_collect undoes when a root hook raises under asl-host's guard: collecting, the mark stack and every mark.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#childAddrFn" :text "The address of gc.c getObjChild's Val idx of o, an object with children.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#typeNameFn" :text "gc.c gcObjTypeName as the address of its C string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#verifyDfsFn" :text "gc.c runVerifyDfs: an iterative DFS from an unmarked object, grey on the stack and black when done; a grey child is a cycle, printed as (:gcCycle :type T :depth D) and raised as ERR_HEAP_CYCLE; past 1048576 frames ERR_LIMIT; a failing realloc of the frame stack prints ERR_OOM and exits 70.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#verifyHeapFn" :text "gc.c gcVerifyHeap: the DFS from every large object, then from every pooled one, then clearMarks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#pageSetReserveFn" :text "gc.c pageSetReserve: room for one more page at load at most 1/2, the set doubled from 256 and rehashed before a page is acquired; a failing calloc, or one gcTestFailNextPageSetGrow asked for, is ERR_OOM.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#pageSetDelFn" :text "gc.c pageSetDel: linear-probe delete by backward shift; an empty set or a page missing from it is ERR_INTERNAL.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#unmapFn" :text "munmap(addr, len); a failure is ERR_INTERNAL, never ignored.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#freshPageFn" :text "A never-used collector page from the target's page source.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#freshGrowPageFn" :text "A never-used 16 KiB page from the current run, growing linear memory 0 by one run of runPages pages when it is spent; the grown memory starts at a 64 KiB boundary, so its pages are aligned; a refused grow (-1) is ERR_OOM 'out of memory allocating GC page'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#freshMmapPageFn" :text "A never-used 16 KiB-aligned page from the current mmap run, mapping a new run of runPages when it is spent; MAP_FAILED is ERR_OOM 'out of memory allocating GC page'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#widenHeapFn" :text "heapLo and heapHi widened to cover lo..hi.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#newPageFn" :text "gc.c newPage: the page set reserved first, a cached page or a fresh one, its header zeroed and set for class sc, entered in the page set and the heap bounds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#freePageFn" :text "gc.c freePage: out of the page set onto the page cache, which releaseCache trims once the sweep has set the next threshold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#releaseCacheFn" :text "Under mmap, keeps at most limit cached pages, the pages the threshold lets the mutator fill before the next collection: the rest leave the cache into the sReleaseBuf scratch array (grown by realloc, a failure ERR_OOM), sorted by address, and are munmapped one run of adjacent pages per call. Linear memory never shrinks, so under memory.grow every cached page stays for newPage to reuse.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#collectFirst" :text "label collects first when ASL_GC_STRESS is set or allocated plus bytes passes threshold, then goes on to next.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#countAlloc" :text "allocated, objectsAllocated and bytesAllocated counted for an allocation of bytes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#allocFn" :text "asl_alloc(type, bytes): a collection first under stress or past the threshold; over 512 bytes, an Arr or a Handle is a large object; else a zeroed slot of its size class with the header written.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#allocRawFn" :text "asl_alloc_raw(type, bytes) (NATIVE-PERF): asl_alloc without clearing a small slot, for emitted code that stores every byte past the header (a Rec's schema, n, keys and values, a Ctor's id, n and fields, a Closure's proto, n and captures) before anything else allocates, so the collector never traces a stale word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#largeClassBits" :text "classIdx 255 in a header word, 255 << 56 as a signed word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#consHeader" :text "A cons cell's header: size 40, type O_CONS, class 3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#allocConsFn" :text "asl_alloc_cons(): a class-3 slot with its header written whole and no clearing, the caller storing car and cdr before it allocates again.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#allocPermFn" :text "asl_alloc_perm(type, bytes): a calloc'd object marked permanent with the large class, counted but never swept; a failing calloc is ERR_OOM.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#allocLargeFn" :text "gc.c allocLarge: a calloc'd LargeObj holding the object, entered in the large list and the address index (marked unsorted when it lands below the last entry), its span the bytes an interior pointer may hit; a failing realloc of the index or calloc is ERR_OOM, as is a size whose LargeObj would wrap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#accountFn" :text "gcAccount(o, bytes): external bytes owned by o count toward pacing; a large object's LargeObj bytes grow (not a permanent object's, which has no LargeObj), its 32-bit size wraps as gc.c's does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#willAllocateFn" :text "gcWillAllocate(bytes): a collection when ASL_GC_STRESS is set or allocated plus bytes passes threshold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#scanConservativeFn" :text "gcScanConservative(lo, hi): every aligned word in [lo, hi) that gcFindObj resolves is marked and drained; outside a collection or with hi below lo it is ERR_INTERNAL.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#beginFn" :text "The start of asl_gc_collect: the start time when ASL_GC_STATS is set (else 0), and collections counted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#stampFn" :text "Under ASL_GC_STATS: the time since since added to the state word slot and the time now returned; else 0, no clock read.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sweepLargeFn" :text "gc.c's large-object sweep, returning the live bytes: the unmarked entries dropped from the index in order, then each unmarked LargeObj unlinked, an Arr's data freed, a Handle's finalizer run (under the guard when there is one, its first raised message kept in fe), the LargeObj freed and counted; a marked one is unmarked and its bytes counted live.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sweepPagesFn" :text "gc.c's page sweep from live bytes, returning the live bytes: each class's free and active pages reset; a page with no mark freed (its allocCount counted freed); else its free list rebuilt from every slot below bumpOffset (the list head and the freed count carried in block parameters and stored once per page), marked slots unmarked and counted live, unmarked in-use ones counted freed and cleared, allocCount set to markedCount and markedCount zeroed, the page put on the free pages when its list is non-empty, else made the active page when there is none and it has bump room.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sweepPhaseFn" :text "The rest of asl_gc_collect after marking: the sweeps, allocated reset and bytesLive set, the threshold min(max(gcMinBytes, live*gcGrowth capped at 2^46), ASL_GC_MAX_MIB room), the page cache cut to the threshold's pages (releaseCache), the verify pass, the collection time and the mark, sweep and release times under ASL_GC_STATS, the first finalizer error re-raised through the guard, and ERR_OOM when live passes ASL_GC_MAX_MIB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#presentFn" :text "1 when the C string at addr is non-null and non-empty.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#errnoZero" :text "errno set to 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#mibOfFn" :text "gc.c's ASL_GC_MIN_MIB and ASL_GC_MAX_MIB parse of the C string at addr: strtoull base 10 with errno cleared, the value when the whole text was read, no errno was set, it does not start with '-' and it lies in [1, 65536]; else 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#envFailB" :text "label prints gc.c's ERR_ENV line for text to fd 2 and exits 2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#getenvI" :text "d (i64): getenv(name).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#initFn" :text "gcInit: ASL_GC_STRESS, ASL_GC_STATS (registering the atexit statistics line), ASL_GC_GROWTH (strtod, finite and in [0.25, 64]), ASL_GC_MIN_MIB and ASL_GC_MAX_MIB (mibOf), the first threshold min(gcMaxBytes, gcMinBytes) when a cap is set, and ASL_GC_VERIFY; a malformed value prints gc.c's ERR_ENV line and exits 2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#wasmInitFn" :text "gcInit on wasm32, which has no environment: no ASL_GC_* variable can be set, so every setting keeps stateBlockText's gc.c default (8 MiB first threshold and minimum, growth 2, no cap, stress, statistics or verification) and nothing is registered for exit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#printStatsFn" :text "gc.c gcPrintStats: the (:gcStats ...) line on fd 2, then the (:gcPhases ...) line: mark, large sweep, page sweep and cache release times, pages mmapped and munmapped and munmap calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#gcFunctions" :text "Every collector function, c holding the triple's facts; unmap only under the mmap page source, the only one that calls it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#pageSize" :text "geometry and value.h constants, gc.c's own")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#sAllocated" :text "state block words: the scalars, then 3 words per size class (pages, freePages, activePage) from word 64, then the root slots from word 256")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#rootPushFn" :text "roots and protos\nasl_gc_root_push(v): ERR_INTERNAL 'gc root stack overflow' past 4096 roots.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#markObjFn" :text "marking\ngc.c markObj: an unmarked, non-permanent object is marked, its page's markedCount counted, and pushed on the mark stack (grown by growMark when full).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#numChildrenFn" :text "heap verification\ngc.c getNumChildren.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#pageSlotFn" :text "the page set\ngc.c pageSlot: ((base >> 14) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15 >> 20) & (cap - 1).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#wasmPageSize" :text "pages\nThe unit of wasm linear memory and of memory.grow.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#poolAllocFn" :text "allocation\ngc.c poolAlloc: a slot of class sc from the first page with a free list, else bumped from the active page or a new one; its inUse bit set and allocCount counted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#findObjFn" :text "conservative lookup\ngc.c gcFindObj: the live object holding address w, start or interior, through the page set for a pooled slot (its inUse bit set) or a binary search of the address-sorted large index (sorted by qsort on demand) within the found object's span; 0 otherwise, for a permanent object too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#monoNsFn" :text "sweep\nclock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC) in nanoseconds, into the state block's timespec scratch; on wasm32 wasmRuntime's asl_wasm_now_ns.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#isOneFn" :text "environment and statistics\n1 when the C string at addr is non-null and starts with '1', as gc.c reads ASL_GC_STRESS, ASL_GC_STATS and ASL_GC_VERIFY.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#" :text "The collector module of a native program (plan units GCASL-1, GCASL-2): collectorText emits asl-target-llvm/gcAsl's functions for a triple's libc facts as one LLVM module (ssa emitLlvmModule, every collector function internal), its helper declarations replaced by their definitions, then the C ABI gc.c defines, so the program's own text and libaslrt.a's floor objects call it unchanged: asl_alloc, asl_alloc_cons, asl_alloc_perm, asl_gc_collect, asl_gc_root_push, asl_gc_root_pop, gcInit, gcWillAllocate, gcAccount, gcRegisterProto, gcFindObj, gcFreedObjects, gcTestFailNextPageSetGrow and gcScanConservative, and the globals gcStackBase, gcStackTop and gcExternalRoots, with the state block, the ccc callbacks the helpers pass (gcAslMarkRootC for the root hooks, gcAslPrintStatsC for atexit, gcAslLargeCmp for qsort) and setjmp declared returns_twice. asl_gc_collect keeps gc.c's guard: under asl-host's gcFloorGuard the mark phase runs with a setjmp handler that clears collecting, the mark stack and every mark before re-raising, and finalizer errors gather in a 4096-byte buffer on its frame. asl/host/build.sh runs main and compiles the module into libaslrt.a as its member gcAsl.o (plan unit GCASL-2), so every native link takes this collector and none links gc.o, which only asl-host's libaslhost.a keeps. A fact the triple lacks or a helper declaration the emitted text does not hold exactly once is ERR_LLVM_GCROUTE.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#collectorModule" :text "gcAsl's functions, externs and strings as one SsaModule for the triple of facts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#collectorModuleForTarget" :text "gcAsl's functions, externs and strings for explicit target properties and libc facts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#sym" :text "The LLVM symbol of the collector function name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#entryNames" :text "The symbols the collector module defines with external linkage: gc.c's whole C ABI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#entryText" :text "gc.c's C entry points, each calling its collector function, and the callbacks the helpers pass. On wasm32, which has no setjmp and no asl-host floor guard, asl_gc_collect marks and sweeps unguarded (no guard, no finalizer error buffer), there is no exit-time statistics callback, and @asl_gc_shadow_top, the head of the program's shadow-root frames (asl-target-llvm/ssa emitLlvmProgramWasm32), starts at 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#extraDecls" :text "Declarations the definitions need, added when the emitted text lacks them; wasm32's have no floor guard, setjmp or atexit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#declares?" :text "True when lines already declare decl's symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#inlinedNames" :text "Collector functions inlined into every caller, as gc.c's static inline ones are: poolAlloc into asl_alloc, asl_alloc_raw and asl_alloc_cons (whose constant slot size then divides by a constant), markObj and markVal into the root marking loops.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#internal" :text "A collector function's definition with internal linkage, alwaysinline for inlinedNames: the emitted module holds only collector functions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#collectorText" :text "The collector module's LLVM text for the triple of facts, as this module's :d describes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#collectorTextForTarget" :text "The collector module's LLVM text for explicit target properties.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#hostTriple" :text "The libc.asl triple of a host whose uname -s -m printed uname, empty for one libc.asl does not cover.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcRoute.asl#main" :text "Writes the collector module for the host this runs on to the path args names, or prints it when args is empty; a host libc.asl does not cover or a failing emission is an err.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#" :text "LLVM IR emitter for the asl-ir SSA contract (asl-ir/types Ssa*). A module is verified with verifySsa first and emitted only when it verifies. Val is the host's 16-byte Val passed by value as %Val = {i64, i64}, the SysV arm64 and x86_64 coercion of {i32 tag, i32 aux, i64 payload}, so runtime calls and closure trampolines need no conversion (valTag, valObj, valAux read it, boxInline builds Int, Float and Bool inline); values typed i64, f64 or i1 stay raw. Block parameters become phi nodes built from the incoming edges; an edge that shares its source and target with another edge of the same terminator gets its own forwarding block so every phi entry names a distinct predecessor. emitLlvmProgram's @main calls an entry with no parameters and exits with its unboxed result, or passes an entry with one Val parameter the command-line arguments as a List of Strings (valrt.args, asl-target-llvm/rtValue) and exits as asl-host run does on its Result (rterr.exit, asl-target-llvm/rtError). Raw primitives (opPrim) lower to native instructions; a primitive that can trap (addInt/subInt/mulInt/quotInt/remInt on Int overflow or a zero or INT64_MIN by -1 divisor) branches to its own block calling llvm.trap (IR-internal, no ASL source path reaches them, NATIVE-trapMessage left this family as is), while floatToInt and rawNarrowI32 (NaN or out of range, same no-source-path status) and the *Host primitives instead branch to rterr.int (asl-target-llvm/rtError) so they fail with a one-line host-style ERR_INT_OVERFLOW message, and continue in dest.p.ok, so the terminator of an SSA block holding one sits in the last such continuation and phis name that block as predecessor. A block ending in a direct call whose result it returns at once, itself or through a chain of joins that only forward their one parameter to a return, to a module function with the caller's return type emits musttail call and ret instead of its terminator; module functions use the tailcc convention (closure trampolines, runtime entries and externs stay ccc), so direct tailcc module calls may retain musttail across differing parameter ABIs only when caller and callee return ABIs match. sysRoute wrappers use ordinary calls because their runtime/extern ABI may differ, and calls with mismatched return ABIs are ordinary calls and can consume stack. No tailcc call passes stack arguments: parameters past 6 integer or 8 float registers travel through the runtime's asl_rt_spill (spillSlots). An unreachable terminator, the no-match block a non-exhaustive match lowers to, calls rterr.match with the function name (the host reports ERR_MATCH_NONEXHAUSTIVE and exits 1) instead of leaving LLVM undefined behaviour; a switch reads the scrutinee's constructor id from its Val and Ctor with extractvalue, getelementptr and load and finds its variant position against @variantIds.<type>, filled once per module by @variantIdsInit.<type> from value.c intern ids, and routes non-Ctor values through the host-style type trap and foreign Ctors through the host-style non-exhaustive-match trap, leaving the default of a switch covering every variant unreachable. An opField or opVariantField result read by exactly one opUnbox to a raw type (Int, Float or Bool) fuses into that opUnbox (fusedMap, RT-INLINE-2): no call and no box on the fast path, which inline-checks the Val's tag (T_CTOR 8 for a variant, T_REC 7 for a record), bound-checks (Ctor.n or a runtime scan of Rec's keys against an interned id cached per field by @fieldId.<field>, filled once by @fieldIdInit.<field> from value.c intern as @variantIds.<type> is), and checks the found field's own Val tag before loading its union payload; any miss falls back to calling objrt.field or objrt.variantField (rtObject) for the real field, then its own inline tag check against the same cold rterr.type block (RT-MEMORY M2), so the error stays the host's; a plain (unfused) opUnbox inlines that same tag check and trap directly against its operand, with no asl_rt_unbox_<kind> call anywhere in emitted IR, as does a termBranch on a Val condition before it extracts the payload bit. An opField whose base is itself defined in the function by opRecord (recordMap, RT-MEMORY M4) knows the field's index in that opRecord's declared field order at compile time, since asl-ir/verify's checkRecord proves it (any opRecord whose fields disagree with the schema's declared order is rejected, ERR_IR_UNKNOWN_FIELD): it reads a %Val slot straight from the Rec at that static index with no call, defensively bound-checking against the record's own field count first and trapping by the function name, as a non-exhaustive match does, on a tag or bound mismatch that would mean a verifier invariant had broken elsewhere (emitStaticFieldRead); an opField whose base no opRecord in the function defines but whose type carries a schema (tyRec, M4b-1, a schema the module declares; typedFieldIndex) knows only the slot that schema's declared order would give, never a proof, since a Rec built by the VM, by C code or by any host builtin may hold the same schema's fields in another order: it loads the %Val at that static slot with no call only after checking the tag is T_REC, the index is below Rec.n and keys[index] equals the field's interned id cached in @fieldId.<field> (staticKeyProbe), and any miss goes to a cold block calling rtObject's objrt.field, so a wrong-order record still reads the right field and a non-record or a record without the field fails with abi.c asl_rt_field's former ERR_TYPE or ERR_FIELD text, never a trap by function name (emitTypedFieldRead); a fused read on such a base tries the same static slot before its runtime key scan (emitFusedFieldUnbox); a field read on any other base is not compile-time-known at all and calls objrt.field, which keeps abi.c asl_rt_field's ERR_TYPE and ERR_FIELD texts. Records, variants, closures, strings, keywords and symbols run as internal rtObject helpers (objrt.*) over value.h layouts, interning names through value.c intern, a function value without native code failing as no evaluator is linked; the remaining operations on Val call extern runtime functions (runtimeDecls lists their signatures, the host C ABI defines them); an opEntry of an intrinsic or libm row calls builtinSym (an @llvm.*.f64 intrinsic or a direct libm declare) with the operand and result types builtinEntry gives, and no opEntry or opBuiltin calls into abi.c or prelude.c, whose by-name asl_rt_builtin and core table left libaslrt.a (PRELUDEASL-Z): a builtin call no emitted IR runs is ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED naming it before emission (builtinDiags), and only a builtinTables name passes an argument array by name to its asl_rt_builtin_<table>; trap, assert and refute call rtError helpers natively (counts in weak @rterr.assertCount and @rterr.refuteCount), and abs, min, max, clamp, int64ToFloat64, float64ToInt64, << and >> (mathBuiltin?, PRELUDEASL-A and PRELUDEASL-Z) call @mathrt helpers emitted only when referenced (mathDefinitions) with prelude.c's semantics and its ERR_TYPE, ERR_RANGE and ERR_INT_OVERFLOW texts; the list and bytes group (PRELUDEASL-B) never reaches abi.c or prelude.c: cons, listHead, listTail, listEmpty?, bytesLength, bytesGet and bytesSet inline as blocks whose misses raise natively, bytesAlloc and the fused @listHeadOr, @listTailOr, @listGetOr, @stringSliceOr, @listFirst and @listRest call @listrt.* and @bytesrt.* helpers, bytesGetFloat64 and bytesSetFloat64 opBuiltins call their @bytesrt helpers, partial builds the runtime's partial Ctor with emitCtorAlloc and a list literal is a straight-line chain of @listrt.cell conses built from its last item (emitListLiteral), every helper emitted only when referenced (mathDefinitions); the string group (PRELUDEASL-C) never reaches abi.c or prelude.c either: stringLength, stringConcat, stringSlice, stringStartsWith?, stringContains? and stringToBytes call @strrt.* helpers over the Str bytes with prelude.c's semantics and want texts (strFunctions), stringFromInt64 calls rtFormat's @asl_rt_format_i64, and an Int operand of stringSlice or stringFromInt64 unboxed for that call alone fails with the builtin's want text (entryUnboxes); the operator group (ABIVAL-3) never reaches abi.c either: an opEntry of +, -, *, /, mod, <, <=, >, >=, =, != or not and the unary minus opBuiltin call @opsrt.* helpers (asl-target-llvm/rtOps) with vm.c's semantics and texts, structural = and != included, so an operator used as a value, a lifted wrapper over the same opEntry, calls them too; the two prelude.c functions routed sys and process code declares, mkBytes and aslLogSpawn, are internal IR definitions of each module that calls them (hostFunctions), never declared; argument arrays are allocas hoisted into the entry block. opConstruct, opRecord and opMakeClosure allocate their Ctor, Rec and Closure (asl/host/src/value.h) directly with asl_alloc, no asl_rt_construct, asl_rt_record or asl_rt_make_closure call (RT-MEMORY M5): every field, value or capture %Val is computed before the one alloc and stays live across it on the stack or in a callee-saved register, visible to the conservative GC scan as any other live Val is, and no further allocation happens before the last field is stored, so the GC never traces a half-built object; a variant's ctor id and a schema's id and key ids are interned ids cached once per name in @ctorId.<variant> or @schemaId.<schema>/@keyIds.<schema> and filled lazily by ctorIdInit or schemaIdInit, exactly as a fused field's id is cached by fieldIdInit, while a closure's Proto is a compile-time constant, @proto.<callee>, needing no runtime lookup by code pointer at all. Symbols, values and labels are encoded by llvmName, which keeps [A-Za-z0-9_] and writes any other byte as $ and two hex digits, so emitted names never contain a dot and the emitter's own names (bb.*, *.argv, @name.*, @str.*, @variants.*, @variantIds.*, @variantIdsReady.*, @variantIdsInit.*, @fieldId.*, @fieldIdReady.*, @fieldIdInit.*, @ctorId.*, @ctorIdReady.*, @ctorIdInit.*, @schemaId.*, @schemaIdReady.*, @schemaIdInit.*, @keyIds.*, @proto.*, @protoName.*, @protoFile.compiled, @nameId.*, @strVal.*, @global.*, @init.*, *.code, @rterr.*, @.rterr.*, @mathrt.*, @.mathrt.*, @listrt.*, @.listrt.*, @bytesrt.*, @.bytesrt.*, @strrt.*, @.strrt.*, @opsrt.*, @.opsrt.*, @objrt.*, @.objrt.*, @.hostrt.*) cannot collide with them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.name" :text "Module name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.functions" :text "Module functions by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.externs" :text "Module externs by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.types" :text "ADT name to variants in tag order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.strings" :text "String pool")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ModEnv.records" :text "Record schema name to its field names in declared order (SsaModule records): the slot a tyRec-typed opField base tries first (typedFieldIndex)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ListCells.lines" :text "Emitted cell lines, last first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ListCells.index" :text "Position of the cell emitted last")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#ListCells.tail" :text "The %Val the next cell's cdr holds")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.mod" :text "Module environment")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.defs" :text "Type of every value the function defines")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.blocks" :text "Blocks by label")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.order" :text "Blocks in emission order, entry first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.retTy" :text "Return type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.name" :text "Function name, carried into its no-match trap")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.fused" :text "opField or opVariantField instructions, by dest, whose only use in the function is a single opUnbox to a raw type; emitInstr emits nothing at the def and inlines the fused read at the opUnbox site instead")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.records" :text "opRecord instructions, by dest, defined anywhere in the function: an opField whose base is one of these dests knows its schema and declared field order at compile time (RT-MEMORY M4) and reads a static slot instead of calling objrt.field; any other base whose type is tyRec only tries its schema's slot behind a keys[i] check (typedFieldIndex, emitTypedFieldRead)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#FnEnv.wants" :text "opUnbox dests read only as Int operands of one stringFromInt64 or stringSlice opEntry (entryUnboxes), each with the builtin's want name constant and the entry's String operand (empty for stringFromInt64)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#llvmName" :text "Encodes an arbitrary identifier as an LLVM-safe identifier with hex escapes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#llvmBytes" :text "Escapes special characters in a string for LLVM string constant literals.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#llvmFloat" :text "Formats a float64 value into its exact hex representation for LLVM IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeTy?" :text "True for the two raw types a C ABI extern uses that no asl-to-asl typed extern or module function signature ever carries, so their presence marks an extern as a native declaration: ccc, not tailcc, and never spilled through asl_rt_spill.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeExtern?" :text "A typed extern declared against the real C ABI (ccc), either because the libc facts table marks it variadic or because a param or the result is ptr or i32.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valTag" :text "Binds <p>.vtag to the tag of the %Val base: word 0 holds the tag (asl/host/src/value.h Tag) in its low 32 bits and the aux, an interned keyword id, in its high 32; word 1 holds the union payload.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valObj" :text "Binds <p>.obj to the object pointer in the payload word of the %Val base.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valAux" :text "Binds <p>.aux to the aux half of word 0 of the %Val base, the interned id of a keyword.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#boxInline" :text "Builds a %Val from a raw value without a call: tag word T_BOOL 1, T_INT 2 or T_FLOAT 3 with aux 0, the payload the i64, the double's bits or the zero-extended i1. opBox never reaches ptr or i32 (asl-ir/verify restricts box and unbox to i64, f64 and i1); the arms below exist only so the match is exhaustive, sign- or pointer-extending into the T_INT representation as a defensive fallback.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rawKind" :text "The fused-unbox tag kind for a raw type. opUnbox never reaches ptr or i32 (asl-ir/verify restricts it to i64, f64 and i1); the arms below exist only so the match is exhaustive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nameIdCellSym" :text "The module cell holding name's interned id, -1 until rtObject's objrt.nameId resolves it: a keyword constant's id and the key a field read's cold path searches for.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strCellSym" :text "The module cell holding string constant index's String Val once rtObject's objrt.str has built and rooted it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nameIdArgs" :text "The cell, name and byte length operands objrt.nameId and objrt.field take for name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fieldMiss" :text "The cold call of a record field read whose inline path missed: rtObject's objrt.field searches base's keys for field and fails with abi.c's ERR_TYPE or ERR_FIELD text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#internId" :text "Binds reg to name's interned id from asl-target-llvm/rtValue's table, for a resolver filling a per-module id cache once.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#protoName" :text "The name the VM gives the Proto of callee's code, which an arity error prints: 'lambda' for a lifted lambda (asl-ir/lower names it <declaration>@lambda<n>, compile.c newProto(\"lambda\")), else the function's own name after its module prefix.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#wrappedCallee" :text "The module function f wraps when f is asl-ir/lower's lifted wrapper of a function value (builtinLambda: parameters named @0, @1, ..., which no source parameter can be), read from its one direct call; none for any other function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#protoNameIn" :text "protoName of callee, or of the function callee wraps when it is a function value's lifted wrapper (wrappedCallee), as the VM's closure over that function carries the function's own Proto.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#externGlobalSym" :text "A foreign C global's own symbol, unprefixed (environ, ...): opLoadGlobal reads one by its real linker name, unlike globalSym's own @global.<name> convention for this module's own GC-managed Val globals.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#runtimeDecls" :text "Returns declarations of external runtime support functions needed by emitted LLVM IR.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeBuiltinEntries" :text "Builtin entries that call an @llvm.*.f64 intrinsic or a libm function directly. Every wrap-kind row runs as emitted IR (nativeEntryName?, formatEntryName?), so no opEntry calls into the runtime library.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#builtinSym" :text "The LLVM symbol an intrinsic or libm builtin entry calls: an @llvm.*.f64 intrinsic or a direct libm declare.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#builtinTables" :text "The C builtin tables a native binary links only on use (asl/host/src sys.c, sysNet.c, parallel.c), each name with its table's suffix: a call of one of these goes to asl_rt_builtin_<table>, whose reference links that table from libaslhost.a; prelude.c's core table is in no native link (PRELUDEASL-Z), every core builtin running as emitted IR. No table reaches the evaluator: hostVerb, which did through asl_rt_builtin_host, left in NX4. The unboxed array and kernel builtins have no table: asl-target-llvm/arrayRoute routes them to asl-target-llvm/arrays before emission.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#builtinTableSym" :text "The runtime function a call of builtin name by name goes through, asl_rt_builtin_<table> for a name of builtinTables; none for any other name, which has no by-name runtime entry since asl_rt_builtin left libaslrt.a (builtinDiags rejects such a call before emission).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#tableCall" :text "A by-name call of a builtinTables builtin over the argument array arr; builtinDiags has rejected any other name before emission, so none emits nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#termOperands" :text "The value names a terminator reads: the condition or scrutinee, the returned value, and every edge's arguments.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#useCounts" :text "How many times each value name is read across the whole function: every instruction's operands plus every block's terminator operands (its condition or scrutinee, its returned value and every outgoing edge's arguments).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fusedInstrs" :text "opField and opVariantField instructions whose result is read exactly once in the function, by a single opUnbox to a raw type: these fuse into that opUnbox, with no call and no box on the fast path (RT-INLINE-2).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fusedFieldNames" :text "Distinct field names fused anywhere in the module, each needing a @fieldId.<field> cache cell and resolver (fieldIdInit); fieldIdNames adds the fields plain typed-base reads check.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#typedFieldNamesIn" :text "Fields f reads by a plain (unfused) opField on a tyRec-typed base (typedFieldIndexFor, emitTypedFieldRead), each needing the @fieldId.<field> cell its keys[i] check compares against.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fieldIdNames" :text "Distinct field names needing a @fieldId.<field> cache cell and resolver (emitFieldIdInit): every fused field (fusedFieldNames), then every field a plain typed-base read checks keys[i] against (typedFieldNamesIn).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#recordMap" :text "opRecord instructions defined anywhere in f, by dest: an opField reading one of these dests as its base knows the schema's declared field order at compile time (RT-MEMORY M4); a base merely typed tyRec is not in this map and gets only typedFieldIndexFor's keys[i]-checked slot.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#recordFieldsFor" :text "The declared field order of the opRecord that defines base in recs, if base is such a dest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fieldStaticIndexFor" :text "field's position in base's compile-time-known schema (recordFieldsFor), the static slot index an opField reading it can try first (RT-MEMORY M4).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#typedFieldIndexFor" :text "field's declared index in the schema base's own type names (tyRec, M4b-1), for a base no opRecord in the function defines (an opRecord base keeps fieldStaticIndexFor's proven layout, RT-MEMORY M4): a slot only worth trying first, never a proof, since a Rec built by the VM, by C code or by any host builtin may hold that schema's fields in another order; none when base is not tyRec, its schema is not declared in the module, or field is not one of its fields.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fusedTagNum" :text "The raw Val tag (asl/host/src/value.h Tag) a fused read must find at the field to trust its union payload: T_BOOL 1, T_INT 2, T_FLOAT 3.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#fusedFastLoad" :text "Loads the raw value at %<p>.valp straight from the Val union (asl/host/src/value.h), binding %<p>.fastval; a Bool is stored as an i64 0 or 1 so it is loaded and truncated.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#unboxPayload" :text "Binds the result lhs assigns from the raw payload word of %Val base, once its tag is already known to match kind: Int reads word 1 straight as i64, Float bitcasts it to double, Bool truncates its i64 0/1 to i1. prefix names the intermediate <prefix>.w temp so two unboxes in the same block (a fast path's own and a fallback's) never collide.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#typeTrap" :text "A cold block, named <lbl>.trap, calling rterr.type with the Val's actual tag (already bound at <p>.vtag) and the raw kind (T_BOOL 1, T_INT 2, T_FLOAT 3) the site expected, then unreachable; rtError reports the same ERR_TYPE text abi.c's deleted type trap and the asl_rt_unbox_<kind> calls before it used to.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitUnboxInline" :text "Inlines a plain (unfused) opUnbox (RT-MEMORY M2): extractvalue the Val's tag and branch to dest.trap, calling rterr.type, when it does not match the destination's raw kind; dest.ok extracts the payload word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#entryUnboxes" :text "opUnbox dests every read of which is an Int operand of one stringFromInt64 or stringSlice opEntry (PRELUDEASL-C), each with that builtin's want name constant and, for stringSlice, its String operand unless that is defined after the unbox in their block (a parameter or a dest of another block dominates the opEntry; coerceAll orders a same-block one first), else empty: their tag miss raises prelude.c's want text naming the builtin (emitEntryUnbox) where any other unbox raises rterr.type's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitEntryUnbox" :text "An opUnbox in entryUnboxes: emitUnboxInline's tag check, whose miss fails as prelude.c's want(a[i], T_INT, who) does (wantTrap), after checking stringSlice's String operand is a String first (want T_STR), the order bStringSlice checks its operands in.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitFusedVariantUnbox" :text "Inlines opVariantField base index fused into an opUnbox to a raw type: a %Val whose tag is T_CTOR (8) holds a Ctor (asl/host/src/value.h) whose field count (offset 12) bounds the compile-time index, whose field at offset 16+index*16 (stride 16, matching variantTagLookup) is read only once its own Val tag matches the destination's raw kind; any miss calls rtObject's objrt.variantField, then branches on that Val's own tag to the same cold rterr.type the fast path's miss would reach, so the error stays the host's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitVariantFieldVal" :text "Inlines a general (non-fused) opVariantField base index whose %Val result is read as a Val rather than unboxed (RT-MEMORY M3): a %Val whose tag is T_CTOR (8) holds a Ctor (asl/host/src/value.h) whose field count (offset 12) bounds the compile-time index; in range, the field at offset 16+index*16 (stride 16, matching emitFusedVariantUnbox and variantTagLookup) is loaded whole as %Val with no unbox and no tag check, since the caller wants the Val itself; a wrong tag or an out-of-range index falls back to rtObject's objrt.variantField so the error stays the host's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#recordKeysPrelude" :text "The <lbl>.rec block of an inline record field read, entered once base's tag is T_REC: binds <p>.obj, the Rec's field count <p>.n (offset 12) and key table <p>.keys (offset 16, i32 ids), resolves @fieldId.<field> once through fieldIdInit (<lbl>.resolve), and opens <lbl>.scan with the field's interned id loaded as <p>.fid; the caller ends <lbl>.scan with its own branch.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#staticKeyProbe" :text "Ends <lbl>.scan (recordKeysPrelude) with the typed-base probe of a schema's declared slot index: index < Rec.n, then <lbl>.sprobe loads keys[index] (i32 stride) and compares it with <p>.fid, the field's cached interned id; equal branches to hit, either test failing branches to miss. A Rec built in declared order passes; one holding the same schema's fields in another order, or another record, fails over to miss and never reads a slot unchecked.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitTypedFieldRead" :text "Inlines a plain opField whose base's type carries a schema (tyRec, M4b-1) with the field at declared index index (typedFieldIndex), base not defined by an opRecord in the function: the type names the schema but does not prove its key order, so the static slot (offset 24+16*index) is loaded with no call only after the tag is T_REC (7), index < Rec.n and keys[index] equals @fieldId.<field> (recordKeysPrelude, staticKeyProbe); any miss goes to the cold <dest>.slow block, which calls rtObject's objrt.field, so a record holding the schema's fields in another order still reads the right field and a non-record or a record without the field fails with abi.c asl_rt_field's former ERR_TYPE or ERR_FIELD text through objrt.field. Unlike emitStaticFieldRead's opRecord bases, a miss here is an ordinary runtime case, never a verifier-invariant breach, and never traps by function name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitFusedFieldUnbox" :text "Inlines opField base field fused into an opUnbox to a raw type: a %Val whose tag is T_REC (7) holds a Rec (asl/host/src/value.h) whose keys (offset 16, length at offset 12) are matched against the field's interned id, cached once per field by @fieldId.<field> and filled by fieldIdInit as variantTagLookup fills @variantIds.<type> (recordKeysPrelude). When base's type carries a schema (static, typedFieldIndex: a tyRec base no opRecord in the function defines) the field's declared index i is tried first (staticKeyProbe: i < Rec.n and keys[i] equal to the cached id), since a record built in declared order holds it there; a miss on that probe, or any base without a static index, scans the keys at runtime, so a Rec holding the same schema's fields in another order (built by the VM, C code or a host builtin) still finds its field. The matching slot (offset 24+index*16, stride 16) is read only once its own Val tag matches the destination's raw kind; any miss (no key, index past the end, or wrong tag) calls objrt.field, then branches on that Val's own tag to the same cold rterr.type the fast path's miss would reach, so the error stays the host's and nothing traps by function name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitFieldIdInit" :text "Fills @fieldId.<field> with the interned id of field (value.c intern) and sets @fieldIdReady.<field>, as emitVariantIdsInit does per variant type.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitCtorIdInit" :text "Fills @ctorId.<variant> with the interned id of variant (value.c intern), the id a Ctor built by emitConstruct stores at Ctor.ctor; sets @ctorIdReady.<variant>, as emitFieldIdInit fills @fieldId.<field> (RT-MEMORY M5).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitSchemaIdInit" :text "Fills @schemaId.<schema> with the interned id of schema and @keyIds.<schema> with the interned id of each declared field in order, the same ids a Rec built by emitRecord stores at Rec.schema and points Rec.keys at; sets @schemaIdReady.<schema>, gating both fills with the one flag, as emitVariantIdsInit fills @variantIds.<type> (RT-MEMORY M5).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitCtorAlloc" :text "Shared ctor-build core of emitConstruct (RT-MEMORY M5) and the Option results listHead/listTail inline (RT-PRELUDE P4, emitListExtract): resolves variant's lazily-cached ctor id (@ctorId.<variant>, filled by ctorIdInit) and allocates a Ctor (asl/host/src/value.h) directly with asl_alloc_raw(O_CTOR 3, bytes) (no clearing: the id, n and every field are stored before anything else allocates, NATIVE-PERF), no asl_rt_construct call, leaving <labelPrefix>.objw (i64, the object pointer) for the caller to box as T_CTOR (8); every field %Val is computed before the alloc and stays live across it, on the stack or in a callee-saved register, visible to the conservative GC scan (abi.c scanStack, externalRoots) as any other live Val is, and no allocation happens between the alloc and the last field store, so the GC never traces a half-built object. fieldVals are already-formatted LLVM values (%name or a literal), not ASL operand names, so both callers can pass either a source operand (through val) or a register this instruction itself just computed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitConstruct" :text "Inlines opConstruct (RT-MEMORY M5): allocates a Ctor (asl/host/src/value.h) directly with asl_alloc(O_CTOR 3, bytes), no asl_rt_construct call, via emitCtorAlloc; the result boxes inline as a T_CTOR (8) %Val around the object pointer, as boxInline boxes a raw Int, Float or Bool.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitRecord" :text "Inlines opRecord (RT-MEMORY M5): allocates a Rec (asl/host/src/value.h) directly with asl_alloc_raw(O_REC 2, bytes) (no clearing: schema, n, keys, values and any key table fill the object before anything else allocates, NATIVE-PERF), preserving omitted-field presence by storing only supplied/defaulted keys and values in a per-record key table. The table is copied from @keyIds.<schema> in declared-index order, so arbitrary ordered subsets keep the same schema and field lookup semantics.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitMakeClosure" :text "Inlines opMakeClosure (RT-MEMORY M5): allocates a Closure (asl/host/src/value.h) directly with asl_alloc_raw(O_CLOSURE 4, bytes) (no clearing: proto, n and captures are stored before anything else allocates; the 4 bytes after n are padding no reader touches, NATIVE-PERF), no asl_rt_make_closure call, under the same GC-safety discipline as emitConstruct. Its Proto is @proto.<callee>, a compile-time constant (emitProto: name 'compiled closure', file '<compiled>', nparams the callee's own declared arity, native its trampoline codeSym) built once per closure target, so no runtime lookup by code pointer is needed, unlike the abi.c protos map asl_rt_make_closure used to build and cache one lazily. Closure.p (offset 8), Closure.n (offset 16) and each capture (offset 24, stride 16) are stored with plain gep/store, and the result boxes inline as a T_FN (9) %Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#idResolvedOp?" :text "True for opConstruct, opRecord and a partial opBuiltin with operands (partialCtor?), which (unlike opMakeClosure) resolve a lazily-cached name id before allocating and so open a .resolve/.alloc pair of blocks past their own dest label (emitConstruct, emitRecord, RT-MEMORY M5): exitLabel needs the .alloc continuation, as it needs a trapping prim's .p.ok (trapping?).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#inlinedEntryName?" :text "Entries whose opEntry inlines as blocks in emitInstr (RT-PRELUDE P4, PRELUDEASL-B): cons, listHead, listTail, listEmpty? and the bytes accessors. Each fast path checks its operand's tag (and, for bytesGet and bytesSet, the slot and byte range) and any miss branches to a cold block raising prelude.c's own ERR_TYPE or ERR_RANGE text natively (@mathrt.want, @bytesrt.slotBad, @bytesrt.notByte), never to an abi.c wrapper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#stringEntryName?" :text "String entries whose opEntry is one call of an @strrt helper (PRELUDEASL-C): stringLength, stringConcat and stringSlice, the three floor primitives, and stringStartsWith?, stringContains? and stringToBytes run as emitted IR over the Str bytes with prelude.c's semantics and texts, never through abi.c or prelude.c; stringFromInt64 is a formatEntryName? instead.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#helperEntryName?" :text "Entries whose opEntry is one call of an internal helper the module carries when it uses it (seqPieces, strPieces): bytesAlloc, the string entries (stringEntryName?) and the fused entries the lowering emits for (optionOr (listHead xs) d) and its kin and for a match on (listHead xs) or (listTail xs).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeEntryName?" :text "Entries that run as emitted IR, never through abi.c (PRELUDEASL-B, PRELUDEASL-C, ABIVAL-3): asl-ir/types builtinEntries keeps their rows only as the operand and result types of opEntry; the operators and not call their @opsrt helper (asl-target-llvm/rtOps).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#inlinedEntrySuffix" :text "The block-label suffix (past the instruction's own dest name) exitLabel must route a block's terminator from once an inlined entry op (inlinedEntryName?) is the block's last instruction: every one of them (RT-PRELUDE P4) ends its fast path in a join block, as a fused field read's join does. Empty for any other op.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#wantTrap" :text "A cold block lbl failing as prelude.c want(v, T, who) does: ERR_TYPE '<who> expects <T>, got <tag>' through @mathrt.want.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitCons" :text "Inlines cons (RT-PRELUDE P4): cdr's own Val tag is checked T_LIST (6), as the host's cons want(a[1], T_LIST, 'cons') does; in that case a Cons (asl/host/src/value.h) allocates directly with asl_alloc_cons() (gc.c's cons slot: Obj h 8 bytes written whole, car and cdr 16 each, no padding since car's 8-byte alignment is already met at offset 8, and no clearing, NATIVE-PERF), car and cdr stored at offsets 8 and 24 before anything else allocates. A tag mismatch raises the host's ERR_TYPE text natively (wantTrap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitListEmpty" :text "Inlines listEmpty? (RT-PRELUDE P4): xs' own Val tag checked T_LIST (6), as the host's want(a[0], T_LIST, 'listEmpty?') does; in that case the answer is whether its object pointer (the Cons, asl/host/src/value.h, or null for nil) is null, no call. A tag mismatch raises the host's ERR_TYPE text natively (wantTrap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitBytesLength" :text "Inlines bytesLength (RT-PRELUDE P4): xs' own Val tag checked T_BYTES (11), as the host's want(a[0], T_BYTES, 'bytesLength') does; in that case an Arr's len (asl/host/src/value.h, offset 8 past its Obj header) loads directly, no call. A tag mismatch raises the host's ERR_TYPE text natively (wantTrap).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitListExtract" :text "Shared by listHead (fieldOff 8, car, who @.listrt.who.listHead) and listTail (fieldOff 24, cdr, who @.listrt.who.listTail), RT-PRELUDE P4: xs' own Val tag checked T_LIST (6), as the host's want(a[0], T_LIST, ...) does; in that case a null Cons (asl/host/src/value.h, the empty list) allocates a 0-field 'none' Ctor, a non-null one reads its field at fieldOff and allocates a 1-field 'some' Ctor around it, exactly as the host's bListHead/bListTail wrap, sharing the lazily-cached @ctorId.some/@ctorId.none cells a module's own opConstruct sites of the same variant would (emitCtorAlloc, RT-MEMORY M5). A tag mismatch raises the host's ERR_TYPE text natively (wantTrap). The none and some arms each finish inside emitCtorAlloc's own .alloc continuation (its .resolve/.alloc pair opens past the dest label this function chose), so the join phi names <none|some>Lbl.alloc as its incoming predecessors, which opt -passes=verify checks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitBytesGet" :text "Inlines bytesGet (RT-PRELUDE P4): xs' own Val tag checked T_BYTES (11), as the host's slot()/want() do; in that case idx, already a raw i64, is checked against the Arr's own len (asl/host/src/value.h, offset 8) unsigned, as slot()'s i < 0 || i >= len test is, and in range the byte at data[idx] (data pointer at offset 24) loads directly, no call. A type miss raises ERR_TYPE (wantTrap) and a range miss slot()'s ERR_RANGE text (@bytesrt.slotBad), both natively.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitBytesSet" :text "Inlines bytesSet (RT-PRELUDE P4): xs' own Val tag checked T_BYTES (11), then idx against the Arr's own len (offset 8) as slot() checks it, then byteVal against 0..255 as bBytesSet does, in prelude.c's order; in range the byte at data[idx] (data pointer at offset 24) stores directly, answering unit (VUNIT, tag 0), no call. Each miss raises natively: ERR_TYPE (wantTrap), slot()'s ERR_RANGE text (@bytesrt.slotBad) or 'bytesSet: <v> is not a byte' (@bytesrt.notByte).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitInlinedEntry" :text "Dispatches an inlinedEntryName? opEntry to its emitter (RT-PRELUDE P4).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitNativeEntry" :text "A nativeEntryName? opEntry: inline blocks (emitInlinedEntry) or one call of its helper typed by its builtinEntries row (helperEntrySym).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqBuiltin?" :text "An opBuiltin of prelude.c's list and bytes group that runs natively (PRELUDEASL-B): partial of any count, bytesGetFloat64 of two and bytesSetFloat64 of three operands. Any other arity keeps asl_rt_builtin and its ERR_ARITY text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#partialCtor?" :text "partial with a function to bind, which builds a Ctor of the runtime's partial variant (emitSeqBuiltin).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitSeqBuiltin" :text "A seqBuiltin? opBuiltin: partial allocates the Ctor prelude.c bPartial builds, its variant id the interned 'partial' keyword the runtime's KW_PARTIAL holds (emitCtorAlloc, @ctorId.partial), every operand a field in order, so objrt.call applies it as vm.c vmCall does; partial of nothing raises bPartial's ERR_ARITY (@listrt.partialNone); the Float64 accessors call their helpers over the boxed operands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#listCell" :text "One cell of emitListLiteral: a Cons holding item ahead of the cells already built (@listrt.cell), stored through kept when it is not empty (emitListLiteralKept).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitListLiteral" :text "Inlines opList as prelude.c bList builds a list: from the last item to the first, each a Cons whose cdr is the list so far (@listrt.cell), straight-line with no argument array and no recursion, so a literal of any length costs no stack beyond its own operands. The list so far and every item not yet stored are live SSA values across each allocation, on the stack or in a callee-saved register the conservative GC scan reaches. An empty literal is nil, a List Val with a null object.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitListLiteralKept" :text "emitListLiteral, each new cell stored after its allocation through the slot pointer kept when kept is not empty (a shadow-root frame slot, rootSlots), so the list so far stays reachable from the frame across the next cell's allocation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitStaticFieldRead" :text "Inlines a plain opField whose base is defined in this function by opRecord with the read field among its declared fields (RT-MEMORY M4, staticFieldIndex): asl-ir/verify's checkRecord rejects any opRecord whose fields disagree with the schema's own declared order (ERR_IR_UNKNOWN_FIELD), and emitRecord always lays a record's physical keys out in that same declared order, so a verified program's base is proven, by that single-assignment definition, to hold exactly that schema with the field at that index; a %Val whose tag is T_REC (7) holds a Rec (asl/host/src/value.h) whose field count (offset 12) is bound-checked defensively against the static index, then the whole %Val slot is loaded (stride 16 from offset 24) with no call. A tag or bound mismatch can only mean a verifier invariant has been violated elsewhere (not a user-facing error, so not objrt.field or its ERR_FIELD text), so it traps by the function name as a non-exhaustive match does (ty/termUnreachable). A base merely typed by a schema (tyRec) proves no such order and reads through emitTypedFieldRead instead, whose misses are ordinary and never trap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#staticFieldInstr?" :text "True when ins is a plain (unfused) opField taking the static-slot fast path (emitStaticFieldRead): emitBlock then needs exitLabel to route a block's terminator from this instruction's single-predecessor .fast continuation, as it does for a trapping prim's .p.ok (trapping?).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#typedFieldInstr?" :text "True when ins is a plain (unfused) opField taking the typed-base path (emitTypedFieldRead: no opRecord base, a tyRec base with the field in its schema): emitBlock then needs exitLabel to route a block's terminator from this instruction's <dest>.join, where its fast and cold reads meet.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillGprLimit" :text "Integer argument registers a tailcc signature may use: x86_64 SysV has 6 (arm64 has 8), a %Val takes 2, an i64 or i1 1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillFprLimit" :text "Float argument registers a tailcc signature may use, 8 on x86_64 SysV and arm64, one per f64.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillCapacity" :text "Slots in the runtime's asl_rt_spill (asl/host/src/abi.c); a signature needing more is rejected with ERR_LLVM_ARITY.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#gprWords" :text "Integer register words for the tailcc spill accounting (spillSlots). ptr and i32 are declared only on native (ccc) externs, which spillDiags/registerParams never walk (nativeExtern?), but each still takes exactly one GPR word if ever asked.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillSlots" :text "Per parameter of a tailcc signature, -1 when it travels in a register, else its slot in @asl_rt_spill. No tailcc call passes stack arguments: LLVM's AArch64 -O0 code reloads spilled values before it re-reserves the call frame a callee-popped tailcc call released, so a caller read garbage after any call with stack arguments; callers store the overflow just before the call and the callee loads it first thing in its entry block, with no allocation between.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#tailCallArgs" :text "The stores that pass a tailcc call's overflow arguments through @asl_rt_spill (spillSlots), and its register argument list.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillLoads" :text "Entry-block loads of the parameters spillSlots passes through @asl_rt_spill, before any call can reuse the slots. Nothing may allocate or call between a caller's spill stores and these loads: the slots are not GC roots and the next call reuses them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#externCallType" :text "The callee's full first-class function type, which a variadic C call site must spell out alongside the call (LLVM has no other way to tell apart the fixed and the ... arguments).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeArgs" :text "Call arguments typed by the extern's declared params where one exists, else by the argument value's own SSA type: a variadic C call's arguments past arity (open's mode, for instance) carry whatever raw or Val type their definition gave them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#calleeArity" :text "callee's own parameter count, read from the module's functions (RT-MEMORY M5): the nparams a closure target's compile-time @proto.<callee> constant bakes in, as the old runtime's lazily-built Proto took it from opMakeClosure's own arity operand.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostTrapUnless" :text "Branch to a block failing as asl-host does, rterr.int (rtError) with the kind (0 to 3 overflow of + - * /, 5 division and 6 mod by zero; 7 and 8, NATIVE-trapMessage, are not asl-host operations, a native-only narrow and float-to-int range check given the same one-line message style instead of a bare signal), when bad holds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostDivPrim" :text "Floor division as asl-host computes it: a zero divisor fails kind 5, INT64_MIN by -1 kind 3, and a truncated quotient with a nonzero remainder of the divisor's opposite sign steps down by one. As in hostModPrim, the truncated quotient is the answer when remainder and divisor are both non-negative; any negative sign branches (unlikely) to the cold @mathrt.floorDivFix (NATIVE-PERF). The continuation is <dest>.p.ok.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostModPrim" :text "Floor modulo as asl-host computes it: a zero divisor fails kind 6, a divisor of -1 gives 0, and a nonzero remainder of the divisor's opposite sign moves up by the divisor. The truncated remainder is already the answer when it and the divisor are both non-negative, the common case, which goes straight on; any negative sign branches (unlikely, llvm.expect) to a call of the cold @mathrt.floorModFix, so the fix-up stays off the dependency chain of a loop carrying the result where a select would sit on it (NATIVE-PERF). Both paths give the same value; the continuation is <dest>.p.ok.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#floatToIntPrim" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: NaN or a value outside int64 fails through rterr.int (kind 8, ERR_INT_OVERFLOW 'Float to Int leaves int64') instead of the bare llvm.trap this used before; low/high are ordered fcmp, so NaN already took the trap branch (ordered compares are false on NaN) and keeps doing so.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#shiftRaw" :text "Masks the shift count to the width (63 for i64, 31 for i32) before shl/lshr/ashr, so every count, including a negative bit pattern, is defined (never poison), rather than LLVM's own undefined behaviour for a count at or past the operand width.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#narrowI32Prim" :text "NATIVE-trapMessage: fails through rterr.int (kind 7, ERR_INT_OVERFLOW 'Int narrow leaves int32') instead of the bare llvm.trap this used before, when the i64 value is outside -2147483648..2147483647; else truncates to i32.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#unfusedVariantField?" :text "True for an opVariantField instruction not fused into an opUnbox (RT-INLINE-2): its %Val result is still inlined (emitVariantFieldVal, RT-MEMORY M3) and so also ends its SsaBlock in a .join sub-block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#exitLabel" :text "The block label from which its terminator's br actually executes: its own label, unless a trapping prim's continuation (dest.p.ok), a static-slot field read's continuation (dest.fast, staticFieldInstr?), a fused field read's join (dest.join), a typed-base field read's join (dest.join, typedFieldInstr?), an inlined variant-field read's join (dest.join), a plain opUnbox's tag-check continuation (dest.ok), an opConstruct or opRecord's id-resolution continuation (dest.alloc, idResolvedOp?, RT-MEMORY M5), an inlined entry op's own continuation (dest.<inlinedEntrySuffix>, RT-PRELUDE P4), or (last, since it is the terminator itself) a Val-typed termBranch's own tag-check continuation (<label>.cond.ok) is the last such sub-block the block opens, since each emits more LLVM blocks after the SsaBlock's own label before the next text is appended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#patternArityCheck" :text "Ends <blk>.scan: a variant the switch names in an arm (armed) whose Ctor holds another field count than typeName declares for it, a same-named variant of another module's type, fails as vm.c OP_TESTCTOR does, ERR_ARITY 'pattern (<variant>) binds <declared> field(s), value has <n>' (objrt.patternArity); otherwise <blk>.check goes on to <blk>.match when the variant was found, <blk>.miss when not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#variantTagLookup" :text "Computes %<from>.tag, the position of the scrutinee's variant in typeName's variant table inline. A non-Ctor value takes the host-style type trap; a Ctor with another type takes the host-style non-exhaustive-match trap; a variant an arm names (armed) with another field count than declared takes vm.c's pattern arity error (patternArityCheck). The switch then sits in <from>.match.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitVariantIdsInit" :text "Fills @variantIds.<type> with the interned id of each variant name (value.c intern), the same id emitConstruct's ctorIdInit stores at a constructed Ctor.ctor (RT-MEMORY M5), and sets @variantIdsReady.<type>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#trapEdge?" :text "A switch default edge to a block that only traps (a non-exhaustive match, asl-ir/lower withTrapBlock): the switch reports the scrutinee as asl-host does, no arm matches <value> in <fn>, through rterr.matchValue in <from>.nomatch instead of reaching that block's value-less rterr.match.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#tailCall?" :text "The block ends in a call whose result is returned at once, itself or through a chain of joins that only forward their one parameter to a return (returnsDest?). A direct call qualifies when its callee is a module function or a typed tailcc extern (another module's function, not hostDefined? and not nativeExtern?) with the caller's return ABI (sameAbi?); a closure call qualifies when the caller returns a Val and its arguments fit asl_rt_spill. Direct tailcc calls retain musttail across signatures; sysRoute wrappers are excluded because their runtime/extern ABI may differ.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#returnsDest?" :text "The block returns dest, directly or through joins that only forward it to a return (returnsParam?).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#sameAbi?" :text "The two SSA types share a register ABI (ty/ssaAbiName), so a call of one may be musttail from a function returning the other.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#closureTailArgs" :text "The stores that put a tail closure call's arguments in the asl_rt_spill prefix, which tailrt.closure hands on as argv; nothing allocates between these stores and the tailCode trampoline's loads.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitTailCall" :text "The musttail call and ret that end a tailCall? block: a direct call through emitCall, a closure call through tailrt.closure with its arguments in asl_rt_spill (closureTailArgs).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitBlock" :text "One SSA block. With a shadow-root frame (frame not empty, rootSlots) every Val its phis and instructions define is stored to its frame slot as soon as it is defined, a list literal's cells as they are built, and the frame is popped (rootPop) before its return or its tail call; with an empty frame the text is the frameless emission, unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootSlot" :text "Binds <name>.root to slot k of the shadow-root frame %rt.frame (slot 0 is the frame header, rootFrameSetup).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootKeep" :text "name stored to its frame slot when the frame holds one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootPop" :text "Unlinks the function's shadow-root frame: the chain head goes back to the frame the caller left (%rt.prev), before every return and tail call, so a frame never outlives its activation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#shadowTopDecl" :text "The chain head of shadow-root frames, defined by the wasm32 collector (asl-target-llvm/gcRoute) and marked from by its mark phase.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootFrameSetup" :text "The entry of a function with n frame slots: %rt.frame, n+1 Vals of linear memory, its header slot holding the caller's chain head (%rt.prev) in word 0 and n in word 1, the n slots zeroed (a unit Val, which the collector skips) so the collector never reads a slot before the function stores to it, and the chain head set to the frame.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootedInstr?" :text "An instruction whose Val result the emitted text defines (not a fused field read, which emits nothing at its def) and may point into the heap (not an opBox, an inline Int, Float or Bool).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#rootSlots" :text "The values a shadow-root frame keeps, one slot each in this order: the Val captures and parameters, each Val block parameter with an incoming edge (one without is frozen poison, never a heap Val) and each rootedInstr? result, less the call a tail-calling block ends in, whose result is returned at once.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitFunctionRooted" :text "One module function as a tailcc definition; when rooted and the function has rootSlots, with a shadow-root frame: rootFrameSetup after the entry's allocas and spill loads, the Val captures and parameters stored to their slots there, and each block's Vals stored as emitBlock does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#listBuilderNames" :text "Prelude list builders emitted as hand-written loops (NATIVE-PERF, listBuilderText) instead of their prelude.asl bodies, which build the result reversed and reverse it: same order of closure calls and the same errors, half the allocation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#listBuilderText" :text "prelude.map f xs and prelude.filter f xs as one loop over xs that links each new cell (asl_alloc_cons) behind the last through its cdr, so the result comes out in order with no reversed copy. Each step does what preludeMapOnto and preludeFilterOnto do, in their order: xs must be a List (else listEmpty?'s want text, as their listHead match raises), its car goes to f through objrt.call, and for filter f's result must be a Bool (else rterr.type with T_BOOL, as their if on a Val does) and only a true one keeps the element. A new cell's cdr is nil until the next cell is linked into it; the head of the result, the rest of xs and f stay live SSA values across every call and allocation, so the conservative scan reaches the cells built so far through the head, and nothing else holds a cell before the function returns it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitCaptureInline" :text "Inlines closure capture i out of %env in a trampoline (RT-MEMORY M3): a %Val whose tag is T_FN (9) holds a Closure (asl/host/src/value.h) whose capture count (offset 16) bounds the compile-time index; in range, the capture at offset 24+i*16 (stride 16) is loaded whole as %Val, no call; a wrong tag or an out-of-range index falls back to rtObject's objrt.capture so the error stays the host's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#distinct" :text "xs without repeats, each name at its first occurrence: a stable sort by name puts each name's first index at the head of its run, and a sort by index restores the order, O(n log n) where a listContains? scan per name is quadratic.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#gather" :text "f's names over ops in order, consed onto a reversed list and reversed once: listAppend onto a growing accumulator copies it per op.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hasStaticFieldRead?" :text "True when f has an opField eligible for the static-slot fast path (staticFieldIndex via recordMap), excluding one already fused into an opUnbox (fusedMap): a fused field is read entirely by emitFusedFieldUnbox at its opUnbox site and never reaches emitStaticFieldRead, so counting it here would claim an @name.<f> constant the emitted IR does not use. emitStaticFieldRead's defensive trap names f by nameSym, as a non-exhaustive match's unreachable block does, so f needs the same @name.<f> constant whether or not it also has a termUnreachable block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#optionEntry?" :text "Entries whose native code allocates an Option Ctor: listHead and listTail inline (emitListExtract), stringSlice in @strrt.slice.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#constructedVariants" :text "Distinct variant names constructed anywhere in the module (opConstruct), needing a @ctorId.<variant> cache cell and resolver (emitCtorIdInit, RT-MEMORY M5), as fusedFieldNames needs @fieldId.<field>; listHead and listTail (RT-PRELUDE P4, emitListExtract) and stringSlice (@strrt.slice, PRELUDEASL-C) need the same cells for 'some' and 'none', the Option variants their Ctor allocation shares with any opConstruct site of the same name, as does a native float64ToInt64 (@mathrt.float64ToInt64, PRELUDEASL-A); a native partial (partialCtor?, PRELUDEASL-B) needs 'partial', the runtime's KW_PARTIAL keyword.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#constructedSchemas" :text "Distinct schema names built anywhere in the module (opRecord), needing a @schemaId.<schema> cache cell, a @keyIds.<schema> array and a resolver (emitSchemaIdInit, RT-MEMORY M5), as switchTypes needs @variantIds.<type>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#loadGlobalNames" :text "Distinct foreign C global names read anywhere in the module (opLoadGlobal: environ, ...), each needing its own `@<name> = external global ptr` declaration -- generalizing @asl_rt_spill's own single hardcoded declaration (assemble's own spill, keyed off a text scan since it is the one fixed name the runtime itself ever spills through) to any number of genuinely foreign globals, found by a real walk of the module's own ops rather than a text scan, since their names are never fixed in advance.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#recordSchemaFields" :text "schema's declared field order, from the module's own record declarations (.-records m), as typeVariants reads a type's declared variants from .-types: asl-ir/verify's checkRecord guarantees every opRecord of this schema agrees with it (RT-MEMORY M5, as RT-MEMORY M4's recordFieldsFor trusts the same invariant per function).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#idCellNames" :text "Distinct names whose interned id the module resolves through a @nameId.<name> cell (objrt.nameId): keyword constants, and the fields of every opField, whose cold path searches the record's keys for the field's id (fieldMiss).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valStringIndices" :text "Distinct string pool indices the module uses as a String Val (a constStr whose destination is not ptr), each needing a @strVal.<index> cell objrt.str builds once.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#protoNames" :text "Distinct Proto names (protoNameIn) of the module's closure targets, each a @protoName.<name> constant.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitProto" :text "The compile-time Proto (asl/host/src/value.h) a closure over callee points Closure.p at (emitMakeClosure, RT-MEMORY M5): name the VM's Proto name for callee (protoNameIn), which objrt.call's arity error prints as vm.c does, and file '<compiled>', nparams callee's own declared arity, maxstack/code/ncode/capcode/consts/nconsts/capconsts zero (unused by objrt.call's native dispatch), native callee's trampoline (codeSym). For wasm32, whose pointers are 4 bytes, each pointer is followed by an i32 0 so every field keeps the 64-bit offset objrt.call reads (nparams at 16, native at 56). After native comes tailCode (tailCodeSym, offset 64; on wasm32 followed by an i32 0 too), the tailcc trampoline tailrt.closure enters with musttail; the C runtime never reads past native.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#byteArray" :text "A NUL-terminated LLVM byte array constant of n+1 bytes: bytes then a trailing \\00, so @str.N is also a valid C string for a native extern's raw ptr argument (RT-SYSCALLS S2). objrt.str still takes its own explicit length argument (constStringLength), never strlen, so a boxed Val string with an embedded NUL is unaffected by the terminator.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#formatEntryName?" :text "Builtin entries (asl-ir/types builtinEntries) whose opEntry calls the module's own formatter helpers (asl-target-llvm/rtFormat).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitFormatEntry" :text "An opEntry of a formatEntryName? builtin: stringFromFloat64's operand is a raw double (entry kind f), stringFromInt64's a raw i64 (entry kind i, ABIVAL-1's @asl_rt_format_i64, prelude.c's %lld digits), stringToFloat64's a String Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#formatOp?" :text "An op whose emitted code calls the module's formatter helpers, so emitDefinitionsRooted appends them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#errorBuiltin?" :text "An opBuiltin rtError runs natively (ABIVAL-2): trap with its code and message, assert or refute with a condition and an optional message. Any other arity, which asl-ir/lower rejects, keeps asl_rt_builtin and its ERR_ARITY text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitErrorBuiltin" :text "trap calls rterr.trap, which never returns; assert and refute call rterr.assert or rterr.refute with the message, unit when absent as abi.c's K_ASSERT arm took it, and give unit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathBuiltin?" :text "An opBuiltin of prelude.c's math and conversion group that runs natively (PRELUDEASL-A): abs, int64ToFloat64 and float64ToInt64 of one operand, min, max, << and >> (PRELUDEASL-Z) and & | ^ ~ (NATIVE-INTRINSICS) of two and one, clamp of three, each a call of its internal helper (mathSym, mathPieces). Any other arity is rejected before emission (builtinDiags).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathSym" :text "The @mathrt helper of a mathBuiltin? name: shiftLeft, shiftRight, bitAnd, bitOr, bitXor and bitNot for << >> & | ^ ~, whose spelling is no LLVM name, else the name itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitMathBuiltin" :text "A mathBuiltin? opBuiltin as a call of its helper over the boxed operands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathText" :text "A private NUL-terminated constant of text, which holds only printable ASCII without a quote or backslash.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathConstants" :text "The builtin names and prelude.c message texts the helpers raise with, by symbol: want's and minmax's ERR_TYPE formats, bClamp's ERR_RANGE format and bAbs's ERR_INT_OVERFLOW text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathTagOf" :text "Binds <p>.tag to the Val v's tag and <p>.bits to its payload word.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathWant" :text "Fails as prelude.c want(%name, T, who) does when the Val %name's tag is not want (T_INT 2, T_FLOAT 3), else continues at label next; binds %name.tag and %name.bits.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathFunctions" :text "The helpers by symbol, each keeping prelude.c's semantics and its message text, raised through rtError's rterr.raise (ABIVAL-2): want and pair format the ERR_TYPE texts of want() and minmax() with value.c tagName (rterr.tagName); abs gives an Int's magnitude (ERR_INT_OVERFLOW 'abs of INT64_MIN') or a Float's with its sign bit cleared; min and max (minmax) need two Ints or two Floats and return a unless a > b (min) or a > b fails (max), so NaN and -0.0 pick the operand prelude.c's ordered compare picks; clamp checks lo, hi and x are Floats in that order, ERR_RANGE when lo or hi is NaN or lo > hi (printed %f), then gives x when NaN, else x limited to lo..hi; int64ToFloat64 rounds an Int to nearest as C's conversion does; float64ToInt64 gives (some n), n truncated toward zero, for -2^63 <= d < 2^63 and (none) for NaN, the infinities and anything outside, its Option allocated as emitConstruct allocates one (emitCtorAlloc).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathBitwise" :text "prelude.c's & | ^ over Vals (NATIVE-INTRINSICS): both operands Int, checked in order with want()'s text, then one and/or/xor; raw Int64 operands never reach this, lower.asl bitPrim gives them the bare instruction.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathShift" :text "prelude.c bitShiftLeft (shl) or bitShiftRight (ashr): both operands Int, checked in order with want()'s text, the count masked to 0..63 so every count is defined; a left shift wraps, a right shift sign-extends.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqConstants" :text "The builtin names and prelude.c and abi.c message texts the list and bytes helpers raise with, by symbol: want's who for each builtin, slot()'s ERR_RANGE format, bBytesSet's and bBytesAlloc's ERR_RANGE formats, mkBytes' ERR_OOM format and code, bPartial's ERR_ARITY text and the ERR_INTERNAL formats of the fused listFirst and listRest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqTag" :text "Binds %<v>.tag to the Val %<v>'s tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqObj" :text "Binds %<v>.obj to the object pointer of the Val %<v>.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqWant" :text "Continues at label next when the Val %<v>'s tag is want, else fails as prelude.c want(v, T, who) does (@mathrt.want); binds %<v>.tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#optionPart" :text "@listrt.headOr (car, offset 8) and @listrt.tailOr (cdr, offset 24): abi.c listArg's ERR_TYPE for a non-list, the default for the empty list, else the field.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#cellPart" :text "@listrt.first (car, offset 8) and @listrt.rest (cdr, offset 24): the field of a non-empty list, else abi.c's ERR_INTERNAL naming the operand's tag.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqFunctions" :text "The list and bytes helpers by symbol, each with prelude.c's or abi.c's semantics and texts, raised through rtError (ABIVAL-2): slotBad formats slot()'s ERR_RANGE; notByte bBytesSet's; alloc is bBytesAlloc and mkBytes (ERR_RANGE for a negative size, an O_ARR Arr from asl_alloc with len at 8, elem 1 at 16 and a zeroed calloc'd buffer of n+1 bytes at 24, ERR_OOM when it fails, gcAccount for pacing); slot8 is slot(a, 8, who) for the Float64 accessors (want Bytes, want Int, slot i inside len/8, unsigned), returning the element address, read and written unaligned; headOr, tailOr, getOr, sliceOr, first and rest are the fused entries abi.c defined (getOr's negative index answers the default before any type check, its walk checks each cdr is a List after the index test; sliceOr copies the bytes into a fresh Str from asl_alloc(O_STR 0, 17+n), its operand used after the allocation so the scan keeps it); partialNone is bPartial's ERR_ARITY.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#seqDecls" :text "The libc and runtime functions the list and bytes helpers call beyond rtError's: calloc and memcpy for bytesAlloc and sliceOr, gcAccount (gc.c) for bytesAlloc's pacing, declared as asl-target-llvm/arrays declares it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strConstants" :text "The builtin names the string helpers and the Int operand checks of stringSlice and stringFromInt64 (entryUnboxes) raise prelude.c's want ERR_TYPE text with, by symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strLength" :text "Binds %<v>.obj, %<v>.lenp and %<v>.len, the byte count at offset 8 of the Str (asl/host/src/value.h) the Val %<v> holds.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strText" :text "Binds %<into> to the first byte of the Str the Val %<v> holds (offset 16), read again from the Val itself so a helper that allocated in between keeps the Val live for the conservative scan, as sliceOr does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strMatchHead" :text "The entry of @strrt.startsWith and @strrt.contains: both operands checked String in order, as prelude.c's str(a[0]) then str(a[1]) do, binding each one's length and first byte.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strFunctions" :text "The string helpers by symbol, each with prelude.c's semantics and its want ERR_TYPE text, raised through rtError (ABIVAL-2) by @mathrt.want: length is bStringLength, the Str's byte count; concat is bStringConcat, both operands checked in order, then one Str from asl_alloc(O_STR 0, 17+n) holding both byte runs and a NUL; slice is bStringSlice over bytes, not code points (none when from < 0, to < from or to past the byte count, else (some s) of a fresh Str, so a slice may cut a UTF-8 sequence as asl-host's does); startsWith and contains are bStartsWith and bContains, byte comparisons by libc memcmp (an empty needle starts and is contained in every String, a needle longer than the haystack in none); toBytes is bStringToBytes, a fresh Bytes from @bytesrt.alloc (mkBytes) holding a copy of the Str's bytes. Every operand Val is read again after the helper's allocation, so the conservative scan keeps it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#strDecls" :text "The libc and LLVM functions the string helpers call beyond rtError's and the list and bytes helpers': memcmp for startsWith and contains, llvm.memcpy for the copies (rtFormat declares it too; assemble keeps one).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostConstants" :text "The texts aslLogSpawn uses, by symbol: the variable naming the spawn log, the fopen append mode, the empty program name and prelude.c's line format, which ends in a newline mathText cannot spell.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostFunctions" :text "IR definitions of the two prelude.c functions routed sys and process code declares as externs (asl-target-llvm/sys mkBytes, asl-target-llvm/sysProc aslLogSpawn), internal to each module so no native link needs prelude.c (PRELUDEASL-Z; assemble declares neither): mkBytes copies n bytes from p, or none when p is null, into a fresh Bytes from @bytesrt.alloc (bBytesAlloc's zeroed n+1 bytes, ERR_OOM text and gcAccount pacing, as mkBytes); aslLogSpawn appends the line '<argv0> <cwd>' to the file ASL_SPAWN_LOG names, when it names one, the cwd empty when getcwd fails, opened for append and created as fileAppendRaw does (fopen mode a: O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_APPEND, 0666 less the umask), a failure to open or write leaving no line as prelude.c's ignored fileAppendRaw result does; it returns 0 for sysProc's i64 declaration of it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostDecls" :text "The libc functions aslLogSpawn calls beyond rtError's snprintf.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#hostDefined?" :text "An extern a module's own IR defines (hostFunctions), which assemble does not declare.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathDefinitions" :text "The math, list, bytes, string, operator and object helpers and constants text reaches, directly or through each other, in mathPieces, seqPieces, strPieces, rtOps then rtObject order: a program carries only those its mathBuiltin?, seqBuiltin?, opsBuiltin?, nativeEntryName?, inlined entry and object code uses.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitDefinitionsRooted" :text "When rooted, every module function with rootSlots keeps a shadow-root frame (emitFunctionRooted) and the definitions declare the chain head (shadowTopDecl). The module's definitions, then the rtFormat helpers when a formatting op or an rtError or rtValue helper the program reaches renders a value, then the rtError and rtValue helpers and constants the definitions and entryCalls (the calls the @main wrapper will make) reach (rterr/rtErrorDefinitions): the intern table, value.c's entry points routed code declares, and the raise, which delivers to a handler a routed parMap worker installed through rtValue's cell. fieldIds is fieldIdNames m, computed once per emit and shared with emitConstants")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#exportDefinitions" :text "When calls, aslCall (asl-target-llvm/rtObject, the call of a function value libaslhost.a's C builtins make) with the object helpers it reaches; then the rtError and rtValue definitions those and roots reach.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valueExports" :text "The C definitions libaslrt.a's C floor calls (asl-target-llvm/rtValue rtValueExportRoots: KW_*, tagName, mkCtor), and aslCall when defs call a C table (asl_rt_builtin_<table>), whose libaslhost.a C calls function values through it, with what they reach, less any defs already hold: an entry module that links the runtime carries them so the link resolves them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#cRuntimeModule" :text "A standalone LLVM module for a native program whose main is C (test fixtures that build values in C as a host builtin would): C-callable intern and mkStr over asl-target-llvm/rtValue's table and allocator, the C definitions libaslrt.a's floor calls (rtValueExportRoots: KW_*, tagName, mkCtor, aslInternShared), aslCall and the raise state, closed over rtObject's, rtError's and rtValue's pieces, with the declarations they use.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#valueDefinedDecl?" :text "A declaration of a value.c function defs defines in IR (asl-target-llvm/rtValue), which the module must not also declare.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#cDeclFits?" :text "A C declaration's arguments all travel in registers: at most 6 integer words (a %Val takes 2) and 8 doubles. LLVM may split an IR {i64, i64} between the last register and the stack where C passes the struct whole on the stack, so a C signature that does not fit could silently disagree.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#overwideCDecls" :text "Runtime C declarations (runtimeDecls, builtin entries included) that cDeclFits? rejects; emitLlvmModule refuses to emit while any exists.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#spillDiags" :text "ERR_LLVM_ARITY for every tailcc signature the module defines or calls, its functions and its typed externs, whose overflow exceeds asl_rt_spill, so no call site stores past the array; ERR_LLVM_ABI for a runtime C declaration whose arguments overflow the registers. A native extern (ccc) is exempt: it is not spilled through asl_rt_spill, LLVM lowers its real platform ABI itself.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeBuiltin?" :text "An opBuiltin of name over n operands that emitted IR runs (emitInstr's opBuiltin arms) or a builtinTables entry links.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#nativeEntryCall?" :text "An opEntry of name over n operands that emitted IR runs (emitInstr's opEntry arm): a native, formatter, intrinsic or libm entry, or a builtinTables entry.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#unsupportedBuiltin" :text "The name and operand count of a builtin call op whose callee has no native definition, as a diagnostic text; none for any other op.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#builtinDiags" :text "ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED for each builtin call with no native definition, located by its function: prelude.c's by-name table left libaslrt.a with asl_rt_builtin (PRELUDEASL-Z), so such a call fails here at build time, never at link time.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#entryInstrs" :text "An opBuiltin over boxed operands of a name builtinEntry types and no other arm runs natively, as SSA built by hand writes cons or stringLength (the lowering emits opEntry itself): each raw operand an opUnbox to the entry's type, named <dest>#<k>, the opEntry, and a raw result an opBox back to the Val dest; any other instruction unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#entryBuiltin?" :text "An instruction entryInstrs rewrites.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#entryBuiltins" :text "m with every opBuiltin entryInstrs rewrites as its opEntry, after verification, so emission sees only builtin calls a native arm runs.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitLlvmModule" :text "Verifies an SSA module and emits its definitions as LLVM IR assembly.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitLlvmModuleWasm32" :text "emitLlvmModule for wasm32: closure Protos keep their 64-bit field offsets (emitProto), and, since the wasm32 collector cannot scan the native stack, precise shadow-root frames: each module function with a Val that may point into the heap links a frame of those Vals into the chain @asl_gc_shadow_top heads, stores each Val there as it is defined and unlinks the frame before it returns or tail-calls, so every live heap Val stays reachable from the chain across any call that allocates.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#replaceFunction" :text "Replaces one complete LLVM function definition while preserving surrounding text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#trapLowering" :text "For wasm trap facts, routes the central runtime raise to the imported asl.trap and removes the native longjmp declaration; all fixed, formatted, assertion and arithmetic raises funnel through this endpoint. Other target facts preserve LLVM text byte-for-byte.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#reportInit" :text "Installs rtError's ASL_ASSERT_REPORT report in every @main, at the point asl_rt_init installed abi.c's assertReport, which is gated by the variable alone: assertions counted by a separately emitted module (the weak rterr counters) are reported though the entry module holds none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitLlvmProgram" :text "Verifies an SSA module and emits an executable LLVM IR program with main entry.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitLlvmProgramWasm32" :text "emitLlvmProgram for wasm32, as emitLlvmModuleWasm32 emits a module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitEntry" :text "emitLlvmProgram after verification: the entry's @main wrapper, by the entry's shape.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/fixtures/nativePerf/bitProbe.asl#" :text "NATIVE-INTRINSICS: & | ^ ~ << >> with operands from argv, each printed twice, once over raw Int64 operands (one and, or, xor, shl or ashr inline) and once over Val operands through an unannotated lambda (the Int-checked @mathrt helper), which must agree; a non-Int Val operand fails with prelude.c want()'s text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/fixtures/nativePerf/trapProbe.asl#" :text "NATIVE-PERF trap preservation: each case reads its operands from argv so nothing folds, and must fail natively exactly as asl-host run does (ERR_INT_OVERFLOW, ERR_DIV_ZERO or the array range error), or print the same value when no trap is due")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeFormGapsTest.asl#" :text "Native form gaps: omitted record fields, keyword record pairs and positional variants.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#" :text "NATIVE-PERF gate: every speedup keeps ASL semantics. trapProbe cases with operands from argv fail natively with asl-host run's own error (Int64 overflow at the limits, division and mod by zero, INT64_MIN / -1, an induction variable stepping past INT64_MAX, a product of a mod result that can still overflow, an array index out of range) and give its value where no trap is due; the bench programs that allocate (list, record, map, str) give asl-host run's output natively with a collection before every allocation and the heap verified (ASL_GC_STRESS=1 ASL_GC_VERIFY=1), so an object the emitted code allocates without clearing is never traced half-built.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#errorTail" :text "From the first line holding ERR_: the text from ERR_ on, without asl-host's (after N asserts) suffix; empty when no line holds ERR_.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#trapCases" :text "Case arguments and the error each must raise, empty for a value.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#testGcStress" :text "The stress variables reach the bench binary alone (built by nativeTest prepareRunIn), not the asl-host that compiles it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#testTypedFields" :text "A schema field declared Int64 read off a tyRec base is raw in the emitted IR: record.step adds (.-pos b) and (.-vel b) with no generic @opsrt.add call (NATIVE-PERF lowerField), red when field reads stay Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#testListBuilders" :text "prelude.map and prelude.filter are emitted as in-order loops (ssa listBuilderText): their bodies allocate cells with asl_alloc_cons and never call the reversing preludeMapOnto, preludeFilterOnto or listReverse; red when the prelude.asl bodies are emitted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#testFloorFix" :text "Floor mod and div keep the truncated result on the non-negative path and fix a negative sign in the cold @mathrt.floorModFix / @mathrt.floorDivFix behind an unlikely branch: loop.go calls floorModFix and carries no select of the fix-up; red when the fix-up is an inline select on the loop's dependency chain.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#bitCases" :text "bitProbe arguments and the line each prints: the raw result, then the Val one, both as prelude.c computes them (and/or/xor/not on the 64-bit pattern, a shift count masked to 0..63, << wrapping, >> sign-extending); asl-host gains & | ^ ~ with unit ALLOCFIX, so these are expected values rather than an asl-host comparison.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativePerfTest.asl#testBits" :text "NATIVE-INTRINSICS: & | ^ ~ << >> over raw Int64 are the bare instruction in bitProbe.rawOp (no @mathrt helper call there, red when they lower to the helpers) and agree with the Val path at INT64_MIN, INT64_MAX, negative operands and shift counts of 64 and below 0; a String operand fails with want()'s ERR_TYPE text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#libcTriples" :text "The target triples this table covers, in table order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#emptyTripleFacts" :text "A TripleFacts with no triple, no rows and :verified false")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#pairFind" :text "The value paired with key in xs; the last pair wins when a key repeats, none when it is absent")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#structFieldOffset" :text "Byte offset of field within the struct, none when the table has no such field")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#structSize" :text "sizeof the named struct on this triple, none when the table has no such struct")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#libcConst" :text "Value of the named O_*, F_*, LOCK_*, errno or _SC_* constant on this triple, none when absent")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#rusageMaxRssUnit" :text "struct rusage's ru_maxrss unit for this triple, man-page-documented rather than a libc constant and so kept out of :consts (which libcTableTest validates against the probe row by row): bytes on Darwin/BSD (1024), kilobytes on Linux (1) -- see RSS_UNIT in asl/host/src/sys.c, which this value must keep matching. 1024 (Darwin's unit) for any other triple, matching libcFacts' darwinArm64Facts fallback.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#exePathSource" :text "How this triple names the running executable, an OS interface choice rather than a header constant and so kept out of :consts like rusageMaxRssUnit: nsGetExecutablePath on darwin (dyld's _NSGetExecutablePath(buf, &size), as asl/host/src/loader.c hostGetExecutablePath), procSelfExe on linux (the /proc/self/exe link); empty for a triple this table does not cover")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#libcVerified" :text "The triple's row's :verified: true for a row measured on a host of that triple (darwin-arm64 by libcTableTest on this host, linux-x86_64 and linux-aarch64 by linuxLayoutGateTest under glibc 2.36), false for a triple the table lacks")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#darwinArm64Facts" :text "Measured on this macOS arm64 host: /usr/bin/clang with the Xcode 17 SDK via tests/fixtures/libcProbe.c")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#concatRows" :text "The rows of groups, in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxCommonConsts" :text "The constants both linux triples share, from the kernel UAPI and glibc headers each group's (:m) comment names; measured on glibc 2.36 for both triples by linuxLayoutGateTest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxCommonStructs" :text "The struct layouts both linux triples share (every struct but stat), each from the glibc header its (:m) comment names; measured on glibc 2.36 for both triples by linuxLayoutGateTest.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxX8664Facts" :text "glibc on x86_64: the shared linux constants and structs, asm-generic's O_DIRECTORY and O_NOFOLLOW and x86_64's stat layout; measured on glibc 2.36 (linuxLayoutGateTest), so :verified.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxAarch64Facts" :text "glibc on aarch64: the shared linux constants and structs, arch/arm64's O_DIRECTORY and O_NOFOLLOW and the asm-generic stat layout, which differs from x86_64 in field order; measured on glibc 2.36 (linuxLayoutGateTest), so :verified.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#libcFacts" :text "The facts row for a triple named by libcTriples, none for any other triple")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#wasm32Facts" :text "wasm32-unknown-unknown has no libc: no errno accessor, no POSIX constants, variadic table or struct layouts, and :verified false since there is no host libc to measure. Its runtime services are runtimeAbi's host imports and the IR asl-target-llvm/wasmRuntime and asl-target-llvm/wasmFormat emit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#runtimeAbi" :text "The runtime services a libc-free target takes from its host, each a module.name host import, or memory.grow for linear-memory pages: wasm32 writes bytes to a file descriptor with asl.write (fd i32, ptr, length i64 -> written i64), exits with asl.exit (code i32), reads monotonic nanoseconds with asl.nowNs (-> i64) and traps with asl.trap (code, message, length i32); none for a libc triple, whose services are its libc.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#hostImport" :text "A runtimeAbi service name module.name split into its wasm import module and name; a name with no module is (pair \"\" service).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxErrnoBase" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/errno-base.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxErrno" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/errno.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxGenericFcntl" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h, no arch override on either")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxX8664OpenFlags" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h, which x86_64 uses unchanged")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxAarch64OpenFlags" :text "arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/fcntl.h overrides the generic values")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxFcntl" :text "include/uapi/linux/fcntl.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSeek" :text "include/uapi/linux/fs.h and glibc unistd.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxConfname" :text "glibc bits/confname.h enum, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxPoll" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/poll.h, no arch override on either")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxResource" :text "include/uapi/linux/resource.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxStatModes" :text "include/uapi/linux/stat.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxDirentTypes" :text "glibc dirent.h DT_* enum, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSocket" :text "glibc bits/socket.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxCmsg" :text "glibc bits/socket.h CMSG_LEN, CMSG_SPACE, CMSG_DATA of int")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSocketType" :text "glibc bits/socket_type.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSocketLevel" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/socket.h, which x86_64 includes unchanged")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxWait" :text "include/uapi/linux/wait.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxClocks" :text "include/uapi/linux/time.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxLimits" :text "include/uapi/linux/limits.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSignals" :text "arch/x86 uapi asm/signal.h equals asm-generic/signal.h here")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSignalHandlers" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSigprocmask" :text "glibc bits/sigaction.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxMmanCommon" :text "include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h; MAP_ANON is MAP_ANONYMOUS")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxMman" :text "include/uapi/linux/mman.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSyscalls" :text "x86_64 syscall_64.tbl and asm-generic/unistd.h agree")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSignalfd" :text "include/uapi/linux/signalfd.h, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxPthreadAttr" :text "glibc bits/pthreadtypes-arch.h __SIZEOF_PTHREAD_ATTR_T")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxX8664Stat" :text "glibc x86_64-linux-gnu/bits/struct_stat.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxAarch64Stat" :text "glibc aarch64-linux-gnu/bits/struct_stat.h, the asm-generic layout")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxFlock" :text "glibc bits/fcntl.h struct flock, both linux triples")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSockaddrIn" :text "glibc netinet/in.h over bits/sockaddr.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSockaddrUn" :text "glibc sys/un.h over bits/sockaddr.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxUtsname" :text "glibc sys/utsname.h, bits/utsname.h _UTSNAME_LENGTH 65")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxTm" :text "glibc bits/types/struct_tm.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxRusage" :text "glibc bits/types/struct_rusage.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxDirent" :text "glibc bits/dirent.h, d_name after d_type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxPollfd" :text "glibc sys/poll.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxTimespec" :text "glibc bits/types/struct_timespec.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxTimeval" :text "glibc bits/types/struct_timeval.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSpawnFileActions" :text "glibc spawn.h posix_spawn_file_actions_t")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSigset" :text "glibc bits/types/__sigset_t.h, 1024 bits")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSigaction" :text "glibc bits/sigaction.h: handler, mask, flags, restorer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSiginfo" :text "glibc bits/types/siginfo_t.h, 64-bit union padding")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxSignalfdSiginfo" :text "glibc sys/signalfd.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxPasswd" :text "glibc pwd.h struct passwd")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxMsghdr" :text "glibc bits/socket.h, size_t msg_iovlen and msg_controllen")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxCmsghdr" :text "glibc bits/socket.h, size_t cmsg_len")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxIovec" :text "glibc bits/types/struct_iovec.h")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxCommonVariadic" :text "glibc fcntl.h, sys/ioctl.h, unistd.h prototypes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/libc.asl#linuxErrnoAccessor" :text "glibc bits/errno.h: errno is (*__errno_location ())")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#" :text "Gate for ABIVAL-5: native code keeps its own intern table, string and argv constructors and error family in IR (asl-target-llvm/rtValue), so libaslrt.a carries no value.c or float.c. (1) nm -P lists no value.o or float.o member of libaslrt.a, and a native program built from keywords, variants, records, argv and an allocation failure has no intern, aslError, valPrint, mkStr or floatRepr symbol. (2) Native programs print and exit as asl-host run does for keywords and constructor names created in two modules and compared, 100000 distinct keywords (the table grows from 1024 slots), argv that is empty, unicode and 10000 arguments, and an allocation failure that gc.c reaches under ASL_GC_MAX_MIB, printing the floor exit's error line and status; the earlier native corpora (nativeFormatTest, nativeTrapTest, nativeOpsTest, nativeObjectTest) pass again.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#valueNames" :text "value.c and float.c symbols no native program may hold.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#chunkSource" :text "fn chunkC listing keywords :wN for N in [C * chunkSize, (C + 1) * chunkSize).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#manySource" :text "manyCount distinct keywords in chunks; main prints their count, a sample, equality and order results, and compares one with a keyword valfx/manyOther made.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#compiled" :text "path through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#memberName" :text "The member an nm -P archive header line names: 'abi.o:' on macOS, 'libaslrt.a[abi.o]:' on Linux.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#archiveMembers" :text "Member names of nm -P output over an archive: the header lines, which end in ':' and hold no space.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#symbolNames" :text "First fields of nm -P output, with the Mach-O leading underscore dropped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testArchive" :text "nm -P lists libaslrt.a's members: rtAbi.o (RT-ABI's IR runtime ABI), gcAsl.o (GCASL-2's ASL collector, appended at runtime() in place of gc.c's gc.o) and strFloor.o, and no abi.o, value.o, float.o or gc.o.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testSymbols" :text "The native program's symbol table holds the IR intern table (valrt.intern) and none of value.c's and float.c's names.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#build" :text "dir/name.asl compiled to dir/name.ll and linked against libaslrt.a into dir/name; returns the executable path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#hostErrorLine" :text "The ERR_<CODE>: <message> part of an asl-host run failure, reported as 'FAIL <file>: ERR_...: ... (after N asserts)'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testParity" :text "The native binary and asl-host run on the same arguments and environment exit alike; at exit 0 they print the same stdout, want is in it and native stderr is empty; at exit 1 native stderr is asl-host's error line alone, which starts with want.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#unroutedSource" :text "Values libaslhost.a's C builtins build and read, on the path a program takes where no route serves them (emitLlvmProgram; the default on Linux): a record whose field names C interned, a Result's ok and err, Options C reads (procSpawnv's cwd and env) and builds (procWaitPid's exit code).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#parSource" :text "A parMap whose element 1 raises natively (division by zero): the worker's raise must reach the handler parMap installed, routed or in parallel.c, and come back as ERR_WORKER_TRAP naming the element.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#unrouted" :text "path through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgram, which routes no builtin: sys, sysNet and parallel calls go to libaslhost.a's C tables.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#linkWith" :text "code written to dir/name.ll and linked with libs into dir/name; returns the executable path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testUnrouted" :text "One intern table: on the unrouted path native code and value.c's C builtins agree on field names, ok and err, some and none (value.c's KW_*), and a native raise in a parallel.c worker reaches parallel.c's handler.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#floorMain" :text "C main: asl_rt_init, then aslCall on the native partial application (spliced only when its Ctor id equals KW_PARTIAL) and on an Int with a handler installed in aslHandlerSlot, which aslCall's failure must longjmp to with its line in aslErrorText.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testFloorCalls" :text "aslCall over native values, from ssa cRuntimeModule's IR since NX4 (abi.c's before): a partial application splices because asl_rt_init gave KW_PARTIAL the id native code interns for partial, and a non-function raises to the installed handler instead of exiting.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/nativeValueTest.asl#testCorpus" :text "An earlier native gate passes again under asl-host test: exit 0, a passed count and no failure line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#tailCodeSym" :text "The tailcc twin of codeSym: the trampoline a proto holds after its native entry, entered by tailrt.closure with musttail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitTailTrampoline" :text "The tailcc entry (tailCodeSym) a closure tail call reaches through tailrt.closure: argv is the asl_rt_spill prefix, loaded before any spill store, and a Val result is passed on with musttail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitTrampolineAs" :text "A closure trampoline under head with the call prefix lhs: captures from env, arguments from argv, then the lambda's call and ret %Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#tailClosureFunction" :text "@tailrt.closure, a closure call in tail position: a native closure of matching arity is entered through its proto's tailCode slot (offset 64) with musttail, so the stack stays flat; any other callee (partial, bytecode, wrong arity, not a function) goes through objrt.call with its errors.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#emitSingletonGet" :text "The always-inlined @globalGet reader of an ssaOpt singleton g: on the first read it calls g's init, stores the value and sets @globalReady, after that it only loads; module init registers the root but never calls the init, so only the readers keep the init and a hoisted closure's code reachable and the linker dead-strips singletons of functions a program never reaches.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#globalGetSym" :text "The LLVM symbol of the emitSingletonGet reader of global name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#" :text "hoistConstants (plan unit MEM-NONE-SINGLETON, MEM-LAMBDA-HOIST): a per-module SSA rewrite run from main.asl before emission (host, Program/ForTarget and native) that turns every nullary opConstruct (a zero-field variant or record constant) and every captureless opMakeClosure built in the module's own functions into a lazily-initialized global, read with opGlobal, instead of allocating the same value afresh on every call; a Hoisted accumulator (keys from constantKey's text to an index, ops in reverse discovery order, count) carries the found constants from collect to the init functions and globals hoistConstants builds, named under singletonPrefix so a second pass over its own output is a no-op.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#singletonPrefix" :text "The per-module prefix (moduleName + \".@ssaOpt$\") this pass's own init functions are named under, so hoistConstants can tell them apart from the module's user functions and never hoist or rewrite its own output.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#singleton?" :text "Whether name is a global or init function hoistConstants made, in any module: it carries the \".@ssaOpt$\" marker singletonPrefix puts after the module name; ssa.asl asks it to emit such a global as lazily filled.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#constantKey" :text "A text key identifying ins's value when it is a val-typed opConstruct with no fields or opMakeClosure with no captures (distinct keys for the two forms so a constructor and a closure never collide), none for every other instruction, including a val-typed opConstruct or opMakeClosure that does carry fields or captures.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#initName" :text "The name of the init function hoistConstants gives the i-th hoisted constant under prefix.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#globalName" :text "The name of the global hoistConstants gives the i-th hoisted constant under prefix: initName with \"$g\" appended.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#noteInstr" :text "acc with ins's constant key recorded at the next index and its op remembered, when ins has one and it is not already in acc.keys; acc unchanged otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#collect" :text "The distinct hoistable constants across every block of every function in fs, in first-seen order, as a Hoisted.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#rewriteInstr" :text "ins with its op replaced by an opGlobal read of the global keys maps its constant key to under prefix, when it has a key found in keys; ins unchanged otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#rewriteFunction" :text "f with rewriteInstr applied to every instruction of every block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#initFunction" :text "The i-th init function under prefix: no parameters, one instruction computing op and returning it, called once to fill its matching global.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssaOpt.asl#hoistConstants" :text "m unchanged when its user functions (those not already named under m's own singletonPrefix) hold no hoistable constant; otherwise m with one SsaGlobal and one init function added per distinct constant collect found, those globals prepended to m.globals (the LLVM emitter fills each on its first read through ssa.asl emitSingletonGet, never in module init), and every user function's matching instructions rewritten to opGlobal reads.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#statePtrText" :text "The weak @asl_gc_state_ptr global, null until gcInit publishes @gcAsl.state through it; the fast-path allocators read it, so a gc.o-linked or uninitialised state always misses.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#fastAllocClass" :text "The small size class an inline fast path serves for an object of type and bytes, none for objects above the largest small class and for types 6 and 7.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#fastAllocCall" :text "The call text for an allocation of type and bytes: its size class's @gcAsl.allocFast helper when fastAllocClass has one, else @asl_alloc_raw.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#fastConsCall" :text "The call text of a 40-byte cons allocation through @gcAsl.allocFastCons, whose miss goes to asl_alloc_cons so a gc.o link pulls no new symbol.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#fastAllocDefinitions" :text "ALLOC-INLINE: one linkonce_odr alwaysinline helper per size class (and the cons helper) whose call text appears in keys, plus statePtrText when inline; inline helpers bump-allocate from the class's active page after the published-state, threshold and stress, free-list and page-room checks, set the inUse bit, header and three counters, and every miss tail-calls the raw allocator; without inline (wasm) each helper only forwards.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFloor.asl#" :text "RT-FLOOR: the runtime floor as LLVM IR text, libaslrt.a's member rtFloor.o in place of strFloor.c: weak gcFloorFail writes code: message (code capped at 125 bytes, message at 1023) and a newline to fd 2 with a write loop retrying EINTR, then exits 1, first handing code and message to the weak gcFloorRaise hook when one is set; weak gcFloorGuard is the guard slot.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFloor.asl#floorText" :text "The rtFloor module text for the target facts, or ERR_LLVM_RTFLOOR when libc.asl has no EINTR or no errno accessor for the triple.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFloor.asl#entryNames" :text "The symbols rtFloor.o defines: gcFloorFail, gcFloorGuard and gcFloorRaise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFloor.asl#main" :text "Writes the host's rtFloor module text to the path argument, or prints it without one; build.sh compiles it into rtFloor.o.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/allocInlineTest.asl#" :text "ALLOC-INLINE and STR-FORMAT gate: emitted record, ctor, closure and cons sites call their size class's inline fast-path helper instead of asl_alloc_raw, the helper's fast path calls nothing and takes the slow path on an unpublished state, a crossed threshold or ASL_GC_STRESS, a class with free pages or a full active page; record, list and allocMix programs report equal objectsAllocated and bytesAllocated inline and raw, collect under stress, and str renders into one stack buffer with one GC allocation per result.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#" :text "GC-MARK-SPEED gate: the collector's drain pushes a child from one block only, never touches the page header's per-object mark count or the marked-bytes slot inside its loop, reaches the push block only through a type-byte branch, and stays within its SSA instruction budget per marked child; record, list, allocMix and a deep tree program give the stdout and gcStats (collections, objectsAllocated, objectsFreed, bytesAllocated, bytesLive) the base collector printed, under ASL_GC_STRESS=1 and ASL_GC_MIN_MIB=1.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/tailCallSpillGcTest.asl#shWithin" :text "shWithin runs cmd with sh -c under tools/fleet/run.asl runOneLimited (timeoutS, 32 descendants, the whole tree killed on a verdict); stdout and stderr go to temp files that are read back and removed, and a kill verdict is appended to stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/tailCallSpillGcTest.asl#runTests" :text "every child runs under sh (runOneLimited); the ASan host build caches under the work directory, never ~/.asl/run/hosts; the work directory is removed before any result is asserted, so a failing assert leaves nothing behind")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/tailCallSpillGcTest.asl#" :text "TAILCALL-SPILL-ROOT: a closure tail call spills its arguments into the global @asl_rt_spill (asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl closureTailArgs), not onto the stack and not through asl_rt_global_root, because musttail is about to tear the caller's own frame down. @tailrt.closure (rtAbi-adjacent, asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl tailClosureFunction) reads argv straight from that global when the callee is not a plain arity-matching closure and falls to the objrt.call slow path (asl-target-llvm/src/rtObject.asl callFunction). This test builds a fresh, otherwise-unreferenced heap record, tail-calls a Partial (forced through the slow path, since a Partial's runtime tag is not the closure tag tailrt.closure checks for) with it as the sole new argument, and checks the record's content survives under ASL_GC_STRESS=1 (collect on every allocation) and under ASan with detect_stack_use_after_return, both with and without a deliberately injected allocation planted inside tailrt.closure's slow label (before objrt.call ever copies argv's contents onto the native stack) to prove the test is sensitive to the exact defect class described: an allocation landing in that window before the spilled Vals are copied somewhere scanned, while @asl_rt_spill itself is scanned by nothing.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#runs" :text "runs lists each fixture run: name, argument, environment, and the stdout and gcStats fields the collector printed on dd434074c (collections objectsAllocated objectsFreed bytesAllocated bytesLive), re-recorded at W34FIX when ssaOpt singletons became filled on first read: the deep rows move from conservative stack retention under the changed code layout, the threshold rows from shifted collections; every row allocates one 16-byte singleton fewer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/rtFloorTest.asl#" :text "RT-FLOOR gate: libaslrt.a holds rtFloor.o, rtAbi.o and gcAsl.o and rtFloor.o defines gcFloorFail, gcFloorGuard and gcFloorRaise; a program exhausting ASL_GC_MAX_MIB=1 exits 1 with the collector's formatted ERR_OOM line, a refused root-table realloc prints its formatted ERR_OOM line, and a set gcFloorRaise hook receives code and message with nothing on stderr.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#RefPiece" :text "RefPiece is a runtime piece with the keys (name + delimiter) whose occurrence makes a text refer to it; plain names (an @ head, no further @, no delimiter byte) are decided by refKeys membership, others by substring search")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#scanLine" :text "done and body accumulate reversed; piecesOf restores source order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refStop?" :text "refStop? is a byte that ends an @symbol scan: @ or one of the refDelimiters")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refAdd" :text "refAdd leaves acc untouched for a key already present (mapSet would copy its path)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refKeysFrom" :text "endNl: text is followed by a newline in the joined text, so a symbol running to its end is keyed with \\n")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refKeys" :text "refKeys is the set of every @symbol in text joined to the delimiter byte that ends it; for a plain name N and delimiter d, N+d occurs in text exactly when N+d is in refKeys text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refKeysJoin" :text "refKeysJoin adds refKeys (stringJoin chunks \\n) to acc without building the joined text: a newline ends every symbol, so each chunk but the last is scanned as if followed by one")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#tailSuffix" :text "tailSuffix takes chunks from the end (reversed) until they span 256 bytes with their newlines")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#tailOfJoin" :text "tailOfJoin is tailOf (stringJoin chunks \\n), joining only the chunks that reach into the last 256 bytes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refFirstKey" :text "refFirstKey is the first refKeys key of text; when text occurs inside a larger text T, that key is in refKeys T")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refPlain?" :text "refPlain? holds for @NAME where NAME has no @ and no stop byte, so its occurrences are exactly refKeys entries")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refersVia?" :text "refersVia? is the text scan text contains name+d for some delimiter d, answered from keys = refKeys text for a plain name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refClose" :text "refClose adds every piece the text refers to, then rescans the last 256 bytes of the text joined to the fresh bodies, until nothing is fresh; chosen maps piece names")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#refCloseJoin" :text "refCloseJoin is refClose (stringJoin chunks \\n) (mapEmpty) pieces; the joined text is built only when a piece name is not plain")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorPieces" :text "rtErrorPieces parses the error and value runtime once; emit passes it to every rtErrorDefinitionsWith of one module")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtError.asl#rtErrorDefinitionsJoin" :text "rtErrorDefinitionsJoin is rtErrorDefinitionsWith pieces (stringJoin chunks \\n) without the joined text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#plainFrom?" :text "plainFrom? holds when every byte of b from i on satisfies keep?; then the escaping functions return their input unchanged")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#declPlain?" :text "declUsed? is stringContains? text (declSymbol decl), answered from keys = rterr/refKeys text when the symbol is a plain @NAME( ")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#usedDeclsJoin" :text "usedDeclsJoin is usedDecls (stringJoin chunks \\n) decls; the joined text is built only for a symbol that is not a plain @NAME(")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathPiecesAll" :text "math pieces refer by name followed by ( ) , space or newline (no ]), unlike rtError pieces")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mathDefinitionsJoin" :text "mathDefinitionsJoin is mathDefinitions (stringJoin chunks \\n) without the joined text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#withEntryCalls" :text "withEntryCalls is the chunk list whose newline join is (str (stringJoin defs \\n) \\n entryCalls)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#pieceAbsent?" :text "pieceAbsent? is not (stringContains? text (stringTrim piece)); a piece whose first @symbol key is missing from keys = rterr/refKeys text cannot occur in text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl#mentionsVal?" :text "mentionsVal? is stringContains? (str a b) %Val without copying a: a match lies in a, in b, or across their seam")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitAllocTest.asl#entryPath" :text "the corpus is the link closure of fixtures/emitAlloc/entry.asl (asl-json/tests/jsonTest, asl-json/json) plus the prelude functions it reaches, emitted for Darwin arm64; main lowers it and, unless its argument is lower, emits it, so the difference of the two runs' ASL_GC_STATS bytesAllocated is the emit allocation")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitAllocTest.asl#emittedBytes" :text "emittedBytes is the total LLVM text length of the corpus (0 per module when emit is false), or -1 when a step fails")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitAllocTest.asl#runTests" :text "emit of the jsonTest corpus allocates (emit run minus lower-only run) below 253.4 MB (1.2x the 211 MB measured 2026-10-10 at this head); measured 2026-10-09 interpreted on Darwin arm64: 727 MB at U3-REFS-SET 811fcbcc0, 450 MB after U9-ALLOC, 211 MB at this head")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsGoldenTest.asl#entryPath" :text "the corpus is the link closure of fixtures/emitRefs/entry.asl (asl-syntax/core/source and its imports) plus the prelude functions it reaches, lowered unit by unit as tools/nativeTest.asl does, emitted for a fixed Darwin arm64 host so the digests do not depend on the machine")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsGoldenTest.asl#corpusTexts" :text "each row is (pair module text) for the emitted LLVM text; a failure is a row whose text starts with ERR")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsGoldenTest.asl#corpusDigests" :text "each row is (pair \"module bytes\" sha256) of the emitted text")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsGoldenTest.asl#main" :text "main prints the digest rows; with a directory argument it also writes each module's text there as NAME.ll (slashes become dashes)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsGoldenTest.asl#expectedDigests" :text "expected rows re-recorded at WAVE3+4 fix-round integration (W34INT on W4INT 0aa29bd02, merging sh/W34FIX then sh/W34LOW): 25 of 29 rows move, all from sh/W34FIX's lazy-singleton change (ssaOpt.asl opGlobal calls an alwaysinline @globalGet reader instead of module init storing every hoisted global directly, so each module's globalReady flag and reader function text changes); asl-syntax/core/print, asl-syntax/core/bytesText, asl-syntax/js/lex and emitRefsEntry are unchanged because those modules hoist no globals. sh/W34LOW touches fleet/compare.asl, lowerScaleTest.asl, gcAsl.asl and rtFormat.asl doc comments only, none of which reach this corpus. Before that: expected rows re-recorded at WAVE4 integration (W4INT on W3INT 75f7142c7): all 29 rows move. Merging one branch at a time, ALLOC-INLINE plus STR-FORMAT (sh/W4RUNTIME: record, ctor, closure and cons sites call gcAsl.allocFast helpers whose linkonce_odr definitions each module appends, and rtFormat renders into a stack buffer) moves all 29, sh/W4REDS (gcAccount declared and called as void) moves 16, sh/W4PRELUDE (listAll? listAny? listTake listDrop match on listTail) moves prelude, and sh/ASL1SELF (checkSemanticTest edit) moves checkSemanticTest, emitRefsEntry and prelude; every other merge moves none. Reverting exactly those hunks (ssa.asl ALLOC-INLINE and gcAccount, rtFormat.asl, prelude.asl, checkSemanticTest.asl) in a scratch copy of the integration head reproduces all 29 W3INT digests byte for byte, so the move is these changes and not an integration conflict; the second-pass merge of sh/ASL1SELF (NATIVE-ARGSMAIN: rterr.reportInit calls unsetenv) then moves emitRefsEntry alone, its .ll differing by exactly the unsetenv call and declare Before that: expected rows re-recorded at WAVE3 integration (W3INT, merge of sh/W3SSAOPT onto WAVEINT c20d96ae2): emitLlvmModuleFor/emitLlvmProgramFor now route through ssaOpt's hoistConstants (main.asl, opt/hoistConstants), which turns every nullary opConstruct and captureless opMakeClosure in a module into a lazily-initialized singleton global read with opGlobal; reverting just that wiring in a scratch build (ssa/emitLlvmModule r / ssa/emitLlvmProgram r entry, no opt/hoistConstants) reproduces every digest below's predecessor unchanged, confirming the move is this merge's effect and not an integration conflict. 25 of 29 rows move (one or more hoisted constant in that module's own functions, mostly smaller emitted text since a repeated construction collapses to one init call); core/print, bytesText, js/lex and emitRefsEntry hold no such constant and keep their digest")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsTimingTest.asl#entryPath" :text "emit time of the 2-line entry wrapper fixtures/emitRefs/sourceEntry.asl (program path, sysRoute for Darwin arm64) and of the module asl-syntax/core/source it imports; lowering is outside the timed span")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsTimingTest.asl#emitMicros" :text "(pair module microseconds) per emitted module, best of three runs; -1 when lowering or emission fails")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitRefsTimingTest.asl#runningNatively?" :text "native code has its own procExePath, the way sysRouteTest tells native from host; asl-host's own procExePath is asl-host itself")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/emitScaleTest.asl#emitCpu" :text "emitCpu is the self CPU microseconds of emitLlvmProgram on the lowered source, -1 when lowering or emission fails")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/fixtures/nativeSha/shaProbe.asl#fill" :text "fill n bytes with a fixed affine sequence so every run hashes the same 1 MB without reading a file")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/fixtures/nativeSha/shaProbe.asl#bestMs" :text "the fastest of three timed hashes of the same data, in ms, so one descheduled run on a loaded machine does not decide the figure")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/ssaOptTest.asl#testNative" :text "spin evaluates (none) and a captureless lambda 1e6 times: 2000009 objects and 40000292 bytes before the pass, 28 objects and 676 bytes after (measured 2026-10-10, Darwin arm64, W3-SSAOPT); the bound 10000 is adopted")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmImportTest.asl#singleCallProbe" :text "a module whose main calls one builtin, with arity 0 or 1 unit-valued arguments, so each wasm import or capability-absence case is tested in isolation")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/wasmImportTest.asl#absentCases" :text "builtins once routed through host imports but now rejected as absent on wasm32-wasi (WASMSYSVAL, f554bbcbd): only print remains a wasm host import; each of these names its own arity so singleCallProbe can exercise it in isolation, including a mismatched arity (nowNs called with one argument still names nowNs, absence is checked before arity)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/gcAsl.asl#defaultMinMib" :text "defaultMinMib is the native collector's floor on new bytes between collections when ASL_GC_MIN_MIB is unset, adopted in .asl/mem/bench/perfBaseline.asn (:gcPolicy)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/src/rtFormat.asl#inlineBufferStart" :text "a format starts in a 256-byte stack buffer flagged by the sign bit of its capacity; rtfmt_put copies it to malloc only when a result outgrows it, and the finish frees only a spilled buffer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/allocInlineTest.asl#functionText" :text "functionText is the text of the definition opening with head, through its closing brace line, or empty when text has no such definition")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/allocInlineTest.asl#countedHeap" :text "countedHeap routes the program's own malloc and realloc calls through counters printed at exit as (:heapCalls :malloc N :realloc M)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#sh" :text "sh runs cmd with sh -c under tools/fleet/run.asl (runOneLimited, 1200 s timeout, 32 descendants, the whole tree killed on a verdict), so every child of this test, asl-host, clang or a built program, is supervised; stdout and stderr go to temp files that are read back and removed, and a kill verdict is appended to stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcAslTest.asl#gcRawIr" :text "gc.c has no asl_alloc_raw, which emitted code calls since NATIVE-PERF (f275a9917); the gc.o link gets it as asl_alloc, whose cleared object is a valid raw one, so the link never pulls gcAsl.o. That link also takes asl-host's strFloor.o, because gc.c passes printf arguments to gcFloorFail and libaslrt.a's rtFloor.o prints its message as given. The whole gc.o reference side goes away at ZC-DELETE")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#drainOf" :text "drainOf is the collector's drain function as gcRoute assembles it for this host, or none when the host has no libc row or the module fails")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#baseOf" :text "baseOf follows a rawIntToPtr back to the integer it converts")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#memOps" :text "memOps lists each raw load or store in instrs as (prim base offset), the base being the integer address and the offset the constant operand, -1 when not constant")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#derives?" :text "derives? holds when name is, or is computed from, a logical shift right of src by 32 (the type byte of a header), searched depth operands deep")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#typeGated?" :text "typeGated? holds for a block that branches on the child header's type byte")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#reachUngated" :text "reachUngated lists the labels reachable from start within one child step, stopping at the child loop head kids and at type-gated blocks")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#pathOps" :text "pathOps counts the non-constant instructions of the named drain blocks that exist")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#interiorPath" :text "interiorPath is the drain's work for a newly marked pooled child with fields: test it, mark it, push it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#leafPath" :text "leafPath is the drain's work for a newly marked pooled child without fields (a string): with the type branch it ends at push, without it the child is pushed, popped and dispatched to leaf")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcMarkSpeedTest.asl#deepSource" :text "deepSource builds trees whose survival runs through every field kind the drain traces: ctor fields (fork), record fields (Leaf), cons cells (pairs) and closure upvalues (getters), then churns the heap while they stay live")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcPolicyTest.asl#sh" :text "sh runs cmd with sh -c under tools/fleet/run.asl runOneLimited (1200 s timeout, 32 descendants, the whole tree killed on a verdict); stdout and stderr go to temp files that are read back and removed, and a kill verdict is appended to stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcPolicyTest.asl#policyPart" :text "policyPart drops the timing field from a (:gcStats ...) line, leaving what the heap policy decides")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/gcPolicyTest.asl#testEffective" :text "testEffective runs one allocation-heavy program with no setting, with the adopted value set explicitly and with 1 MiB: the built runtime's default is the adopted value when the first two collect identically and the third differs")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/rtFloorTest.asl#refusedReallocIr" :text "refusedReallocIr is a program whose own realloc refuses every request, so the first asl_rt_global_root call fails growing rtAbi's root table to 16 slots; it defines the KW_* globals and aslInternShared a program's IR normally provides")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/rtFloorTest.asl#raiseHookIr" :text "raiseHookIr sets gcFloorRaise, as asl-host's vm.c does, to a handler that prints what it was given and exits 3, then fails through the floor")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-llvm/tests/tailCallSpillGcTest.asl#plantSlowAlloc" :text "plantSlowAlloc simulates, deterministically, what an allocation landing in tailrt.closure's slow label (ahead of objrt.call ever reading argv) would be free to do to the only copy of the tail-called argument's Val if that spot were not rooted: @asl_rt_spill's first slot (fresh's tag word, as closureTailArgs left it) is overwritten right before objrt.call is handed argv, which still points at it. Forcing the exact same corruption through an actually-reused, GC-collected page was tried first (asl_alloc_raw matching Boxed's own tag/size exactly, under ASL_GC_STRESS) and did not reproduce: this allocator frees a page wholesale once every live slot in it dies (sweepPages's pfree path in gcAsl.asl), rather than handing that same slot back out on the very next same-size request, so a single collection right there does not happen to clobber fresh's bytes. The direct store proves the thing that actually matters for this gate: a write landing in that unrooted window, between the spill and objrt.call's read of it, is caught by this test's output check, which is exactly the failure mode rooting (or proof of no allocation there) is meant to rule out.")
